window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS=(window.CULTIVATION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2201,"title":"Chapter 2201: Inferno Alchemists","paragraphs":["Three days had passed since they entered the Land of Inferno.","Yuan suddenly noticed the cultivator’s pace quickening, as though impatience—or something else—was driving him forward.","\"Is there something wrong?\" Yuan asked him.","\"W-What?\" The cultivator muttered as he turned to face Yuan, looking startled by the question.","\"You’re speeding up, almost like you cannot wait to arrive at our destination.\"","\"Isn’t that obvious? The faster we reach our destination, the faster I get to go home,\" he said.","Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly and spoke, \"What are you hiding? It’d be in your best interest to tell me the truth before you do something stupid.\"","\"I’m not hiding anything!\" the cultivator snapped, his tone firm—but the flicker of nervousness in his eyes betrayed him.","Yuan fell silent for a moment before speaking again, \"Let’s see... What are the chances that instead of taking me to the Burning Tree like I told you, you’re actually bringing me to another location?\"","The cultivator’s body twitched at his words.","Seeing his reaction, Yuan continued with a cold smile, \"What if you’re actually taking me to the Chaotic Sect instead?\"","\"That’s nonsense! You’re just making shit up!\" The cultivator came to a halt and shouted with a flushed face. \"If you want to kill me, just do it! There’s no need for you to make excuses!\"","Yuan then said, \"You know what? I don’t trust you, but I’ll still give you the benefit of the doubt. However, I must warn you. If you’re actually taking me to the Chaotic Sect, things won’t play out like you’re hoping, and you’ll be the reason for their destruction.\"","\"...\"","The cultivator didn’t immediately respond, and after a moment of silence, he continued flying without a word.","Yuan also didn’t say anything and continued to follow him.","Several days later, Yuan remarked, \"According to you, we should’ve arrived at the Burning Tree by now.\"","\"I... I accidentally took the wrong turn. We should arrive at our destination in five days. I apologize for the inconvenience,\" he said.","\"Is that so? Be more careful this time.\" Yuan didn’t pursue the matter and patiently waited.","After another two days, they came to a halt when an individual wearing red and gold robes blocked their path.","\"You’re not allowed to go any further unless you want to offend the Asura Clan. Turn around and leave,\" said the man who was clearly from the Inferno Alchemists.","\"Unfortunately, I cannot do that, as I have some business with the Asura Clan,\" said Yuan.","The Alchemist immediately frowned at his words and replied, \"The Asura Clan? Who are you? And what is your relationship with them?\"","\"We’re something like friends, I guess.\"","\"...\"","The Alchemist stared at Yuan with wide eyes filled with disbelief before he suddenly burst out laughing.","\"Hahaha! Friends?! Surely, you must have a better lie than that! The Asura Clan has no friends!\"","\"Who are you to claim they have no friends? Are you that close with the Asura Clan?\" Yuan questioned, which instantly halted the Alchemist’s laughter.","\"If you claim to be his friend, what is your name? We’ll ask the Asura Clan about you, and if you turn out to be lying...\"","\"Tell them Tian Xian is here to see them. If I am lying, you can turn me into dog food or whatever you want,\" Yuan responded with a confident smile.","\"Don’t worry, I’ll do just that. Until we can confirm your identity, you will have to stay with us at the Inferno Alchemist’s headquarters. After all, we don’t want you to run away after making such a bold claim.\"","\"How long will this take?\" Yuan asked.","\"I don’t know since it’s not like we can contact the Asura Clan as we please.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan nodded, \"Alright.\"","Although he didn’t say it out loud, he decided to give them a month at most. If they couldn’t contact the Asura Clan by then, he would head to the Burning Tree by force.","\"Umm... what about me? I have brought you to your destination, so...\" The cultivator from the Chaotic Sect said.","Yuan silently glared at him for a moment before responding, \"Yes, as promised, you’re free to go.\"","\"T-Thank you!\"","Without hesitation, the cultivator immediately turned around and began fleeing like his life depended on it.","Even as he put distance between them, Yuan’s voice trailed after him. \"When you return, try to convince the Chaotic Sect not to seek revenge. You wouldn’t want to squander the second life I gave you, do you?\"","\"What was that about?\" asked the Alchemist.","\"Oh, don’t worry about him. He was just a guide.\"","\"...Whatever. Follow me.\"","Yuan nodded, and he and Mu Xuelian followed the Alchemist back to the Inferno Alchemist’s headquarters.","A day later, they arrived at the Inferno Alchemist’s headquarters, a place built like a sect but on a much smaller scale.","When they arrived, the Alchemist brought Yuan to a guest house before leaving to report the situation to his superiors. Of course, he didn’t leave Yuan and Mu Xuelian unsupervised and had several people guard their place.","\"What? A friend of the Asura Clan? What nonsense is that?\"","The elders almost couldn’t believe their ears and were very dismissive about the situation.","\"They’re definitely just some troublemaker trying to reach the Spirit Tree. Fools like them occasionally show up.\"","\"Right? Just kill them and save the trouble. We cannot bother the Asura Clan over such insignificant issues.\"","However, the Alchemist who brought Yuan to their headquarters said, \"That’s what I thought at first, too. But he’s unlike the others. There’s something different about him, and he’s strangely confident. Otherwise, he wouldn’t have followed me back here. What if he’s telling the truth? If we act too prematurely without even investigating a little and accidentally kill someone close to the Asura Clan... wouldn’t that spell the end of our faction?\"","\"...\"","The elders found logic behind the Alchemist’s words, and the room quickly fell silent as they pondered their situation more seriously."]},{"number":2202,"title":"Chapter 2202: The Chaotic Sect’s Response","paragraphs":["\"What Alchemist Shen said is logical. If those two are truly connected to the Asura Clan in some way and we kill them, it’d spell the end of our faction,\" one of the elders said, breaking the silence.","\"Then what should we do with them? The chances of them being ’friends’ with the Asura Clan are slim to none, and if we bother the Asura Clan, it might affect our relationship with them,\" said another elder.","\"Why don’t we hold off on contacting the Asura Clan and examine them for a little while before we make any decision?\"","\"That’s a good idea. We can just stall this for a little. If they turn out to be troublemakers, we’ll kill them.\"","Though the Inferno Alchemists’ stance might seem excessive, it revealed the depth of their fear toward the Asura Clan. In the Primordial Realm, even something as simple as approaching them to confirm an identity was anything but simple.","\"I’ll let them know,\" said Alchemist Shen, who guided Yuan and Mu Xuelian to their headquarters.","While the elders continued to contemplate the situation some more, Alchemist Shen returned to Yuan’s guest house.","\"We will be sending someone to the Asura Clan to confirm your identity soon,\" Alchemist Shen said to Yuan.","\"So, how long is this going to take?\"","\"I’m not sure... but we’ll let you know immediately when we receive an answer.\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly and said, \"There’s no way it should take more than a few hours, a few days at most. Don’t you have something to contact them directly?\"","Alchemist Shen looked at him with a dumbfounded face and said, \"Only our leader has direct communication with the Asura Clan, but even then, he can only use it during emergencies.\"","Yuan sighed out loud, \"Why are they so hard to contact?\"","Alchemist Shen remained silent.","\"In any case, we just need to wait, right? Alright, but don’t take too long.\"","\"Thank you for your understanding.\"","Meanwhile, at the Chaotic Sect, the cultivator who managed to survive revealed the situation to the Sect Leader and other elders.","\"What did you say?! A mere True Immortal killed four God Ascension cultivators?! Do you really expect me to believe that?!\" The leader of the Chaotic Sect angrily shouted after receiving this news from the sole survivor.","\"I swear on my soul it’s true!\"","The room fell silent for a moment.","\"Sect Leader Zu! We must avenge Elder Zi and the others!\" One of the elders suddenly exclaimed.","\"How dare that bastard kill people from our Chaotic Sect! Our elders, no less!\"","Hearing that they wanted revenge, the cultivator quickly said, \"No! We shouldn’t!\"","Everyone in the room turned to look at the cultivator with deep frowns on their faces.","\"Elder Jiang, what are you saying? Are you telling us not to avenge Elder Zi and the others? Are you out of your damn mind?!\"","\"Did you get brainwashed by that bastard or something, Elder Jiang?\"","\"Y-You don’t understand! That guy wasn’t human! He killed everyone in the blink of an eye, and he did so with immense ease! He might also have connections with the Asura Clan!\" Elder Jiang exclaimed.","\"T-The Asura Clan...?\"","The atmosphere in the room instantly changed at the mere mention of the Asura Clan.","\"Elder Jiang.\" The Sect Leader suddenly spoke in a chilling tone, causing him to tremble. \"Putting the issue with the Asura Clan aside, are you claiming that a single Immortal is stronger than the entire Chaotic Sect, so we should not offend him?\"","\"That’s...\" Elder Jiang could not find a proper response.","After a moment of silence, he shook his head and responded, \"No, unless he’s as powerful as the head of the Asura Clan, there’s no way a single person could threaten our Chaotic Sect. I apologize. It seems I haven’t been thinking straight from fear.\"","\"Very well. Now, let’s get back to the other subject. You said he has a connection with the Asura Clan. How certain are you on that?\"","\"That’s... Honestly, I’m not very certain. He had me bring him to the Burning Tree. If he truly had a connection with the Asura Clan, he wouldn’t need me to take him there. However, there’s something about him that reminds me of those from the Asura Clan.\"","The Sect Leader stood up and said, \"Regardless of whether he’s related to the Asura Clan or not, I will not let someone who killed four of our people get away with it. Gather all of the elders. We’re going to avenge the others.\"","\"As you command!\"","A week later, at the Inferno Alchemists’ headquarters.","\"Master! We have an emergency! The Chaotic Sect’s leader and many of their members are currently at our gates!\"","\"The Chaotic Sect? What do they want from us?\" The leader of the Inferno Alchemist was immediately alarmed by this news.","\"They’re demanding your presence, and that’s all we know!\"","\"What a bunch of arrogant bastards. Are they trying to start a war with us or something?\"","The leader of the Inferno Alchemist went to meet with the Chaotic Sect shortly after.","\"Sect Leader Zu, what is the meaning of this? To show up unannounced with so many of your elders... are you trying to invade us? Do you not fear the Asura Clan?\"","Sect Leader Zu quickly responded, \"Don’t worry, Leader Yang. We have no business with the Inferno Alchemists today. We’re here for that bastard who came to your place recently—the one who’s trying to go to the Burning Tree. Is he still here?\"","\"...\"","Leader Yang responded, \"Yes, he’s still here. Why are you looking for him?\"","\"That bastard killed four of our elders, and we’re here to make him pay for his crimes.\"","\"What...?\" Leader Yang wore a dumbfounded look on his face as he was fed this information.","\"Are you sure you have the right person? That man is only a True Immortal, and your elders are all at least God Ascension cultivators. Yet you claim he killed four of them?\" he asked."]},{"number":2203,"title":"Chapter 2203: The Chaotic Sect’s Revenge","paragraphs":["\"I am aware of how ridiculous it sounds, but it is the truth,\" said Sect Leader Zu.","\"Hmm...\"","After a moment of silence, Leader Yang responded, \"I understand your situation. Unfortunately, I cannot just hand him over to you.\"","\"Why are you protecting him?\"","\"First of all, he is our guest. If we hand him over simply because you demand it, our reputation will be tarnished. Second—and more importantly—that man may have ties to the Asura Clan. I trust I don’t need to spell out what that means,\" said Leader Yang.","\"Hahaha!\" Sect Leader Zu suddenly burst out laughing. \"Don’t tell me that man actually managed to fool the Inferno Alchemists with such an obvious lie!\"","Leader Yang narrowed his eyes slightly and replied, \"Are you saying that he’s lying about being connected with the Asura Clan?\"","\"Do I really have to answer such an obvious question?\"","\"Do you have any proof to back up your claim? Although we don’t have proof that he’s connected with the Asura Clan, we also don’t have evidence that he’s lying to us. It’s better to be safe than sorry.\"","\"Proof? I don’t need such a thing! Even an idiot can tell that he’s lying!\"","\"Then I may be an idiot. Can you enlighten me?\"","\"...\"","Sect Leader Zu fell silent, as he did not have a proper response.","\"Enough of the chitchat. Regardless of whether he’s related to the Asura Clan or not, it’s a fact that he killed four of my elders. This will be my last time asking. Will you hand him over to us or not?\"","Sect Leader Zu’s aura suddenly started increasing.","\"And what are you going to do if we refuse your demands? Attack us? Do you not fear the Asura Clan’s wrath?\"","\"Don’t worry, we won’t harm the Inferno Alchemists. However, we will drag him back with us even if we have to be a little forceful.\"","\"...\"","Leader Yang fell silent. The Inferno Alchemists numbered barely a hundred; if the Chaotic Sect truly wished to annihilate them, resistance would be futile. However, due to their connection with the Asura Clan, the Chaotic Sect wouldn’t dare to do such a thing. Moreover, so long as no harm befell the Inferno Alchemists directly, the Chaotic Sect believed there was a good chance the Asura Clan would overlook the matter.","’If we hand Tian Xian over to them, we would look like pushovers, and if he happened to really be connected to the Asura Clan, we would have no excuse. However, if we refuse and they forcefully take him away, our reputation would still take a blow, but at least, we can tell the Asura Clan that we had no choice since we’re no match for the Chaotic Sect.’","After weighing the choices, Leader Yang gave his answer, \"My answer is no. We won’t hand him over to you. If you want to take him, you’ll have to do it with force.\"","This way, the Inferno Alchemists wouldn’t be held responsible for Yuan’s death.","Sect Leader Zu sneered before commanding the hundreds of disciples that came with him, \"You heard him. Search every nook and cranny and bring that bastard back to me!\"","\"Yes!\"","At his command, the Chaotic Sect’s disciples invaded the Inferno Alchemists’ territory to look for Yuan.","\"Leader! What should we do?! Are we really going to just stand here and let them invade our territory?! Even if they’re not here for us, they’ve crossed a line they shouldn’t!\" The elders of the Inferno Alchemists asked as they watched the sea of disciples fly past them.","Leader Yang shook his head and said, \"There’s nothing we can do but let the Asura Clan deal with them.\"","He turned to glare at Sect Leader Zu and spoke angrily, \"You’ll regret this, Sect Leader Zu.\"","In response, Sect Leader Zu merely sneered with disdain.","Meanwhile, Yuan stopped studying the Mystic Sword Tablet and sighed out loud, \"Looks like I have guests.\"","\"Need my help?\" Mu Xuelian asked as she watched him stand up and approach the exit.","\"I’ll be fine.\"","Stepping outside, Yuan spotted dozens of black-robed cultivators prowling the area, banging on doors as they wandered from house to house like a bunch of law enforcers looking for a fugitive.","\"They sure brought a lot of trash...\" Yuan sighed.","\"H-Hey! I think that’s him!\"","One of the disciples shouted when he saw Yuan.","\"You might be right. He matches the description.\"","Yuan smiled and calmly spoke out loud, \"If you’re looking for the one who killed your elders, you’ve definitely found him.\"","\"I-It’s him! Someone let the elders know that we have found him!\"","The disciples immediately surrounded Yuan and his building.","Yuan swept the crowd with a mocking gaze. \"Not a single God-Ascension among you—what do you expect to accomplish here?\"","\"With our Sect Leader and most of the elders present, resistance would be pointless. Do the sensible thing and surrender yourself peacefully.\"","\"Peace? You forfeited that option when you came here for revenge, even though I warned you—or did that one I spare not tell you not to come here?\"","\"Shut up! Who do you think you are, telling us what to do? Did you really expect us not to seek revenge after you killed four of our elders?!\" one of them snarled, his tone full of killing intent.","\"No, I figured you would come after me. However, I still held onto some hope. Anyway, let’s kill some time before your elders arrive, shall we?\"","Before the disciples could even react, Yuan struck first. With most of them being at the Immortal Realm, it took him little effort to cut them down. Of course, he didn’t wield any weapon and used only his Supreme Sword Aura.","In mere moments, Yuan reduced their numbers by half, staining the place with their blood.","\"W-What a monster!\"","\"How is he this powerful when we have the same cultivation?!\"","\"Fuck! I can see how he defeated our elders!\"","Until they faced Yuan’s overwhelming might firsthand, most of the disciples had doubted that he could have slain their elders.","\"We must keep him here until the elders arrive at all costs!\""]},{"number":2204,"title":"Chapter 2204: Unfathomable Killing Intent","paragraphs":["\"Keep me here...?\" A smile appeared on Yuan’s face as he stopped his killing spree. \"I believe there is a misunderstanding. I have no intention of going anywhere, much less running away.\"","\"Do you really believe you can defeat the Chaotic Sect by yourself?! Our leader is at the 7th level of God Ascension powerhouse! He’s not someone you can even touch, let alone defeat!\"","\"Seventh level, huh? It might be a little difficult, but it’s definitely doable.\"","The disciples stared at him with stunned disbelief. After a moment of silence, they all burst out laughing.","\"Hahaha! He really thinks he can defeat our Sect Leader! What a fool!\"","\"That’s already beyond foolishness!\"","Meanwhile, at the Sect Leader’s location.","\"Sect Leader! Elders! We have found that bastard!\" declared the disciple who left to find them.","\"Oh? Take us there.\"","\"Right away!\"","Sect Leader Zu and the elders hurried after the disciple to Yuan’s guest house. What greeted them there left them stunned—the ground was strewn with the mutilated corpses of their disciples, blood soaking the earth in a grisly scene.","\"Took you long enough,\" said Yuan, who was casually sitting by his doorstep.","\"I-Impossible... He killed all of them in such a short time?!\"","The disciple who went to find the others was terrified. After all, it’d only been ten minutes at most since he left.","\"You bastard...\" Sect Leader Zu growled through clenched teeth, fury blazing in his eyes. \"Not only did you kill four of our elders, but you also slaughtered dozens of our disciples now!\"","\"You must be the Sect Leader,\" said Yuan after noticing his cultivation at the 7th level of God Ascension. \"Didn’t you get my warning? I warned you that if you came after me after I spared one of your elders, that I would kill all of you, right?\"","Yuan’s gaze shifted to Elder Jiang, whom he’d spared.","\"Who do you think you are to threaten my Chaotic Sect?! Not even the Asura Clan has threatened us!\" Sect Leader Zu roared. \"And you killed four of our elders! Do you really expect us to sit back and pretend it never happened?!\"","\"Why are you making it sound like I killed your elders for no reason? In the first place, your elders tried to rob and kill me, something you approved of. Was it wrong for me to kill them? Am I not allowed to defend myself? You should count yourself lucky I didn’t visit the Chaotic Sect to kill you. And yet here you are, marching to my door. You must really have a death wish.\"","Sect Leader Zu trembled, his blood boiling with rage. For millions of years, no one—not even the other powerhouses—had dared speak to him in such a manner. Yet now, a mere Immortal stood before him, looking down on him as if he were nothing.","A powerful aura erupted from Sect Leader Zu, flooding the air with a torrent of killing intent. Sensing his killing intent, even his own disciples trembled in fear.","\"...\"","Of all the foes Yuan had faced in this life, none radiated more killing intent than Sect Leader Zu, a testament to the countless lives he had already taken.","After countless eras, few cultivators from the Primordial Era still remained, and Sect Leader Zu was one of the rare survivors. Thus, it made sense for him to exude such killing intent. \"Look at you—paralyzed with fear from nothing more than my killing intent,\" Sect Leader Zu sneered, watching Yuan stand motionless, eyes slightly widened.","A cold smile curved Yuan’s lips. \"Fear? I’ll admit, your killing intent is impressive, but only in the eyes of ordinary people.\"","\"Hahaha! Still pretending to be tough, huh? Then how about this?!\"","Sect Leader Zu unleashed the full extent of his killing intent, so dense and potent that it began to take form in the air, a feat Yuan himself had displayed before.","With this much killing intent filling the air, the disciples around him, including the elders, subconsciously started backing away.","Channeling his killing intent, Sect Leader Zu forged a spear of crimson and black, its tip leveled menacingly at Yuan.","\"Let’s see if you can still act so arrogantly after having a taste of my killing intent!\"","Yuan watched calmly as the spear hurtled toward him, making no move to evade. It pierced straight through his body, yet left no wound. Unlike Sword Aura or spiritual energy, pure killing intent held no power to inflict physical harm despite its seemingly solid form, which was why it passed through him so effortlessly.","Instead, killing intent assailed the mind. For those lacking mental strength or unaccustomed to its pressure, it could shatter their mind, leaving them a hollow shell, or worse, killing them outright.","Sect Leader Zu and the others watched with smug expressions, waiting for Yuan to break into screams.","Yet, that moment did not come.","Yuan slowly closed his eyes, and at once the atmosphere shifted. A red aura seeped from his body, spreading through the air and draping the place in an ominous presence.","\"W-What is this...?\" The disciples’ eyes widened as killing intent poured from Yuan’s body, swelling with each passing moment until it rivaled Sect Leader Zu’s killing intent.","But Yuan’s killing intent did not stop—it surged higher and higher until it pierced the black sky. His eyes bled crimson, and behind him unfurled a pair of ominous wings, seemingly wrought from blood itself.","\"This is...\"","Sect Leader Zu swallowed hard, his eyes wide with disbelief and horror. Yuan’s killing intent didn’t just eclipse his own. It devoured it, swallowing his aura whole.","Despite the countless lives he had taken over tens of millions of years, Sect Leader Zu could not even begin to fathom how many Yuan must have slain to cultivate such unfathomable killing intent.","Meanwhile, not far from their location and hidden within its own dimension, a handsome middle-aged man with sharp features suddenly opened his eyes, revealing irises of deep violet.","\"This killing intent...\" he murmured, a flicker of nostalgia stirring within him."]},{"number":2205,"title":"Chapter 2205: Fighting Sect Leader Zu","paragraphs":["\"This killing intent... it feels familiar...\" the middle-aged man murmured as he rose to his feet, stepping onto the surface of a small, tranquil pond where he had been seated in meditation.","After a moment of silence, he spoke in a slightly loud and clear voice, \"Xiao Meilin.\"","In the next moment, a tall and beautiful woman with facial features similar to Xiao Hua but much more mature appeared before him like a ghost.","\"Is this about the killing intent?\" she asked.","He nodded, \"Investigate it.\"","\"Could it be... him?\"","The man turned to look at a certain object in the distance and responded after a moment of pause, \"It’s a little earlier than anticipated, but it’s possible.\"","A broad and somewhat sadistic smile appeared on Xiao Meilin’s face.","\"I’ll be back,\" she said before vanishing like smoke.","She disappeared the next instant.","Back at the Inferno Alchemist’s headquarters, once Yuan’s killing intent stopped increasing, he created a sword using it.","\"Do you dare to ’experience’ my killing intent?\" Yuan asked in a provocative tone as he glared at Sect Leader Zu.","\"That’s...!\"","Sect Leader Zu hesitated.","Meanwhile, his disciples were all shaking uncontrollably just from being in the presence of Yuan’s killing intent.","\"What’s with the hesitation? Don’t tell me... you’re afraid?\" Yuan laughed, his voice dripping with mockery.","\"DO NOT UNDERESTIMATE ME!\" Sect Leader Zu roared, taking Yuan’s obvious bait as he flung his arms wide in a defiant, inviting gesture.","Without a word, Yuan flicked his sleeve, launching the sword of killing intent straight into Sect Leader Zu’s chest.","\"Sect Leader!\" his disciples cried in alarm, their confidence in his strength wavering as worry clouded their eyes.","In the next instant, Sect Leader Zu’s pupils blew wide, his eyes darkening until nearly black. He threw his head back and screamed in agony.","\"AHHHHH!!!\"","An unfathomable surge of killing intent flooded into him, dragging his mind into a torrent of unending nightmares.","\"S-Sect Leader!\"","\"You bastard! What did you do to our Sect Leader?! There’s no way that was just your killing intent!\"","\"He must have used some sort of technique!\"","However, Yuan ignored them and continued watching Sect Leader Zu writhe in pain.","A minute later, blood trickled from Sect Leader Zu’s eyes. Moments after, it seeped from his ears, nose, and even his pores—until, in the blink of an eye, his entire body was drenched in crimson.","\"K-Kill him!\"","One of the elders suddenly pointed at Yuan and roared.","Though fear gnawed at them, hundreds of disciples hurled themselves at Yuan, their own killing intent blazing. Yuan said nothing, and he simply awakened the True Dragon within and advanced to meet them head-on.","While Sect Leader Zu battled Yuan’s killing intent in the depths of his mind, his disciples clashed with Yuan in reality.","One minute... three minutes... ten minutes.","It took Sect Leader Zu thirteen grueling minutes, but at last he broke free from Yuan’s killing intent. Yet the reality that awaited him was not much better than the nightmares. Not only the ground, but even Yuan’s guest house was drenched in blood, its walls adorned with severed limbs and spilled entrails.","In the time it took Sect Leader Zu to break out of Yuan’s killing intent, Yuan had slaughtered half of his disciples.","\"What... What is this...?\" he muttered with a look of disbelief.","Yuan shrugged, \"Don’t look at me. They attacked me first.\"","\"Y-You bastard!!!\"","Once Sect Leader Zu snapped out of his daze and understood the situation more clearly, his body erupted with killing intent and spiritual energy.","\"I’ll skin you alive!\" Sect Leader Zu lunged at Yuan while wielding a Mythic-grade spear.","Yuan produced Number One Under Heaven and enhanced himself with Chaotic Essence to confront the Sect Leader.","\"A Soul Weapon?!\"","Sect Leader Zu almost couldn’t believe his eyes when he saw Yuan’s weapon, as there was no Soul Weapon in the Primordial Realm—at least until today. In fact, Mythic-grade was the highest quality of treasure that could be found within the Primordial Realm.","Sect Leader Zu was not only injured and drained from resisting Yuan’s killing intent, but his weapon was also far inferior. His sole advantage lay in his cultivation at the seventh level of God Ascension—and if not for that, he would have already fallen to Yuan within a hundred exchanges.","\"There’s no way...\"","The watching disciples were struck speechless, their faces etched with disbelief. None of them could comprehend how their Sect Leader struggled against Yuan, a mere True Immortal that he should have been able to crush with a flick of his finger.","The elders eventually snapped out of their daze and shouted, \"We need to help the Sect Leader!\"","Without hesitation, they joined the battle against Yuan.","\"By the heavens, what am I watching right now?\"","The alchemists watching from afar were utterly bewildered. Yuan’s overwhelming prowess, effortlessly suppressing the Chaotic Sect alone, stirred memories of the Asura Clan.","\"Don’t tell me he actually has connections to the Asura Clan...\"","Leader Yang swallowed nervously and couldn’t help but feel relieved that they didn’t act too hastily and kill—try to kill Yuan. Not only would they have been slaughtered, but they would’ve also offended the Asura Clan.","\"Hm? This feeling...\"","Leader Yang’s brows shot up, and he quickly turned away from the battle before him as he sensed a familiar presence suddenly approaching their direction at the speed of light.","Before Leader Yang could even gather his thoughts, the owner of the presence appeared before the alchemists like a ghost, startling them.","However, when they saw and recognized this person’s beautiful face, they became even more terrified.","\"Y-Y-You are! Crimson Empress!\"","\"We greet the Crimson Empress!\"","Leader Yang and the alchemists instinctively bowed. Yet the woman gave them no notice, as though they didn’t exist, and her gaze fixed solely on the two figures locked in battle nearby—or more specifically—the handsome man wielding a greatsword.","\"Ahh...\" The Crimson Empress suddenly released a euphoric moan.","\"At last, you’ve returned...\""]},{"number":2206,"title":"Chapter 2206: The Crimson Empress’ Appearance","paragraphs":["\"Do you recognize that man?\" Leader Yang asked Xiao Meilin after hearing her mumbling.","However, she didn’t respond.","\"Senior Crimson Emper—?\"","Without turning to look at him, Xiao Meilin’s attention remained fixated on Yuan as she spoke in a chilling tone, \"You’re disturbing a significant and special moment for me. If I hear another peep out of your mouth without my permission, I’ll kill you.\"","Though she exuded no killing intent, Xiao Meilin’s words terrified Leader Yang and the other alchemists more than Yuan’s killing intent, and they no longer dared to open their mouths, even going as far as to halt their breathing just in case that annoyed her.","Meanwhile, Yuan continued to fight Sect Leader Zu. Although the other disciples tried to help, the clash between the two of them was so intense that they couldn’t even get close.","As the battle dragged on, Sect Leader Zu’s confidence gave way to unease. Initially, he was unconcerned about failing to overpower Yuan outright, given that his seventh-level God Ascension cultivation guaranteed significantly greater spiritual energy reserves. Sooner or later, Yuan should have been exhausted. Yet the expected weakness never came. Instead, with every clash, Yuan seemed only to grow stronger.","’No! He’s not getting stronger! I am the one getting weaker!’ Sect Leader Zu cried inwardly.","’How?! How the fuck does an Immortal have this much spiritual energy?! Or does he have a way to replenish his spiritual energy—’","\"Bastard! You must be secretly recovering your spiritual energy with spirit stones! How many do you actually possess?!\" Sect Leader Zu roared, misunderstanding the situation.","Since he couldn’t sense Chaotic Essence, there was no way for him to realize that Yuan was recovering his spiritual energy with it.","\"Spirit Stones?\" A smile appeared on Yuan’s face as he spoke, \"Even if I were using them, so what?\"","Sect Leader Zu gritted his teeth and suddenly stopped attacking.","\"Wait! Let’s talk about this!\"","\"What?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Think about it. Even if you’re using spirit stones to recover, you can’t have many left. Keep this up, and you’ll inevitably run out of spirit stones and still die by my hands. So why waste them? If you agree to apologize and hand over every last stone, I’ll spare your life and pretend as if none of this ever happened,\" Sect Leader Zu said with a confident smile.","Yuan fell silent for a moment before bursting out with laughter.","\"Run out of spirit stones? Why don’t you see for yourself whether I’ll run out or not!\" Yuan snapped open his spatial ring, releasing a flood of spirit stones that swiftly piled into a glittering mountain before him.","The jaws of Sect Leader Zu and the others dropped at the absurd, almost obscene sight. There were thousands—millions of spirit stones, enough to make everyone in the Primordial Realm a cultivator.","\"Impossible! Why does he have so many spirit stones?!\"","\"They must be fake! There’s no way he has so much!\"","Suddenly, Sect Leader Zu clenched his fists and muttered, \"You... there’s been a rumor of someone from the outside world entering the Primordial Realm going around recently. I didn’t believe it at first, but now... You must be that person!\"","\"What?! He came from the outside world?! Does that mean the Primordial Realm is open again?!\"","The disciples couldn’t believe their ears, their eyes glued to the spirit stones.","However, Yuan quickly stored the spirit stones back inside his spatial ring the next moment.","\"Now then, let’s see who falls first: you, or I when I run out of spirit stones,\" Yuan said, his glare sharp as a blade.","Sect Leader Zu trembled at the challenge.","\"I—!\"","But just as Sect Leader Zu opened his mouth to respond, a surge of killing intent exploded nearby, crashing over the battlefield like a tidal wave.","Before Sect Leader Zu could even turn his head to face the source of the killing intent, it appeared behind him like a ghost and—","Pop!","Sect Leader Zu’s head suddenly exploded like a juicy watermelon.","\"?!\" Yuan’s eyes widened at this sudden development.","\"Y-You are—! Crimson Empress?! What is the meaning of this?!\" Sect Leader Zu, whose head was crushed but still survived as a soul, exclaimed in shock after seeing the identity of his attacker.","\"Why? Because you ruined such a precious moment for me,\" she responded in a nonchalant tone.","\"What?! What nonsense are you—\" Sect Leader Zu’s words died in his throat as he felt her cold glare fall upon him. In that instant, he was sure that if he dared to continue, she would shatter his soul.","\"Crimson Empress...\" Yuan muttered as he admired her beautiful and familiar appearance, recalling when Xiao Hua disguised herself as her in the past.","Xiao Meilin stopped paying attention to Sect Leader Zu without a second thought, turning instead to meet Yuan’s gaze with eyes burning with passion.","Yuan opened his mouth to speak, but before he could utter a word, Xiao Meilin suddenly charged forward and launched an attack on him.","\"?!?!\"","Her unexpected action left Leader Yang and Sect Leader Zu speechless.","’She wasn’t on his side?!’ they cried inwardly.","\"Since that bastard ruined it, allow me to continue it,\" Xiao Meilin muttered in a low voice as she retrieved a Mythic-grade sword and swung it at Yuan.","\"What are you doing?\" Yuan asked with a calm expression on his face as he blocked her attack.","Despite being attacked, there was no killing intent coming from Xiao Meilin, so he wasn’t worried that she was trying to kill him.","\"Please excuse my behavior, Master Tian. However, I just cannot contain it any longer—\"","A crushing pressure swept through the area as Xiao Meilin’s body erupted with the aura of a ninth-level God Ascension cultivator, intertwined with a surge of intense Supreme Sword Aura.","\"My love and lust for you, that is!\" she shouted as she continued her assault.","Although Xiao Meilin did not seem to have any desire to kill him, Yuan didn’t dare to underestimate her and instantly used Eternal Essence."]},{"number":2207,"title":"Chapter 2207: The Crimson Empress’ Appearance(2)","paragraphs":["\"You have no idea how long I have waited for this moment, Master Tian!\" Xiao Meilin laughed chaotically as she swung her sword mercilessly, despite the difference in their cultivation.","\"You’re really enjoying yourself, aren’t you?\" Yuan remarked with a stiff smile on his face.","For some reason, he didn’t feel the need to tell her to stop attacking him, almost as if he knew that it would be pointless and that the only way for her to stop was to satisfy her.","Meanwhile, Leader Yang and the others were left speechless by the unexpected situation.","\"Why are they fighting? I thought they were friends?\"","\"You idiot, look at the Crimson Empress’ face! I have never seen her smile before, yet she’s smiling from ear to ear right now!\"","\"Y-You’re right! Good lord, who is that man?!\"","The men there couldn’t help but feel smitten by Xiao Meilin at this moment, even though they were terrified of her just moments ago, and it was caused by a single smile.","As for Yuan, he was barely just strong enough to fight Xiao Meilin without being completely overpowered.","Xiao Meilin was at the ninth level of God Ascension, essentially the peak of the cultivation world. Moreover, unlike the other cultivators, she possessed an abundance of spiritual energy in her Dantian, allowing her to fight without restraint.","Of course, she wasn’t using Celestial Qi, or Yuan wouldn’t stand a chance even with Eternal Essence.","A minute... ten minutes... an hour passed in the blink of an eye.","As Yuan continued fighting Xiao Meilin, his memories of the Asura Clan started to resurface, such as their first encounter, how they started as enemies but ended as allies, and his relationship with Xiao Meilin and the other members.","Noticing a profound flicker in Yuan’s eyes, Xiao Meilin remarked, \"You dare think about other things while clashing swords with me? That arrogance—you haven’t changed one bit since we last met during the Primordial Era!\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"I can say the same to you. Don’t tell me you’ve spent your time in this place cultivating?\"","\"Isn’t that obvious? There’s nothing else to do in this shithole besides cultivating.\"","\"You were only at the second level of God Ascension the last time I saw you. To reach the ninth level while stuck in this place... very impressive.\"","Xiao Meilin chuckled as she swung her sword, \"You, on the other hand, have gotten a lot weaker.\"","\"Are you disappointed?\"","\"...\"","After several exchanges in silence, Xiao Meilin responded with a sadistic grin on her beautiful face, \"Seeing you weaker than me... it’s actually very exciting.\"","Xiao Meilin’s expression sent chills down Yuan’s spine.","\"It won’t stay like this for long,\" he quickly said.","\"Then I should take advantage of this moment while I still can,\" she said while licking her lips.","The next moment, Xiao Meilin’s prowess skyrocketed, and she started pushing back Yuan with seemingly no effort.","Even when using nearly every trick he had, Yuan still found himself completely overwhelmed by Xiao Meilin’s prowess.","’Not only is she not using her Celestial Qi, but even her weapon is lacking! Yet, she’s overpowering me to such an extent!’ Yuan couldn’t help but smile despite the situation.","If Xiao Meilin were released to the outside world and upgraded her weapon, who knows how much more of a monster she would become?","After being tossed around by Xiao Meilin for several more hours, Yuan finally said, \"Alright, how much longer do you intend to mess around? I need to speak to your father. It’s about Xiao Hua.\"","Xiao Meilin stopped her movements and lowered her sword.","\"My junior sister? Now that you mentioned her, where is she? Did you not come here with her?\" she said as she looked around.","\"She’s currently in my Dantian, but she cannot come out due to reasons.\"","Xiao Meilin narrowed her eyes slightly and mumbled, \"Could it be... did it already start?\"","\"What do you mean?\" Yuan asked after hearing this.","Xiao Meilin shook her head and said, \"I’ll let father explain it to you instead. I’ll take you to him now.\"","\"Alright.\" Yuan nodded as he stowed away his weapon.","\"Ah, right. Before we leave...\" Xiao Meilin’s expression suddenly hardened as her cold gaze swept over Sect Leader Zu and the others. \"What should we do with them? Want me to kill them all?\"","Despite Xiao Meilin not paying attention to them, none of them dared to leave the scene. After all, even if they snuck away, they would never be able to truly escape.","\"Have mercy!\" Sect Leader Zu, who was still in his soul form, pleaded.","However, Yuan remained indifferent as he commanded, \"Kill them all.\"","\"As you wish.\"","Immense killing intent erupted from Xiao Meilin the next instant, her body shrouded in a crimson aura that bled into the air, saturating the atmosphere with malice.","As Xiao Meilin raised her sword, every member of the Chaotic Sect instinctively turned to flee. But before they could escape, she brought her blade down in a single, fluid motion. In the blink of an eye, the air split—and so did they, their bodies torn apart into countless pieces all at once.","’Power of the Void!’ To Yuan’s astonishment, Xiao Meilin was wielding the Power of the Void, an ability so rare that few cultivators could even comprehend it, let alone command it to such a degree, and although slightly, her understanding surpassed even his.","\"What do you think?\" Xiao Meilin asked, turning to Yuan with a faint flicker in her eyes, as though expecting his praise after annihilating the Chaotic Sect.","\"Where’d you learn to wield the Power of the Void?\" he asked.","\"I comprehended it through studying Spiritual Rifts,\" she calmly responded.","\"Seriously? How long did that take?\"","\"Longer than it took me to reach the ninth level of God Ascension.\"","\"I see...\"","\"Ready to leave?\" Xiao Meilin then asked.","\"Yes—Actually, hold on.\"","Yuan nearly forgot about Mu Xuelian and went to fetch her.","\"Who’s that?\" Xiao Meilin asked, her eyes narrowing in suspicion as they fell upon Mu Xuelian."]},{"number":2208,"title":"Chapter 2208: Meeting the Asura Clan","paragraphs":["\"This is a friend of mine, Mu Xuelian,\" Yuan casually introduced her.","\"Hmm...\" Xiao Meilin suddenly vanished into thin air before appearing before Mu Xuelian like a ghost.","\"Can I help you?\" Mu Xuelian calmly asked.","Xiao Meilin narrowed her eyes slightly and responded, \"There’s something about you that I don’t like... What are you hiding?\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow at Xiao Meilin’s words and wondered if she could sense Shiva, who was hiding within Mu Xuelian’s body. If so, that would be pretty impressive.","Sure enough, Xiao Meilin could sense something mysterious lurking within Mu Xuelian, something that made even a powerhouse like her instinctively tread with caution.","\"I don’t know what you’re talking about,\" Mu Xuelian shook her head.","\"Whatever. Just don’t cause any trouble.\"","Xiao Meilin vanished into thin air again. This time, she reappeared right beside Yuan.","\"Let’s go, shall we?\" Xiao Meilin said as she grabbed his arm and pulled him forward, speeding into the distance.","Sometime later, they arrived at the Burning Tree—a colossal black tree wreathed in purple flames. Beside it lay a vast, dried-up lake, its cracked surface reflecting the eerie glow of the fire.","Yuan gazed at the tree, his eyes narrowing slightly. Though its flames burned with fierce intensity, the heat was far weaker than he’d anticipated, and there was something inherently unusual about their nature.","\"What kind of fire is that?\" Yuan asked, unable to discern its nature.","Xiao Meilin shrugged. \"Who knows? That tree was once just an ordinary one. But after being struck by countless bolts of lightning, it caught fire, and the flames have never gone out. It’s been burning for tens of millions of years now.\"","’I believe it’s a type of alchemy flame,’ Feng Yuxiang remarked within Yuan’s Dantian.","’Alchemy flames, huh? Is there a way for me to collect it?’ he asked.","’Yes, there is. Inside my spatial ring, you’ll find the Phoenix Sealing Jar. It’s a treasure that is specifically used to collect flames.’","Yuan ignored the ominous name and searched Feng Yuxiang’s spatial ring for the item. A moment later, he used it to collect the purple flames.","Xiao Meling watched his actions without uttering a word, almost as if it was none of her concern.","Only when Yuan finished with his business did Xiao Meilin speak, \"Done?\"","\"Yes.\"","Without another word, she swept her arm through the air, rending space itself open and revealing a pitch-black gateway to the void before entering it.","Yuan and Mu Xuelian silently followed her.","Moments after stepping into the void, a flash of blinding light engulfed Yuan. When his vision cleared, he found himself beneath a radiant sun suspended in a clear blue sky—a striking contrast to the apocalyptic gloom of the Primordial Realm he had just left behind.","Not only that, but spiritual energy was abundant around them, almost as if they’d returned to the Nine Heavens.","\"Did we leave the Primordial Realm?\" Mu Xuelian questioned as she looked around with a puzzled face.","\"No, we’re still inside the Primordial Realm,\" Xiao Meilin said.","\"But the spiritual energy here...\"","\"It’s from the Spirit Tree.\"","\"What is the Spirit Tree, anyway?\" Yuan suddenly asked.","\"You’ll find out soon enough,\" Xiao Meilin replied with a mysterious smile.","\"Now, let’s meet the old man.\"","Not far ahead stood a vast estate, its ancient architecture reminiscent of the grandeur of the Primordial Era.","Even without using his divine sense, Yuan could sense many powerful presences coming from it.","When they reached the entrance, they were greeted by a handsome young man who looked to be in his early twenties.","\"Let me introduce you to Xiao Chen, the youngest in our family. He’s my little brother.\"","\"Hm?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow at this information and remarked, \"But I don’t recall such an individual in the Asura Clan.\"","\"That’s because he was born after we entered the Primordial Realm,\" Xiao Meilin explained.","\"Born? Your father hooked up with someone in this place?\" Yuan wore a dumbfounded look on his face at this revelation.","\"Something like that.\"","\"Does that mean you have a new mother right now?\"","Xiao Meilin silently nodded.","\"...\"","A strange sensation suddenly rippled through Yuan, stirring a buried memory of Xiao Meilin’s first mother and his bitter connection with her.","\"You must be Master Tian. It’s an honor to finally meet you after all these years,\" said Xiao Chen, snapping Yuan out of his thoughts.","Yuan looked at him and said, \"You don’t have to address me as Master Tian since I never taught you. Just call me Yuan.\"","\"Meilin, you too. Tian Xian is long dead. I am now Yuan,\" he continued while staring her in the eye.","\"Is that an order?\" she asked with a perplexed look in her gaze.","\"No, it’s not.\"","\"Then I will continue to call you Master Tian since it’s what I am used to,\" she calmly responded.","\"If that’s what makes you more comfortable,\" Yuan said with a defeated smile.","\"Anyway, you can get to know more about Xiao Chen later. The old man is waiting for you.\"","Yuan nodded, and they stepped into the residence. Yet instead of stopping inside, they continued straight through the estate and into the line of trees beyond.","A few minutes later, they reached a tranquil lake, where a handsome middle-aged man with a naturally sharp and stern countenance sat cross-legged upon the water’s surface, silently cultivating.","\"Go ahead,\" Xiao Meilin said to Yuan.","Yuan silently approached the lake the next moment.","When Yuan reached the edge of the lake, the handsome man slowly opened his eyes and spoke in a soft tone, \"Forgive me, but I cannot move from this spot right now, much less give you a proper greeting.\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes and asked, \"Is there something wrong?\"","\"I must remain focused right now, so I’ll explain everything to you in a bit.\"","\"Take your time,\" Yuan said before sitting down on the soft grass.","\"Thank you, my lord.\" The middle-aged man closed his eyes again and fell silent."]},{"number":2209,"title":"Chapter 2209: Meeting the Asura Clan(2)","paragraphs":["While Yuan waited for the Patriarch of the Asura Clan to finish with his business, he recalled Tian Xian’s past with them.","After avenging Xiu Mei’s death, Tian Xian did not stop his rampage. Since the Celestial Emperor was the true reason behind Xiu Mei’s assassination, he swore that he would not stop until he killed the Celestial Emperor.","Aware of Tian Xian’s desire for his life, the Celestial Emperor had no choice but to dispatch the Asura Clan—his strongest allies at the time—to confront him.","Before the Asura Clan betrayed the Celestial Emperor and joined Tian Xian’s side, they were the most powerful family in the Divine Heavens with influence that surpassed even the Celestial Family.","However, as powerful as they were, they still obeyed the Celestial Emperor. While most people swore their loyalty to the Celestial Emperor out of fear or desire, the Asura Clan assisted the Celestial Emperor mostly because their ancestor, their first Patriarch, Xiao Xin, was a close friend of the Celestial Emperor.","At the Celestial Emperor’s orders, the Asura Clan sent elite warriors to deal with Tian Xian, but alas, not even they were able to stop Tian Xian. If anything, it ignited his fury and onslaught even further.","When even their most seasoned warriors failed to halt Tian Xian’s rampage, Xiao Xin commanded his son, Xiao Cangming, and his daughter-in-law, Fei Zhen’er, to confront him.","Xiao Cangming and Fei Zhen’er were the most powerful in the Asura Clan, only slightly weaker than Xiao Xin himself individually. Together, not only were they stronger than Xiao Xin, but they would even be able to give the Celestial Emperor a fair fight.","With such a powerful combo going after Tian Xian, everyone figured that it was only a matter of time before Tian Xian took his last breath.","Yet, after Xiao Cangming and Fei Zhen’er finally clashed with Tian Xian, the outcome sent ripples of shock throughout the entire cultivation world.","Not only did they fail to defeat Tian Xian, but the battle also claimed the life of Fei Zhen’er. Her death struck Xiao Cangming especially hard, as he had opposed his father’s decision to aid the Celestial Emperor from the start, and he had never wanted Fei Zhen’er to be involved.","Many expected Xiao Cangming to pursue Tian Xian—the murderer of his wife—just as Tian Xian had once hunted Supreme General Mo for slaying Xiu Mei. Yet, to everyone’s shock, Xiao Cangming turned his fury and blade not toward Tian Xian, but toward his own father, Xiao Xin.","After killing his own father, Xiao Cangming turned his attention to the Celestial Emperor, who was baffled and enraged by this betrayal.","After a series of fateful encounters, Tian Xian and the Asura Clan eventually began working together. Naturally, their relationship was strained at first—after all, Tian Xian had slain Fei Zhen’er. Yet, as time passed and their cooperation deepened, the hostility between them slowly began to fade.","In time, Xiao Cangming came to forgive Tian Xian completely. However, Xiao Cangming had two daughters with Fei Zhen’er, and they still hated Tian Xian even after their father forgave him.","Although they, too, would eventually come to forgive Tian Xian, it would take much longer, especially the youngest daughter.","A few days after Yuan began delving into Tian Xian’s memories, Xiao Cangming—who had been calmly cultivating atop the lake—suddenly opened his eyes and unleashed a deafening roar that shook the entire world. Snapping out of his trance, Yuan quickly assessed the scene: Xiao Cangming, once serene, now writhed in agony, veins bulging across his face and body.","\"Meilin, is this normal?!\" Yuan turned to look at her for answers.","\"Yes, it’s normal,\" she calmly responded. \"He’ll be done in a few minutes.\"","Witnessing her calmness—even nonchalance, Yuan quickly calmed down, and he continued to analyze Xiao Cangming’s state.","As time passed, blood started bleeding from Xiao Cangming’s eyes, nose, and ears.","’He looks poisoned, but it cannot be something that simple... A curse, perhaps?’ Yuan tried figuring out Xiao Cangming’s condition but came up empty-handed.","A few minutes later, Xiao Cangming slowly calmed down, just as Xiao Meilin said.","After splashing his face with the cool water below, Xiao Cangming rose from the pond in a single motion, landing before Yuan with effortless grace.","\"Thank you for waiting, my lord. How long has it been since we last met?\"","\"I’m not sure, since I have yet to restore all of my memories,\" Yuan shrugged.","\"Is that so... Well, the last time you visited, you were called Tian Yi.\"","\"Tian Yi...? The Immortal Monarch?\" Yuan was surprised to learn that he’d visited the Asura Clan as the Immortal Monarch.","\"That was several eras ago—at least a hundred million years.\"","\"In that case, it’s definitely been a while. Anyway, let’s return to my residence first. We have a lot to talk about, after all.\"","\"Alright.\"","Yuan followed Xiao Cangming back to the Asura Clan’s residence.","As Yuan, Xiao Cangming, and Xiao Meilin entered the room, Xiao Chen escorted Mu Xuelian to the guest room to relax.","Once they were seated, Xiao Cangming looked at Yuan and asked, \"Where do we begin?\"","\"Why don’t we start with your condition? Are you poisoned? Cursed? Even though Xiao Meilin has managed to reach the peak of God Ascension, you, on the other hand...\" Yuan said.","Unlike Xiao Meilin, Xiao Cangming’s cultivation was only at the first level of God Ascension—far weaker than before he entered the Primordial Realm. Rather than advancing, his cultivation had actually regressed.","\"My condition is neither poison nor a curse. It’s something akin to an illness,\" said Xiao Cangming.","\"What?\" Yuan raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner. \"An illness? I don’t recall you ever being sick.\"","\"Well, it started after your last visit. More specifically, after I started growing the Spirit Tree,\" he explained.","\"The Spirit Tree? You grew it? I thought it was something that originated from the Primordial Realm.\"","Xiao Cangming shook his head and said, \"No, it was entrusted to me by Tian Yi—by you during your last visit.\"","\"What?!\" Yuan exclaimed at this revelation."]},{"number":2210,"title":"Chapter 2210: Meeting the Asura Clan(3)","paragraphs":["\"I told you to grow the Spirit Tree? Then...\"","Seeing Yuan’s reaction, Xiao Cangming could guess why he was worried and said, \"Indeed, I grew the Spirit Tree under your instruction. However, my illness did not originate from the Spirit Tree. That being said, it is related to my illness.\"","\"What?\" Yuan raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner.","Xiao Cangming continued to explain, \"Firstly, about my weakened cultivation. It has nothing to do with my illness. To grow the Spirit Tree, I had to feed it my cultivation. Naturally, my cultivation would decline afterward, so I would have to regain my cultivation and repeat the process. I had recently finished feeding the Spirit Tree my cultivation, hence why I am only at the first level of God Ascension.\"","Yuan swallowed nervously before asking, \"How many times did you feed the Spirit Tree?\"","Xiao Cangming fell silent for a moment before responding in a nonchalant tone, \"Ten times. I cultivated to the peak of God Ascension from the first level ten times, so this will be my eleventh time.\"","Yuan stared in shock at such a ridiculous answer. Although ten may seem like a small number, one must consider the time and effort it takes to reach the ninth level of God Ascension from the first level.","The vast majority of people cannot even do it once in their lifetime, much less ten. Even if one possesses the innate talent and ability to reach the peak of God Ascension, it’d take them millions of years to achieve it a single time.","Xiao Cangming continued, \"Normally, the process isn’t as painful as what you witnessed today, but that has become the routine after I was inflicted with the illness.\"","\"Inflicted? So someone gave you the illness?\"","\"Not someone. Something.\" Xiao Cangming sighed.","\"Not long after the Spirit Tree sprouted, something tried to devour it,\" Xiao Cangming said. \"It came without warning—like a lightning strike from a clear sky. I tried to stop it, and after years of fighting, I managed to keep the Spirit Tree from being devoured. However, I was inflicted with this illness during the fight.\"","\"What is this thing?\" Yuan asked with a deep frown on his face, wondering if it was caused by an Eternal.","Xiao Cangming shook his head and said, \"It had an ethereal form, so whatever attacked wasn’t its true body. However, even without its true body, it was more powerful than anything I’ve ever faced before.\"","\"How does this illness affect you?\" Yuan asked.","\"It attacks my Dantian from time to time,\" Xiao Cangming replied. \"When it does, I have to focus everything I have just to defend myself. In those moments, I can barely even move a finger.\"","\"Let me take a look,\" said Yuan.","Xiao Cangming nodded and silently extended his arm, allowing Yuan to analyze his body with spiritual energy.","Sure enough, Yuan sensed an ominous energy coiling around Xiao Cangming’s Dantian—like a sinister flame devouring it from within. However, it was currently suppressed by Xiao Cangming.","Yuan retrieved the Sacred Chalice of Purification and said, \"Feed it some of your blood. This treasure can remove pretty much any curse out there.\"","Xiao Cangming didn’t question Yuan and followed his instructions.","The chalice consumed Xiao Cangming’s blood, but it did not react, meaning that he wasn’t cursed.","\"Now that we’ve confirmed it’s not a curse, let me try to absorb it.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Cangming instantly retrieved his arm and said in a stern tone, \"Absorb it? What if it inflicts you, as well? Sorry, but I’ll have to refuse.\"","Yuan shook his head and said, \"I just want to see if it’s poison. Don’t worry, I have achieved True Poison Immunity in case it is.\"","\"It’s still too risky.\"","\"Cangming, have you forgotten who I am?\" Yuan said with a slight frown on his face. \"Or are you looking down on me?\"","\"No, that’s not it...\" Xiao Cangming hastily responded.","\"Then what is it? You have managed to survive this long with it, yet you don’t think I can handle it? Are you trying to say that you’re now above me?\"","Xiao Cangming opened his mouth only to close it shut without uttering a word. Then, after a moment of silence—","\"Alright, you win.\" Xiao Cangming sighed in a defeated manner as he extended his arm again.","Xiao Meilin kept a serious expression as she watched their exchange, though she was smiling inwardly. This somewhat obedient, vulnerable side of her father was something she only ever got to see when he faced Yuan.","Yuan tried to absorb the ominous energy within Xiao Cangming the next moment, but alas, his poison immunity did not react to it, either.","\"I guess it’s truly neither poison nor a curse...\" Yuan shook his head as he released Xiao Cangming’s arm.","\"But don’t worry, I’m sure we’ll figure it out.\"","\"While it would be great if I could get rid of this illness, it’s not like I cannot live without being cured. Though this illness was life-threatening at first, I have long since gotten used to it. Now, it’s just a mild annoyance, akin to a seasonal cold that comes and goes.\"","\"Even if you say that, we should definitely try to get rid of it. It might not threaten you now, but things can always change, especially when we know nothing about it.\"","Xiao Cangming nodded, then said, \"Now that you know my situation, let’s talk about you, my lord. What brought you to the Primordial Realm this early? The Spirit Tree hasn’t fully grown yet, you know? It’s about 95 percent there.\"","\"Early? Did we schedule my next arrival date last time?\" Yuan asked with raised eyebrows.","\"Not exactly, but you said that you’d return once the Spirit Tree is fully grown and ready to be harvested.\"","\"I see... well, the reason I rushed to the Primordial Realm is because of her—\"","Yuan proceeded to summon Xiao Hua from his Dantian. Of course, she was still slumbering.","\"Junior sister...\" Xiao Meilin mumbled when she saw Xiao Hua’s face.","Xiao Cangming remained silent, but his eyes were slightly squinted, as if assessing her condition."]},{"number":2211,"title":"Chapter 2211: The Solution to Xiao Hua’s Issue","paragraphs":["\"I understand the situation,\" Xiao Cangming muttered after a moment of silence. \"The balance between the two souls within her is broken, and they’re currently clashing with each other—trying to consume each other.\"","\"What?!\" Yuan exclaimed in shock after hearing the last few words in Xiao Cangming’s sentence.","\"Their souls are trying to consume each other?! This is the first time I’m hearing this! I was told they were only fighting for control of the body!\"","If he’d known it was this serious, he would’ve taken this matter much more seriously and visited the Primordial Realm much sooner.","\"Perhaps that might have been the case initially, but from what I am seeing right now, that is no longer the case.\"","Xiao Cangming looked at Yuan and asked, \"How much do you know about our Asura Clan’s powers?\"","Yuan closed his eyes to ponder, \"The Violent Nebula Physique, right? Come to think of it, I don’t actually know much about it, other than the fact that it makes you immune to physical attacks.\"","Xiao Cangming nodded and explained, \"That’s normal, since we didn’t tell you about it. Of course, it’s not like we were trying to hide it from you. Honestly, even we didn’t know much about our own physiques in the past. However, as we continued to study and experiment with it, we’ve grown to understand our physique much better now.\"","\"Anyway, our physiques’ true power lies in ’reincarnation’.\"","\"What...?\" Yuan’s eyes widened in shock.","\"Reincarnation,\" Xiao Cangming repeated calmly. \"But it comes with strict limitations and conditions that we still don’t fully understand, even now. And so far, only one member of our family has ever experienced it.\"","\"You mean Xiao Hua?\"","\"Yes, and she has experienced reincarnation more than once.\"","\"How does it work?\" Yuan asked.","\"Well, we call it reincarnation, but it technically isn’t true reincarnation,\" Xiao Cangming explained. \"She doesn’t return to the cycle to await rebirth like others do. Instead, she’s more like a phoenix—revived after death, her soul never truly departing.\"","\"Then how does she return?\"","\"After her death, her soul will wander the world until it finds a suitable vessel—usually before they are born. Once the conditions are fulfilled, she would take over that body, hence two souls in one body, and depending on the two souls’ compatibility, they will either exist in harmony or...\"","\"They fight for control,\" Yuan sighed.","\"But there’s something that I don’t understand,\" he then said. \"Xiao Hua’s soul should be incomparably stronger, so why does it seem like she’s struggling?\"","\"It’s not that she’s struggling. If she truly wanted to consume the other soul, it wouldn’t take any effort. However, doing so could cause irreparable harm to the body. Most importantly, since she is aware that it isn’t her true body, she’s trying her best to hold back.\"","\"So she’s actually trying to stop herself from consuming the other’s soul right now?\"","Xiao Cangming nodded. \"Yes. Unfortunately, her soul is so powerful that once the process begins, she must constantly suppress herself. If she falters even for a moment, the other soul will be devoured. As for the other soul... she’s subconsciously trying to fight back, even though it’s doing more harm than good.\"","\"How often does this happen? And is there a solution to it?\" Yuan then asked.","Xiao Cangming closed his eyes and sighed, \"This is the second time it’s happened, and she’s reincarnated over a dozen times. There are only two ways we can fix this. Either Xiao Hua’s soul consumes the other and takes permanent control of the body, or we remove Xiao Hua’s soul and place her into a different vessel.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan asked, \"What did you do the last time?\"","\"Xiao Hua consumed the other’s soul since that was the only option we realistically had.\"","\"Another question. Her personality... Who have I been talking to this entire time? Is it Xiao Hua, or the other soul? Or do they swap from time to time?\"","Xiao Hua’s personality had remained largely consistent throughout their time together—aside from the moment of her awakening. From that, Yuan deduced that only one soul had been in control until the awakening, likely the body’s original soul. Still, he needed confirmation.","\"For her new vessel to be compatible, the soul must closely resemble Xiao Hua’s—particularly in personality,\" Xiao Cangming explained. \"To maintain harmony, Xiao Hua must also share her memories with the vessel’s original soul. So even though two souls inhabit one body, they essentially become a single being. In simpler terms, her persona is a fusion of both. Even if the souls were separated, they wouldn’t differ much from each other.\"","Hearing this, Yuan finally understood why Xiao Hua could seem like an innocent little girl at times, yet mature and cruel at others.","\"That said,\" Xiao Cangming continued, \"this only holds true when the souls remain in harmony. The fact that they’re now in conflict means one of them has changed—so drastically that they’re no longer compatible.\"","\"So, what should we do, my lord?\"","Without hesitation, Yuan responded, \"Naturally, we’re going to separate them.\"","\"Then we will need to find another vessel for Xiao Hua.\"","\"Does it have to contain another soul?\" Yuan then asked.","\"That condition is only for when she reincarnates. Since we’re simply relocating her soul, a soulless vessel will work just fine.\"","Though it might sound complex or unnatural, the process was akin to that of a God Ascension cultivator whose physical body had been destroyed and required a new vessel.","\"Do you happen to have an empty vessel lying around—or enough materials to create one?\" Yuan asked.","Xiao Cangming shook his head.","\"Unfortunately, we’re still in the Primordial Realm, so things like creating a new vessel are simply unfeasible, as we need more than just spiritual energy.\"","\"Are you telling me that I have to leave the Primordial Realm to obtain a new vessel for her? Even if I can do that, I don’t think we’ll have enough time for that.\" Yuan rubbed his eyes in a stressful manner.","However, before Xiao Cangming could respond, Feng Yuxiang’s voice resounded, \"Young Master, if I may... we might already have enough resources to craft Xiao Hua a new vessel if we consider the treasures we already own—mostly mine.\""]},{"number":2212,"title":"Chapter 2212: The Solution to Xiao Hua’s Issue(2)","paragraphs":["’Is that true? We have enough resources to craft Xiao Hua a new vessel?’ Yuan asked for confirmation just in case he misheard.","’Honestly, it depends on how complicated you want the vessel to be, but for a temporary vessel, we should have enough,’ said Feng Yuxiang.","Like treasures, a vessel can be stronger or weaker depending on the resources used to create it.","’What about your Soul Weapon? The one that used to be occupied by Ji Ran,’ Yu Ning suddenly reminded Yuan about the Baneful Abyss. ’We could use it as a vessel until we craft her a proper one.’","Hearing Yu Ning’s words, Yuan asked Xiao Cangming, \"I have a Soul Weapon without any occupants right now. Can I put her soul inside until we finish her new vessel? I have used it to house the soul of a God Ascension cultivator before without any issue.\"","Xiao Cangming pondered for a moment before responding, \"We’ve never tried putting her soul in a Soul Weapon before, but we have tried to temporarily contain her soul in a treasure with a similar function before. The result? She subconsciously broke out of the treasure to find a new and more natural vessel, damaging her soul slightly in the process. Unlike normal people, Xiao Hua cannot maintain consciousness as a soul, and she will instinctively seek out a proper one, likely a side effect of her powers.\"","\"Anyway, to properly answer your question, it might work for some time, but it’s risky, and if you don’t find her a new vessel in time, she will try to break out of the Soul Weapon and hurt herself in the process.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan asked, \"How long does it take to craft a new vessel? I might have the resources with me.\"","\"I will have to see the resources first,\" he quickly replied.","\"Feng Feng. Show him the materials we have.\"","Feng Yuxiang emerged from his Dantian and immediately started looking through her spatial ring.","\"A phoenix, huh? The last time you came here, you also had a phoenix with you,\" Xiao Cangming remarked as he stared at Feng Yuxiang.","\"This is Feng Yuxiang. There are a few more resting within my Dantian right now.\"","Lan Yingying and Yingzi also came out the next moment, revealing themselves.","Xiao Cangming stared at Lan Yingying for a brief moment before turning to look at Yingzi.","\"It’s not exactly the same, but it’s similar,\" he mumbled a moment later.","\"Similar? To whom?\" Yuan asked out of curiosity.","Xiao Cangming responded as his gaze returned to Lan Yingying, \"She reminds me of that white-haired Divine Serpent. As for this one... what were they called again? They have the ability to manipulate shadows.\"","\"Shadow Dweller.\" Xiao Meilin answered for him.","\"Did I bring all of the Nine Divine Supremes with me the last time I visited?\" Yuan asked with a raised eyebrow.","Xiao Cangming nodded, \"Yes, and you claimed that you lot were on the way to confront Gods. How did that turn out?\"","\"How much do you know about the Outer Gods?\" Yuan then asked.","\"I am aware of their existence, but that’s about it. I don’t know anything about their purpose or prowess. You left without explaining much, if anything, after all.\"","\"Is that so... Well, about that fight...\"","Yuan explained everything that happened after their clash with the Outer Gods—how they split the Divine Heaven into nine different realms and Earth, as well as the existence of Cultivation Online.","Xiao Cangming listened with intrigue.","\"Nine Heavens and Cultivation Online, huh? The world sure has changed a lot since the Primordial Era, but I guess that’s only to be expected.\"","\"How long do you think it’s been since you were thrown into this world?\" Yuan smiled.","\"...\"","After a brief pause, he asked, \"Say... why did you decide to remain inside the Primordial Realm? I’m sure I could’ve taken your entire family out of this place the last time I visited. The fact you’re still here must mean that you decided to stay here instead, right?\"","Xiao Cangming nodded, \"That’s right. After all, I had something to do here.\"","\"You mean the Spirit Tree?\" Yuan asked. \"Does it have to grow in the Primordial Realm? Why can’t you cultivate it elsewhere?\"","\"Because such a thing can only grow in this kind of environment,\" Xiao Cangming calmly replied. \"A place utterly devoid of spiritual energy. Quite the paradox, isn’t it? The Spirit Tree generates spiritual energy—yet it cannot survive within it. It also needs spiritual energy to grow, but it must be force-fed by sacrificing one’s cultivation, like a hatchling unable to feed itself.\"","\"...I should’ve probably asked this earlier, but what even is the Spirit Tree? And why did I ask you to grow it?\" Yuan then questioned.","\"That...\" Xiao Cangming’s expression suddenly turned serious, making Yuan swallow nervously.","\"I don’t know.\" Xiao Cangming responded in a serious tone.","\"What?\" Yuan’s eyes widened with shock at his response.","\"My lord, if I may be blunt for a moment... you’re absolutely terrible at explaining things. In fact, most of the time you don’t explain anything at all and just give the bare minimum of instructions.\"","Xiao Cangming rubbed his eyes and continued, \"Do you know what you told me when you handed me the Spirit Tree?\"","\"Word for word, you said—nurture this to the best of your ability. I’ll return when it matures.\"","Xiao Meilin couldn’t help but chuckle at his words.","\"That being said, I am also at fault for not demanding more details.\"","\"That’s...\" Yuan was left speechless.","\"Maybe I’ll remember once I see the Spirit Tree for myself later,\" he said after a moment of silence.","Xiao Cangming let out a faint sigh.","\"Of course, the Spirit Tree isn’t the only reason I chose to remain here. After the war... I needed time to gather my thoughts—and to atone for my failures, both as a leader and as a husband.\"","\"...\"","Yuan wasn’t sure how to respond, so he remained silent.","Suddenly, Feng Yuxiang’s voice resounded.","\"Young Master, it’s done. I have gathered all of the resources that can be used to create a vessel.\"","\"We’ll continue this later,\" Yuan said to Xiao Cangming before turning toward the table, where more than a dozen treasures lay neatly arranged."]},{"number":2213,"title":"Chapter 2213: Li Zhenwu","paragraphs":["\"Well, what do you think?\" Feng Yuxiang asked as she showcased her treasures with a prideful air around her.","Xiao Cangmang took a moment to look over the treasures before responding with a surprised expression, \"I’ll be honest with you. I can’t identify even half of the treasures here, but judging from their intense aura, I’m sure they’re all priceless treasures—beyond anything I anticipated. If we have this quality of treasure, we can definitely make a top-grade vessel.\"","\"In that case, allow me to introduce them to you,\" Feng Yuxiang said as she began identifying the treasures and explaining their uses.","\"This right here is the Exalted Divine Crystal, a treasure used to store a massive amount of spiritual energy. It can be used to create the Dantian.\"","\"The item right next to it is the Nine-Flame Heart Pill, which can be used to create the heart. Not only will it give her vessel improved resistance to fire, but it will strengthen any fire-element techniques.\"","\"Next is the Primordial Essence Root, which will be used for her spiritual veins and give her superior cultivation speed.\"","Feng Yuxiang pointed at a bottle of red liquid and continued, \"This is phoenix blood—mine, to be precise. However, we will need more blood, preferably human blood from the same family.\"","\"I can give my blood,\" Xiao Meilin raised her hand.","Feng Yuxiang nodded and continued explaining the treasures, \"This is the Heavenly Marrow Essence. It’s usually used for crafting treasures, but it can also be used to forge bones.\"","\"These are the main ingredients for her vessel. The rest are mainly used to enhance their effects, but I will still explain them.\"","A few minutes later, Feng Yuxiang finished.","Not just Xiao Meilin, but even Xiao Cangming was left speechless by Feng Yuxiang’s resources.","\"Are you sure we can use such precious ingredients? Honestly, even I would want to move my soul into a vessel made with these ingredients,\" said Xiao Cangming.","Feng Yuxiang looked at Yuan and said, \"Originally, I planned on using them to strengthen the Young Master.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"Just your thoughts are enough. Moreover, at my current level, these treasures will have minimal effect, so it’s better to use them for Xiao Hua.\"","\"Feng Yuxiang, right? I—the Asura Clan will never forget this debt,\" Xiao Cangming said with his head slightly lowered.","Feng Yuxiang rubbed her nose and responded in a stiff tone, \"Honestly, I am only doing this for the Young Master, so you don’t owe me anything.\"","\"It doesn’t change the fact that you’re the reason Xiao Hua will have a new vessel.\"","\"So, is this enough to craft her vessel? If so, how long do you think it’ll take?\" Yuan asked a moment later.","Xiao Cangming nodded and replied, \"This is more than enough. In fact, we can make a vessel with only half of it. The rest is just a bonus. As for how long it will take... I haven’t attempted to craft a vessel since the Primordial Era, so it might take me a couple of weeks just to be safe. I don’t want to mess up these precious ingredients, after all.\"","\"Alright, I’ll leave it in your hands then.\"","Yuan placed Xiao Hua back inside his Dantian shortly after.","\"I’ll need a few days to prepare myself. Make yourself at home until then.\"","Xiao Cangming left to prepare a moment later.","Meanwhile, Xiao Meiling brought Yuan to Mu Xuelian, who was waiting in the guest room.","However, when they arrived, Mu Xuelian was not alone, and there was another beautiful woman in the room with her.","The two were quietly sharing tea, but the moment Yuan saw the woman’s face, his body went rigid, his eyes widening in utter shock and disbelief.","\"Fei Zhen’er...?\" Yuan muttered.","The beautiful woman greatly resembled Xiao Cangming’s dead wife—the one Tian Xian had personally killed in the past. The resemblance was so uncanny that he wouldn’t be surprised if this woman were actually Fei Zhen’er.","Seeing Yuan, the woman stood up and gracefully bowed to him, \"You must be Master Tian. I have heard a lot about you from my husband. I am Li Zhenwu, and it’s an honor to finally meet you.\"","Yuan turned to look at Xiao Meilin, who was standing right behind him and chuckling at his reaction.","\"I knew you’d be surprised when you see her. The resemblance is uncanny, right?\" she remarked.","Li Zhenwu smiled and said, \"I was told that I greatly resemble my husband’s late wife, but I never really took it to heart. However, seeing your reaction... I cannot help but wonder just how much I resemble her now.\"","Yuan swallowed nervously and replied, \"You’re a splitting image of her. If you claimed to be Fei Zhen’er, I wouldn’t have doubted you in the slightest.\"","\"If you don’t mind me asking, are you busy right now?\" Li Zhenwu suddenly asked.","\"Me? No, I am not busy.\"","Li Zhenwu clasped her hands together at his words and spoke with an excited smile, \"In that case, can you tell me some stories about my husband? This might sound weird, but he only ever talks about you, so it’s not an exaggeration to say that I know you better than my own husband.\"","\"I don’t mind... but wouldn’t it be better if you just asked him?\"","Li Zhenwu shook her head and sighed, \"I have tried, but the topic always ends up shifting to you.\"","\"Alright, I’ll tell you everything I know about Cangming.\" Yuan nodded.","\"Thank you! Let me grab some more tea first!\"","Once Li Zhenwu left the room, Xiao Meilin looked at Yuan and said with a smile, \"Try not to kill her this time, okay?\"","Yuan rubbed his eyes and sighed.","\"I know you’re joking, but...\"","Xiao Meilin chuckled for a bit before suddenly turning serious.","\"Master... she doesn’t know how my late mother died—how you killed her, so try not to mention that.\"","\"...Alright.\" Yuan nodded with a serious face."]},{"number":2214,"title":"Chapter 2214: Li Zhenwu(2)","paragraphs":["Once Li Zhenwu returned to the room with more tea leaves, Yuan began telling her stories of his adventures with Xiao Cangming.","Mu Xuelian stayed in the room to listen since she had nothing else better to do. Xiao Meilin also decided to stay for the nostalgia.","Meanwhile, Xiao Cangming began preparing to forge Xiao Hua’s new vessel, running countless simulations within his mind. Just as Tian Qiyuan could refine his crafting skills through mental training alone, true masters possessed the ability to temper their skills entirely within the realm of thought.","Naturally, this was no simple feat, and it placed immense strain on the mind and demanded extraordinary Soul and Mental Strength.","Three days passed in the blink of an eye, and Xiao Cangming emerged from his room with a confident look on his face. After doing hundreds of simulations within his head, he was now prepared to create Xiao Hua’s vessel for real.","\"Where’s the lord?\" Xiao Cangming asked Xiao Chen, who had been waiting outside for him to finish.","\"He’s currently with mother and senior sister,\" Xiao Chen calmly responded.","\"Bring me to him.\"","Xiao Chen nodded and, without a word, led Xiao Cangming to the guest room.","Even before they reached the room, Xiao Cangming could hear Li Zhenwu’s gentle laugh echoing in the halls.","When they arrived, Xiao Cangming walked through the already-opened door and said, \"I should’ve introduced you to my wife first before I went into seclusion. I apologize.\"","Yuan looked at him and casually dismissively waved his hand, \"It’s fine. I was just telling her about our adventures in the past.\"","\"After all, you never talk about yourself,\" Li Zhenwu said as she sipped on her tea.","\"I don’t?\" Xiao Cangming replied with raised eyebrows.","\"You would try, but you always end up talking more about Master Tian here.\"","Xiao Cangming opened his mouth but closed it when he realized she was right.","\"Anyway, I am ready to start crafting Xiao Hua’s new vessel. Do you want to watch, my lord?\"","Yuan nodded.","\"You’re making a new vessel for Xiao Hua? This is the first time I am hearing this,\" Li Zhenwu spoke with a surprised face.","\"I’ll explain on the way,\" said Xiao Meilin.","Sometime later, they all gathered in another room, one that was fortified with many powerful formations. The room also had a strong medicinal scent, and a cauldron sat in the middle of the room.","\"The alchemists mainly use this place for their alchemy,\" Xiao Cangming said. \"Also, we will need an alchemist for this, so...\"","Yuan followed Xiao Cangming’s gaze to Li Zhenwu and asked, \"You’re an alchemist?\"","She nodded, \"Yes. In fact, I was once the leader of the Inferno Alchemists. I handed that spot to the current leader after marrying into the Asura Clan.\"","\"Is that so...\" Yuan wondered if Li Zhenwu’s connection to the Inferno Alchemists was the true reason behind their collaboration with the Asura Clan.","Xiao Cangming retrieved the ingredients for Xiao Hua’s vessel and placed them beside the cauldron.","\"Here are the ingredients we will be using,\" Xiao Cangming said to her.","Li Zhenwu approached the ingredients with a look of shock on her face.","\"I don’t even recognize them,\" she responded in a stiff tone.","\"I’ll explain them to you now.\" Xiao Cangming said before repeating what Feng Yuxiang told him.","A few minutes later, Li Zhenwu sighed. \"You know, I would’ve appreciated a bit of warning about this—at least enough time to prepare. Although I have crafted vessels before, they’re all low-quality, made from trash ingredients.\"","\"This is like suddenly handing a craftsman who is only used to low-quality material the best materials in the world and telling them to create a masterpiece.\"","\"Sorry, but I forgot. It’s also been a while since I crafted a vessel, so I immediately went into seclusion. If you need some time to practice, we can wait for you. I will need a few days to prepare the ingredients, anyway.\"","\"Practice with what ingredients? Even if you give me a decade to practice with trash ingredients, it won’t help me with these priceless ingredients. Mental training won’t help either since I have never handled ingredients even close to the ones before me right now.\"","\"You’re the best alchemist in the Primordial Realm, so I’m sure you’ll be fine.\"","\"In here, perhaps. But I doubt I will be able to compare to even ordinary alchemists in the outside world.\"","\"Don’t sell yourself short now. Moreover, you’ll only be working as my assistant this time, as I will be doing most of the work. I just need you to assist me because my cultivation has declined back to the first level of God Ascension,\" said Xiao Cangming.","\"If I am only working as your assistant... guess that’s much more manageable,\" she nodded.","During their whole conversation, Li Zhenwu’s gaze never left the ingredients, almost as if she were mesmerized by them.","Suddenly, she turned to Yuan and asked, \"Are ingredients like these abundant in the world outside of the Primordial Realm?\"","\"No,\" Yuan calmly shook his head. \"Even in the Nine Heavens, such ingredients are considered a rarity—priceless, even.\"","\"And you’re willing to use them to craft a vessel for Xiao Hua? You’re very generous,\" she said with a warm smile.","Yuan shook his head.","\"There is no ingredient or material in this world that is more valuable than Xiao Hua.\"","\"Anyway, even though I’ll only be working as an assistant, I need to study these ingredients before we begin. Give me a few days,\" Li Zhenwu said.","\"Alright.\"","\"Master, since we still have some time, why don’t you spar with me? I’ve been itching to exchange swords with you for a while now.\"","Yuan responded with a stiff smile, \"Didn’t we spar with each other right before coming here?\"","\"That doesn’t count!\" she quickly said.","\"Why don’t you take him to the Spirit Tree instead?\" Xiao Cangming suddenly said.","\"Oh? That’s a good idea. Let’s see the Spirit Tree first. If we have time afterward, I’ll spar with you,\" said Yuan.","\"Fine. I’ll take you to the Spirit Tree.\" Xiao Meilin nodded."]},{"number":2215,"title":"Chapter 2215: Saaruk","paragraphs":["Sometime later, Xiao Meilin brought Yuan to the Spirit Tree, which was located only a few miles away from the Asura Clan’s residence.","Shortly after they left the residence, Mu Xuelian, who followed them, spoke, \"Yuan, Lord Shiva has something to tell you.\"","\"Hm? What is it?\" Yuan turned to look at her.","\"She said that man doesn’t have long to live.\"","\"What?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"That first-level God Ascension cultivator we were just with.\"","\"Cangming? What is her reason for saying such a thing?\" Yuan immediately stopped moving and glared at her with a serious frown.","Mu Xuelian closed her eyes and, after a moment of silence, responded in a different tone.","\"That man has been afflicted with a particular technique by a certain Eternal,\" said Shiva, who just took control of Mu Xuelian’s body.","\"You mean his illness? So an Eternal was involved, after all...\" Yuan sighed.","\"What are you talking about?\" Xiao Meilin asked.","Yuan explained calmly, \"The beings we know as Outer Gods refer to themselves as Eternals—and your father’s illness was caused by one of them.\"","\"And how does she know that?\" Xiao Meilin glared at Mu Xuelian with a suspicious face.","\"Long story short, there’s an Eternal living within her.\"","Xiao Meilin’s eyes narrowed at the revelation. \"I knew there was something off about her the moment I saw her,\" she muttered. \"Now I understand why.\"","\"Master, why are you traveling with someone like that? Aren’t you enemies with these Outer Gods?\"","He nodded, \"Yes, but there are many of them out there, and I am not at war with all of them.\"","\"Is that so? Well, this is news to me,\" said Xiao Meilin.","\"Anyway, what was that about father? He’s going to die soon? Can you elaborate on that? He’s managed to survive tens of millions of years with this illness, after all.\"","\"That’s because the technique used on him wasn’t meant to kill him quickly,\" Shiva said. \"It was designed to inflict pain for as long as possible. Tens of millions of years may seem long to mortals—but to us Eternals, it’s nothing. In fact, I have taken naps far longer than that.\"","\"Since you know what it is, do you know how to cure him?\" Yuan then asked.","Shiva calmly nodded, \"Of course. It’s actually very simple.\"","\"I’m listening.\"","\"You just need to absorb it.\"","\"What?\" Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Have you forgotten the essence of our powers already—the power of your physique?\"","\"You mean I can just refine the illness into essence and absorb it, turning it into my power?\" Yuan asked with a somewhat dumbfounded face.","Shiva silently nodded.","\"In that case, let’s return now,\" Yuan said to Xiao Meilin.","\"What about the Spirit Tree? We’re about to arrive.\"","\"That can wait. Your father will be crafting Xiao Hua’s vessel soon, and I don’t want anything to go wrong when that happens.\"","Yuan didn’t want to risk Xiao Cangming’s illness affecting him during the creation of Xiao Hua’s vessel and decided to take care of it as soon as possible. Moreover, Xiao Cangming’s life was on the line.","\"If you say so.\"","Xiao Meilin didn’t argue and immediately turned around.","Sometime later, they returned to the room where Xiao Cangming and Li Zhenwu were.","\"You’re back already? Did you forget something?\" Xiao Cangming asked.","\"No. I came back because I learned about the cause of your illness and the method to cure it,\" said Yuan.","\"What?\" Xiao Cangming stared at him with a bewildered face.","\"How did you acquire this knowledge in such a short time?\"","After all, they’d only been gone for a few minutes.","Yuan looked at Mu Xuelian and explained, \"Actually, there is an Outer God dwelling within my friend here, and she was the one who told me about it.\"","\"That’s...\"","Xiao Cangming was left speechless. As far as he was aware, all Outer Gods were enemies.","Seeing his reaction, Yuan quickly explained, \"Just like humans, not every Outer God is friendly with each other, and they even fight amongst themselves. In other words, not all of them are our enemies.\"","\"I see... So, what about my illness?\"","Mu Xuelian then spoke, \"According to Lord Shiva, it’s a technique used by the one known as ’Saaruk’, meant to torment you with unbearable pain.\"","\"Then what about the treatment?\"","\"I just need to absorb it,\" Yuan replied.","\"Didn’t you try that already?\"","\"That’s different, since I treated it like a poison. What I am going to do this time is entirely different.\"","\"It sounds risky. How risky is it?\" Xiao Cangming asked with a slight frown.","\"That’s... it shouldn’t be too risky, right?\" Yuan turned to look at Mu Xuelian.","\"Lord Shiva said it’s not risky, but it will be very painful for you, the absorber, since you’re essentially consuming the power of an Eternal.\"","\"You heard her. It’s not risky.\" Yuan said with a calm smile.","\"When do you plan on absorbing it?\" Xiao Cangming then asked.","\"Right now.\"","\"Right now? But we’re about to start crafting Xiao Hua’s vessel.\"","\"That’s exactly why we must do it now. I don’t want anything to go wrong, and since there’s a chance the illness might strike during the process, I want to deal with it before you start.\"","Xiao Cangming couldn’t refute his reasoning. Since it was true that the illness could surface at unpredictable intervals, Yuan’s concern was entirely justified.","\"Alright, let’s get this over with.\" Xiao Cangming nodded.","Hearing this, Yuan gestured for Xiao Cangming to take a seat before him.","Once Xiao Cangming was seated, Yuan took his place behind him and rested both hands against his back.","Yuan closed his eyes and started trying to sense the illness in Xiao Cangming’s body.","Li Zhenwu, who had been focused on the ingredients, paused and watched them in silence, a faint trace of worry flickering in her eyes.","A few minutes later, once Yuan found the source of the illness, he said, \"I am going to start now.\"","Then, he started to refine its very essence.","Shortly after Yuan started to absorb it, a loud and unfamiliar voice thundered inside his head.","\"Which bastard dares to covet this mighty Saaruk’s power?!\""]},{"number":2216,"title":"Chapter 2216: Saaruk’s Threat","paragraphs":["When Yuan heard this voice, he immediately delved into his mind, as this voice seemed more than just his imagination.","Within his consciousness, he sensed that a fragment of the Saaruk’s power had transformed into a kind of link, forging a connection between them. It functioned much like a communication jade slip, allowing their minds to intertwine and exchange words directly.","\"Hm? Wait a second... this presence... you’re not an Eternal!\" Saaruk’s voice returned before Yuan could respond to it.","\"A mortal! How dare a mere mortal attempt to covet the power of the mighty Saaruk!\" the voice roared, its fury intensifying as it realized its own strength was being refined by a human.","\"And what are you going to do about it?\" Yuan responded in a provocative tone.","\"This mighty Saaruk has memorized your scent! The moment you leave the safe zone, this mighty Saaruk will devour you!\"","\"Hahaha!\" Yuan burst into laughter. \"You, who was driven back by a mere mortal while trying to steal the Spirit Tree, think you can devour me? You Eternals truly have wild imaginations!\"","For a moment, the voice fell silent. When it returned, it dripped with malice. \"You are but an insignificant insect—one who cannot even begin to comprehend the magnitude of our power. Were it not for the Absolute Power’s interference, your pitiful existence would have long since been erased.\"","\"When this mighty Saaruk attempted to covet the Spirit Tree, this mighty Saaruk had only been using a single percent of their true power while severely underestimating their opponent. However, it will not happen a second time.\"","\"If you’re truly so powerful and mighty, then why do you need the Spirit Tree—something planted by the very mortals you so disdain?\" Yuan asked calmly.","\"This mighty Saaruk has no intention to entertain a mortal’s curiosity. Leave the safe zone if you dare... This mighty Saaruk will be waiting for you...\"","The voice gradually faded, and the link between them was abruptly severed. Though their exchange had lasted only a few brief sentences, several days had passed in the real world, and Yuan had refined half of Saaruk’s power from Xiao Cangming.","Once he returned to his senses, Yuan ramped up the speed he absorbed Saaruk’s power, and after a few more hours, he completely devoured it.","<Eternal Constitution(Incomplete) activated>","<Eternal Constitution(Incomplete) has refined Saaruk’s Essence>","<Through Saaruk’s Essence refinement, your understanding of Eternal Essence has improved drastically>","Yuan lifted his sweat-soaked palms from Xiao Cangming’s back and drew a deep breath. \"It’s done,\" he said softly.","Xiao Cangming stared at his hands in awe. \"The invisible weight that’s always pressed down on me is gone.\"","Ever since Saaruk’s power took hold, his body had always felt sluggish and burdened, but now, that sensation had completely disappeared.","He turned around to face Yuan, who was utterly drenched in sweat, and asked, \"Are you okay, my lord?\"","Yuan nodded, \"Despite my appearance, I am actually overflowing with energy.\"","He turned to look at Mu Xuelian and said, \"I spoke with Saaruk.\"","Shiva instantly took over Mu Xuelian’s body and responded, \"What did you talk about?\"","\"Nothing much. They only threatened to devour me the moment I leave the Nine Heavens.\"","Shiva laughed, \"I can’t say I’m surprised. You should prepare yourself.\"","Yuan raised an eyebrow and asked, \"What do you mean?\"","\"Even amongst the Eternals, Saaruk is considered very powerful—around the top 20.\"","\"You guys have a ranking? How many Eternals are out there?\"","\"Before I was sealed in the Nine Heavens, there were a total of 76 Eternals. Although more may have been born since then, it won’t be more than a handful.\"","\"76 Eternals, huh? Then where do you rank?\" Yuan asked.","\"Somewhere in the middle, I guess.\"","Yuan was surprised to hear this.","Shiva frowned at Yuan’s expression. \"How dare you look at me like that? Are you mocking me for my ranking? Yes, there’s a ranking among us, but the difference in prowess isn’t as vast as you think. Saaruk may rank above me, but that’s only because the order is based on the quantity of our Essence. In terms of strength, the gap isn’t that great. If we fought seriously, there’s no telling who will win.\"","\"You misunderstood. I wasn’t looking down on you.\" Yuan calmly shook his head but refused to elaborate further.","\"Anyway, I have a question,\" Yuan said. \"The Primordial Realm lies at the edge of the Nine Heavens, so it should still be within the safe zone. Yet Saaruk still managed to attack Cangming. I thought the Eternals weren’t allowed to intervene because of this Absolute Power?\"","\"The Absolute Power’s influence weakens the farther you are from its center,\" Shiva explained. \"So while we can’t touch the Nine Heavens, we’re still able to intervene through other methods. However, even then, it’s not easy and requires a lot of energy.\"","\"Is that why Saaruk hasn’t returned since he failed to covet the Spirit Tree?\" Yuan mumbled to himself.","After a moment of silence, Yuan asked Shiva, \"What are the chances of me defeating Saaruk right now?\"","Shiva sneered in disdain, \"With your current level of Eternal Essence, you won’t be able to touch him, let alone defeat him.\"","\"Is that so?\" Yuan didn’t inquire further.","Sometime later, Xiao Cangming said, \"Now that my illness is gone, I feel far more confident about our chances of success.\"","He looked at Li Zhenwu and asked, \"How are your preparations going?\"","\"I will be ready to begin tomorrow,\" she confidently replied.","While they continued to prepare, Yuan went to take a bath.","Time passed quickly, and after a full day of preparation, it was time to create Xiao Hua’s new vessel.","\"My lord, before we begin, there’s something I must warn you about,\" Xiao Cangming said to Yuan.","\"What is it?\"","\"Once we transfer Xiao Hua’s soul into her new vessel, it may take some time for her to adjust. During that period, her memories could regress, and it will take some time for them to return.\""]},{"number":2217,"title":"Chapter 2217: Xiao Hua’s New Vessel","paragraphs":["\"Her memories will regress? How far will it regress?\" Yuan asked after hearing this.","Xiao Cangming shook his head and said, \"It differs every time, so we won’t know until it happens.\"","\"I see. Then we can only deal with it when the time comes,\" Yuan said.","Moments later, Xiao Cangming and Li Zhenwu approached the cauldron and sat before it.","\"Ready?\" Xiao Cangming asked as he faced Li Zhenwu.","She took a deep breath before responding in a serious tone, \"I am ready.\"","Without another word, Li Zhenwu summoned her alchemy flames. Crimson fire blossomed around her, surging forward to envelop the cauldron until it was completely engulfed.","While Li Zhenwu tended to the cauldron, Xiao Cangming focused on preparing the ingredients. Once the cauldron reached the proper heat, he began adding them one by one. Yet not every material required the cauldron, as some demanded entirely different techniques and handling.","There were many methods to craft a vessel, but Xiao Cangming chose the most ancient one, as it was the only one that existed in the Primordial Era.","As the ingredients within the cauldron melded together, Xiao Cangming employed a special technique to shape the remaining materials. The result, however, resembled not a human form, but rather a crude doll.","\"The ingredients are ready,\" Li Zhenwu said a few hours later.","Without a word, Xiao Cangming opened up the cauldron and tossed the doll inside.","Once the doll entered the cauldron, Xiao Cangming began infusing the rest of the ingredients together.","Time flowed swiftly, and before they knew it, three days had passed since they began crafting Xiao Hua’s vessel.","\"It’s ready,\" Xiao Cangming said as he lifted the lid of the cauldron and carefully drew out the vessel. Yet it was far from complete, as the vessel bore no resemblance to a human form, but rather an enlarged pill of condensed flesh.","\"My lord, can you take out Xiao Hua?\"","Hearing this, Yuan immediately retrieved Xiao Hua from his Dantian.","\"Meilin.\" Xiao Cangming suddenly called for her.","Without a word, she walked over to Xiao Hua before placing her hand on her head.","\"I’m going to split her soul now. It will take a moment, and she will start squirming around. Restrain her movement as much as possible,\" Xiao Meilin said to Yuan.","\"Alright,\" he nodded.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Xiao Meilin shouted, \"Now!\"","The next instant, Xiao Hua jolted awake—and a piercing scream tore from her lips, as though she were being consumed by unbearable pain.","Yuan quickly restricted her movements.","\"AHHHH!\"","It was Yuan’s first time seeing Xiao Hua in such agony, and the sound of her screams made his chest tighten with a deep, aching pain.","Xiao Hua’s screaming did not stop for several minutes, but eventually, Xiao Meilin managed to separate her soul from the other.","After retrieving Xiao Hua’s soul, Xiao Meilin immediately gave it to Xiao Cangming, who forcefully shoved it into the pill of flesh.","Almost instantly, the fist-sized pill began to expand, swelling until it grew to the size of a watermelon within moments.","Moments later, limbs began to sprout from the pill, its shape twisting and expanding until it rapidly took on the form of a human body.","The form first took shape as that of a newborn, then swiftly matured into a young girl. As the growth ceased, her features began to refine, each detail becoming clearer, her face and form taking on a lifelike complexity.","In the span of a single minute, the pill had transformed into a beautiful young lady, her features resembling Xiao Hua’s, yet distinct enough to seem like a different person.","Lastly, her hair began to flow down her back—a lustrous pitch black, streaked with faint shades of violet that shimmered in the light.","\"How did it go?\" Yuan asked in a slightly nervous tone.","Xiao Cangming responded as he placed a piece of cloth over Xiao Hua’s naked body, \"It went well. Her soul has accepted its new vessel. Now, we just need to wait for her to wake up.\"","\"What about her?\" Yuan looked at the young girl resting in his arms.","Xiao Meilin pressed her hand against the young girl’s forehead to check her soul.","\"Her soul isn’t damaged, but it’s severely weakened. If you have any soul-strengthening medicine, feed it to her once she wakes up.\"","\"Alright.\"","Ding!","<Xiao Hua’s status has been updated!>","[Xiao Hua]","[Servant Grade: Celestial]","[Master: Yuan]","[Cultivation: First Level Spirit Apprentice]","[Legacy: Supreme Heaven’s Legacy + Evil God’s Legacy]","[Bloodline: Chaotic Asura Bloodline]","[Physique: Violet Nebula Physique]","’Huh?’ Yuan raised an eyebrow when he saw Xiao Hua’s updated status.","\"What’s wrong, my lord?\" Xiao Cangming asked after seeing his puzzled face.","\"Your bloodline... What is it called, again?\" Yuan asked.","\"The Chaotic Asura Bloodline.\" Xiao Cangming quickly replied.","\"Not Evil God’s True Bloodline?\" Yuan stared at him with a dumbfounded face.","\"No. We’re not related by blood, so how could we carry your bloodline?\"","\"Then...\" Yuan swallowed nervously as many questions appeared in his mind.","However, before he could even ponder them, another notification appeared.","Ding!","<??? Status has been updated!>","[???]","[Servant Grade: ???]","[Master: Yuan]","[Cultivation: Ninth Level Spirit Enlightenment]","[Legacy: Supreme Heaven’s Legacy]","[Bloodline: Evil God’s True Bloodline]","[Physique: ???]","\"?!?!\"","Yuan’s eyes widened with shock after seeing this second notification.","’Evil God’s True Bloodline? If Xiao Hua’s status has already been updated, then this status must belong to...’","Yuan stared at the young girl in his arms, his heart pounding rapidly.","\"Hey, Cangming, a quick question. Where did Xiao Hua find this girl? Who are her true parents?\"","Xiao Cangming pondered for a moment before responding, \"Normally, when Xiao Hua reincarnates, we follow her soul until she finds her next vessel. However, this time... she purposefully hid her reincarnation from us, so we didn’t realize she’d reincarnated until she returned home, already in her new vessel.\"","\"Additionally, we didn’t intend for her to participate in the Supreme Heaven’s Legacy, and it was entirely her own decision to leave the Primordial Realm to search for you,\" he revealed, leaving Yuan speechless."]},{"number":2218,"title":"Chapter 2218: Evil God’s True Bloodline","paragraphs":["\"So Xiao Hua becoming an exile wasn’t part of our plans...?\" Yuan mumbled after learning of this surprising information.","\"Why do you ask? Is there something wrong with that girl?\" Xiao Cangming asked.","Yuan looked at the slumbering girl and sighed, \"She has the Evil God’s True Bloodline.\"","\"What?! That’s impossible!\" Xiao Cangming immediately exclaimed in a voice of pure disbelief. \"Unless there is another Evil God out there that we don’t know about, that would imply she belongs to your family!\"","Even Xiao Meilin couldn’t help but stare at him with eyes as wide as saucers.","Yuan sighed. \"I’m just as confused as you are. At first, I thought the bloodline belonged to Xiao Hua, but now it’s clear that the original owner of this body is the one who possesses the bloodline.\"","\"It makes no sense,\" Xiao Cangming said. \"There’s no doubt this girl was born in the Primordial Realm. Unless you conceived a child during your last visit, there’s no way she could carry your bloodline. Unlike physiques, bloodlines must be inherited.\"","Yuan shook his head. \"Not always. Some bloodlines aren’t tied to one’s flesh, but to the soul itself. I’m living proof of that.\"","\"You are...?\" Xiao Cangming mumbled.","Despite never bearing a child as the Immortal Monarch, Yuan somehow managed to be born with the Immortal Monarch’s Bloodline, which meant that some bloodlines—if unique and powerful enough—could be bound to one’s soul and be passed down even after their death through reincarnation.","Yuan spoke softly, \"Before any being comes into existence, their soul must first take shape. In other words, the soul is born before all else, meaning even an unborn child would possess one.\"","\"Are you saying that this child is the reincarnation of your...?\" Xiao Cangming swallowed nervously at Yuan’s suspicion.","Yuan smiled and said, \"While this is just pure speculation, I cannot think of another reason why she possesses such a bloodline. Maybe there really is another ’Evil God’ out there, and she is their child.\"","Xiao Cangming shook his head. \"Do you know what it takes for a bloodline to be recognized by the heavens—the universe—and come into existence? Power and fate. Only those with immense strength and a destiny that shakes the world have their bloodline recognized. The greater one’s fate, the stronger their bloodline. If there was truly another Evil God who managed to create their own bloodline, there’s no way we wouldn’t have known.\"","The existence of bloodlines didn’t simply appear out of nowhere. When a being of immense power and destiny left a lasting impact on the world, that influence would be recognized by the heavens themselves, thus giving birth to a unique bloodline. Such bloodlines could then be passed down through generations, granting their descendants extraordinary abilities beyond those of ordinary lineages.","However, if one’s existence surpassed mortal comprehension—like that of the Immortal Monarch—their bloodline would transcend the limits of mere flesh and blood and instead bind itself to the soul.","\"To think such a thing was possible... This is news to me.\" Xiao Cangming muttered with a dumbfounded look on his face.","\"If this little girl truly turns out to be the reincarnation of your unborn daughter... what will you do then?\" Xiao Cangming asked quietly.","Yuan fell silent for a long moment before replying, \"How the hell am I supposed to know? Across all my reincarnations, I’ve only ever had one child—as Tian Xian—and she died before she was even born.\"","He paused, his voice softening. \"Besides, even if she truly is the reincarnation of my unborn daughter, she has new parents now. She’s no longer my daughter... No, in the first place, she can’t even be considered my daughter. After all, my daughter was never born.\"","Unlike Meixiu and Chu Liuxiang, who retained memories of their past lives, Yuan found it difficult to have any special attachments toward her, much less see her as his daughter. Since his own child had never been born, there had been no chance for a bond to form between them.","\"With that said, while she may not be my daughter, she is still family to me, something akin to a little sister.\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan spoke, \"Alright, let’s stop lingering around and put these two to rest properly.\"","While Xiao Meilin carried Xiao Hua, Yuan continued to carry the nameless young girl, bringing them to a room where they could rest on a bed.","Sometime later, Xiao Cangming appeared before him and asked, \"I know you returned early, but did you get to see the Spirit Tree?\"","\"No,\" Yuan calmly said.","\"Why don’t we go now? These two will probably remain asleep for a few days, so we have some time,\" Xiao Cangming suggested.","\"Sure,\" he nodded.","Thus, they set out for the Spirit Tree again with Xiao Cangming tagging along this time.","Meanwhile, Li Zhenwu stayed behind to watch over the slumbering girls.","Sometime later, they arrived at their destination.","\"This is the Spirit Tree...?\"","Yuan’s eyes widened in surprise at the sight of the Spirit Tree. It was nothing like what he’d imagined, and its appearance defied expectation to an almost absurd degree.","\"What were you expecting? A grand and massive tree?\" Xiao Meilin chuckled.","\"Honestly? Yes.\" He admitted.","Before Yuan stood the Spirit Tree—a laughably small ’tree’ that barely reached his knees in height. Though its size was laughably small and disappointing, the tree itself was breathtakingly beautiful, almost ethereal. Its trunk gleamed with a soft emerald light, and its leaves shimmered with a gentle, otherworldly radiance.","Beyond its appearance, the tree exuded an overwhelming surge of spiritual energy, so vast and pure that Yuan had never experienced anything like it before.","\"How can something so small generate so much spiritual energy?\" Mu Xuelian remarked with a bewildered look on her face. \"I am feeling bloated with spiritual energy just from being near it.\"","\"If you want to know its origins, you’ll have to ask my lord,\" said Xiao Cangming.","However, Yuan shook his head and sighed, \"Unfortunately, I don’t remember, and it’s not triggering any memories right now.\""]},{"number":2219,"title":"Chapter 2219: Spirit Tree","paragraphs":["\"By the way, you said the Spirit Tree hasn’t fully matured yet?\" Yuan suddenly recalled Xiao Cangming mentioning this earlier.","He nodded and confirmed, \"The Spirit Tree is still growing...\"","After a brief pause, he continued, \"...No, that’s not quite right. To be honest, the Spirit Tree hasn’t grown in tens of millions of years. No matter how much cultivation I pour into it, it remains unchanged. In the beginning, it responded, showing clear signs of growth each time I fed it my energy, but that ceased not long after it reached this form.\"","He sighed softly. \"I suspect there’s a unique cultivation method required to nourish it. Unfortunately, I lack that knowledge... so this may be as far as I can go.\"","\"Is that so?\"","Yuan stared at the small eternal tree before him with a pondering gaze, seemingly in deep thought.","Xiao Cangming and the others silently waited for his next action.","After a moment of stillness, Yuan raised his hand, palm facing downward above the Spirit Tree. Without warning, he drew a sharp cut across his palm, letting his blood drip onto the tree below.","The others watched in quiet intrigue, while Yuan himself felt strangely numb, as his actions were guided not by thought, but by pure instinct.","The moment Yuan’s blood touched the Spirit Tree, it was instantly absorbed, almost like a sponge with water. In the next breath, the entire tree began to change, its glowing green hue bleeding into a brilliant crimson.","\"Oh?\" Yuan muttered in a surprised voice after seeing the aftermath.","However, the Spirit Tree wasn’t finished with its transformation.","Mere moments later, the ground started to shake, growing more violent with every passing second.","\"This is... an earthquake?\" Xiao Meilin looked at the ground with a dumbfounded look.","Natural earthquakes in the Primordial Realm were impossible, and the only time the ground would shake was when cultivators collided. However, there was obviously nobody fighting right now.","Then, right before their very eyes, the Spirit Tree started to expand in size. Seeing this, Yuan and the others hastily backed away from it.","In the blink of an eye, the Spirit Tree, which was only as tall as one’s knees, enlarged until it rivaled the massive tree in Feng Yuxiang’s Immortal Cave.","Moreover, it wasn’t just its size that changed, as the amount of spiritual energy it produced drastically increased, too.","In fact, the Spirit Tree released so much spiritual energy that it became visible to the naked eye, spreading through the world as a shimmering mist—an exceedingly rare phenomenon that only appears in such extreme conditions.","Ding!","<The Spirit Tree has accepted your blood>","<The Spirit Tree is resonating with your blood>","<The Spirit Tree is attempting to form a blood contract with you>","\"A blood contract?\" Yuan mumbled after seeing the notification.","However, before he could think further, he sensed something trembling and retrieved a certain object from his robes.","\"What’s that?\" Xiao Meilin questioned out of curiosity as she glared at the token in his grasp.","\"This is...\"","Upon seeing the token, Yuan was reminded of the man who had planned to strike against the Asura Clan when the chance arose—the same man who had given him this token as a signal for when that moment would come.","\"I completely forgot about this, but there is a group of individuals who have been planning to attack the Asura Clan because of your monopoly on the Spirit Tree, and they’re heading here now,\" he gave them a brief explanation.","\"Is that so?\" Xiao Cangming didn’t seem surprised in the slightest by this information, almost as if he was aware of their intentions.","He looked up at the sky and said, \"A crack appeared in this world when the Spirit Tree grew, so anybody can enter this place right now. If there’s a good time to attack us, it’d be right now.\"","\"Can you not fix the crack?\" Yuan asked.","\"I already tried, but due to the Spirit Tree, I am unable to fix it. This world is too small for it, so it forcefully created more space.\"","\"It can do something like that?\" Yuan looked at the Spirit Tree with raised eyebrows.","\"I’m sure you can tell, but the Spirit Tree isn’t an ordinary treasure, and it has its own will.\"","\"A treasure with its own will... Well, that’s not surprising, considering how long it’s lived.\" Yuan said.","Ding!","<The Spirit Tree is attempting to form a blood contract with you>","\"And it’s trying to form a blood contract with me at this very moment.\"","\"So it recognizes you as its master, huh?\" Xiao Cangming remarked. \"Anyway, I’ll go deal with the intruders. You can stay here to form the contract, my lord.\"","\"Alright.\"","\"Meilin, you’re coming with me.\"","\"You don’t need to tell me,\" she said with a cold smile on her face. \"It’s been a while since I last had some fun. Hopefully, there will be many of them.\"","Xiao Cangming and Xiao Meilin left shortly after to confront the crowd gathering outside at the Burning Tree.","<The Spirit Tree is attempting to form a blood contract with you>","\"I get it, I get it. Let’s form the contract now.\"","Yuan said as he approached the Spirit Tree and placed a hand on it.","<The Spirit Tree has initiated a blood contract with you>","<Do you accept this blood contract?>","\"Accept.\"","<Blood contract has been initiated>","Crimson roots abruptly burst from the ground, coiling tightly around Yuan—firm, yet not painful. Moments later, an unfathomable surge of spiritual energy flowed into his body, flooding every fiber of his being. However, even with the immense amount of spiritual energy entering his Dantian, they did not affect his cultivation in the slightest, almost as if the energy was being used for something else.","Meanwhile, Xiao Cangming, Xiao Meilin, and the rest of the Asura Clan moved to confront the intruders gathered outside at the Burning Tree. By the time they arrived, thousands of experts had already assembled, their auras filling the air like a storm on the verge of breaking."]},{"number":2220,"title":"Chapter 2220: Spirit Tree(2)","paragraphs":["Even before Yuan arrived at the Asura Clan, scouts had been stationed near the Burning Tree, watching closely for any opportunity to strike.","Then, when Yuan awakened the Spirit Tree, it cracked open the Asura Clan’s world, opening its sanctuary to the outside world.","\"The Asura Clan’s world is open, but I don’t see anyone going in or coming out.\"","\"Did something happen to the Asura Clan?\"","\"This might be our chance! We need to notify the others immediately!\"","Without hesitation, they activated the token, assembling everyone involved in the plan.","In mere minutes, thousands of experts gathered at the Burning Tree, with many more to come.","\"What happened here?\"","\"Are we attacking the Asura Clan today?\"","The scouts explained the situation to the experts, \"We don’t know what exactly, but something definitely happened inside the Asura Clan, as their world has been open for several minutes now without anyone going in or out. This has never happened before.\"","\"Could this be a trap?\"","\"No, that doesn’t seem to be the case. The portal is different than normal. It’s cracked, almost as if it was forcefully opened.\"","\"Not to mention the spiritual energy leaking from the portal... I can only imagine how much spiritual energy is on the other side.\"","The people there swallowed nervously, their eyes shimmering with greed and desperation, their desire to take control of the Spirit Tree surging.","At that moment, ripples emanated from the portal, and they watched as several figures appeared one after another.","These figures were Xiao Cangming, Li Zhenwu, Xiao Meilin, Xiao Chen, and several of the Asura Clan’s servants.","\"The Asura Clan is here!\" The experts gathered at the Burning Tree were immediately alerted by their appearance.","\"Quite the crowd we have here today,\" Xiao Cangming remarked as he swept the crowd with a calm yet overbearing gaze.","\"However, I don’t recall calling any of you here,\" he continued. \"Or is there a banquet nearby that I am not aware of, Zhao Juechen?\"","Xiao Cangming’s gaze stopped on one of the figures standing at the forefront—a man he recognized as the current patriarch of the Zhao Family, one of the three great powers alongside the Inferno Alchemists and the Chaotic Sect.","Zhao Juechen took a deep breath before speaking out loud, \"Xiao Cangming! We’ve come to deliver an ultimatum! Your greed and monopoly over the Spirit Tree have gone on long enough! For millions of years, countless cultivators have been starved of spiritual energy, while your Asura Clan hoards it without limit!\"","His eyes burned with indignation. \"This ends today! Have you learned nothing from the Celestial Emperor you once fought against? The War of Immortals and Gods began because he monopolized the world’s resources, forcing all under his rule! What you’re doing with the Spirit Tree is no different!\"","\"...\"","Hearing Zhao Juechen’s words, Xiao Cangming didn’t even bat an eye and calmly responded, \"Then allow me to ask you two questions. If you nurture a chicken in your backyard, who owns the eggs it bears? And are you responsible for feeding everyone in the world with those eggs?\"","\"What kind of nonsense is that?\" Zhao Juechen frowned.","\"Just answer my questions.\"","\"The answer to such a question is obvious! I am not going to entertain you!\"","Xiao Cangming sighed and said, \"I asked you those questions because the Spirit Tree was grown by me, so what’s with monopolizing it? And who are you to demand the spiritual energy it produces?\"","\"What?!\" Zhao Juechen and the others expressed shock after hearing such a thing, as it was their first time learning about the Spirit Tree’s origin.","\"D-Don’t lie to us! There’s no way you could’ve grown the Spirit Tree!\" Zhao Juechen shouted, swinging his arm through the air in denial.","\"I am lying? Then answer me this. Why is the Spirit Tree in my world, where everything within is my creation? If you’re going to claim that I moved the Spirit Tree inside, then where was the Spirit Tree beforehand?\"","\"That’s—!\" Zhao Juechen opened his mouth but was speechless.","There were many experts present who had existed in the Primordial Realm since the very beginning, but not a single one of them had ever encountered or heard of the Spirit Tree before the Asura Clan created their own territory.","Zhao Juechen gritted his teeth in frustration, but he couldn’t stop there.","\"Regardless of whether you had grown the Spirit Tree or not, it cannot be compared to a chicken! It doesn’t change the fact that you can still share it with others!\"","Xiao Cangming’s eyes narrowed, a flicker of anger flashing within them. \"Have I not shared it with you?\" he said coldly. \"I’ve shared its spiritual energy with the Inferno Alchemists so the entire world could benefit from their pills. Not only that, but everyone here has received its spiritual energy before. For you to stand before me and claim otherwise is nothing short of a bold-faced lie.\"","Zhao Juechen trembled at his words before responding in a furious tone, \"If you have a full bowl of rice and you only share one or two grains with us, can you really call that sharing?! How shameless of you!\"","Xiao Cangming sneered, \"Do you think the Spirit Tree has unlimited spiritual energy or something? I have shared what I could. If you’re not satisfied with that, it’s none of my issue. In the first place, the Spirit Tree doesn’t even belong to me. I am merely looking after it for someone.\"","\"Another lie! If the Spirit Tree doesn’t belong to you, who does it belong to?! Your mother?! Don’t make me laugh!\"","Whoosh!","Xiao Cangming’s expression darkened, and immense killing intent surged from him.","Seeing this, Zhao Juechen and the others subconsciously backed away.","However, they quickly stopped and moved forward.","\"Don’t think you can control us with fear any longer, Xiao Cangming!\"","\"That’s right! We’re not afraid of you any longer!\"","Xiao Meilin suddenly stepped forward and said, \"Father, I can’t hold it any longer. Why waste your breath on them? They’ll become corpses in a bit, anyway. Let me bathe in their blood already!\"","After a brief moment of silence, Xiao Cangming quietly nodded his head before muttering, \"Go ahead.\""]},{"number":2221,"title":"Chapter 2221: Spirit Tree(3)","paragraphs":["With Xiao Cangming’s approval, Xiao Meilin drew her sword as she stepped forward, approaching the sea of experts before them.","\"Do you really think you can defeat all of us with your pitiful numbers?\" Zhao Juechen sneered. \"Only two of you are at the ninth level of God Ascension. The rest of you are between the first level and the seventh level. Even if you doubled your number, you won’t be able to defeat us!\"","Zhao Juechen was unaware that Xiao Cangming had fed his cultivation to the Spirit Tree and regressed back to the first level of God Ascension, so in reality, only Xiao Meilin was at the peak of God Ascension.","Li Zhenwu had the second-highest cultivation in the Asura Clan at the seventh level of God Ascension, with Xiao Chen being the third at the fifth level. The others were only between the first and third levels.","Xiao Meilin smiled at his words and said, \"This won’t be our first time dealing with a crowd that far exceeds us in numbers.\"","Suddenly, her aura erupted, flooding the area with an overbearing pressure that crushed down on the experts like an invisible mountain. Without uttering a single word, Xiao Meilin’s figure blurred and vanished like a ghost.","When she reappeared, she stood amidst their ranks—her presence radiating with a murderous intent so dense it made the air tremble.","\"W-Watch out—\"","Before anyone could even react, Xiao Meilin swung her sword through the air. It seemed to strike nothing, only empty space. Yet, a heartbeat later, more than twenty cultivators around her plummeted from the sky, their bodies cleaved into countless pieces.","The cultivators froze in shock for an instant, but quickly regained their senses and retaliated, unleashing everything they had at Xiao Meilin without a thought for their spiritual energy.","In the blink of an eye, the entire area erupted into chaos, transforming into a full-fledged battlefield. Li Zhenwu and the others didn’t remain idle and swiftly joined the fray. However, Xiao Cangming decided to stay behind to guard the portal, as he didn’t want anyone to sneak inside and disturb Yuan.","Because of the Asura Clan’s unique physique, which rendered physical attacks ineffective, the intruders were forced to abandon their weapons and rely solely on martial techniques to fight.","Of course, this limitation applied only to Xiao Cangming and those who possessed the Violet Nebula Physique. Li Zhenwu and the servants, who were not part of the Asura Clan by blood, remained vulnerable to physical attacks. That said, their weakness did not make them any easier to deal with.","\"Asura’s Blade of Execution!\" Xiao Chen summoned a colossal blade forged entirely from killing intent, and with each swing, dozens of experts fell, their lives snuffed out in an instant.","As the battle raged on, the sky and earth were drenched in blood, crimson rain falling without end. Hundreds of experts under Zhao Juechen had already fallen, yet their ranks showed no sign of thinning, as reinforcements continued to pour in, replenishing their numbers as fast as they died.","\"Do not falter! It is only a matter of time before the Asura Clan falls! Ming Xuanyang, Bai Zhentian, Wu Moyun, come with me! We’ll take care of Xiao Cangming together!\" Zhao Juechen roared as he went to confront Xiao Cangming, followed by three other experts.","Zhao Juechen was a powerhouse at the seventh level of God Ascension, while the others were at the fifth or sixth level.","Yet, despite being on at the first level, Xiao Cangming didn’t show even the slightest hint of fear or worry in his gaze.","\"God of War’s Astral Arts!\" Xiao Cangming wrapped himself in a massive purple avatar and fought back without moving from his location.","Though his cultivation had weakened to the first level of God Ascension, the God of War’s Astral Arts relied more on Soul Strength than cultivation. And since only his cultivation had been affected by feeding the Spirit Tree, Xiao Cangming’s Soul Strength was still unfathomably strong, allowing him to contend with powerhouses of far higher realms easily.","In just several exchanges, Xiao Cangming had not only repelled Zhao Juechen but even killed one of the powerhouses.","\"What the hell is this?! I knew he was powerful, but this is beyond anything we know!\" Ming Xuanyang exclaimed in shock after witnessing Xiao Cangming’s overwhelming prowess.","\"This bastard must’ve been hiding his strength this entire time!\"","\"That’s impossible! He was already monstrously strong before, and you’re saying that wasn’t even his full power?!\" Zhao Juechen shouted, clenching his fists as he glared at Xiao Cangming, his voice trembling with disbelief and the bitter realization of his mistake.","\"Zhao Juechen,\" Xiao Cangming said suddenly, his voice cutting through the chaos like a blade. \"Your greatest sin today isn’t daring to bare your fangs at me or the Asura Clan—it’s coveting the Spirit Tree, which belongs to my lord.\"","\"Your lord? What the hell are you talking about?!\"","\"Still pretending you don’t know what I’m talking about?\" Xiao Cangming said, shaking his head in disappointment. \"There’s only one person I would ever address as my ’lord.’ And you—someone who stood on the battlefield during the Heavenly War of Immortals and Gods—should know exactly who that is.\"","Zhao Juechen’s entire being froze as a certain individual appeared in his mind.","\"You don’t mean...\" he swallowed nervously.","\"No! That’s impossible!\" Zhao Juechen shook his head. \"There’s no way he’s still alive! After all, he perished alongside the Celestial Emperor!\"","Although most of the earliest inhabitants of the Primordial Realm were imprisoned before the fall of the first Celestial Emperor, the realm itself wasn’t sealed until his successor took the throne. Before permanently closing it, the second Celestial Emperor cast a few more individuals inside, who revealed the aftermath to the others. Of course, this included the Celestial Emperor’s defeat and Tian Xian’s death.","\"Does it look like I am joking to you?\" Xiao Cangming said with a serious expression, refusing to elaborate further.","\"...\"","Zhao Juechen fell silent, but the fear in his eyes was as clear as day."]},{"number":2222,"title":"Chapter 2222: Spirit Tree(4)","paragraphs":["After a moment of silence, Zhao Juechen muttered in a low voice, \"So what...?\"","\"SO WHAT IF THE EVIL GOD IS ALIVE?!\" he suddenly roared.","\"It doesn’t change anything! As long as we’re stuck in this world, the Spirit Tree is necessary to us, and we’ll do anything to acquire it!\"","Xiao Cangming sneered, \"Even if you somehow manage to acquire the Spirit Tree, it’s not something you can manage. Do you truly think the Spirit Tree is a treasure with limitless power? How naive. Once the Spirit Tree runs out of power, you will return to being deprived of spiritual energy.\"","\"T-That’s—!\"","Zhao Juechen couldn’t refute Xiao Cangming’s words. In fact, he never really thought about the Spirit Tree running out of power. After all, the Spirit Tree has supplied the Asura Clan with seemingly limitless spiritual energy for millions of years without any issue.","Of course, nobody but the Asura Clan was aware that to keep the Spirit Tree alive, Xiao Cangming had to feed it his cultivation.","\"Zhao Juechen, I will give you and everyone here one last opportunity to turn around and forget about the Spirit Tree. Otherwise, I will have to cut you down,\" Xiao Cangming said.","He turned to look at Xiao Meilin, who was still slaughtering everyone around her like a madman, and added, \"The longer you take to decide, the more casualties you will have.\"","Zhao Juechen gritted his teeth and trembled. After a moment of silence, he responded, \"I will not yield! Today, I will either acquire the Spirit Tree or perish trying!\"","Xiao Cangming shook his head in a disappointed manner.","\"What a stubborn and foolish decision. If you wish to die so badly, allow me to grant your wish.\"","Without another word, Xiao Cangming resumed their battle, attacking first with God of War’s Astral Arts.","Meanwhile, inside the Asura Clan’s world, Yuan finished forming the blood contract with the Spirit Tree.","<You have successfully formed a blood contract with the Spirit Tree>","After forming the contract, the massive Spirit Tree had disappeared from the Asura Clan’s world and somehow entered Yuan’s Dantian.","\"Y-Young Master! What is this?! The Spirit Tree has taken root inside your Dantian!\" Feng Yuxiang exclaimed in shock.","\"I formed a blood contract with it... But I didn’t expect it to move into my Dantian,\" he said as he looked inside his Dantian to see Feng Yuxiang and Lan Yingying gazing at the Spirit Tree with intrigue.","<Due to the Spirit Tree, your cultivation speed has increased by 500,000%>","<Due to the Spirit Tree, your Dantian has significantly expanded in size, allowing you to hold more spiritual energy>","Although the effects of the Spirit Tree seemed extremely good at a glance and could easily turn an ordinary cultivator into a prodigy, it wasn’t very beneficial to Yuan, who already had a ridiculously fast cultivation speed. As for increasing his Dantian’s size, it definitely helped a little, but it wasn’t anything game-changing.","\"There must be another use for the Spirit Tree...\" Yuan refused to believe that he had made Xiao Cangming sacrifice so much of his time and effort for something so insignificant and believed that he had yet to see the Spirit Tree’s true prowess.","Unfortunately, he didn’t have the time to study the Spirit Tree, as Xiao Cangming and the others were still dealing with the intruders.","However, just as Yuan prepared to leave to group up with the others, he halted his movements when he noticed a figure approaching him from a distance.","The approaching figure was a beautiful young woman who appeared to have only just reached adulthood, yet within her eyes lingered an unfathomable depth of experience.","\"Xiao Hua...?\" Yuan muttered as his eyes fell upon her.","He should’ve felt joy at seeing her awake, but instead, unease gripped his heart. Something was wrong. Her gaze burned with unmistakable fury, and the killing intent radiating from her was so intense it felt almost tangible, all of it directed straight at him.","\"What’s wrong, Xiao Hua?\" Yuan called out to her in a soft voice. \"Are you hurt somewhere?\"","As Xiao Hua slowly approached, a look of pure disdain twisted her beautiful facial features. Her voice dripped with venom as she snapped, \"Don’t you dare act so familiar with me, you bastard!\"","\"...\"","Yuan was speechless, but he had an idea what was going on.","Meanwhile, Xiao Hua quickened her pace, her aura flaring violently as she began to release her cultivation. Although her cultivation had reverted to the first level of Spirit Apprentice upon obtaining her new vessel, the divine nature of her new body—combined with the dense spiritual energy saturating the air—caused her cultivation to soar uncontrollably, and with every step she took, her cultivation leapt by several levels.","\"My father may have forgiven you,\" Xiao Hua continued, her voice trembling with fury, \"but I will never forgive you for killing my mother!\"","Sure enough, just as Xiao Cangming had warned, Xiao Hua’s memories had regressed, returning to the Primordial Era, to a time before she had forgiven Tian Xian for killing her mother.","\"Calm down for a minute, Xiao Hua. Your memories are a bit messed up right now, but they should return to normal—\"","\"Shut up!\" Xiao Hua suddenly summoned a sword and leaped forward, striking Yuan without warning.","Yuan calmly caught her blade with his fingers and sighed, \"If it’ll make you feel better, you can strike at me as much as you want.\"","Yuan decided to let Xiao Hua do as she pleased until she calmed down and immediately loosened his fingers, releasing the sword.","Without a word, Xiao Hua struck again with zero hesitation, this time with more power.","Yuan didn’t even bother to block her sword and allowed her to strike his body.","Even though her attacks had no effect on Yuan, Xiao Hua refused to stop, striking at him again and again—like a child throwing a tantrum in her fury.","\"I swear I will kill you!\" Xiao Hua roared as her cultivation soared again, entering Spirit Enlightenment."]},{"number":2223,"title":"Chapter 2223: Xiao Hua’s Awakening","paragraphs":["As Xiao Hua’s cultivation rose, her strikes became heavier and more powerful, and she even started using martial techniques.","\"Young Master, it looks like she really wants to kill you,\" Feng Yuxiang remarked as she watched from inside his Dantian, feeling a bit dazed, as she could’ve never imagined Xiao Hua attacking Yuan so fiercely.","\"Her memories regressed back to the Primordial Era—to a time when we didn’t have the best relationship. Back then, she would always try to kill me when she had the chance,\" Yuan sighed with a bitter smile.","\"I don’t blame her, though. I did kill her mother, after all.\"","\"What did you do to calm her?\" Lan Yingying asked.","\"If you do it again, it might calm her again.\"","\"I didn’t do anything special. Whenever she tried to kill me, I would fight back and beat her up quite badly. It took some time and a lot of beating, but eventually, she calmed down,\" Yuan said as he recalled his past.","\"...\"","Feng Yuxiang and Lan Yingying were left speechless by his words.","\"If you’re going to ask me if I am going to repeat the same process, I’ll have to decline. I was a very different person back then.\"","\"So what are you going to do? Continue to let her try to kill you until she regains her memories? Who knows when that will happen.\" Feng Yuxiang said.","\"If you’re unwilling to fight her, I’ll gladly do it in your place,\" she said with a faint smile. \"I’ve always wanted to face her seriously. Besides, as fellow servants under the same master, it’s our duty to clean up each other’s messes.\"","Of course, Feng Yuxiang didn’t mean it in a malicious way. Due to their competitive relationship, it was only natural for her to want to fight Xiao Hua.","Sensing Feng Yuxiang’s desire to fight, Yuan seriously pondered letting her fight Xiao Hua.","\"Don’t worry, I won’t harm her too much,\" she assured him.","\"Alright.\" Yuan eventually agreed. He wanted to see if fighting Feng Yuxiang might help Xiao Hua regain her memories faster.","Right as Xiao Hua went for another strike, Feng Yuxiang immediately emerged from his Dantian to block it.","\"Who the hell are you?\" Xiao Hua exclaimed as she distanced herself from them.","\"I am the Young Master’s number one servant,\" she proudly declared.","\"Attacking your own master is a grave sin for a servant, even if you have lost your memories.\"","\"Servant? What the hell are you talking about? There’s no way in hell I’d serve the bastard who killed my mother!\" Xiao Hua roared.","Normally, servants were incapable of attacking their masters. However, Yuan didn’t view Xiao Hua or her strikes as a threat. In his eyes, she was just having a harmless tantrum, so no penalty was imposed on her.","Feng Yuxiang shrugged, \"Anyway, if you insist on continuing to attack the Young Master, I will have to put an end to it.\"","\"You? Stop me? I’d like to see you try!\" Xiao Hua shouted as she lunged at Feng Yuxiang.","By now, Xiao Hua’s cultivation had reached the peak of Divine Grandmaster. Meanwhile, Feng Yuxiang was at the peak of True Immortal.","Yet, despite the disparity between their cultivation, Xiao Hua went on the offensive, striking without a care, almost as if the difference didn’t exist.","If Feng Yuxiang had been an ordinary cultivator, Xiao Hua might have been able to overcome their difference and defeat her. However, Feng Yuxiang was no ordinary cultivator but a Primordial Phoenix with the Immortal Monarch’s seal.","Feng Yuxiang dodged most of Xiao Hua’s strikes but would occasionally strike back with her flames, barely putting any power into it, almost as if she was toying with Xiao Hua.","\"This power... a phoenix?\" Xiao Hua narrowed her eyes after recognizing Feng Yuxiang’s flames.","Though she couldn’t explain why, Xiao Hua felt an inexplicable irritation toward Feng Yuxiang’s very presence, despite having no memories of her.","\"A phoenix serving a human? That’s unheard of,\" Xiao Hua muttered to herself, disbelief flashing in her eyes.","\"What’s wrong, you little brat? Is this all you’ve got? You won’t be able to defeat me at this rate, much less defeat the Young Master,\" Feng Yuxiang continued to mock Xiao Hua as they fought, which only irritated her even further.","\"Shut up, you damn pigeon! You’re annoying as hell!\" Xiao Hua shouted as her cultivation soared past the Divine Realm and entered the Immortal Realm, becoming a Bronze Immortal.","Yuan raised an eyebrow when he heard Xiao Hua call Feng Yuxiang a \"pigeon\"—a remark that sounded exactly like something the present Xiao Hua would say.","’Is fighting Feng Feng triggering her memories subconsciously?’ Yuan wondered. ’This is working even better than I expected...’","Feng Yuxiang also noticed this and began to tease Xiao Hua even more.","In response, Xiao Hua’s attacks grew more fierce, and her killing intent soared.","As of this moment, Xiao Hua’s urge to kill Feng Yuxiang has surpassed her desire to kill Yuan.","Sometime later, Xiao Hua’s cultivation reached True Immortal. However, it wasn’t just her cultivation that improved. Her fighting style and movement have undergone drastic changes since they began, forcing Feng Yuxiang to fight more seriously.","\"Hahaha! This is more like it! I have always wanted to fight you seriously, but never got the chance!\" Feng Yuxiang laughed excitedly as she started using her phoenix power more seriously, even transforming.","After several thousand more exchanges, Xiao Hua’s aura suddenly erupted, her cultivation surging past the Immortal Realm and stepping into God Ascension. A flood of Celestial Qi burst from her body, shaking the air around them.","\"Seriously?!\" Feng Yuxiang cried out, eyes wide with disbelief. She had never imagined Xiao Hua’s cultivation would break beyond the True Immortal realm.","Upon reaching the first level of God Ascension, Xiao Hua’s strength soared to unimaginable heights, and she began driving Feng Yuxiang back with overwhelming force. Yet her aura showed no sign of stabilizing, and a few minutes later, her cultivation surged again, breaking through to the second level.","\"Second level God Ascension?! That’s cheating!\" Feng Yuxiang exclaimed."]},{"number":2224,"title":"Chapter 2224: Fighting Xiao Hua","paragraphs":["After Xiao Hua’s cultivation reached the second level of God Ascension, Feng Yuxiang was no longer a match and was forced to go on the defensive.","\"What’s wrong, you annoying bird?! Why have you gone quiet when you were talking so much just moments ago?!\" Xiao Hua spoke with a mocking smile on her face.","Feng Yuxiang gritted her teeth in frustration. She could never have anticipated that Xiao Hua would enter the God Ascension realm this quickly. After all, it would normally take decades for someone to regain their full cultivation after obtaining a new vessel, but it hadn’t been a full day since Xiao Hua entered her new vessel.","\"Don’t you dare look down on me, you little brat!\" Feng Yuxiang roared as her body erupted in flames, transforming into her true phoenix form. In an instant, a blazing pressure swept across the world, igniting the very air around her.","\"Primordial Fire!\" Feng Yuxiang cried, beating her massive, flame-wreathed wings once. A storm of invisible fire cascaded from above, raining down upon Xiao Hua like divine wrath.","A vicious light flickered within Xiao Hua’s eyes as her aura condensed for a brief moment before exploding like a bomb.","\"Asura Clan’s Immortal Slaying Art!\" Xiao Hua roared as she unleashed one of the Asura Clan’s supreme techniques. In the blink of an eye, her power swept across the sky, extinguishing every trace of the Primordial Fire.","\"What?!\" Feng Yuxiang’s eyes widened with shock, unable to believe how easily Xiao Hua had removed her fire.","However, Xiao Hua’s prowess wasn’t the only thing that shocked Feng Yuxiang, as Xiao Hua’s cultivation had increased by another level right before she struck, reaching the third level of God Ascension.","\"Young Master... I don’t think I can handle her any longer, especially if her cultivation continues to rise...\" Feng Yuxiang said to Yuan using voice transmission.","\"...\"","Yuan wasn’t too surprised about Xiao Hua’s cultivation since she had already reached this level in the past. That said, he was definitely taken aback by how quickly she regained it.","’This can’t be just the result of her new vessel...’ he thought.","He checked her status, but the only thing that had changed from it was her cultivation.","\"Young Master!\" Feng Yuxiang cried for his help again when she could no longer hold back Xiao Hua.","Immediately, Yuan responded, retrieving Number One Under Heaven to block Xiao Hua’s attack.","\"I’ll take care of this,\" he said to Feng Yuxiang.","Although he had no intention of fighting Xiao Hua, the situation had escalated to the point where he could no longer afford to hold back.","\"Look who’s finally done hiding behind a pathetic bird,\" Xiao Hua mocked.","Before Yuan could respond, Xiao Hua shifted her gaze to Feng Yuxiang and continued, \"And you... Now that you can no longer deal with me, you’re going to make your master fight? How laughable.\"","\"This damn brat...!\" Feng Yuxiang’s clenched fists trembled, and her eyebrows twitched uncontrollably. However, she couldn’t refute Xiao Hua’s words.","\"Too bad it won’t make any difference. Once I kill this bastard, I’ll definitely take my time to kill you next!\" Xiao Hua roared as she changed her focus to Yuan, her aura surging as she attacked him with newfound ferocity.","Unlike his prior opponents, Xiao Hua used her Celestial Qi without restraint. Although it wasn’t as strong as it should be for someone at her cultivation due to how quickly she improved it, it was still strong enough to push him back.","\"What’s wrong, Tian Xian?! You’re a lot weaker than I remember!\" Xiao Hua mocked as she continued pushing him back.","\"That’s because I am not Tian Xian. My name is Yuan.\"","Xiao Hua’s brows furrowed at his response, and she shouted, \"Do you really think I will fall for such a bald-faced lie?!\"","\"My father may be foolish enough to forgive you, but I am not like him!\"","Xiao Hua’s cultivation continued to surge, and after many exchanges, she had another breakthrough, reaching the fourth level of God Ascension.","\"Just how much further is her cultivation going to increase?!\" Feng Yuxiang’s jaws dropped at the scene.","In order to clash with Xiao Hua without hurting her or losing to her, Yuan was forced to use True Dragon Awakening and Chaotic Essence.","\"Why did you have to kill Mother?! Why?!\" Xiao Hua suddenly exclaimed, tears flowing down her face.","\"I’m sorry.\" Yuan had no excuse and could only offer his apology.","\"If you truly regret it, then let me kill you! Atone with your death!\"","\"Sorry, but I cannot do that.\"","\"Then you don’t really mean it!\" Xiao Hua roared, her cultivation entering the fifth level of God Ascension.","\"I hate you! I hate, hate, hate you!\"","Xiao Hua’s cultivation continued to soar without any sign of slowing down. In fact, it was speeding up.","When Xiao Hua reached the sixth level, Yuan had to use Eternal Essence.","A few exchanges later, Xiao Hua’s cultivation entered the seventh level.","Xiao Hua was now a threat that even Yuan could not handle.","\"Damn it!\" Yuan growled through gritted teeth. Seeing no sign of Xiao Hua calming down, he was left with no choice but to invoke his authority as her master for the first time ever.","\"Halt!\" Yuan commanded, his voice echoing with undeniable authority. In an instant, Xiao Hua froze mid-motion, her body stopping as if bound by invisible chains.","\"What the hell is this?! What did you do to me?!\" Xiao Hua exclaimed with a bewildered look on her face.","\"He simply commanded you as your master,\" Feng Yuxiang calmly responded.","\"What?! That’s impossible! I am not even his servant!\"","Feng Yuxiang shrugged, \"If you’re not willing to believe it despite the evidence before you, there’s nothing else I can say that will convince you.\"","Xiao Hua fell silent for a moment. Then, a purple aura—burning like ethereal flames—began to rise from her body, rippling through the air with intense power.","\"I am... not... his... servant!\" Xiao Hua roared, her voice echoing with defiance as she attempted to defy Yuan’s authority.","As a result, the authority immediately retaliated, inflicting immense pain upon her.","Yet, Xiao Hua continued to resist and fight back, to the point where blood started flowing from her eyes, ears, and nose.","\"This crazy little—!\" Feng Yuxiang was left utterly speechless."]},{"number":2225,"title":"Chapter 2225: Fighting Xiao Hua(2)","paragraphs":["\"Stop fighting against it. You’ll only hurt yourself doing so,\" Yuan said after seeing Xiao Hua attempting to resist his authority, almost subconsciously withdrawing it.","\"Shut up! I don’t know what you did to me, but I would never willingly be your servant!\" she shouted back. \"You must’ve forced me into becoming your servant without me noticing somehow!\"","\"You’ll kill yourself at this rate!\" Feng Yuxiang said.","\"So what?! I’d rather die than become my mother’s killer—this bastard’s servant!\"","Feng Yuxiang looked at Yuan with a worried face. If Xiao Hua continues to resist, she will definitely die.","A master and servant pact was as sacred and powerful as a heavenly oath, so not even a God Ascension cultivator would be able to resist it.","\"Ahhhh!\" Xiao Hua started screaming, not from pain but from sheer determination.","\"I forgot how stubborn you were in the past...\" Yuan sighed.","It was clear that Xiao Hua would keep resisting—either until she broke free from his authority or perished in the attempt.","With no other choice, Yuan withdrew his authority over her.","The instant the restraints on her were released, Xiao Hua’s aura skyrocketed, and her cultivation soared straight into the eighth level of God Ascension. However, not even a heartbeat later, it entered the ninth level, reaching the peak of God Ascension.","\"Ninth level God Ascension?! Don’t tell me she’s going to become a Cultivation God next?!\" Feng Yuxiang exclaimed.","The moment she broke free, Xiao Hua lunged forward, her arms snapping toward Yuan’s neck in a seizing motion.","The pressure radiating from Xiao Hua’s aura was so immense that Yuan couldn’t even move a finger. In that instant, she seized his neck effortlessly, her grip tightening with terrifying strength.","Then, with her other hand, she thrust her sword forward, driving the blade straight into Yuan’s heart.","Yuan coughed up a mouthful of blood, but despite how grave it appeared, his life was not in danger, and the wound was only superficial.","However, Xiao Hua didn’t stop there, and her aura surged violently, almost as if she was preparing for her ultimate technique.","\"Young Master!\"","Seeing this, Feng Yuxiang immediately attempted to help, but Xiao Hua’s overbearing pressure was so immense that she couldn’t even lift a finger, much less help.","\"Today, Tian Xian, I’ll avenge my mother by killing you!\" Xiao Hua cried, her voice raw with grief and burning fury.","Suddenly, a calm yet familiar voice echoed through the air. \"Stop.\"","Xiao Hua instinctively turned toward the sound, but before she could fully face it, she felt a firm hand press against her head, halting her movement.","’When did they get behind me?!’ she cried inwardly.","The voice continued, \"I won’t let you hurt Brother Yuan anymore.\"","\"Brother Yuan? Who the hell are you?\" Xiao Hua demanded as she turned fully toward the voice.","To her astonishment, she was met with the sight of a young girl who shared her facial features—so much so that it felt as though she were staring into a mirror.","\"That’s...\" Feng Yuxiang swallowed hard after seeing the individual standing behind Xiao Hua, as she was the original owner of Xiao Hua’s previous vessel.","\"A mere mortal... what do you think you can achieve?\" Xiao Hua sneered after realizing the young girl’s inferior cultivation.","\"Although our souls may have separated, I still have your memories,\" said the young girl.","Then, without warning, she activated a memory-transfer technique, one she had learned from Xiao Hua’s own memories.","In the next instant, a torrent of memories surged into Xiao Hua’s mind—the very memories she had once lost.","From the moment she forgave Tian Xian in the Primordial Era to when she first met Yuan in the Lower Heaven, millions of years of memories overwhelmed Xiao Hua.","Xiao Hua released her grip on the sword and collapsed to her knees, her expression blank and unfocused, almost as if she’d become a soulless body. However, in reality, the memories she had just regained spanned millions of years, and it would take time for her mind to fully comprehend them.","While Xiao Hua was in such a state, the young girl shifted her focus to Yuan.","\"Brother Yuan, are you okay?\" she approached him with a worried face.","Even though Yuan knew the person before him was no longer the Xiao Hua he once knew, a wave of nostalgia washed over him, as if she had never left his side at all.","\"I’m fine,\" Yuan said as he forcefully yanked Xiao Hua’s sword from his body. \"Is she okay? What did you do to her?\"","\"I only returned to her her memories,\" she calmly replied. \"It might take some time for her to snap out of it, but she’ll be fine.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan asked, \"You’re the original owner of that body, right? What is your name?\"","\"I...\"","The young girl opened her mouth, but she froze for a moment before responding, \"I don’t have a name. By the time my consciousness had formed, I was already known as Xiao Hua.\"","\"What about your parents? Surely, they gave you a name.\" Feng Yuxiang said.","The young girl shook her head softly and said, \"I don’t have any parents. To be precise, I wasn’t born through ordinary means between two beings. From what I know, I came into existence without a physical body and wandered this world as a formless being—until Xiao Hua’s soul merged with mine. Only then did my body begin to take form.\"","\"What in the...?\" Feng Yuxiang was left speechless by such an odd story.","\"A natural birth? Like natural treasures and spirits? Are you even human?\" she couldn’t help but ask.","The young girl looked at her hands, seemingly pondering Feng Yuxiang’s question.","\"Does it even matter?\" Yuan suddenly said.","He approached the young girl and patted her head like he used to before asking, \"If you don’t have a name, you can just give yourself one.\"","The young girl stared him in the eyes and calmly said, \"Brother Yuan, I want you to give me a name.\""]},{"number":2226,"title":"Chapter 2226: Lingyue","paragraphs":["\"Me? Naming you?\" Yuan’s eyes widened slightly at the young girl’s request.","The young girl nodded in confirmation.","\"...\"","Yuan fell silent for a good moment before speaking again, \"In that case, how does Lingyue sound?\"","A weird light flickered within Yuan’s eyes as he spoke the name.","\"Lingyue...\" The young girl mumbled.","\"Do you want a different name?\" Yuan asked after seeing her reaction.","\"No!\" she hastily responded. \"Lingyue is good!\"","\"It’s a pleasure to meet you, Lingyue.\"","\"Un!\" Lingyue nodded with a bright smile on her face.","\"Ugh...\" A grunt suddenly resounded, causing Yuan and the others to look at Xiao Hua, who was starting to wake up from her daze.","A few more moments later, Xiao Hua no longer had a blank look on her face, and she started looking around with a somewhat confused expression.","\"Xiao Hua,\" Yuan called softly.","She turned to face him but remained silent. Then, her expression began to contort with sorrow, and moments later, tears streamed down her face as she broke into a heart-wrenching cry.","\"Waaah! I’m so sorry!\" she started apologizing.","\"What are you apologizing for?\" Yuan said with a smile. \"If this is about what happened just now, it’s not your fault. Your memories were messed up, after all.\"","\"That doesn’t change the fact that I pointed my blade at you! I even seriously tried to kill you! If she hadn’t stopped me in time, I would’ve likely killed you!\" Xiao Hua said as she looked at Lingyue.","\"Kill me?\" Yuan chuckled. \"You should know me well enough to know that I won’t die to something like that.\"","\"Regardless of what you say, I deserve to be punished! Please, punish me, Brother Yu—Master Tian!\" Xiao Hua said. \"I won’t complain even if you decide to kill me!\"","\"What would I gain from killing you?\" Yuan shook his head. \"As for punishing you...\"","He pondered for a moment before speaking, \"Alright, I have decided your punishment. You are forbidden from calling me Master Tian.\"","\"That’s...\" Xiao Hua wore a dumbfounded look on her face.","\"What? Don’t tell me you’re not going to accept the punishment?\"","\"But what else am I supposed to call you...?\" she asked.","\"That’s something for you to decide. You can continue to call me Brother Yuan, but now that you have regained all of your memories, I understand that it might be difficult for you, so I’ll let you decide.\"","\"...\"","Xiao Hua fell silent for a good minute before responding, \"Master Yu—\"","\"Rejected,\" Yuan instantly interrupted her from finishing.","\"I won’t accept anything that starts with ’master’ or ’lord’ or anything similar,\" he continued.","Xiao Hua sighed and said, \"In that case, I’ll just call you Yuan.\"","Yuan nodded.","\"Now then, we’ve wasted enough time here. Let’s go out and help the Asura Clan with the intruders. We’ll continue this afterward.\"","\"Okay.\"","They quickly left the Asura Clan’s world and appeared outside shortly after.","However, by the time they arrived, Xiao Cangming and the others had already cleaned up half of the intruders.","\"My lord,\" Xiao Cangming, who was still guarding the portal, greeted him the moment they appeared.","\"Sorry it took so long. Something came up.\" Yuan said, his eyes pointing at Xiao Hua and Lingyue.","\"They’re already awake?\" Xiao Cangming was surprised by how quickly they woke up, as he had anticipated it would take several days, if not weeks.","\"I’ll explain everything later. What happened here?\" Yuan asked, though the answer was already clear to him.","The ground was strewn with mangled corpses and soaked in blood—a sight eerily reminiscent of the Primordial Era, when he himself had painted countless battlefields in crimson as Tian Xian.","Xiao Cangming turned toward Xiao Meilin and the others, who were still fighting off the intruders, and said calmly, \"We gave them a chance to turn back and leave, but as you can see, they chose otherwise.\"","\"...\"","Without a word, Yuan suddenly approached the battlefield.","\"All of you, stop.\"","His calm voice rippled across the battlefield, imbued with quiet authority, and in an instant, all movement came to a halt.","\"If you came here for the Spirit Tree, you’re too late, as it no longer exists. So you can either leave now with your life or die a pointless death.\"","\"The Spirit Tree no longer exists? You’re lying!\" one of them shouted.","Yuan merely shrugged. \"Go see for yourself if you don’t believe me. Even if I were lying, it changes nothing—you still won’t get the Spirit Tree, and trying will only get you killed.\"","The cultivators gritted their teeth in frustration, yet none could refute Yuan’s words. With most of their comrades already defeated, continuing the battle was meaningless. Still, none bothered to flee since they knew that even if they turned their backs now, the Asura Clan would hunt them down without mercy.","Yuan could see their concerns and said, \"If you leave now, I promise you that we won’t chase after you later. We’ll even pretend none of this happened.\"","Yuan was willing to show them mercy, for he found little fault in their actions. Deprived of spiritual energy and driven by desperation, these cultivators had turned their blades against the Asura Clan, who had long monopolized the Spirit Tree, something that would solve their problem, even if only temporarily.","Moreover, these cultivators had no clue about the origin of the Spirit Tree or that the Asura Clan had grown it. In their eyes, the Asura Clan was doing something the first Celestial Emperor had done, and if Yuan had been in their shoes, he would’ve likely done the same.","\"How... How do we know that you won’t go back on your word?\" One of the cultivators suddenly questioned, his face full of skepticism.","Yuan shrugged, \"You will have to take my word for it. Or would you rather continue this meaningless battle and die for certain? The choice is up to you.\"","When no one moved after a full minute, Yuan spoke again—this time to the Asura Clan.","\"If any of them remain by the time I finish counting to three, kill them all.\"","\"As you wish, Master!\"","Xiao Meilin was the first to acknowledge Yuan’s command, showing the cultivators that Yuan truly held some authority over the Asura Clan."]},{"number":2227,"title":"Chapter 2227: As a Friend","paragraphs":["\"Did I hear that right? The Crimson Empress just called that man her ’Master’!\" the cultivators gasped in shock, their eyes wide with disbelief.","\"One!\" Yuan suddenly started counting down.","\"Fuck! Are we really going to leave? What about those who had perished before us?!\"","Some cultivators hesitated to leave. To them, retreating now felt like a betrayal—an insult to the countless comrades who had already fallen. If they turned their backs, it would be as though their companions’ sacrifices had been for nothing.","\"Two!\" Yuan continued to count.","\"Stay here if you want, but I’m out of here!\" one shouted. \"If you’d rather waste your life like the others, be my guest!\"","Many cultivators didn’t hesitate. To them, the dead mattered little compared to their own survival, and they refused to be counted among those who’d already fallen.","In the blink of an eye, the majority of the remaining cultivators fled.","\"Three!\"","However, a few indecisive ones remained even after Yuan finished his counting.","Without waiting for another breath, Xiao Meilin suddenly charged at those who stayed behind.","\"Aahh!\"","Seeing this, these cultivators immediately made up their minds and started running away. Yet, Xiao Meilin didn’t care and chased after them.","\"W-Why are you chasing us?! We’re leaving!\" one of them cried out in despair.","\"I was ordered to kill anyone still here after three,\" Xiao Meilin replied coldly, her voice devoid of mercy. \"As far as I’m concerned, running now won’t save you.\"","Without hesitation, she continued her relentless slaughter, killing everyone who stayed after Yuan counted to three.","Once the area was quiet again, Yuan said, \"Let’s return.\"","Xiao Cangming nodded, and the Asura Clan followed him back into their world.","Some time later, Yuan and the Asura Clan gathered in a room to talk about Xiao Hua’s situation and the Asura Clan’s future.","The moment they sat down, Xiao Cangming shifted his gaze toward Xiao Hua and spoke, \"Even though it’s normal for cultivators who have changed vessels to regain their cultivation quickly, you have recovered your cultivation a little too quickly. Did something happen?\"","Xiao Hua’s body trembled at Xiao Cangming’s words, but not out of fear that he would discover what had happened. Merely recalling the moment she had attacked Yuan was enough to send a shiver through her.","\"I don’t know. It just happened,\" she calmly replied.","Xiao Cangming turned to look at Yuan to see if he knew anything, but he also shook his head.","\"In that case, what about your memories? How much did it regress?\" Xiao Cangming continued to question Xiao Hua.","\"That’s...\"","Xiao Hua hesitated to tell the truth this time. After all, if Xiao Cangming learned that she’d tried to kill Yuan, regardless of her situation, he’d definitely be enraged. Of course, she wasn’t afraid of him and preferred not to deal with him.","\"Don’t worry, she’s regained all of her memories already,\" Yuan suddenly answered. \"And it was all because of her.\"","Xiao Cangming followed Yuan’s gaze to Lingyue, who was quietly sitting beside him.","\"You’re...\"","\"My name is Lingyue,\" she introduced herself.","\"What?\" Xiao Cangming’s eyes widened with bewilderment after hearing her name.","It was a reaction that puzzled Xiao Hua and the others in the room. After all, it was a secret that Yuan had revealed only to him.","\"I gave her that name,\" Yuan explained.","\"...\"","Xiao Cangming fell silent for a moment before muttering, \"Is that so...\"","Like Xiao Hua, Lingyue’s cultivation had risen since her awakening, though not as dramatically. She had only managed to reach the peak of the Divine Ancestor realm.","That said, it wasn’t unnatural. After all, Xiao Hua had reached the peak of God Ascension in her past lives, while Lingyue was just someone who’d received her memories.","Soon, they moved the topic to the Spirit Tree.","\"What about the Spirit Tree?\" Xiao Cangming asked.","\"It entered my Dantian,\" Yuan replied.","\"Without the Spirit Tree, this world will collapse soon,\" Xiao Cangming remarked.","In the Primordial Realm, only the Asura Clan had the luxury of having their own world because it required an immense amount of spiritual energy to maintain one, something they could only achieve with the Spirit Tree.","Seeing the guilty look on Yuan’s face, Xiao Cangming smiled and said, \"Well, it doesn’t really matter since we won’t be staying in the Primordial Realm for much longer.\"","\"Does that mean you plan to leave the Primordial Realm?\" Yuan asked even though he already knew the answer.","\"That’s right. Now that you have returned and I have fulfilled my mission, there’s no longer any reason for us to stay in here.\"","\"I see... What will you be doing once you are outside?\"","Xiao Cangming pondered for a moment before asking, \"The Shadow Army, do they still exist?\"","He nodded, \"Yes, and they’re more active than ever.\"","\"In that case, I’ll stay with them and work towards recovering my cultivation. Only then will I be able to serve you properly again.\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"Cangming, you have already served me long enough. Now that you have a wife again, you should focus on your family.\"","\"That’s unacceptable. I swore to be your sword until I draw my last breath,\" he quickly refused.","However, Yuan shook his head and said, \"Don’t take this the wrong way, but a lot of time has passed since then, and I already have a reliable sword by my side. You have done enough for me.\"","\"...\"","Xiao Cangming fell silent again.","After several minutes of silence, Yuan spoke, \"With that being said, I will likely still need your help from time to time, and when that time comes, I hope you will be willing to assist me as a friend.\"","\"As a friend, huh?\" A profound smile appeared on Xiao Cangming’s face.","\"If this is what you truly want, then I have no reason to decline.\"","\"Just call me Yuan from now on.\"","\"Alright, Yuan.\"","\"Thanks.\"","Xiao Meilin stared at her father with wide eyes, utterly surprised that he had agreed to something like this so easily.","\"W-What about me?\" she suddenly asked."]},{"number":2228,"title":"Chapter 2228: A Broken Treasure","paragraphs":["\"W-What about me?\" Xiao Meilin suddenly asked.","Yuan looked at her and replied with a question, \"What about you? I never even accepted you as my servant in the first place.\"","\"No way! How can you say that to me now?! That’s too cruel, Master Tian! Are you really going to throw me away after using me for so long?!\" Xiao Meilin exclaimed.","Yuan showed a stiff smile and said, \"Don’t make it sound so weird. You’re not a toy. Also, while you’re not my servant, you’re still my disciple. Do you intend on staying as a disciple for the rest of your life?\"","\"Of course!\" Xiao Meilin answered without any hesitation.","Yuan rubbed his eyes and sighed, \"In that case, I have failed as your teacher and don’t qualify to be one anymore.\"","\"You’re acting pathetic, Elder Sister,\" said Xiao Hua. \"You should stop bothering Yuan.\"","\"That’s easy for you to say since you’re always following him around! I’ve been wondering for a long time now, but why did you get to go with him while I am stuck here? And did you just call him ’Yuan’?! What happened to Master Tian? Did you really regain all of your memories? Or did you hit your head somewhere after awakening?\"","\"Blame your own incompetence for not being chosen,\" Xiao Hua said with a calm sneer. \"I was chosen because I’m not only more talented and powerful than you but, more importantly, I’m not annoying like you.\"","\"You little bitch... are you looking for a fight with me now?\" Xiao Meilin’s eyebrows twitched nonstop at Xiao Hua’s provocation.","\"Stop it. Both of you.\" Yuan sighed.","Xiao Meilin gritted her teeth and fell silent, but it was only for a brief moment.","\"You didn’t answer my other question. Why are you suddenly calling him by his name? That’s disrespectful, and you should know that.\"","\"That’s none of your business,\" Xiao Hua said, refusing to answer.","Yuan then said, \"I told her to stop calling me Master Tian. I’m sure I asked you to do the same when we first met.\"","\"So not only is she annoying, but she’s also disobedient? Why am I not surprised?\" Xiao Hua chuckled.","Xiao Meilin trembled in anger, and her aura started to surge violently. However, before she could even say another word, Xiao Cangming hammered her head with his fist, instantly wiping away her killing intent.","\"Your inability to control your temper is exactly why I never allowed you to follow Yuan,\" he said calmly. \"Rather than be helpful, you’d only cause more trouble for him.\"","\"...\"","Xiao Meilin fell silent again.","\"Don’t be so down,\" Li Zhenwu finally spoke up. \"You can always temper your control, and now that we’ll be leaving the Primordial Realm, you’ll have plenty of chances to—\"","\"I know.\" Xiao Meilin interrupted, but she didn’t say more and fell silent again.","Some time later, Yuan spoke, \"I have been thinking about something. The Primordial Realm... It’s no longer filled with criminals like it was in the past, correct?\"","Xiao Cangming nodded, \"Yes, since most of the first generation are long dead. Why do you ask? Don’t tell me you want to...\"","Yuan smiled faintly. \"I wonder... would it be alright to open the Primordial Realm and let those who wish to leave do so?\"","He had been pondering this ever since his encounter with Wu Qi, and that thought had only deepened after witnessing the cultivators’ desperation.","Xiao Cangming responded seriously, \"Honestly, I have thought about this more than just a few times. While there are many who wish to leave this world, and we have the power to release them, the problem is what comes after.\"","\"If the current Celestial Emperor wanted to release us, he would’ve done so long ago,\" Xiao Cangming said with a faint bitterness in his tone. \"While it’s technically possible to leave through the Supreme Heaven’s Legacy, that so-called path is nothing but false hope—a cruel game that dangles freedom before the desperate. After all my time in the Primordial Realm, I can count on one hand those who’ve ever succeeded in fulfilling the legacy.\"","\"So what you’re saying is, we have to deal with the Celestial Emperor before we can release these people? I figured it would be like this.\" Yuan sighed.","\"After all, even if the people get to leave, as long as they have the exile’s branding on them, they won’t truly be free.\"","Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly and asked, \"This branding... what is it? It can’t be a curse since it didn’t appear when I used the Sacred Chalice of Purification on you.\"","Xiao Cangming shook his head.","\"I’m not sure either.\"","\"It’s a curse.\"","\"What?\"","Everyone in the room turned to Mu Xuelian, who’d just spoken.","\"Lord Shiva said it’s a curse.\"","\"Can you elaborate? If it’s a curse, why didn’t my Sacred Chalice of Purification activate? It’s a treasure that can remove all curses.\"","Shiva took control of Mu Xuelian’s body and beckoned Yuan, \"Show me that little treasure of yours.\"","Yuan didn’t question her and handed her the Sacred Chalice of Purification.","\"Hmph.\"","Shiva took a quick glance at it before tossing it back to Yuan as if it were trash.","\"The curse was created with the power of an Eternal. A broken toy like that won’t have any effect on it.\"","\"Wait a second...\" Yuan rubbed his eyes in a stressful manner and continued, \"So you’re telling me that not only is an Eternal involved, but my Sacred Chalice of Purification is a ’broken’ treasure? Even though it functions properly and is powerful enough to remove most curses in existence?\"","\"An Eternal also created that treasure, and I happen to know its creator,\" Shiva revealed.","\"What? An Eternal creating treasures?\" Yuan’s eyes widened at this information.","\"I didn’t even think an Eternal would show such interest.\"","Shiva snickered, \"Not even Gods are impervious to boredom, you know? And while that thing might be a treasure to you, it’s nothing but a toy in our eyes. In fact, most of the treasures that appear ’naturally’ in this world are our creation.\""]},{"number":2229,"title":"Chapter 2229: Forbidden Void Treasures","paragraphs":["\"The Eternals are the creators of natural treasures? You’ve got to be kidding me...\" Yuan mumbled in a bewildered voice after learning this information from Shiva.","\"Most people believe treasures are creations of the Heavens,\" Shiva continued, her tone laced with mockery. \"But that’s merely a delusion born from their ignorance of the unknown. Honestly, it’s quite hilarious.\"","Xiao Cangming then said, \"But I have witnessed treasures materializing out of thin air with my very eyes. It usually happens in places where spiritual energy is abundant.\"","\"Sorry to disappoint you, but that is also not ’natural’. As for how it’s achieved... It’s a little complicated, so I’ll save myself the trouble.\"","Yuan then spoke, \"I couldn’t care less how it’s done. I want to know why. I highly doubt the Eternals are putting these treasures in our world for fun.\"","Shiva smiled faintly and said, \"Then you underestimate how unbearably bored we become. We Eternals have existed since the dawn of time—you can’t even begin to fathom how many ages we’ve spent drifting alone in the void.\"","\"That said, I’m sure not every Eternal is doing it just for fun. Some probably don’t want to waste their effort or just want their toys to be used.\"","\"What about cursed treasures?\" Li Zhenwu asked. \"Those that possess great power but also carry dangerous backlashes.\"","\"Anything that you humans didn’t create was created by Eternals.\"","Yuan then spoke with a mocking tone. \"In that case, we humans aren’t far behind—and some of us might even surpass the Eternals in craftsmanship, considering how some of those natural treasures are complete trash.\"","\"Hahaha!\" Shiva suddenly burst out laughing.","Moments later, she stopped and said, \"How naive. Most of the treasures were made trash on purpose.\"","\"Why would they do something like that?\" Xiao Meilin asked.","\"Due to the absolute power, our influence in this world is heavily restricted, and that includes our creations. If we created treasures too powerful, they wouldn’t be able to enter this world.\"","\"Wait a second...\" Yuan suddenly spoke up. \"Are you referring to the Forbidden Void Treasures?\"","\"What are Forbidden Void Treasures?\" Xiao Chen asked with a puzzled look on his face.","\"There existed treasures born from the Starry Sky—found drifting within the endless void,\" Yuan explained. \"However, no matter the method, these treasures could never be brought back to the Nine Heavens, as though some unseen force forbade their entry into our world. That is why they came to be known as Forbidden Void Treasures.\"","\"I have never heard of such a thing until today,\" Xiao Cangming remarked, and he considered himself very knowledgeable.","\"Me neither,\" Xiao Meilin said.","\"Well, they weren’t discovered until after the Immortal Monarch’s Era came to an end,\" he said.","\"That explains it.\"","\"Anyway, you said my Sacred Chalice of Purification is broken? How can I fix it?\"","\"Fix it? You don’t have that capability.\" Shiva said while shaking her head.","\"I may not look like it, but I know a thing or two about crafting treasures,\" said Yuan.","\"So what? Even if you’re the best craftsman in the world, you won’t compare to an Eternal.\"","\"So it’s a matter of technique.\"","\"At least you get it.\"","Yuan may have been the God of Creation in the past with god-like abilities, but there’s a vast difference between god-like and truly godly skills. Not only that, but Eternals likely had their own crafting methods, so regardless of Yuan’s abilities, he wouldn’t be able to fix the treasures created by them until he acquired their techniques.","\"Then do you have any suggestions?\" Yuan then asked.","\"Who knows? Maybe I do, maybe I don’t. I’ll consider it if you ask me nicely.\"","Yuan sighed, \"If I had known you would be this useless, I wouldn’t have agreed to letting you follow me.\"","Shiva frowned at his obvious provocation and said, \"What an odd way of asking nicely.\"","Yuan silently shrugged.","After a moment of silence, Shiva spoke, \"If you do something for me, I’ll not only tell you how to restore that toy, but also teach you how we Eternals craft treasures.\"","\"What are you scheming?\" Yuan narrowed his eyes at her, clearly suspicious of whatever she was thinking.","\"I know of an Eternal who was sealed in this world even before me, and he’s very proficient when it comes to crafting. If you help me unseal him, I’ll persuade him to teach you his techniques.\"","\"Interesting,\" said Yuan. \"Can you tell me your relationship with this Eternal?\"","\"...\"","\"He’s something akin to a mentor to me.\"","\"Do you know where he’s being sealed?\"","\"I do.\"","Yuan pondered her offer for a moment before responding, \"Let me speak with him first. If I deem him to be a threat, I won’t unseal him.\"","\"Fine by me.\" Shiva nodded. \"I’ll give you more details after we leave this place.\"","\"Sure.\"","Yuan returned to talking about the Primordial Realm with the Asura Clan shortly after.","\"At the end of the day, as long as the Celestial Emperor is our enemy and the people’s exile brand remains, they won’t be able to live peacefully even if they leave this world, so we can only wait until after we deal with these two issues,\" said Yuan.","Xiao Cangming nodded, \"There are also a lot of other things that we must consider.\"","Some time later, Yuan asked them, \"Now then, are you all ready to leave the Primordial Realm?\"","\"I have been waiting for this moment since I was born,\" said Xiao Chen, his face full of excitement.","Yuan nodded.","\"Then we’ll leave in a week. If you need more time to pack your things, let me know.\"","Yuan retrieved a handful of spatial rings and placed them on the table.","\"You can use these.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Once everyone in the Asura Clan had a spatial ring, they left to pack their belongings.","However, Xiao Hua stayed behind since she had nothing to pack.","\"Yuan, I have a question,\" Xiao Hua suddenly spoke to him.","\"What is it?\"","\"Once we leave the Primordial Realm... will I still be able to follow you? Or am I going to have to stay with my family?\" she asked."]},{"number":2230,"title":"Chapter 2230: Leaving the Primordial Realm","paragraphs":["Yuan smiled and responded to Xiao Hua’s question, \"That will depend on you. If you want to continue following me, I have no reason to refuse. Of course, if you wish to stay with your family, I will also respect that decision.\"","\"I wish to continue following you!\" She immediately gave her answer.","He nodded with a warm smile.","\"What about me?\" Lingyue suddenly asked.","\"Of course, the same goes for you. What do you want to do?\"","\"I wouldn’t know what else to do if I were not by your side, Brother Yuan. If it’s possible, I would like to continue to follow you.\"","\"Then it’s decided.\"","Moments later, Lingyue entered Yuan’s Dantian to rest.","\"Wow, it’s so different in here,\" Lingyue remarked after seeing the Spirit Tree.","\"What do you think about it?\" Yuan asked.","\"It’s very comfortable in here because of the abundance of spiritual energy, and with the Spirit Tree constantly producing more spiritual energy, I can feel my cultivation improving just by being in here.\"","\"That’s good to hear.\"","Inside his Dantian, Lingyue faced Feng Yuxiang and Lan Yingying.","Lingyue offered them a sheepish smile as she spoke, \"Um... I know I’m not Xiao Hua, but I still have all her memories. Still, I don’t expect you to treat me the same as before, so—\"","\"What are you talking about?\" Feng Yuxiang cut her off. \"Xiao Hua or not, you were essentially the same person back then. Our bond with her is the same bond we share with you.\"","Lan Yingying nodded with a gentle smile, \"She’s right, so don’t suddenly start acting like we’re strangers.\"","\"Thank you, Senior Feng, Senior Lan...\" Lingyue spoke with teary eyes.","\"That’s not right. You can call me Senior Sister or Feng Feng.\"","\"You can also call me Sister Yingying.\"","\"Un. Senior Sister, Sister Yingying.\"","Feng Yuxiang then spoke, \"Also, I didn’t get to say this back then, but thank you for stopping Xiao Hua.\"","\"Please don’t mention it. I only did what I had to in order to protect Brother Yuan.\"","\"Still, you did what I couldn’t.\" Feng Yuxiang sighed in a dejected manner.","However, she didn’t stay dispirited for long, and she said, \"With that being said, I am still the Young Master’s number one servant.\"","\"Of course.\" Lingyue nodded with a bright smile.","Meanwhile, Xiao Hua said to Yuan, \"Since we have some time, there’s something I would like to do with you.\"","\"What is it?\"","Xiao Hua retrieved a book from her spatial ring and said, \"I would like to read you this book.\"","A nostalgic smile immediately appeared on Yuan’s face when he saw the book in Xiao Hua’s grasp.","\"Sure.\"","The two of them left the Asura Clan’s residence and took a seat under a nearby tree.","Some time later, Xiao Hua opened the book and began reading its contents.","Yuan listened with closed eyes.","<Your comprehension of Heaven’s Secret Art has improved significantly>","<Heaven’s Secret Arts Mastery Level has increased to level 5>","<Your comprehension of Heaven’s Secret Art has improved significantly>","<Heaven’s Secret Arts Mastery Level has increased to level 6>","\"...\"","A few hours later.","<Heaven’s Secret Arts Mastery Level has reached max level>","\"I know you already fully comprehended this technique in the past, but I still wanted to do this,\" Xiao Hua said as she closed the book.","Since Heaven’s Secret Arts had been with the Asura Clan even before they were sealed inside the Primordial Realm, Tian Xian had already learned and mastered it in the past.","Yuan smiled and said, \"It may not be the strongest technique out there, but it is definitely one of the most unique.\"","\"...\"","\"Yuan, before we leave the Primordial Realm, there is something I must tell you,\" Xiao Hua suddenly said. \"Although my soul has accepted this vessel, and there are no compatibility issues, my soul right now is greatly weakened, so even though I am at the peak of God Ascension, I won’t be able to use my full power until I recover enough.\"","\"Don’t worry, I won’t ask you to fight.\"","\"That’s not—\"","\"I know,\" Yuan interrupted. \"But even if you were in perfect condition and had the cultivation of a Cultivation God, I still wouldn’t want you to fight for me. At the end of the day, you’re a precious comrade, and unless absolutely necessary or we’re just messing around, I don’t want to put you in harm’s way.\"","\"Also, we have another expert at the peak of God Ascension with us, so if I ever encounter a threat I cannot handle, we still have her.\"","Xiao Hua quietly nodded.","Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, a week had passed.","The moment had finally come for Yuan and the Asura Clan to depart from the Primordial Realm.","\"Are you all ready to leave?\" Yuan asked them.","\"We are,\" said Xiao Cangming.","Without another word, Yuan retrieved the Ancient Key and used it to open a portal before them that would lead them straight outside.","\"Then, I’ll see you on the outside,\" Yuan said before entering the portal, disappearing from the Primordial Realm.","Mu Xuelian and Xiao Hua went afterward, followed by Xiao Chen, Li Zhenwu, the servants, and finally, Xiao Cangming.","Once outside, Yuan expected to find Dong Ye and the others waiting for him. However, the sight that greeted him was entirely different.","Dong Ye and the rest of the Shadow Army were still there, but they were locked in fierce battle against a vast force of cultivators. Over a thousand soldiers clad in armor filled the battlefield, each one emanating the aura of the God Ascension realm.","’Those guys! Heaven’s Mandate! Did the Celestial Emperor anticipate my plan to enter the Primordial Realm and set up an ambush here?’ Yuan pondered with a deep frown on his face.","\"My liege! Thank the lord! You’re out just in time!\" Dong Ye’s voice suddenly resounded through voice transmission.","\"What’s the situation?!\" Yuan asked.","\"As you can see, the Celestial Emperor’s dogs are here. A surprise inspection took place a few days ago, and although we were prepared for it, something unforeseen occurred, messing everything up! Long story short, the Celestial Emperor is now aware of the Primordial Realm being opened!\""]},{"number":2231,"title":"Chapter 2231: Outside the Primordial Realm","paragraphs":["\"What is going on out here? Why are we suddenly in the middle of a battlefield?\" Xiao Chen questioned with a dumbfounded look on his face after coming out of the Primordial Realm, the excitement on his face quickly replaced by confusion.","\"Their armor... They’re the Celestial Emperor’s lapdogs, the Heaven’s Mandate!\" Xiao Meilin’s eyes flickered with killing intent after seeing their familiar-looking armor.","Despite being in the Primordial Realm for tens of millions of years, she’d never forget the Heaven’s Mandate.","\"My lord—Yuan, what is the situation?\" Xiao Cangming asked him.","\"According to Dong Ye, there was a surprise inspection, which alerted the Celestial Emperor of our activity,\" he gave a brief explanation.","Xiao Cangming narrowed his eyes.","\"So, can we kill them all?\"","Yuan pondered for a moment before responding, \"Go help out Dong Ye and the Shadow Army, but be prepared to leave at any moment. Since the Celestial Emperor is aware of our activity, there’s a good chance more reinforcements will appear. We’re not prepared to fight the Celestial Emperor and his army right now.\"","Without another word, Xiao Cangming and the Asura Clan joined the battle.","Of course, Heaven’s Mandate had been aware of their presence since they left the Primordial Realm.","\"Exiles have escaped the Primordial Realm! Kill them all!\" The commander of the army shouted and commanded over a hundred God Ascension experts to deal with them.","Soon, the Asura Clan and Heaven’s Mandate clashed.","\"Hahaha! I never thought I would get to fight with the Celestial Emperor’s dogs so soon after leaving the Primordial Realm! How refreshing!\" Xiao Meilin laughed excitedly as her cultivation exploded outward.","\"Be careful! That exile is at the peak of God Ascension!\"","\"What?! How did she reach such a level within the Primordial Realm?! I thought there was no spiritual energy in that world!\"","The soldiers were both bewildered and puzzled by the Asura Clan’s unexpected prowess.","Most of the soldiers there were between the third level and the fifth level of God Ascension, so they were all powerless before Xiao Meilin.","\"God of War’s Astral Arts!\"","Despite his lack of cultivation, Xiao Cangming was still an unstoppable force on the battlefield with his martial techniques.","Yuan didn’t immediately join the battle and continued speaking with Dong Ye.","\"My liege, we’re only staying here to fight because you were still inside the Primordial Realm. Now that you’re out, we should leave this place as soon as possible,\" said Dong Ye.","\"Not only will there be more reinforcements later, but there’s a small chance the Celestial Emperor might even show up himself.\"","\"I agree. I’ll distract them while you withdraw with the Asura Clan.\"","\"You will? How are you going to do that?\"","\"I have my ways. However, there are a little too many people for me to do it right now, so I’ll start once we cut down their number some more.\"","\"I understand.\"","\"Time to warm up,\" Yuan mumbled to himself when he noticed several presences approaching him.","When he turned to look at them, he could see four soldiers soaring directly at him, and the strongest amongst them was only at the third level of God Ascension.","\"Let me deal with them for you,\" Xiao Hua suddenly said.","\"No, you should save your energy and focus on recovering your soul. I can handle them without breaking a sweat.\"","\"Okay...\"","Without another word, Xiao Hua entered his Dantian.","Shortly after, the soldiers arrived and surrounded Yuan.","\"You’re not an exile. Who the hell are you?\"","The soldiers questioned him when they couldn’t sense the aura of an exile on him.","\"I’m the one who went inside the Primordial Realm and freed those people,\" Yuan calmly responded.","\"A mere Immortal like you? You have no idea what you got yourself into!\"","\"Let’s not kill him and capture him instead. We’ll need to question him,\" one of them said.","\"Good idea.\"","Yuan chuckled and said, \"I’d like to see you try.\"","The very next moment, Yuan retrieved Number One Under Heaven and struck first, attacking the strongest amongst them.","Despite his sudden attack, none of the soldiers seemed concerned. If anything, they sneered in disdain.","\"How foolish.\"","The soldier targeted by Yuan muttered as he raised his weapon to block the incoming attack.","However, Yuan’s aura suddenly exploded right before he struck.","Not only did he activate True Dragon Awakening, but he also enhanced his prowess with Chaotic Essence.","Before they left the Primordial Realm and while the Asura Clan prepared for their departure, Yuan approached Xiao Cangming to see if he had any Chaos Coins for him to consume.","As the most influential and powerful family in the Primordial Realm, the Asura Clan was naturally unfathomably rich. Although most of their wealth was made up of the Inferno Alchemists’ currency, they also held currencies from the other two powerhouses.","In the end, Yuan was able to acquire around a hundred billion small Chaos Coins, ten times the amount he attained from selling the spirit stone. And with that amount of Chaos Coins, he was able to advance his second cultivation to the peak of Chaotic Immortal, which was equivalent to a True Immortal who was on the verge of entering God Ascension realm. However, for Yuan, in terms of prowess, he could easily rival a third-level God Ascension cultivator if he used it to enhance his strength.","\"W-What the hell is that ridiculous power?! Is he really a True Immortal?!\" The soldiers cried out in shock after witnessing his overwhelming prowess.","As for the soldier targeted by Yuan, he had died in a single strike because he had underestimated Yuan and failed to block his attack.","After killing the first soldier, Yuan immediately turned his attention to the next closest one.","Seeing this, the other two soldiers quickly reacted and went to help their comrade.","However, not only were they unable to save their comrade, but they also died at the hands of Yuan in a single strike."]},{"number":2232,"title":"Chapter 2232: An Otherworldly Presence","paragraphs":["After defeating the four soldiers, Yuan immediately went to assist the others.","\"Fuck! Who the hell are these bastards?!\"","The commander of the soldiers trembled in anger after witnessing how badly they were losing to the Asura Clan.","\"Wait a second! That technique he just used! Why does it look so familiar?!\"","Although he didn’t realize it at first, the commander slowly started to recognize the Asura Clan’s martial techniques.","\"Their overwhelming killing intent... those techniques... don’t tell me—! The Asura Clan?!\"","Even though he had never fought against the Asura Clan or seen their techniques before, the commander was almost certain of their identity.","Due to the Asura Clan’s immense reputation and their pivotal role in the Heavenly War of Immortals and Gods, their legacy remained ingrained in history and taught to every new soldier of Heaven’s Mandate, even to this very day.","Even so, the commander could hardly believe it.","\"The Asura Clan—second only to the Evil God in their contributions in their war against the first Celestial Emperor—has escaped the Primordial Realm?! No! I cannot allow them to leave alive!\" the commander barked, clenching his fists.","He immediately retrieved a communication jade slip and requested more reinforcements even though he’d already done so earlier.","\"Send the reinforcements immediately, and send as much as you can! The Asura Clan has escaped from the Primordial Realm!\"","The receiver of the commander’s transmission jolted in shock upon hearing the message.","\"The Asura Clan?! I must notify His Majesty, the Celestial Emperor, immediately!\" he exclaimed, his voice trembling with disbelief.","Without even the slightest delay, the man rushed to find the Celestial Emperor. However, he was stopped at the Celestial Palace’s front gate.","\"What do you want now, Messenger Huang?\" The guard asked the messenger.","\"This is about the Primordial Realm! I must speak with the Celestial Emperor as soon as possible! It’s an emergency!\"","\"The Primordial Realm? The reinforcements are already on their way.\"","\"No! You don’t understand! I just received news from Commander Lee that some exiles have just escaped from the Primordial Realm, and they’re the Asura Clan!\"","\"Asura Clan...?\" The name didn’t immediately register in the guard’s mind.","\"The Asura Clan?!\"","However, once he realized the severity of the issue, he immediately opened the gates to allow the messenger through.","Some time later, the messenger reached the Celestial Emperor’s room. But he was stopped at the door again.","\"Messenger Huang? What are you doing here?\"","The messenger immediately repeated what he said to the guard outside.","\"The Asura Clan, you say?!\"","The guard quickly retrieved a communication jade slip and relayed the information to the other holder.","Moments later, the door behind him started to open, and a servant walked out.","\"His Majesty, the Celestial Emperor, is already aware of the Asura Clan’s situation. You may return.\"","Without waiting for a response, the servant closed the doors.","\"The Celestial Emperor is already aware? Did he predict this would happen?\" The messenger mumbled to himself before leaving the Celestial Palace shortly after.","Meanwhile, the Celestial Emperor stood calmly before a massive device, staring at the slumbering figures shown within it.","\"The Asura Clan... the ones who fought beside the Evil God, Tian Xian, against the first Celestial Emperor, huh?\" he muttered with a faint smirk. \"They may have been formidable once, but now they’re nothing more than ancient relics—hardly worth mentioning.\"","Suddenly, his entire body stiffened as he caught sight of movement from one of the slumbering figures. What began as faint, almost imperceptible twitches soon grew more pronounced, rippling through the stillness of the void.","A wide smile appeared on the Celestial Emperor’s face as he rejoiced, \"At last!\"","Meanwhile, outside the Primordial Realm, Yuan and the Asura Clan had cut down more than half of Heaven’s Mandate’s forces.","\"Alright, all of you, prepare to leave.\" Yuan sent a voice transmission to everyone from the Asura Clan and the Shadow Army.","Yuan suddenly stopped moving and started gathering his spiritual energy, even using his Eternal Essence.","A few moments later, his aura exploded forward, enveloping everyone there.","\"What is he trying to do?!\"","The soldiers of Heaven’s Mandate were instantly alerted and turned their attention to him.","\"Heaven’s Seventh Art — Heaven’s Grand Snare!\"","In the next instant, hundreds of golden chains materialized around Yuan and lashed outward toward the soldiers, as if seeking to ensnare them.","The soldiers hastily launched counterattacks, but to their horror, their spiritual energy scattered the moment it touched the chains, rendering their techniques utterly useless.","As for those who struck using their weapons, not even Mythic-grade treasures were able to put a mark on the chains, almost as if they were indestructible.","Some tried to flee, but the golden chains moved at the speed of light, outspeeding them with ease.","\"What the fuck is this?!\" The soldiers cried out loud as the golden chains wrapped around their bodies, restricting their movements while sealing their cultivation at the same time.","\"Now! Leave!\" Yuan commanded them to leave once he had captured nearly every single soldier there.","Without hesitation, Dong Ye retrieved a treasure and immediately created an escape portal.","\"Over here!\"","Seeing the portal, the Shadow Army and the Asura Clan quickly rushed toward it.","While the others escaped, Yuan focused on maintaining the technique. Since he had to use the technique on hundreds of God Ascension cultivators, his spiritual energy was being drained at a drastic rate.","Yet, with his powerful cultivation speed, Yuan was able to restore his spiritual energy just fast enough to barely keep up with the demand.","\"My liege, everyone has safely escaped!\"","Hearing Dong Ye’s words, Yuan deactivated the technique and rushed toward the portal, as he was unable to move while using the technique.","However, right before reaching the portal, Yuan suddenly stopped moving.","\"My liege?! What are you waiting for?! The portal will close soon!\" Dong Ye exclaimed.","Yuan gritted his teeth and responded with voice transmission, \"Something is restricting my movements!\"","\"What?!\"","Before Yuan could say another word, an unfathomable presence suddenly descended, enveloping the space around him with an otherworldly presence.","\"This presence... an Eternal!\"","Yuan’s brows furrowed into a frown after recognizing the identity of the presence."]},{"number":2233,"title":"Chapter 2233: The Appearance of an Eternal","paragraphs":["\"Dong Ye, listen to me carefully. Close the portal immediately. An Eternal is coming,\" Yuan said.","\"What?! What about you, my liege?!\"","\"I cannot move my body right now, let alone leave. It’s clear that this Eternal has business with me, and that it won’t let me leave.\"","\"Are you telling me to leave you to face a God alone?! Impossible! I will return to assist you!\" Dong Ye exclaimed.","\"Dong Ye, are you disobeying me right now?\" Yuan spoke in a cold tone.","\"That’s not—\"","\"Even if you are here with me, what can you achieve? Can you fight a God?\" Yuan interrupted in a cold tone.","\"No... I cannot...\"","As much as he hated to admit it, Dong Ye stood no chance against an Eternal and would only be a burden.","A calm smile appeared on Yuan’s face as he spoke, \"Have you forgotten who I am? This isn’t my first time dealing with them. I’ll return once I deal with the Eternal.\"","\"I understand. Please, be safe, my liege.\"","The portal started closing the very next moment, leaving Yuan stranded in the Primordial Chaos with the remaining soldiers of Heaven’s Mandate and an incoming Eternal.","\"Where is Yuan? Why did you close the portal?\" Xiao Cangming demanded after seeing the portal close, his expression darkening into a deep frown as killing intent flickered in his sharp gaze.","\"I swear... If you’d betrayed us...\"","Xiao Meilin and the others subconsciously reached for their weapons.","\"Don’t you dare mock me! Even if it’s you, I won’t stand for such slander!\" Dong Ye snapped back, his voice full of anger.","\"Then why the hell did you—\"","\"It was his liege who commanded me to close the portal! He was halted by a God before he could enter the portal!\"","\"What?! An Eternal appeared?!\" Xiao Cangming’s eyes widened with disbelief. \"Then we need to go back and—\"","\"And do what?! We may be powerful, but we’re nothing but ants in the eyes of these Gods! Only his liege has the power to face them!\"","Xiao Cangming fell silent at Dong Ye’s words, the tone of defeat in his voice leaving no room for response.","\"We’d only get in his way if we were there,\" Dong Ye continued with a deep sigh. \"The only thing we can do now is wait for his return.\"","\"Hey, let me go.\"","A voice suddenly resounded.","\"What?\" Dong Ye turned to look at Mu Xuelian, who’d just spoken. \"Did you not hear what I just—\"","\"You may not be able to handle an Eternal, but don’t compare me to you mortals.\"","\"What the hell are you...?\"","\"There is an Eternal residing in her body,\" said Xiao Cangming.","\"What?!\" Dong Ye jumped in a startled manner.","After snapping out of his daze, Dong Ye spoke, \"In that case, you might be able to help my liege!\"","\"Help? You’re misunderstanding something. I won’t be helping him.\"","Dong Ye frowned at her words, but before he could say anything, Mu Xuelian, now controlled by Shiva, continued, \"I am an observer—his observer, so I want to witness his fight with the Eternal. That brat dared to claim that he could put Eternals to sleep, so I want to witness it myself.\"","\"With that being said, if he begs me to save his life, I might consider it.\"","Dong Ye gritted his teeth when he saw Shiva’s sadistic expression.","\"What are you waiting for? Hurry up. I don’t want to miss the show,\" she urged him.","\"Fuck! Whatever!\"","Dong Ye activated the treasure, creating a portal that led back to Yuan.","Without hesitation, Shiva walked into the portal,","\"Are you sure that was a wise move?\" Xiao Meilin asked.","\"What else was I supposed to do? If she’s really a God, nobody here can defy her. Also, despite what she said, I doubt she’d really let him die.\"","Xiao Cangming nodded in agreement, \"I don’t know why she’s following Yuan, but I’m sure she won’t let him die so easily.\"","Meanwhile, Yuan let out a deep sigh as the portal closed before him. He then shifted his gaze toward the soldiers who had taken the opportunity to surround him while his movements were restricted.","\"I don’t know why you didn’t escape while you had the chance, but you won’t be going anywhere now,\" said the commander.","Yuan smiled and calmly responded, \"If you guys value your lives, you should leave while you still can.\"","\"Still acting tough? I don’t know what martial technique you used to restrict our movements, but I bet it’d exhausted your cultivation, and I doubt you will be able to do it again. Maybe it’s the reason why you cannot move right now.\"","Suddenly, the space before Yuan twisted.","\"What the?\"","Yuan’s eyes widened as the portal that had closed moments ago reopened, and a beautiful figure emerged from it.","\"Mu Xuelian...? No... Shiva.\" Yuan mumbled after seeing her beautiful face. \"What are you doing, coming back here?\"","\"Did you really think I would give up the opportunity to watch you clash against an Eternal?\" Shiva responded as the portal closed behind her. \"Don’t worry, I won’t ruin your fun, as I am only here as a spectator.\"","\"How twisted.\" Yuan sighed.","\"I don’t know what the hell is going on, but—\" The commander began, only to be cut off as an unfathomable pressure suddenly descended, crushing the air around him.","\"W-What the hell is this pressure?!\" he exclaimed in a terrified voice, his body trembling uncontrollably. It wasn’t just him. Every single soldier there was shaking like they were naked in a blizzard.","\"Speaking of the devil...\" Shiva mumbled with a calm smile on her face.","\"You had your chance to leave, but alas...\" Yuan sighed.","\"Run! Get away from here as soon as possible!\" The commander roared, shouting at his soldiers.","Yet, none of the soldiers left, as they were all frozen in fear.","As the pressure intensified, agonized screams resounded. One by one, the soldiers’ bodies began to swell like overfilled balloons until they burst apart in a gruesome chain reaction, starting with those of the weakest cultivation."]},{"number":2234,"title":"Chapter 2234: Fighting an Eternal","paragraphs":["\"What the hell is going on?! What did you do to us?!\" The commander shouted at Yuan for answers, thinking he was responsible for the situation.","Yuan calmly replied, \"I didn’t do anything. Hell, I was even nice enough to give you a warning. Unfortunately, you didn’t heed it, and as a result, you’ll die.\"","In mere seconds, all of the soldiers perished under the pressure.","\"AHHHH!\" The commander—stronger than the rest—managed to endure the crushing pressure for a few moments longer before unleashing a final, agonized scream. Moments later, his body erupted violently, and his soul was instantly annihilated, leaving him no chance to escape.","Though the soldiers of Heaven’s Mandate had been annihilated, Yuan couldn’t afford to relax, as the true threat was rapidly approaching.","Moments later, a massive, ethereal figure materialized before Yuan. It had no physical form, its ghostly body wavered like mist, yet it radiated an overwhelming aura of malice that seemed to corrode the very space around it.","Of course, it was no ordinary aura, as it was formed from Eternal Essence, and the sheer concentration of it far surpassed anything Yuan had attained thus far.","\"Did you really have to kill them? Aren’t they on your side?\" Yuan asked.","\"What nonsense are you uttering?\" The Eternal responded in a coarse voice.","Yuan raised an eyebrow at the unexpected response.","\"The Celestial Emperor didn’t send you here?\"","\"The Celestial Emperor...?\" The Eternal repeated in a puzzled voice. \"Have you already forgotten about this Mighty Saaruk? Even though you were acting so boldly not too long ago?\"","\"You’re Saaruk?!\" Yuan exclaimed after realizing the Eternal’s identity.","\"I didn’t think you’d come after me so soon. Are you really that impatient?\"","\"Hahaha! Are you trembling in fear? Do you regret opposing this Mighty Saaruk?!\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan responded, \"To be honest, I was expecting more from an Eternal ranked in the top 20.\"","\"Hmph!\" Saaruk sneered. \"Because we’re still within the Absolute Power’s influence, I can appear only in this ethereal form, and while in this form, I can wield barely ten percent of my true strength.\"","Saaruk had originally planned to wait until Yuan left the Absolute Power’s domain before making good on his threat, but impatience won out, so he arrived ahead of time at the cost of this inconvenience.","\"Even though I am only wielding 10 percent of my true prowess, it’s more than enough to handle an ant like you,\" Saaruk mocked.","\"We’ll see about that,\" Yuan replied.","\"There’s nothing to see when you can’t even break out of such a simple restraint.\"","Saaruk pointed at Yuan, who still had his movements restricted by an invisible force.","\"You mean this little trick?\"","Yuan’s body suddenly erupted with Eternal Essence, and within moments, he shattered the restraints binding him.","Saaruk didn’t react to Yuan breaking free. Instead, his gaze shifted toward Shiva, who hovered calmly nearby, watching the scene unfold with the detached air of a spectator.","\"How unexpected,\" Saaruk said, his tone laced with disdain. \"This Mighty Saaruk hadn’t anticipated encountering another Eternal here, much less someone like you, Shiva. When did you regain your freedom?\"","\"Very recently,\" she calmly replied.","\"Who helped you break out of the seal? Don’t tell me... this ant?\"","\"...\"","Shiva didn’t respond.","\"Hahaha!\" Saaruk burst into laughter, his voice echoing like thunder. \"Truly hilarious! To think an Eternal would stoop so low as to seek help from a mere mortal! Did you lose your pride during the time you were sealed?\"","\"I can’t wait for Ishrak to hear about this! I wonder how he’ll react to you breaking out of his seal. Maybe he’ll track you down to seal you again.\"","Shiva’s eyes flickered with immense killing intent after hearing the name Ishrak.","\"How dare you speak his name in my presence? I’d love to make you pay for it, but I’ll let him deal with you today,\" she growled.","\"You will make this Mighty Saaruk pay?\" Saaruk started laughing again. \"With what? That mortal body? You won’t be able to defeat this Mighty Saaruk even if you had your eternal body, much less in that trash!\"","Enraged by Saaruk’s provocation, Shiva erupted in a burst of Eternal Essence. The surge was overwhelming, and Mu Xuelian, merely a mortal, could not withstand it and started bleeding from her orifices.","\"Hey, what the hell are you doing? Have you forgotten that body doesn’t belong to you? Or are you trying to kill Mu Xuelian?\" Yuan frowned after seeing this.","\"If you’re just going to observe, do it properly.\"","\"...\"","Upon hearing Yuan’s words, Shiva quickly calmed down and immediately withdrew her Eternal Essence before starting to heal Mu Xuelian’s injuries.","\"To think you’d shut Shiva up with so little effort. Not bad, mortal,\" Saaruk remarked with a mocking smile.","\"Are you done talking? If so, let’s get this over with. I have other business to attend to.\"","\"Do you really want to die so quickly? Unfortunately for you, this Mighty Saaruk has no plan on letting you die a swift death. It’ll be a slow and painful one.\"","Without another word, Yuan activated True Dragon Awakening and retrieved Number One Under Heaven before making the first move.","However, wary of Saaruk and his unknown power, Yuan kept his distance and attacked using Supreme Sword Aura.","Saaruk didn’t move an inch, showing no intent to defend himself. When the Supreme Sword Aura struck him, it fractured instantly—shattering like glass against an invisible wall—leaving Saaruk completely unharmed.","\"Using a mortal’s power on this Mighty Saaruk... You’re nothing but talk.\" Saaruk shook his head in disappointment while a thick layer of Eternal Essence shrouded his entire form.","Of course, having fought Eternals before, Yuan was well aware that only Eternal Essence would be able to harm them. However, he’d never fought an Eternal in their ethereal form, so he had to do some tests.","\"Don’t just stand there now. Come. Keep entertaining this Mighty Saaruk. This Mighty Saaruk won’t attack until you realize that you are powerless before this Mighty Saaruk and fall into despair,\" Saaruk beckoned Yuan, his voice full of arrogance."]},{"number":2235,"title":"Chapter 2235: Mighty Saaruk!","paragraphs":["Despite Saaruk’s provocation, Yuan remained calm.","\"Since you insist, I’ll continue doing just that,\" he said as he continued trying different things.","From martial techniques to spiritual techniques such as True Primordial Fire, Heaven’s Final Judgement, and even Heaven’s Bane. Yet, they were all useless against Saaruk and his Eternal Essence. It was akin to trying to destroy a brick wall with nothing but raw eggs.","\"You’re much more foolish than I thought, mortal ant,\" Saaruk laughed loudly at Yuan’s futile efforts.","Even Shiva couldn’t help but feel agitated at Yuan.","\"What the hell are you doing?! Are you seriously messing around before an Eternal?!\" she yelled at him using voice transmission.","\"Does it really look like I am messing around?\" he asked.","\"Yes, it does! Now start fighting him seriously, or you’ll really die!\"","Yuan sighed inwardly..","The next moment, his aura shifted drastically, and Eternal Essence surged from his entire being.","Saaruk narrows his eyes at the sight.","\"A mortal being using Eternal Essence, what an odd and unpleasant sight,\" he muttered with a disgusted expression.","To Saaruk, watching Yuan wield something meant only for Eternals was like seeing a pig pretend to be human—not just distasteful, but downright offensive.","However, amidst his disdain, Saaruk was also astonished by Yuan’s achievement. He couldn’t fathom how a mere mortal could have learned to wield Eternal Essence, as it wasn’t something that could be taught.","After all, most humans would perish just from learning about the existence of Eternals, much less learning and wielding their powers.","He looked at Shiva and wondered if she had anything to do with it.","\"The real fight will start now,\" Yuan said.","Then, without warning, he launched his strike.","An overwhelming amount of Eternal Essence engulfed Number One Under Heaven, and it unleashed a devastating sword light that was made entirely out of Eternal Essence.","Yet, despite knowing that Yuan’s strike contained Eternal Essence and could potentially harm him, Saaruk didn’t lift even a finger, almost as if he still had no intention of blocking it.","In the next instant, Yuan’s Eternal Essence collided head-on with Saaruk. Unlike his earlier techniques, it didn’t shatter upon impact, but even so, it failed to break through Saaruk’s barrier.","Not only did it fail to break through, but it was even absorbed by Saaruk.","\"So this is what Eternal Essence created by a mortal ant tastes like. As expected, it’s weak and disgusting.\"","Saaruk narrowed his eyes at Yuan and spoke in a disinterested tone, \"This won’t do. At this rate, forget about entertaining this Mighty Saaruk. You’ll bore this Mighty Saaruk to death instead.\"","The very next moment, the Eternal Essence around Saaruk became violent, and his aura surged. Then, he vanished into the void.","Yuan became as still as a statue as he searched for Saaruk, but his divine sense picked up nothing.","Suddenly, a numbing sensation crawled up Yuan’s back, and he instinctively turned—only to find Saaruk standing behind him like a ghost, silent and menacing.","’That was the Power of the Void!’ Yuan realized what Saaruk just did because of his own understanding of the Power of the Void.","\"This Mighty Saaruk could’ve killed you a hundred times just now,\" said Saaruk.","\"Then why didn’t you?\"","\"Because this Mighty Saaruk has yet to torture you for daring to bare your fangs at a God. However, it will start now.\"","Saaruk raised a single finger, forming a ’small’ spear-like projectile with Eternal Essence before shooting it at Yuan.","Saaruk’s ethereal form was vast—large enough to rival a small planet—so to Yuan, it truly felt as though he were an ant fighting against a giant.","When Yuan attempted to block Saaruk’s strike, he was immediately sent flying deeper into the void.","’The difference is immense! And he can only use 10 percent of his full prowess?!’ Yuan cried inwardly.","Even without witnessing Saaruk’s full power, Yuan could tell that this Eternal far surpassed any he had faced before. The realization struck him hard—that the Eternals he’d once battled were nothing more than small fry in comparison.","\"Do you understand the difference between us now, you insignificant mortal ant?\" Saaruk mocked after seeing how far Yuan was thrown.","\"...I’ll admit that you’re a little stronger than I anticipated. However, it doesn’t change anything, as I will still defeat you in the end,\" he said.","\"...\"","Saaruk remained silent, but the displeasure in his gaze was as clear as day.","\"A mere lowly mortal ant...\" he suddenly mumbled. \"I’ve had enough of your disrespect and arrogance.\"","Without another word, Saaruk charged at Yuan, his entire figure engulfed with overwhelming Eternal Essence.","Yuan didn’t falter and charged straight into close-quarters combat with Saaruk. Despite channeling every ounce of Eternal Essence he could muster, he was steadily forced back, overwhelmed by Saaruk’s sheer might.","\"...\"","Shiva watched in silence. Even though Yuan was losing to Saaruk, she was still impressed by his prowess, as this was her first time witnessing a human fighting an Eternal.","’No mortal has ever defied an Eternal before, much less directly clash with them,’ she sighed inwardly.","Yuan had been fighting Saaruk for an entire week at this point.","’It’s a pity that he offended someone like Saaruk. Although our journey was short, it was enjoyable while it lasted.’","Without a word or warning, Shiva’s figure suddenly vanished into the void. In her eyes, Yuan’s defeat was inevitable, and once he fell to Saaruk, she would be targeted next.","\"Lord Shiva, are we really going to leave him alone?\" Mu Xuelian asked as they traversed using the Power of the Void.","\"His fate is already sealed. There is no point staying around and waiting for our turn. It’s unfortunate, but there’s nothing I can do against another Eternal while I am in this condition.\"","\"What are we going to do now?\" Mu Xuelian then asked.","\"We’ll focus on strengthening your body and cultivation. Once prepared, we’ll start looking for my body.\"","\"I understand.\"","Even if Mu Xuelian didn’t want to abandon Yuan, she had no choice in the matter. After all, Shiva could take control over her body at any time, and her orders were absolute.","Shortly after Shiva left, Saaruk noticed their disappearance.","\"Hahaha! Shiva, that coward!\" Saaruk roared with laughter. \"To think she’d flee while her savior lies on the brink of death!\"","His mocking voice echoed as he gazed at Yuan—bloodied, exhausted, and barely conscious.","Despite having powerful regeneration, Saaruk’s Eternal Essence seemed to have a property that weakened his regenerative abilities.","\"Young Master! This monster is too powerful! I’ll distract him while you escape!\" Feng Yuxiang’s voice suddenly responded in Yuan’s head.","\"I will also help,\" Xiao Hua then said.","\"...\"","Lan Yingying and Lingyue also wanted to help, but they were too weak to even do anything.","\"No, I won’t allow that,\" Yuan immediately refused.","\"Then what do you suggest?! You’ll die to that monster at this rate!\" Feng Yuxiang exclaimed.","\"Just a little more...\" Yuan responded.","\"What?\"","\"Just give me a little more time.\"","Without explaining further, Yuan temporarily sealed off his connection with them, so their voices could no longer reach him.","\"Young Master?!\" Feng Yuxiang was left baffled and confused.","\"Let’s just believe in him,\" Lan Yingying suddenly said. \"I don’t think Yuan has any plans on dying here, especially not when we’re still with him.\"","\"I want to believe him, but I have never seen the Young Master in such a bad state before,\" Feng Yuxiang sighed.","\"What’s wrong, mortal ant? You’ve gotten quiet.\" Saaruk spoke.","Yuan smiled and said, \"I don’t blame Shiva for leaving. There was nothing she could do, anyway.\"","\"That’s because she’s weak. If she were even half as strong as this Mighty Saaruk, she wouldn’t have been sealed away in the first place.\"","\"Anyway, this Mighty Saaruk has wasted enough time on you. You should feel honored to have fought and died at the hands of this Mighty Saaruk.\"","\"What’s the rush? I’m not done yet.\" Yuan said as his weakened aura suddenly started surging again.","However, Saaruk didn’t even bat an eye and said, \"No, you’re done. The only reason you even lasted this long is because this Mighty Saaruk allowed you. Moreover, your Eternal Essence is too weak to do anything.\"","\"If it’s too weak, then I just need to strengthen it.\"","\"Strengthen it? Hahaha! You’re just a mortal ant! Regardless of how you learned how to wield Eternal Essence, only true Eternals can strengthen it!\"","Saaruk was unaware of Yuan having a true Eternal Constitution, hence why he doesn’t believe Yuan could strengthen his Eternal Essence.","Without a word, Yuan suddenly closed his eyes and took a deep breath.","\"It took some time, but I can finally feel the ’essence’ of the void,\" he mumbled a second later.","\"What...?\" Saaruk’s eyes widened at his words.","<Eternal Constitution(Incomplete) activated>","<Eternal Constitution(Incomplete) has begun refining ’???’>","A moment later, Yuan started absorbing the essence of the void.","\"Y-You! Are you actually trying to absorb essence from the void?!\" Saaruk exclaimed, his voice filled with shock for some reason."]},{"number":2236,"title":"Chapter 2236: Essence of the Void","paragraphs":["When Yuan started attempting to refine the essence of the void, Saaruk didn’t intervene. In fact, he even watched with intrigue, almost as if he wanted to see the results.","’A mortal ant wants to absorb the essence of the void? How laughable! Even Eternals with a true Eternal Constitution struggle to do so!’ Saaruk sneered inwardly.","Unlike spiritual energy or any other known force, the void was something entirely different. Though it enveloped most of the universe, even experts with millions of years of cultivation failed to comprehend it, let alone wield it. For that reason, the Power of the Void was regarded as the most difficult and enigmatic path in all of cultivation.","This held true even for the Eternals, gods of the universe. While their boundless experience and knowledge allowed them to comprehend the Power of the Void, refining its essence was an entirely different matter altogether.","Because of this, Saaruk had been utterly shocked when Yuan claimed he could sense the essence of the void. And when Yuan went so far as to attempt refining it, Saaruk couldn’t resist witnessing it himself—to see whether a mere mortal could truly accomplish the impossible despite already knowing the answer.","’There’s no way he’ll be able to refine the essence of the void. The moment he attempts to do so and fails, his entire being will be erased from existence. Although this means this Mighty Saaruk won’t be able to kill the mortal ant with his own hands, it’ll be worth it!’ Saaruk laughed inwardly.","While Saaruk watched with excitement and anticipation of his gruesome death, Yuan calmly refined the essence of the void.","’He’s not doing anything to stop me? So he must be confident that I would fail or that I still wouldn’t be able to defeat him...’ Yuan thought to himself after seeing Saaruk’s reaction.","’Whatever his reason is, this is beneficial for me, so there’s no reason for me to stop here.’","Without a moment’s hesitation, Yuan started refining the essence of the void that existed in every direction and even further than he could perceive.","<You have refined the ’essence’ of ???>","<Your understanding of the Power of the Void has increased significantly>","Yuan was pleasantly surprised to see his comprehension of the Power of the Void improve in such a manner.","He could also feel an immense amount of energy flowing into him, causing his Eternal Essence to strengthen quickly.","However—","’As expected, this isn’t going to be easy!’","Yuan gritted his teeth as an overwhelming pressure built within him, threatening to tear his body apart. The essence of the void was so fierce and volatile that it reminded him of the time he had attempted to refine the Dragon God’s blood essence.","But unlike that time when Dragon Goddess Yeyou assisted him, nobody could help him refine the essence of the void at this moment.","Suddenly, Yuan’s body started swelling up like a balloon with blood seeping from his pores. It was a weird and gruesome sight that would make even experts churn.","\"Hahaha! That’s what you get for trying to refine the essence of the void when you’re a mere mortal!\" Saaruk burst out laughing.","However, moments later, Yuan’s body started returning to normal, and his aura grew fiercer.","Saaruk’s laughter halted immediately, his eyes wide with shock and disbelief.","\"Impossible!\" he exclaimed.","<Your understanding of the Power of the Void has increased significantly>","<Your understanding of the Power of the Void has reached the next realm>","<You have acquired Advanced Void Understanding>","<Your understanding of the Power of the Void has increased significantly>","<Your Void Manipulation has reached a new level>","Even as he achieved Advanced Void Understanding, Yuan continued to improve his void mastery just as fast as before.","A few minutes later, once Saaruk confirmed that Yuan could, in fact, refine the essence of the void, he clenched his fists and mumbled to himself, \"This cannot happen.\"","\"This Mighty Saaruk will not permit a mere mortal to touch something that is too good for him!\"","To Saaruk, watching Yuan refine the essence of the void—something only Eternals were meant to touch—was like seeing a pig sit at the same dinner table and eating the same food as humans. The sight didn’t just anger and disgust him; it drove his fury to the very brink.","Without hesitation, Saaruk immediately went for a killing blow while Yuan was still immersed in his refinement.","However, just as Saaruk reached him, Yuan suddenly opened his eyes, which flickered with newfound strength.","Although he’d only spent a few minutes refining the essence of the void, it had not only fully recovered his strength but also improved it drastically. That was just how powerful the essence of the void was.","Without the slightest hesitation in his movements, Yuan went to block Saaruk, who struck with all of his strength in a fit of anger.","\"This is...!\"","Even though Saaruk was in an ethereal form, Yuan could tell that he was trembling in anger after having his attack blocked.","\"This is your second time underestimating a human,\" said Yuan. \"It will also be your second time being defeated by one.\"","Yuan’s aura erupted, his Eternal Essence surging outward like a tidal wave that crashed violently against Saaruk.","\"If you think you can defeat this Mighty Saaruk just because you refined some essence of the void, you’re greatly mistaken! This Mighty Saaruk has been refining the essence of the void for countless years!\"","\"Had you fought with your full strength, I wouldn’t have stood a chance, but that’s not the case, is it?\" Yuan remarked with a calm smile.","Even as they clashed, Yuan continued refining the essence of the void, his Eternal Essence steadily evolving—growing denser, sharper, and gradually surpassing Saaruk’s own.","Eventually, Yuan’s Eternal Essence grew strong enough to overwhelm Saaruk, allowing him to reach Saaruk’s ethereal form.","\"Argh!\" Saaruk roared in agony as Yuan’s strike pierced him, inflicting pain upon him for the first time.","\"To think a mere mortal ant would inflict pain upon this Mighty Saaruk! This Mighty Saaruk will never forget this humiliation!\""]},{"number":2237,"title":"Chapter 2237: Enraged Saaruk","paragraphs":["Realizing he could no longer overpower Yuan, Saaruk abruptly withdrew, putting distance between them, as if he’d lost all intention of continuing the fight.","\"Where the hell do you think you’re going?!\" Yuan shouted as Saaruk pulled farther away. \"Don’t tell me you’re running! A god fleeing from a mere mortal?! That’s hilarious!\"","Yuan didn’t bother giving chase. He knew that if Saaruk truly intended to flee, there was no way he could catch him.","\"Running away? This Mighty Saaruk?\" Saaruk sneered in disdain at the thought of running away.","\"Even if this Mighty Saaruk has to suffer a little, this Mighty Saaruk will make sure you die here today!\"","Suddenly, Saaruk’s Eternal Essence skyrocketed, instantly surpassing Yuan’s Eternal Essence.","’What the hell?! Don’t tell me he hasn’t been using his full strength this entire time?!’ Yuan exclaimed inwardly after seeing Saaruk’s aura suddenly become nearly twice as strong as before.","Unbeknownst to Yuan, Saaruk had been using his full strength before.","Although the Absolute Power’s restrictions bound the Eternals’ prowess within its vicinity, they could temporarily exceed those limits as long as they were at the edge of the power’s influence, where it was the weakest. Moreover, they had to pay a tremendous cost.","\"Bear witness, mortal ant! This is Mighty Saaruk unleashing twenty percent of his true power!\" he roared with manic laughter, hurling an attack that was twice as devastating as before.","\"Twenty percent?! What nonsense is that?! What about the Absolute Power?!\" Yuan exclaimed as he channeled as much Eternal Essence as he could muster to block the incoming strike.","\"Argh!\"","Moments after unleashing his attack, Saaruk suddenly screamed in agony, as though an unseen force were ravaging him, inflicting far greater pain than anything Yuan’s blows had caused.","Then, without waiting around to see the outcome, Saaruk immediately turned tail and fled, racing in a direction that took him farther and farther from the Nine Heavens until he was no longer within its vicinity.","Had he hesitated even a second longer, his ethereal form would have been annihilated by the unseen force. Though it wouldn’t have killed him outright, the damage would have weakened his Eternal Essence, requiring trillions of years to recover.","However, that wasn’t to say Saaruk escaped unscathed. By daring to defy the Absolute Power and drawing upon strength beyond what was permitted, he’d forfeited roughly ten percent of his total strength. It was a heavy price, enough to drop his standing among the Eternals and cast him out of the top twenty.","After escaping and returning to his true body somewhere in the endless void, Saaruk unleashed a deafening roar of fury so powerful that it vaporized every star within hundreds of light-years, erasing entire constellations in an instant.","\"THAT DAMN MORTAL ANT! HOW DARE HE HUMILIATE THIS MIGHTY SAARUK IN SUCH A MANNER?!\"","Saaruk caused such a disturbance within the void that it attracted the attention of other nearby Eternals, and when they saw that he had weakened, they wasted no time questioning him.","\"Saaruk, what happened to your Eternal Essence? It’s so much weaker than before!\"","\"Who did you fight this time?\"","\"Can you even call yourself mighty now that you’re this weak?\"","Of course, they also didn’t hesitate to mock him.","Saaruk ignored the other Eternals, refusing to entertain them. If they ever discovered that a mere mortal had reduced him to such a pitiful state, he would be mocked and scorned until the end of time.","Fortunately for him, Shiva had left before she witnessed everything, and he was sure that Yuan had perished from his final strike.","\"...\"","\"What is this ruckus you’ve caused in my domain, Saaruk?\"","Suddenly, another voice called out to him.","Saaruk’s body tensed up slightly after hearing this voice.","\"No reason at all...\" he responded, as the voice belonged to an Eternal that he couldn’t afford to ignore.","\"So you destroyed all those resources for nothing? Is that what you’re telling me?\" The voice returned, its tone colder than the void itself and dripping with restrained fury.","To the Eternals, all of existence was nothing more than a reservoir of resources, something to be refined into essence and consumed for power. Of course, this included the stars Saaruk had destroyed in his fury.","\"Saaruk offers his apology...\"","Not only did he lower his head in apology, but before this Eternal, Saaruk didn’t even dare refer to himself as ’the Mighty Saaruk’, a title he proclaimed with pride before all others.","As for the other Eternals, they left the moment they noticed the presence of this Eternal.","After a silence that seemed to stretch across the stars, the voice returned, its tone no longer angry, but tinged with curiosity.","\"Your condition... It was caused by the Absolute Power, wasn’t it?\"","\"T-That’s—!\" Saaruk hesitated to answer.","\"So, even you seek to covet that power for yourself now? Tell me—what for? To defy me?\" the voice said, its tone cold and razor-sharp, like judgment itself.","\"No! That’s not it! Saaruk swears upon his essence!\"","\"In that case, you won’t mind sharing with me your memories, will you?\"","Saaruk fell silent. Of all beings in existence, this was the one he most dreaded discovering his humiliation. Unfortunately, he could not refuse, as it would result in humiliation far worse than what Yuan had inflicted upon him.","\"Go ahead,\" he said in defeat.","In the next moment, a light flickered in the far reaches of the void—first like a distant star, then rapidly expanding, its brilliance devouring the darkness itself.","Within moments, the star reached him, and as it got close enough to see, it revealed itself to be the end of a single glowing string. The moment it touched Saaruk, it latched onto his body like a divine tether.","Several minutes later, the voice returned, its tone laced with amusement and intrigue.","\"A mortal who not only wields our power but could even refine the essence of the void? How fascinating... how utterly unprecedented!\"","\"...\"","Saaruk was dumbfounded by the Eternal’s reaction; never before had he witnessed them display such excitement. However, he was also nervous, as he had already slain the very being that had stirred such a reaction."]},{"number":2238,"title":"Chapter 2238: Unknown Eternal","paragraphs":["After reading all of Saaruk’s memories, the unknown Eternal withdrew its glowing string from his body and fell silent.","\"It’s been so long since I last experienced excitement. I must speak with this mortal who stirred such an emotion within me,\" said the unknown Eternal.","\"!!!\"","Saaruk’s eyes widened with disbelief at the unknown Eternal’s words.","\"B-But Saaruk has already killed that mortal!\"","The unknown Eternal responded, \"You left before you could confirm the mortal’s death, didn’t you?\"","\"That’s correct, but there’s no way he could’ve survived twenty percent of Saaruk’s power! It’s simply impossible!\"","Saaruk refused to believe that Yuan had survived his attack, especially after he’d sacrificed a portion of his own strength to ensure the mortal’s destruction.","\"Impossible, you say? That mortal has already defied logic and done the impossible multiple times. Even if there’s only a slight chance that the mortal is alive, I’m willing to bet on that chance. After all, it’s not like there’s anything else for me to do right now.\"","\"...\"","Saaruk was speechless.","\"I was going to punish you for destroying my resources, but since you have made such an exciting discovery, I’ll forgive you this time,\" said the unknown Eternal.","Saaruk sighed in relief after hearing this. There were very few things—enough to count with one hand—that Eternals feared in this universe, and this unknown Eternal was one of them.","As for the reason, it was pretty simple. This unknown Eternal possessed such overwhelming strength that it could instill fear in other Eternals.","\"Saaruk is grateful,\" he said.","The unknown Eternal no longer spoke, almost as if they’d left. Sure enough, Saaruk could feel the unknown Eternal’s presence getting further and further away.","While one might assume that the unknown Eternal could reach Yuan’s location swiftly, in truth, it would take many years to traverse such an immense distance, even with its prowess and the Power of the Void. The only reason Saaruk had found Yuan so quickly was because he’d already been nearby, and the only reason he returned to his true body so fast was due to being in his ethereal form.","As for the unknown Eternal, Saaruk could tell that they were traveling with their true body.","Meanwhile, after Saaruk had left, Yuan poured all of his power into defending against Saaruk’s attack, which contained 20 percent of his true prowess.","Unfortunately, there was simply no way he could completely defend it, and the most he could do was weaken it and hope for the best. As for trying to avoid it... the attack was as massive as a star, making evasion impossible unless his Power of the Void reached a certain level that allowed him to travel through the void.","Right before the attack reached him, Yuan activated the Robes of Destruction’s ability.","<Dragon of Destruction’s Ultimate Chaos activated>","When Saaruk’s attack finally struck, the Robes of Destruction absorbed as much of the energy as it could. Afterward, the unthinkable happened.","Despite being said to be indestructible, it shredded into countless pieces and was reduced to nothing.","<Robes of Destruction have been destroyed>","Although the treasure was said to be indestructible by the system, it was a system that did not take into account Eternals, godly beings with unfathomable prowess.","However, even though the Robes of Destruction were destroyed beyond repair, it still managed to do its job, absorbing as much of Saaruk’s attack as it could, even rebounding what it absorbed as it was destroyed.","Because of the Robes of Destruction, Saaruk’s attack was weakened even further.","But even with that, Saaruk’s attack remained immensely powerful and still a threat to Yuan’s life.","Suddenly, Number One Under Heaven trembled, and Zi Xuan’s spirit emerged from it.","Without uttering a word, she swung her arm at Saaruk’s attack and unleashed a powerful aura that was similar to Supreme Sword Aura but was clearly different at the same time.","The sword energy clashed with Saaruk’s attack and managed to endure for a full second before being destroyed.","After unleashing her attack, Zi Xuan quietly returned to Number One Under Heaven and immediately went into a deep slumber after exhausting all of her energy.","Although Zi Xuan couldn’t stop Saaruk’s attack, she managed to weaken it some more.","After Zi Xuan disappeared, Dragon God’s Vengeance appeared of its own will, and Goddess Yeyou emerged from it.","She cast a quick glance at Yuan before turning toward Saaruk’s attack, her mouth opening wide. In the next instant, a radiant beam erupted forth, piercing through Saaruk’s assault like a needle tearing through silk.","Saaruk’s attack dispersed like mist for a fleeting moment before reforming, but its strength had drastically weakened. What once carried the might to annihilate even a Cultivation God with ease was now weak enough for Yuan to defend against it.","\"Thank you all,\" Yuan said as Dragon Goddess Yeyou disappeared alongside the Dragon God’s Vengeance.","Now that Saaruk’s attack was weak enough, Yuan faced it with what little Eternal Essence he had left before leaving the rest for his physique to deal with.","<Eternal Constitution(Incomplete) activated>","<Eternal Constitution(Incomplete) has refined Saaruk’s Essence>","<Through Saaruk’s Essence refinement, your understanding of Eternal Essence has improved drastically>","In the midst of blocking the attack with his bare body after exhausting his Eternal Essence, Yuan actually started to refine the attack, turning it into his own power.","Since he’d already refined Saaruk’s powers once, he was able to do so again with much more ease.","Some time later, Saaruk’s attack had vanished, and Yuan drifted motionlessly through the void, his body battered and bare. Every inch of him ached, and even the slightest movement felt impossible.","\"Young Master! Are you okay?!\" Feng Yuxiang emerged from his Dantian and immediately began applying medicine to his body, pouring various expensive elixirs all over his body.","Xiao Hua also appeared and started transferring spiritual energy into his body.","\"I’m fine,\" he said calmly. \"My body isn’t injured, just drained. I pushed myself past my limits and exhausted too much Eternal Essence. It’s not something medicine can heal. Give me some time, and I’ll be able to move again soon.\"","\"Okay...\" Feng Yuxiang nodded with teary eyes.","Yuan fell silent, his gaze drifting into the endless void, eyes distant as if searching for something beyond its darkness.","\"I am still too weak,\" he suddenly mumbled.","\"You’re not weak!\" Xiao Hua said.","\"She’s right, Young Master. There is nobody at your cultivation who could hope to accomplish what you can. You can even defeat God Ascension cultivators despite only being in the True Immortal realm.\"","Yuan let out a hollow chuckle. \"Cultivation? Such things are meaningless before the Eternals. My true enemies aren’t cultivators. They’re the Eternals themselves. So what does it matter how many cultivators I can defeat if I can’t overcome them?\"","\"Don’t beat yourself so much, Yuan.\" Lan Yingying said. \"I know you’ve experienced many reincarnations, but you’re currently still young and have a lot of room to improve.\"","Yuan smiled faintly. \"I know. I’m just lamenting my own failures. I’ve been trying to take things slowly, even though I know time isn’t on my side. Forget Saaruk—those Eternals I put to sleep before will awaken soon enough and resume their attempt to destroy our world.\"","\"What about the Absolute Power? Although I don’t know anything about it, doesn’t it protect the Nine Heavens from the Eternals?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","\"I don’t know much about the Absolute Power either. However, while it may restrain the Eternals from wielding their power, it cannot suppress their influence. Take the Celestial Emperor, for instance. The second Celestial Emperor once served the Eternals, carrying out their will in their stead.\" Yuan sighed.","\"Although I was able to stop him before he could do any damage, there are probably many more out there doing their bidding.\"","\"Then what should we do?\" Xiao Hua asked.","\"While we can stop them, it’ll only delay the inevitable unless we can take care of the core problem—the Eternals themselves.\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan declared, \"I am no longer going to take things slowly and will try to regain my strength as fast as possible.\"","Meanwhile, somewhere in the Starry Sky, Saaruk sensed that his essence had been absorbed.","\"This feeling! That mortal ant is still alive!\"","His body trembled in anger. He wanted to return to kill Yuan immediately, but with the unknown Eternal already making their way to Yuan, it would be impossible for him to reach Yuan before them.","Moreover, even if he somehow managed to reach Yuan first, he would definitely incur the unknown Eternal’s wrath if he killed Yuan while knowing that they were interested in him.","That said, he had no intention of giving up.","After pondering for a moment, Saaruk remembered something and thought of an idea to deal with Yuan without incurring the unknown Eternal’s wrath.","\"That’s right! Those Eternals trying to acquire the Absolute Power are using the mortals to do their bidding! This Mighty Saaruk can do the same and let them slaughter that wretch in his stead!!\"","Even though it meant he wouldn’t personally deliver the killing blow, Saaruk no longer cared. All that mattered now was seeing Yuan dead."]},{"number":2239,"title":"Chapter 2239: Reinforcements","paragraphs":["It took several days, but Yuan finally recovered enough to move his body.","\"It’s a pity the Robes of Destruction got destroyed, but it served its purpose perfectly.\"","Yuan gathered its scattered pieces and tossed them inside his spatial ring.","The treasure was destroyed beyond recognition, and its material was no longer usable. Still, Yuan decided to keep what remained.","Over the last several days, Yuan contemplated how he should prepare for his next fight with the Eternals.","\"If I want to fight Eternals without my treasures breaking left and right, I will need to create treasures that can handle Eternal Essence and surpass Celestial-grade.\"","Unfortunately, Shiva—who was supposed to lead him to the Eternal capable of teaching him the Eternals’ crafting techniques—had vanished without a trace, leaving Yuan with no choice but to find another way to learn.","He would’ve gone to meet the sealed Eternal if he had known their location, but Shiva never told him the location.","Suddenly, Yuan recalled the sealed Eternal within the Heavenly White Tiger Clan’s territory.","’Since I was able to release Shiva from her seal, I should be able to release that Eternal, too.’","However, he wasn’t certain if it was wise to approach another Eternal so soon. After all, he’d just fought one and barely escaped with his life.","In the end, Yuan decided to wait a little longer before returning to unseal the Eternal. He wanted to be more prepared just in case the Eternal had ulterior motives.","’Since I am already here, I might as well continue advancing my Power of the Void and strengthen my Eternal Essence at the same time.’","Thus, Yuan started cultivating in the void.","<You have refined the ’essence’ of ???>","<Your understanding of the Power of the Void has increased significantly>","A few days later, Yuan sensed his comprehension of the Power of the Void teetering on the edge of a breakthrough. Yet, no matter how much he tried, that final fragment of understanding eluded his grasp. Moreover, his Eternal Essence had stopped improving long ago.","Just like his cultivation, which required his physique to advance before further improvement was possible, there was a limit to how much Eternal Essence Yuan could absorb at his current level. Unlike cultivation, however, refining more Eternal Essence demanded that he first strengthen his Soul Strength rather than his physique.","However, Yuan was still satisfied with his progress. Even though his cultivation was still only at the True Immortal Realm, if he used his Chaotic Essence, True Dragon Awakening, and Eternal Essence, he could fight on par with a cultivator at the ninth level of God Ascension. In other words, he now stood at the peak of the cultivation world, only being below the Cultivation Gods.","\"Now then, let’s get out of here.\"","He reached for his communication jade slip that connected him with Dong Ye.","However, Yuan abruptly stopped moving when he suddenly sensed many presences approaching his direction.","Fortunately, these presences did not belong to the Eternals. Unfortunately, they were likely Heaven’s Mandate’s reinforcements.","\"Dong Ye, can you hear me?\" Yuan spoke to his communication jade slip.","\"My liege! Are you okay?!\" Dong Ye immediately responded, sounding like he’d just found his lost son who had been missing for many years.","\"The issue with the Eternal has been dealt with for now, but another problem came up. The Heaven’s Mandate’s reinforcements are here.\"","\"Are you fighting them right now? I can open up a portal at your location, but it’ll take some time to locate you.\"","\"Not yet, but they should be here in about ten minutes.\"","\"An hour—no, half an hour! Do you think you’ll be able to hold them off for half an hour? If not, you should escape while you can, and I’ll open the portal once you’re safe.\"","\"That won’t be possible. They already know I am here. Even if I leave now, they’ll just chase after me,\" said Yuan.","Despite the situation, his voice was awfully calm.","\"Half an hour, right? Start preparing the portal. I’ll hold them off until then.\"","\"As you command!\"","While Dong Ye immediately started working on the portal, Yuan calmly waited for the reinforcements to arrive.","Eight minutes later, the reinforcements arrived earlier than he anticipated, mostly because they sped up the moment they noticed him.","Over ten thousand soldiers, all experts within the God Ascension realm, wasted no time surrounding Yuan the moment they arrived.","Most of these soldiers were between the first and fourth level of God Ascension, but there were two at the sixth level and one at the eighth level of God Ascension.","\"Even though you probably realized that running was futile, I’ll applaud you for not running away,\" said the soldier at the eighth level of God Ascension as he glared at Yuan.","He then asked, \"What happened to others?\"","\"What do you think? They’re all dead.\"","The soldiers wore shocked looks on their faces upon hearing Yuan’s words.","\"The Sixth Squad was wiped out?! There’s no way!\"","The eighth-level God Ascension expert, who was the commander of this specific squad, narrowed his eyes and spoke in a doubtful tone, \"I don’t believe you.\"","Yuan shrugged, \"Whether you believe me or not is up to you. I won’t try to convince you, either.\"","\"You don’t have to talk if you don’t want to. There are plenty of ways to make someone talk, anyway,\" said the commander, his voice as cold as ice. \"We can do this the easy way or the hard way. Which do you prefer?\"","Yuan smiled, \"How scary. Are you sure you’re soldiers of the Celestial Emperor and not gangsters?\"","\"The hard way, huh?\" The commander muttered before shouting out loud, \"Squad Leader Guang!\"","\"Squad Leader Guang present!\" One of the soldiers with a fourth-level God Ascension cultivation base moved forward, stepping out of the formation.","\"Cripple this little bastard and bring him before me!\"","\"As you command!\"","The next moment, Squad Leader Guang charged at Yuan with a wide grin on his face."]},{"number":2240,"title":"Chapter 2240: The Power of Void Manipulation","paragraphs":["\"Let’s not make this any more difficult than it has to be,\" said Squad Leader Guang as he reached Yuan. \"Extend your arms and offer your limbs to me. If you struggle, I might accidentally cut more than I was ordered to.\"","Yuan calmly looked at the Squad Leader and said, \"Aren’t you even the slightest bit curious why I am the only one alive when everyone else is dead?\"","\"What?\" Squad Leader Guang frowned at his words. Now that Yuan mentioned it, he definitely found it odd that a mere True Immortal survived, while everyone else had supposedly perished.","Yet, when the Squad Leader examined Yuan with divine sense, he couldn’t find anything out of the ordinary about him. Hell, even the clothes Yuan wore were ordinary clothes.","\"I’ll give you the same warning I gave to the last group,\" Yuan suddenly said. \"Leave if you don’t want to die.\"","\"That’s not possible,\" said Squad Leader Guang. \"I don’t know what happened to the Sixth Squad or how you killed them, but it won’t work on our Second Squad, as we’re not only stronger, but we have more experience than they do.\"","Yuan shrugged and said, \"In that case, cut my limbs if you can.\"","Yuan suddenly extended his arms outward, almost as if he were asking to be handcuffed.","Squad Leader Guang narrowed his eyes suspiciously. Something felt off about the situation, but he had no time to ponder.","Without hesitation, he took out his sword and swung it at Yuan’s arms with the intent to cut them.","However, the instant his sword struck Yuan’s arm, it was violently repelled, and the Squad Leader felt as though he had just hit a slab of metal.","\"What the—?!\"","Squad Leader Guang looked at his Mythic-grade sword with wide eyes and a confused face. The other soldiers who also witnessed it were just as puzzled.","\"What’s wrong? I thought you were going to cut my limbs?\" Yuan’s voice resounded, snapping the Squad Leader out of his daze.","Although he didn’t understand what had just happened, he still went for a second strike. This time, he enveloped his sword with Enhanced Sword Aura and swung it with all of his might.","The sword struck Yuan’s arm once more, but this time it didn’t rebound. Instead, it simply stopped, frozen in place, unable to pierce even a fraction of his skin.","\"Impossible!\" Squad Leader Guang exclaimed in shock.","\"What a pity.\" Yuan shook his head. \"I gave you two chances, but you still squandered them. Now, it’s my turn.\"","Hearing Yuan’s words, Squad Leader Guang subconsciously retreated, his body soaked in cold sweat.","After retreating from Yuan, he noticed that Yuan was now holding a sword, as if it had materialized from thin air. Just as Squad Leader Guang exhaled in relief for having pulled back in time, a strange sensation crept up from beneath him, causing him to look down.","\"?!?!\"","When he looked down and saw the massive sword gash across his chest, Squad Leader Guang’s eyes widened in utter disbelief.","’When the hell did he?!’ he cried inwardly.","\"Hey,\" Yuan suddenly called out to him.","When the Squad Leader lifted his head to look, Yuan swung his sword in his direction, which startled him a bit. However, they were miles apart, and Yuan didn’t seem to have employed any techniques.","\"What are you—AHHH!\"","In the midst of his sentence, the Squad Leader screamed in agony as the sensation of being slashed by a sword assaulted him. He looked down again, and this time, he was horrified to find all four of his limbs severed.","\"That power—the Power of the Void!\" the commander of the Second Squad exclaimed, his voice trembling with disbelief. \"And to strike from such a distance... he must’ve reached Advanced Void Understanding!\"","\"A True Immortal with Advanced Void Understanding?! That’s ridiculous!\"","\"Heavens! Who the hell is that bastard?!\"","The soldiers couldn’t fathom how an Immortal could attain something even a Cultivation God would struggle to achieve.","In fact, fewer than ten individuals have ever reached such a realm since the Primordial Era.","’This is a good chance for me to test out my Void Manipulation,’ Yuan thought to himself.","\"Squad Leader Guang! Retreat!\" The commander suddenly shouted.","Without hesitation, the Squad Leader immediately started flying back to the formation.","\"And where do you think you’re going?\"","However, Yuan didn’t allow it and struck again using Void Manipulation.","When Yuan swung his sword, it seemed to the soldiers as though he were striking nothing but empty air. Yet, in the next instant, Squad Leader Guang’s body split cleanly in two, almost as if he’d been attacked by a ghost.","\"This bastard!\" The commander trembled in anger.","\"Second Squad, kill that bastard and avenge Squad Leader Guang!\"","The soldiers hesitated for a brief moment before they started charging at Yuan.","Over ten thousand soldiers closed in from every direction, yet Yuan didn’t appear the slightest bit concerned.","With a calm smile, Yuan began slashing his sword in rapid succession, each motion as effortless as breathing. With every swing, soldiers fell where they stood, perishing without even realizing they had died.","Without at least a basic grasp of the Power of the Void, evading or blocking his strikes was simply impossible.","In other words, the soldiers were no different than sitting ducks at this moment, and the only advantage they had over Yuan was their numbers.","By the time they reached him, Yuan had killed over a thousand soldiers.","\"Kill that bastard!\"","\"Don’t give him the chance to use Void Manipulation!\"","The soldiers charged at Yuan, bombarding him with martial techniques.","Seeing this, Yuan used Void Manipulation on himself, disappearing into the void.","\"Where did he go?!\"","The soldiers started looking around frantically.","A few seconds later, Yuan reappeared behind one of the soldiers and beheaded him before he could react.","\"He’s over here!\" One of the nearby soldiers warned the others.","However, Yuan disappeared into the void again before they could take any action.","Although Yuan could only traverse short distances with his current mastery of the Power of the Void, it was more than enough to throw the soldiers’ formation into complete chaos."]},{"number":2241,"title":"Chapter 2241: The Power of Void Manipulation(2)","paragraphs":["With his Void Manipulation, Yuan traversed the battlefield like a ghost, appearing and disappearing at will.","Every time he appeared, one or more soldiers of Heaven’s Manadate would die.","The soldiers fought desperately, but with not a single one of them having even the most basic Void Understanding, it was impossible for them to fight back properly, and the only thing they could do was hope to react fast enough or attack randomly.","Seeing how much of a mess his soldiers were, the commander gritted his teeth in anger and said to the two experts by his side.","\"Captain Ma, Captain Su, I want both of you to put an end to this madness.\"","\"At your command, Commander Du.\"","They acknowledged his order with a bow before heading into the battlefield.","\"Soldiers, get back!\" Captain Ma warned them.","The soldiers sighed in relief after hearing his voice and command, and without hesitation, started flying away.","Seeing this, Yuan didn’t chase after them. He merely stood still and waited for the captains to arrive.","When they arrived, Captain Su glared at Yuan and said coldly, \"How dare a mere Immortal defy Heaven’s Mandate? Do you not fear the Heavens?\"","Yuan’s gaze remained calm as he replied, \"If by ’Heavens’ you mean the Celestial Emperor, then no, I couldn’t care less about a dog like him.\"","\"The blasphemy!\" Captain Ma shouted in anger, his brows furrowed deeply into a frown. \"His Majesty, the Celestial Emperor, is the most powerful and respected individual in this universe! You will not disrespect him!\"","\"The most powerful, huh? Maybe in your little world, but in my eyes, he’s nothing more than a dog trying to please his masters.\"","\"His masters?! What the hell are you talking about! Do you even know who the Celestial Emperor is?!\"","Captain Ma then said to his comrade, \"Forget it. He’s obviously not well in the head.\"","\"You’re right. Let’s quickly kill this bastard and get it over with.\"","These two captains were at the Sixth Level of God Ascension, and unlike the other ordinary soldiers, they had a fundamental comprehension of the Power of the Void.","When they attacked and Yuan tried to use Void Manipulation to traverse, the captains were able to see the changes in the void, allowing them to somewhat follow Yuan’s movements through the void.","Although it wasn’t perfect, they could make up for what they lacked in experience.","When Yuan emerged from the void, they were able to react in time to intercept him.","\"Your Void Manipulation is useless before us!\" Captain Su declared.","\"Oh, really?\"","Yuan struck with his sword, and the blade disappeared for an instant.","Captain Ma suddenly turned around and raised his sword—Clang!","He managed to block Yuan’s strike.","\"What did I just say?\" Captain Su sneered as he launched his own strike, which was engulfed in Celestial Qi.","They were still within the Nine Heavens, where the use of Celestial Qi should have been heavily restricted. Yet Captain Su wielded his Celestial Qi at full strength. Such was one of the privileges granted to those who served the Celestial Emperor, as they could partially bypass the laws that bound others.","Of course, this privilege wasn’t granted to just anyone who served the Celestial Emperor. Only those he trusted deeply and who held high-ranking positions were allowed such authority.","Without the restriction, the captains were incomparably stronger than the other soldiers, allowing them to fight Yuan on equal terms—for now, at least.","\"I guess it’s time for me to stop messing around,\" Yuan muttered as he activated his Chaotic Essence.","\"What the hell?! His aura suddenly skyrocketed!\"","\"What an ominous aura! Is he even human?!\"","The captains halted their movements when they sensed the chaotic energy surging around Yuan.","While the captains were alarmed, Yuan disappeared into the void with Void Manipulation.","\"Void Manipulation again?! It won’t work—\" Captain Su’s words were halted when a painful sensation suddenly struck his back.","\"What?!\"","When he looked, he saw a massive sword cut on his back.","\"Impossible!\" he exclaimed in disbelief.","\"Did you really think you would be able to stop me with your level of Void Understanding?\" Yuan’s voice resounded in their heads.","\"Today was my first time using Void Manipulation to such a degree, so I was just testing it. Now that I have a good understanding of its powers, it won’t be like before.\"","\"Ah!\" Captain Ma shouted in agony when he was also struck. However, unlike Captain Su, he was hit directly in the chest.","\"This bastard...!\"","Yuan continued to attack them from the void without showing himself. Although he could only traverse short distances, he could easily stay in the void as long as he didn’t move too much.","This meant that unless the captains could strike into the void, it was impossible to hit Yuan.","Of course, the two captains quickly realized this and requested help from Commander Du.","\"Commander! His level of Void Understanding is beyond our comprehension! We cannot deal with him!\"","Hearing this, Commander Du gritted his teeth in anger. As much as he wanted to assist them, his level of Void Understanding wasn’t much better than theirs. If they were powerless against Yuan, so was he.","After a moment of silence, he shouted, \"This is an opponent that we cannot handle! Withdraw!\"","Without hesitation, Commander Du activated a treasure similar to the one used by Dong Ye, creating multiple portals.","\"Withdraw!\" He repeated.","The soldiers quickly withdrew into the portals, disappearing from the battlefield.","Yuan wanted to chase after them, but he knew when to stop. The portals likely led to the Celestial Emperor’s territory, and at his current level, going into such a place without proper preparations was no different than suicide.","\"Don’t think this is over, you bastard!\" Commander Du shouted as he was the last to retreat from the battlefield.","Yuan smiled faintly and replied, \"Bold words for someone fleeing with their tail tucked between their legs.\"","Commander Du trembled with rage. He hadn’t been insulted like this since attaining his position tens of thousands of years ago. What stung even more was the humiliating retreat after losing thousands of his soldiers. He knew that once word spread, the other squads would mock him behind his back. Hell, he wouldn’t be surprised if his squad was demoted for this failure.","Without responding to Yuan’s provocation, Commander Du disappeared into the portal."]},{"number":2242,"title":"Chapter 2242: Sword-Shaped Token","paragraphs":["Minutes after Heaven’s Mandate’s retreat, another portal appeared, and a familiar figure emerged from it.","\"My liege! We’re here to assist you!\" Dong Ye’s voice could be heard even before his body fully emerged from the portal.","However, when he came out and saw the empty scene, Dong Ye turned to look at Yuan with a puzzled face.","He wasn’t alone, as the Shadow Army came with him, and they were just as puzzled. They were even prepared to fight to the death with Heaven’s Mandate.","\"My liege, what happened to Heaven’s Mandate?\" he asked.","Yuan responded with a calm smile, \"They ran away.\"","\"What? Run away? Heaven’s Mandate?\" Dong Ye’s eyes widened with surprise.","He didn’t even know such a thing was possible.","After a moment of silence, he asked, \"Do you happen to know which squad they belonged to?\"","\"The Second Squad. Why does that matter?\" Yuan asked with curiosity.","\"The Second Squad?! You actually forced the Second Squad to retreat by yourself?! You’re amazing, my liege!\" Dong Ye exclaimed with excitement.","He proceeded to explain, \"There are thirteen squads in Heaven’s Mandate, and the Second Squad is the third strongest, only below the First Squad and the Elite Squad.\"","\"Is that so? Well, they were pretty weak.\"","\"Maybe that is the case for you, but my liege, you cannot compare yourself to the average person. Even the entire Shadow Army would have trouble dealing with the Second Squad.\"","\"How much stronger is the First and Elite Squad?\" Yuan then asked.","\"The First Squad consists of a single Ninth Level God Ascension expert as its commander, with 20,000 soldiers between the first and fourth level God Ascension. As for the Elite Squad, they have fewer than five hundred soldiers, but each one is at least at the fifth level of God Ascension,\" he explained.","\"There’s even a rumor that their commander is a Cultivation God.\"","\"Only a rumor? Has nobody seen their commander?\"","\"The Elite Squad is a highly secretive group even within the Celestial Emperor’s circle, after all. Moreover, they have never been deployed before.\"","\"I see,\" Yuan said. \"Anyway, let’s leave.\"","Dong Ye nodded, but before leaving, he asked, noticing that a particular individual was missing, \"By the way, what happened to that woman Mu Xuelian?\"","Yuan shrugged and said, \"She left while I was fighting.\"","\"What?!\" Dong Ye exclaimed in disbelief. \"She actually ran away and left you behind?! Even after everything she said?!\"","Yuan smiled and spoke to him through voice transmission, \"It didn’t happen while I was fighting Heaven’s Mandate, but during my fight with the Eternal. Things were looking very bad at the end, so I don’t really blame her for leaving.\"","\"That’s even worse! To think she’d abandon you during your fight against a God! I thought she was a God, too!\"","\"She may be an Eternal, but she doesn’t have her true body, and without it, there’s no way she could fight against another Eternal. Anyway, let’s leave before more reinforcements arrive.\"","They left through the portal shortly after and regrouped with the Asura Clan.","\"Master Tian! You’re back!\" Xiao Meilin smiled brightly upon his return.","\"How was the fight against the Eternal?\" Xiao Cangming asked with a curious gaze.","\"You won’t believe who I fought,\" said Yuan.","Xiao Cangming raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Who?\"","\"The same bastard who tried to steal the Spirit Tree and injured you.\"","\"What!\"","Yuan proceeded to recall the whole event to them.","\"Even though that bastard was only using ten percent of his strength, I was barely able to defeat him. When he used twenty percent of his strength, I was powerless even after refining the essence of the void. I still have a long way to go.\"","\"What are your plans now?\" Xiao Cangming asked.","\"I need to regain my original strength as fast as possible. To do that, I’ll need to find whatever my previous incarnations left behind.\"","Xiao Cangming then said, \"In that case, I have something for you.\"","He reached inside his spatial ring and retrieved a small jade token in the shape of a sword, and continued, \"You also left this behind when you visited me as the Immortal Monarch.\"","\"What’s this?\" Yuan asked with a puzzled face, as he still doesn’t recall such memories.","Xiao Cangming shrugged, \"Beats me, but it seems to be a key to something.\"","\"A key, huh?\" Yuan accepted the sword token.","The moment Yuan touched the token, it started to shimmer, and memories started flowing inside his head.","\"Yuan?\" Xiao Cangming called out to him when he suddenly froze with a blank look on his face.","A few minutes later, Yuan blinked a few times.","\"I remember now,\" he said with a profound smile.","\"What did you remember?\"","\"The purpose of this token, as well as the Spirit Tree’s origin and what it’s meant for.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"I’ll tell you about this sword token now, but as for the Spirit Tree, I’ll tell you once it’s fully grown,\" said Yuan.","\"The Spirit Tree is still growing?\"","He nodded, \"In order for the Spirit Tree to mature, a certain treasure is required, and this key will lead me to it.\"","\"When will you be leaving?\" Xiao Cangming then asked.","\"Right now.\"","Xiao Meilin suddenly spoke, \"I already know your answer, but I still want to ask... can I follow you?\"","\"Not right now since the place I will be going is a little unique, and I plan to climb to the Ninth Heaven soon.\"","Despite the rejection, Xiao Meilin showed excitement, as Yuan had implied she would be able to follow him soon.","\"In that case, stay safe!\" she said.","\"In the meantime, we’ll stay here as planned,\" said Xiao Cangming. \"Not only do I need to recover my strength, but the Celestial Emperor will probably be looking for us.\"","Dong Ye then spoke in a confident voice, \"As long as you stay here, not even the Celestial Emperor will be able to find us.\"","Yuan nodded, \"Then I’ll be leaving now. Dong Ye, can you teleport me to the Eighth Heaven? Anywhere near a city with a teleportation device will do.\"","\"Of course.\"","Some time later, Dong Ye created a portal for Yuan.","\"What a convenient treasure,\" Yuan remarked.","Dong Ye chuckled and said, \"Well, it belonged to the Celestial Emperor before we stole it.\"","\"No wonder it’s so similar to the one used by Heaven’s Mandate.\" Yuan also laughed.","\"See you later, my liege. If you need anything, just contact me.\"","\"Alright.\"","Yuan said as he entered the portal and returned to the Eighth Heaven."]},{"number":2243,"title":"Chapter 2243: The Second Squad’s Punishment","paragraphs":["Somewhere in the Celestial Palace, Commander Du approached the throne, where a tall, handsome man sat.","Standing on both sides of Commander Du in the room were ten other individuals, each of them a Squad Commander for Heaven’s Mandate. Since there were thirteen squads in total, two commanders were missing.","The commander for the Elite Squad, which was a regular occurrence, and the commander of the Sixth Squad, who was killed in action recently and hadn’t been replaced yet.","\"Now, tell me everything that happened and why you decided to retreat,\" said the Celestial Emperor.","Commander Du lowered his head in shame as he recalled the events that happened between Yuan and his Second Squad.","\"When we arrived at the location, the Sixth Squad was gone, and the only person waiting for us there was an unknown man with only a cultivation at the True Immortal realm. We questioned him about the Sixth Squad’s situation, and he implied that he had killed them all.\"","\"We tried to capture him at first, but quickly realized that he could wield the Power of the Void. Not only can he use Void Manipulation, but his Void Understanding has reached at least the Advanced realm.\"","\"An Immortal with Advanced Void Understanding?! That’s impossible! You’re just making up bullshit excuses for your humiliating retreat!\" One of the commanders suddenly exclaimed.","The speaker was Commander Wong, the commander of the First Squad, as he was the only one in the room who would dare to rebuke Commander Du so openly.","However, this time, the other commanders also chimed in. After all, they could already see Commander Du being demoted in this meeting with the Celestial Emperor.","\"Commander Wong is right. How can a True Immortal even grasp the Power of the Void, much less reach the Advanced level?\" said the commander of the Seventh Squad.","\"In my entire life, I only know three individuals who have managed to grasp Basic Void Understanding while they were still in the Immortal realm, and they were all monsters,\" said the commander of the Third Squad.","\"If you’re going to create a story, at least make it more believable.\" The commander of the Tenth Squad shook her head.","\"Are you sure this individual was even a True Immortal?\" asked the commander of the Eighth Squad.","Commander Du trembled in anger at their remarks, and he snapped at them, \"How dare you mock me before His Majesty, the Celestial Emperor! I am not lying or making excuses! I am simply telling it as it is!\"","\"Enough.\" The Celestial Emperor’s calm voice resounded, instantly halting the rising heavy atmosphere.","\"Your Majesty, you must believe me! I am even willing to share my memories with you to prove my claims!\" Commander Du said.","The Celestial Emperor nodded and responded, \"I believe you, but that doesn’t change the fact that you lost thousands of excellent soldiers and retreated without any results.\"","\"...\" Commander Du had no words for his failure.","\"Even if you only had a slim chance of victory, you should’ve fought with your life on the line,\" the Celestial Emperor continued. \"At least, Heaven’s Mandate’s reputation wouldn’t have been smeared. Because right now, its name is being dragged through the mud.\"","\"What?!\" Commander Du’s eyes widened with disbelief. He couldn’t believe how quickly the news had spread, as he’d only just returned from the battlefield.","\"The Second Squad’s failure isn’t just spreading within Heaven’s Mandate, but throughout the Nine Heavens, as well.\" Commander Wong added.","\"How’s that possible?!\" Commander Du exclaimed, wondering if his own soldiers were spreading the news.","’Even if they were spreading the news, it’s spreading way too quickly! It hasn’t even been a full day since I returned!’ he cried inwardly.","Unbeknownst to him, the rumors were actually being spread by the Shadow Army, who never wasted an opportunity to smear the Celestial Emperor’s reputation.","The commander of the Seventh Squad continued, \"According to the rumor that’s being spread, the Second Squad of Heaven’s Mandate suffered a humiliating defeat and was forced to retreat with their tails tucked between their legs after being completely overwhelmed by a single powerhouse.\"","\"You left out the most entertaining part,\" said Commander Wong before continuing with a mocking smile, \"They’re saying that the commander of the Second Squad was so scared that he didn’t even dare to participate in the battle, even though he led thousands of his own men to die.\"","\"That’s—!\" Commander Du’s aura exploded outward abruptly.","Without a word, the other commanders also released their aura, even drawing their weapons and pointing them at Commander Du.","\"You dare to release your cultivation before His Majesty’s presence?!\" Commander Wong shouted at him.","\"This is too much even for you, Commander Du!\" said another commander.","\"Enough!\" The Celestial Emperor raised his voice. \"I will not repeat myself for a third time!\"","His voice instantly dropped the tension in the room, and all of the commanders retrieved their aura.","\"I will now deliver my verdict,\" the Celestial Emperor declared. \"Commander Du, your Second Squad will be demoted to the Thirteenth Squad and will restart their training from the beginning, as if they had just enlisted. As for you, Commander, you are hereby relieved of your position and duties until further notice.\"","\"This subordinate acknowledges his punishment!\" Commander Du responded with clenched fists. Even though he anticipated such punishment, it still pained him greatly.","’I swear I will get my revenge! Just you wait, bastard!’","The other commanders showed no outward reaction to the punishment, yet inwardly they rejoiced. Though they all served under the Celestial Emperor, rivalry ran deep among them, and one squad’s demotion was another’s promotion.","\"You are all dismissed.\" The Celestial Emperor spoke as he stood from his throne.","The commanders bowed to him and remained in such a position until he completely left the room.","Once the Celestial Emperor was gone, the commanders started talking amongst themselves. As for Commander Du, he silently disappeared from the room with a determined expression on his face."]},{"number":2244,"title":"Chapter 2244: A Heinous Crime","paragraphs":["After leaving through Dong Ye’s portal, Yuan found himself back in the Eighth Heaven.","\"You could’ve at least said goodbye to your family,\" Yuan said to Xiao Hua, who emerged from his Dantian afterward.","\"Why?\" she asked with a genuinely puzzled look on her face.","\"Well... forget it.\" Yuan sighed.","Lingyue appeared a moment later and asked, \"Brother Yuan, where will you be going next?\"","\"I’m going to visit the Myriad of Techniques first before I head to my next destination—the vault this key opens,\" he replied while showing the sword-shaped token.","\"I see. It’s been a long time since you visited your friends, after all.\"","Some time later, Yuan arrived at a nearby city. However, Myriad of Techniques didn’t exist in the city, so he had to teleport to another one that did.","Upon arriving at the Myriad of Techniques, Yuan entered it.","\"Welcome to Myriad of Techniques!\" A beautiful woman greeted him at the door.","\"Hm?\" The woman suddenly raised her eyebrows. \"You... why do you look so familiar? Have we met before?\"","Yuan responded with a smile, \"Maybe.\"","\"What’s your name?\"","\"Yuan.\"","\"Yuan... Yuan?!\" The woman exclaimed with a shocked look on her face, and she started analyzing him from head to toe.","\"No way... I can sense Immortal Qi emitting from you, but that’s only possible for those who have entered the Immortal Realm!\" she muttered in a dumbfounded voice.","\"That’s because I am at the Immortal Realm. A True Immortal, to be precise,\" he said.","The woman’s jaw dropped, leaving her mouth wide open.","\"It’s been a while, Miss Zhu. How have you been?\" Yuan suddenly greeted her.","This woman was Zhu Yuying, someone he met during his first visit to the Myriad of Techniques.","\"You’re really... Yuan?\" Zhu Yuying muttered in disbelief.","He had changed so much since their last meeting. Not only had he grown taller and more strikingly handsome, but the sheer speed of his cultivation left her utterly stunned.","\"Is it really that hard to believe?\" Yuan chuckled at her exaggerated reaction.","\"Of course! I have never seen anyone progress as fast as you!\" she exclaimed.","\"Anyway, what are you doing here? Looking for more techniques? Or...?\"","\"I’m here to speak with Senior Bai. Is he available?\"","\"He was... until a few hours ago.\"","\"Where did he go?\" he asked.","\"I’m not sure, but it seemed to be an emergency.\"","\"In that case, I’ll leave him a message and come back later.\"","Yuan retrieved Senior Bai’s communication jade slip and left him a message.","\"You have Master Bai’s communication jade slip? Just what is your relationship with him?\" she asked, her eyes full of curiosity.","\"Close friends, I guess.\"","\"Is that so... By the way, do you have to leave immediately? It’s been a while since we last spoke. Why don’t we have a little chat? Who knows, maybe Master Bai will return soon.\"","\"I guess I can stay here for a little.\" Yuan nodded.","\"Great! Give me a moment to find a replacement.\"","Zhu Yuying retrieved a communication jade slip and spoke into it. A few moments later, she said to Yuan, \"Alright, let’s go.\"","Zhu Yuying led Yuan to a private room used by those working in the Myriad of Techniques.","After serving him some simple tea, she asked, \"So, what have you been doing recently? Since your cultivation improved so much, I guess it’s mostly training, right?\"","He nodded, \"Yes. I took a trip to White Hell.\"","\"White Hell?!\" she exclaimed, and nearly dropped her teacup. \"That means you’re already in the Eighth Heaven...\"","\"Remember when I said we could meet again once you reached the Fifth Heaven?\" she chuckled.","\"At that time, I also couldn’t have predicted how fast I’d climb the Nine Heavens.\"","The two spent the next hour catching up. Yuan shared stories of his recent adventures without mentioning any of the crazy stuff, while Zhu Yuying spoke about her experiences as a disciple of the Gates of Heaven.","\"To be honest, I was recently promoted to the Gates of Heaven in the Seventh Heaven, so I no longer need to work in Myriad of Techniques. However, I still decided to come back here one last time, so this will be our last meeting here,\" she said.","\"Gates of Heaven, huh? I’ll take a look when I have time,\" said Yuan.","\"Make sure to visit me when you do!\" Zhu Yuying chuckled.","Yuan nodded.","At that moment, Yuan sensed Senior Bai’s communication jade slip trembling.","\"Looks like Senior Bai responded,\" he said as he listened to Senior Bai’s message.","A moment later, he stood up and said, \"He said that he’ll be coming soon and that I can wait in his world.\"","\"Alright. I’ll lead you there.\"","Once they arrived, Zhu Yuying said, \"See you next time at Gates of Heaven.\"","\"See you.\"","Yuan nodded before entering Senior Bai’s world to wait for him.","About ten minutes later, Yuan could sense another presence entering the world.","When Yuan finally saw Senior Bai, he couldn’t help but raise an eyebrow.","Senior Bai looked utterly exhausted, as if he hadn’t slept in ages.","\"Sorry for the late response,\" Senior Bai said as he landed before Yuan.","\"No worries. Did something happen? This is my first time seeing you look so tired.\"","Senior Bai rubbed his eyes and sighed, \"It’s related to the Celestial Overlords. It’s in a mess right now because of some crazy bastard.\"","\"Crazy bastard?\"","\"Our faction’s karma suddenly plummeted out of nowhere, throwing everyone into a frenzy,\" explained Senior Bai.","Yuan tilted his head slightly, still looking puzzled.","\"You know how factions gain karma when their members perform righteous deeds, right? Well, the same karma declines when someone does the opposite.\"","\"The Celestial Overlords have always held the highest karma among all factions in the Nine Heavens, and it’s been that way since its founding. But for some reason, our karma has recently plummeted to rock bottom, shocking everyone.\"","\"With how drastically our karma has fallen, someone must have committed a crime so heinous it defies imagination. After all, even slaughtering an entire city of innocents wouldn’t cause such a massive decline.\"","He continued with a troubled look, \"What’s worse is that, under normal circumstances, we can track every member’s karma. But this time, for some reason, we can’t trace the cause of this phenomenon at all, almost as if it was committed by a ghost.\""]},{"number":2245,"title":"Chapter 2245: Karma","paragraphs":["Yuan wore a dumbfounded look on his face after hearing about the Celestial Overlords’ situation from Senior Bai. He was, without a shadow of doubt, confident that he was responsible for their karma’s decline.","After all, he’d recently killed thousands of soldiers from Heaven’s Mandate, servants of the Celestial Emperor, and such an act was definitely considered defying the heavens, a crime worse than killing innocent people.","Naturally, he never had such intentions. In fact, he didn’t even consider how his actions could have such tremendous effects on the faction. Unfortunately, it was too late, and there was nothing he could really do about their karma. Unless he killed every individual within the Primordial Realm, since exiles granted a lot of karma, it would likely take millions of years of hard work for them to return to fix their karma.","\"So, what are the members doing about this?\" Yuan asked.","\"For starters, we’re investigating the cause of this phenomenon,\" Senior Bai replied.","\"Honestly, many of us believe it’s some kind of mistake, given how unprecedented this situation is. As I mentioned earlier, even the massacre of an entire city of innocents wouldn’t result in such a drastic loss of karma. And since there’s been no report of any major incident, we suspect it may simply be an error.\"","Since word of Heaven’s Mandate’s defeat had yet to spread at this moment in time, no one was aware of what had truly happened.","After a brief silence, Yuan spoke. \"Forgive me for being blunt, but does a faction’s karma really matter that much? Isn’t it just a measure of how righteous they appear to be?\"","\"If you look at it that way, then no, it doesn’t seem that important,\" Senior Bai explained. \"However, most factions treat their karma as a reflection of their reputation, and some even see it as part of their strength. To possess high karma is to have Heaven’s approval, and the more you have, the more trustworthy and revered you become.\"","\"How long would it take to recover the karma that was lost?\" Yuan then asked out of curiosity.","\"That’s...\" Senior Bai had to ponder his question for several minutes before responding, \"If we consider how much karma we gain every decade on average for the last ten thousand years, it’ll take at least seven million years to regain what we lost.\"","Yuan swallowed nervously when he learned that he’d erased seven million years of the Celestial Overlords’ hard work in less than half an hour.","\"Sorry...\" Yuan subconsciously apologized.","\"Hm? Why are you apologizing? It’s not like you’re responsible... right?\" Senior Bai looked at him with narrowed eyes.","\"I just felt like apologizing...\" Yuan said with a stiff smile.","Despite his close relationship with Senior Bai, Yuan couldn’t bring himself to reveal the truth. It wasn’t a matter of trust—he simply didn’t want to drag the old man into his troubles. Yuan knew that even if Senior Bai learned the truth, he wouldn’t place any blame on him.","Senior Bai sighed, \"Anyway, that’s our current situation. Let’s switch topics.\"","He then said, \"The Sword Emperor Qualification concluded a few years after you earned your title. We had planned to hold the celebration soon after, but since you weren’t available—and the Heavenly Son insisted he’d only attend if you were present—we decided to postpone it until your return.\"","\"Now that you’ve returned, what do you think about participating?\"","Yuan shook his head and said, \"Unfortunately, I have my hands full right now. I also plan to climb to the Ninth Heaven soon.\"","Senior Bai pondered for a moment before replying, \"Well, we’ve already delayed the celebration this long—waiting a little longer won’t hurt. More importantly, if neither you nor the Heavenly Son is present, no one would care to attend anyway. It’d be meaningless.\"","\"Sorry for the trouble.\"","\"It’s fine. I know you’re busy, especially considering how much you’ve progressed since I last saw you. To be honest, I almost didn’t recognize you—no... I likely wouldn’t have recognized you if I didn’t know you were waiting for me,\" Senior Bai admitted.","Naturally, he wasn’t talking about Yuan’s appearance but his aura and presence.","Senior Bai glared at Yuan with a profound expression.","\"At this rate, you’ll be at the God Ascension realm during our next meeting,\" he continued.","Yuan smiled and said, \"Well, I am definitely not too far away from achieving the next realm...\"","He wasn’t exaggerating, either. All he needed to do to reach the God Ascension Realm was comprehend Celestial Qi—something he had been neglecting. If he took his cultivation seriously for a while, he would undoubtedly break through the Immortal Realm. The only uncertainty was whether his physique still had any bottlenecks left.","\"Enough about me. What about my friends? How have they been doing?\" Yuan then asked about the Demon Sealing Faction.","\"They’ve been working hard ever since they set out to walk their own paths,\" Senior Bai said.","\"Hm? What do you mean?\" Yuan asked, unaware of their circumstances.","Senior Bai then explained how each of the members had joined different sects and taken on new masters to broaden their experience and deepen their ties with the cultivation world.","\"Let’s start with your partners,\" Senior Bai continued with a smile on his face.","\"Meixiu accepted Kelan’s sister, who is a bow expert, as her new master and has been traveling the Nine Heavens, undergoing all sorts of training.\"","\"Kelan’s sister? I didn’t know he had a sister.\" Yuan remarked.","\"He doesn’t like to talk about his family,\" Senior Bai said with a smile.","\"Chu Liuxiang joined my sect, the Gates of Heaven in the Ninth Heaven,\" he continued. \"To be honest, she’s been struggling to adapt, as the gap in talent between her and the other disciples is considerable. Even so, she hasn’t given up and continues to work hard to improve. I was planning to transfer her to the Gates of Heaven in the Seventh Heaven, where she’d be more comfortable, but I decided to wait until she chooses to give up on her own.\"","Although Chu Liuxiang was undeniably talented—far surpassing most of her peers—she still fell short compared to the true prodigies and monsters of the Ninth Heaven, where the most gifted cultivators in existence gathered."]},{"number":2246,"title":"Chapter 2246: An Outrageous Rumor","paragraphs":["\"I see... so Lulu is in the Ninth Heaven...\" Yuan murmured after hearing about her situation from Senior Bai. Though it pained him to know she was struggling, it wasn’t unexpected, as she had been sent to a place far beyond her current abilities. Yet, if she could overcome those challenges and push past her limits, he knew she would emerge far stronger than before.","\"Falling behind the others isn’t her only hardship,\" Senior Bai continued. \"She also has to endure the mockery and disdain of her fellow disciples. Even though I warned her beforehand, she still chose to face the challenge. I can’t constantly shield her since there’s only so much favoritism I can show a single disciple, but I make sure nothing goes too far.\"","\"That’s a given,\" Yuan nodded in agreement. \"As much as I care for Lulu, I can understand the other disciples’ frustration. They worked hard to earn their place in the sect, while she entered through connections despite lacking the same abilities. For that, I owe you my gratitude, Senior Bai—thank you for looking after her.\"","Senior Bai laughed out loud, \"Considering our relationship, this is the least I can do. And as I already told her, connection is as important as talent in the cultivation world, so don’t overthink it too much.\"","\"Anyway, let’s continue to the others. About Li Jinxi, I haven’t received much news from her, but according to what I’ve heard from others, she’s been making waves in Heaven’s Sect.\"","\"Heaven’s Sect?\" Yuan found the name familiar but couldn’t recall where he had heard it from.","\"It’s one of the top three sects in the Ninth Heaven, overseen by the Tian Family—the Heavenly Son’s family,\" said Senior Bai. \"Not only does it gather the most talented cultivators, but its environment is also among the harshest and most demanding. Even so, Li Jinxi has been making a name for herself there, astonishing everyone with her overwhelming talent.\"","\"In fact, I heard that she even caught the attention of the Tian Family in the short time that she’s been there. I knew she was talented before, but she still managed to surpass my expectations. She’s quite similar to you in that way, Yuan.\" Senior Bai chuckled.","\"I’m more surprised that she agreed to join a sect,\" Yuan said with a smile. \"She’s the type to wander.\"","\"You know her very well. Indeed, she initially planned to wander the Nine Heavens alone, but I managed to convince her to join a sect. After all, I didn’t want her to waste her potential.\"","Senior Bai continued to discuss the other members and how each of them was adjusting to their new environments.","\"As for Wang Xiuying, I heard that she—\" Senior Bai suddenly stopped speaking and reached into his pocket to retrieve a communication jade slip.","\"Give me a moment,\" he said as he listened to the message he’d just received.","As he did, Senior Bai’s expression darkened, and he let out a heavy sigh. A few moments later, he put the communication jade slip away and sighed once more.","\"What’s wrong?\" Yuan asked.","\"I just received word that someone clashed with the Second Squad of Heaven’s Mandate, and not only did that person kill thousands of their soldiers, but even forced them to retreat,\" Senior Bai explained, his tone filled with disbelief and concern.","Yuan’s body stiffened at this news.","\"If this news is true, it would explain our sudden drop in karma,\" Senior Bai continued. \"Someone from the Celestial Overlords must have clashed with Heaven’s Mandate, and that conflict triggered the decline.\"","\"With that said, it still doesn’t make any sense!\" Senior Bai slammed the table in frustration. \"How can a single person force the entire Second Squad to retreat? Even if all of the Celestial Overlords worked together, they still wouldn’t be able to achieve such a feat, let alone the rest of the members! This is something that would only be feasible by a Cultivation God, but we don’t have such a powerhouse in the faction!\"","\"...\"","Yuan remained silent as Senior Bai expressed his frustration, cold sweat soaking his back.","\"So, what happens now?\" Yuan eventually asked.","\"There’s nothing we can do until we confirm the information,\" Senior Bai replied. \"However, if it turns out to be true, Heaven’s Mandate will likely make the first move.\"","\"Sorry, but I have to leave now.\"","Yuan nodded, \"No worries. Let’s continue once everything has calmed down.\"","After saying their goodbyes, Senior Bai left, and Yuan returned to the Myriad of Techniques.","\"Did you speak with Master Bai?\" Zhu Yuying asked him.","\"Yes, I did.\"","\"Then did you ask about the situation? I hope it’s nothing too serious.\"","Yuan wore a bitter smile on his face as he responded, \"It’ll sort itself out. If not, I’ll do something about it.\"","\"You will?\" Zhu Yuying stared at him with wide eyes.","He nodded, \"Anyway, I’ll be leaving now.\"","\"Alright. Don’t forget to visit me at Gates of Heaven when you have the chance.\"","\"Of course.\"","With that, Yuan left the Myriad of Techniques. Zhu Yuying also decided to end her work there and left shortly after.","Meanwhile, after returning to the Celestial Overlords’ headquarters, Senior Bai went straight into a meeting with the other Celestial Overlords and Overlords present.","\"So, has everyone heard the news about Heaven’s Mandate?\" Qiang Qing Yun was the first to speak once everyone had gathered.","\"Of course, but it’s an outrageous rumor and pure nonsense,\" said one of the other Celestial Overlords, a handsome man with long, dark green hair. \"Besides a Cultivation God, who is capable of forcing the Second Squad to retreat? They’re the Celestial Emperor’s third most powerful force with over ten thousand God Ascension experts in their formation!\"","\"Right? Nobody is stupid enough to believe such nonsense,\" someone else remarked.","\"Ignoring whether it’s even possible, if we consider our current situation, doesn’t it make sense?\" someone suddenly spoke up. \"I can’t imagine any other scenario that would cause our karma to plummet so drastically.\"","The room fell silent at these words."]},{"number":2247,"title":"Chapter 2247: Portrait of the Culprit","paragraphs":["The idea of someone from the Celestial Overlords clashing with Heaven’s Mandate was hard to believe. Yet, when they considered the current circumstances and the timing of events, it somewhat made sense.","Even so—despite how neatly the pieces fit together—it was still an absurd conclusion, one so far-fetched it bordered on impossible to believe. After all, unless the entire Celestial Overlords fought together, it was simply impossible for them to overpower the Second Squad of Heaven’s Mandate.","\"There’s no point in overthinking it,\" Xu Jiaqi suddenly said. \"Whether our drop in karma is connected to Heaven’s Mandate or not, we’ll find out soon enough.\"","\"How can you stay so damn calm in a situation like this? Do you have any idea how much damage this incident has caused to our faction’s reputation? It hasn’t even been a full day, and we’ve already become a laughingstock,\" the green-haired Celestial Overlord snapped at her.","Xu Jiaqi shifted her gaze toward the green-haired man and spoke, \"Calm? Do I really look calm to you, Liu Yucang?\"","Her eyes narrowed, and she revealed the immense killing intent and anger she had been hiding within, sending shivers down his spine.","\"I don’t care who or how, but the bastard responsible for tarnishing this faction—my father’s legacy will wish they were never born. This includes anyone who’s trying to take advantage or covet it.\"","Her warning wasn’t meant just for the one responsible for the loss of their karma, but a warning to those opposing her in the faction, mainly the other Celestial Overlords currently fighting to gain control of the faction.","The green-haired Celestial Overlord, Liu Yucang, couldn’t ignore her blatant threat and retorted, \"Aren’t you ashamed of yourself, constantly using the founder’s name to your advantage? You call him your father, yet you’re not even related by blood. That alone isn’t the issue—the problem is that there’s no proof he ever adopted you. In other words, anyone could claim to be his child.\"","Rather than getting angry at his remark, Xu Jiaqi merely sneered, \"If you doubt my claim, then you can go ahead and ask Senior Tian Xianling, one of my father’s closest friends and also the co-founder of this faction.\"","Liu Yucang frowned.","\"Tian Xianling? The Celestial Doctor? Can her words even be trusted when she abandoned the Celestial Overlords?\" he sneered.","\"What the hell do you know about the Celestial Doctor?\" Qiang Qing Yun suddenly interjected. \"She left because she was disappointed in what the faction has become—because of bastards like you and him.\"","Qiang Qing Yun shot a cold glare at Liu Yucang and the Celestial Overlord sitting beside him—an elderly man with a gleaming bald head and a long white beard that trailed all the way to the floor.","At first, the old man appeared to be asleep, his eyes fully shut. But then he suddenly spoke, his voice calm and aged, \"This old man must agree with Overlord Qiang. If not for the Celestial Doctor, I wouldn’t be alive today.\"","\"Are you seriously siding with them, Old Man Bi?\" Liu Yucang glared at him.","Old Man Bi didn’t respond and remained silent.","\"Let’s get back on topic,\" Qiang Qing Yun then said. \"What are we going to do about our karma? If it’s really an error, can it even be fixed?\"","\"Unfortunately, that likely won’t be possible,\" said Xu Jiaqi. \"As far as I am aware, karma can only be influenced through our actions, so we will have to build our karma back up again.\"","\"Maybe we should complain to the Celestial Emperor. If anyone can directly affect a faction’s karma, it’d be him,\" said Old Man Bi.","\"And what if it was the Celestial Emperor who directly stripped away our karma?\" Xu Jiaqi asked, voicing the possibility aloud.","\"What? You think the Celestial Emperor personally targeted us?\" Qiang Qing Yun’s eyes widened in disbelief. \"But why would he do something like that? It’s not as if we’ve ever had any conflict with him.\"","Xu Jiaqi didn’t respond right away, as only she knew that their founder might have harbored some kind of grievance against the Celestial Emperor. However, even if that were true, it made no sense for the Celestial Emperor to act now, especially when their founder was long gone.","\"As ridiculous as that sounds, it’s still more believable than that nonsense about us clashing with Heaven’s Mandate,\" Liu Yucang said, one of the rare times he sided with Xu Jiaqi.","\"If the Celestial Emperor truly is responsible,\" Xu Jiaqi said in an icy voice, \"then I’ll make sure he answers for it, regardless of his status.\"","\"Let’s not get ahead of ourselves,\" Old Man Bi interjected. \"The Celestial Emperor has no reason to target us. Doing so would anger not only our faction, but also our allies and the other major powers. It would create consequences far too severe to ignore.\"","The meeting continued, with the faction’s members offering their opinions and proposing how they should proceed.","After some time had passed, a sudden knock echoed from the doors. A voice called from outside, urgent and strained, \"Seniors! We have an emergency! Heaven’s Mandate has arrived and is requesting an audience!\"","\"What?\"","Before any of them could respond, the doors swung open, and several individuals in Heaven’s Mandate uniforms brazenly strode into the room, moving with the arrogance of people who believed they owned the place.","The one leading the group spoke loudly, his voice full of authority, \"I am the commander of the First Squad of Heaven’s Mandate, Wong Xianwen, and I have been instructed by His Majesty, the Celestial Emperor, to bring justice to the blasphemous individual who dared to attack Heaven’s Mandate!\"","\"Commander of the First Squad?!\" The people in the room exclaimed with surprised faces.","\"Does this mean the rumors of the Second Squad being attacked were true?!\"","Xu Jiaqi rose to her feet and approached the squad, a deep frown creasing her face.","\"I don’t care who you are. What gives you the right to barge in uninvited? Do you take our headquarters for your own home?\"","Commander Wong replied calmly, \"I am aware that our conduct is improper, but we are pressed for time. I must ask for your understanding.\"","He turned to the others and continued, \"As you’ve likely heard, there’s a rumor circulating about someone attacking the Second Squad of Heaven’s Mandate. That rumor is true, and until now, we were unaware of the attacker’s identity. Shortly after the incident, the Celestial Overlords’ karma plummeted. Given the timing, the culprit must belong to your faction. If you don’t wish to further tarnish your reputation, hand over the one responsible immediately.\"","The room immediately fell silent, and the atmosphere became heavy as the members exchanged looks with each other.","A moment later, Senior Bai rose to his feet and broke the silence.","\"Are you certain there isn’t some mistake? The Celestial Overlords have no one capable of forcing the Second Squad to retreat, let alone slaughtering them.\"","\"Overlord Bai is right,\" Qiang Qing Yun added sharply. \"Or are you trying to claim we’ve been hiding a Cultivation God in our ranks?\"","\"Then how do you explain your karma?\" Commander Wong shot back, deliberately ignoring their question. He had no intention of admitting that someone had utterly humiliated their proud military forces, even if it was the truth.","Senior Bai shook his head. \"Honestly, we’re just as puzzled as you are.\"","Without another word, Commander Wong reached into his spatial ring and produced a large scroll. He unfurled it, revealing a detailed portrait of a handsome young man—an image reconstructed from the Second Squad soldiers’ memories.","\"Then tell me,\" Commander Wong said, eyes narrowing as he closely studied their reactions, \"are you claiming that this person does not exist within the Celestial Overlords?\"","Senior Bai’s and Xu Jiaqi’s eyes widened in shock the moment they saw the portrait, as it was unmistakably Yuan. Aside from those two, no one else in the room showed any significant reaction.","’That’s Yuan?! Impossible!’ Xu Jiaqi cried inwardly after seeing his portrait.","Senior Bai stood frozen, looking like he’d just seen a ghost.","Commander Wong didn’t miss their reactions. His lips curled into a wide, knowing smile as he pressed, \"So he does exist within the Celestial Overlords. Isn’t that right... Xu Jiaqi, Bai Ling?\"","\"What?!\"","Qiang Qing Yun and the other members turned to look at the two with wide eyes.","After a moment of silence, Xu Jiaqi spoke, \"Yes, we know him.\"","\"How unexpected.\" Liu Yucang remarked with an entertained smile on his face.","\"Then—\"","Commander Wong opened his mouth to speak, but was interrupted by Xu Jiaqi, who continued speaking, \"However, that man had already left the faction. In fact, he left the faction over two decades ago, long before he attacked the Heaven’s Mandate.\"","\"Oh? Then what is your relationship with this man?\" Commander Wong then questioned.","\"He’s an ’Outsider’ that we recruited long ago,\" Xu Jiaqi spoke in a calm and clear voice, almost as if she’d rehearsed this scenario a thousand times."]},{"number":2248,"title":"Chapter 2248: Portrait of the Culprit(2)","paragraphs":["\"An Outsider, you say?\" Commander Wong nearly burst out laughing at Xu Jiaqi’s response, but managed to hold it in.","\"While the Outsiders were given assistance by the Celestial Emperor to help with their growth, there’s no way any of them could defeat a single soldier of Heaven’s Mandate at this time, much less slaughter thousands using Void Manipulation at the advanced level!\"","\"Void Manipulation? And even at the advanced level?\" The others expressed shock after learning this information for the first time.","Xu Jiaqi calmly replied, \"I don’t know anything about that. I am merely telling you what I know about the man you claim to be the culprit.\"","Commander Wang then asked, \"You also claimed that this individual had already left the faction, correct? In that case, why did his actions affect your faction’s karma? If he’d truly left the faction as you’d claimed, your karma wouldn’t have declined as a result.\"","Xu Jiaqi shook her head and sighed, \"Unfortunately, I am just as confused as you.\"","\"You’ll need more than that to convince me,\" Commander Wong said.","\"Then don’t believe me. I already told you what I know about the culprit.\"","\"If you continue to make this difficult for us, we’ll have to use more forceful methods.\"","\"Oh? I would love to see such methods.\" Xu Jiaqi narrowed her eyes and stared at him with a provocative gaze.","The atmosphere in the room shifted instantly. Those aligned with Xu Jiaqi rose to their feet, their auras flaring, making it abundantly clear they were ready for battle at a moment’s notice.","\"This is outright defiance,\" Commander Wong said with a deep frown. \"And since I’m acting under the Celestial Emperor’s orders, your resistance is no different from defying the Celestial Emperor himself.\"","As much as he wanted to pressure Xu Jiaqi into revealing everything, he was clearly at a disadvantage in numbers. Moreover, even if her behavior was undeniably suspicious, he couldn’t simply arrest her, as she was an enormously influential figure in the Nine Heavens, and doing so would provoke outrage from countless individuals.","Commander Wong suddenly shifted his focus to Senior Bai and spoke, \"And you, Bai Ling? Do you also intend to defy the Celestial Emperor? Someone as highly respected and righteous as you wouldn’t be foolish enough to lie for a criminal... would you?\"","Senior Bai responded calmly, without the slightest hesitation, \"I was present with Celestial Overlord Xu during both the recruitment of that individual and his departure. I will corroborate her statement.\"","\"Then would you be willing to let us read your memories?\" Commander Wong suddenly asked.","\"I refuse,\" Xu Jiaqi rejected without hesitation.","\"Why not? Because you’re guilty?\"","\"Guilty of what? Knowing someone?\" she scoffed. \"My memories contain countless private matters and priceless techniques—hardly something I’d allow a stranger to sift through. And let’s not forget that the Celestial Emperor showed great interest in my father’s legacy. What if this is nothing more than a ploy to get his hands on it?\"","Xu Jiaqi’s refusal to have her memories read wasn’t unusual, even given the circumstances. Outside of servants or those working in environments like Heaven’s Mandate, requesting to inspect someone’s memories was considered highly intrusive and outright disrespectful, all the more so when directed at a powerhouse like Xu Jiaqi. Even if she were personally accused of killing the soldiers, she still wouldn’t share her memories, even if doing so would clear her name.","That was why no one in the room—besides Commander Wong—questioned her refusal, not even Liu Yucang, who would have benefited the most from her downfall.","Commander Wong trembled with anger as he snapped, \"You think the Celestial Emperor would stoop so low just to covet a few damn techniques?! You must be out of your mind!\"","\"And you dare to demand my memories?\" Xu Jiaqi’s voice turned frigid, her gaze slicing through him like a blade. \"Tell me, Commander—who here has truly lost their mind?\"","\"Enough of this.\" Old Man Bi suddenly interjected. \"Lady Xu and Old Bai are not the type to lie, especially when it concerns the integrity of the Celestial Overlords. I cannot fathom either of them fabricating a story for someone who has tarnished our reputation, regardless of any prior connection.\"","\"I agree,\" Qiang Qing Yun said. \"Moreover, you’ve provided no proof that the man in your portrait was responsible for anything. If you refuse to take our word for it, why should we accept yours?\"","\"...\"","Commander Wong fell silent for a long moment before responding, \"Very well. Since I only came here to investigate and nothing more, I shall retreat for now and report back to the Celestial Emperor first.\"","He turned around and began walking toward the exit.","\"If I were in your shoes, I’d make sure to find the criminal before it’s too late,\" he said before leaving with his soldiers.","The room became dead silent after Heaven’s Mandate left.","\"So... care to explain yourselves?\" Liu Yucang broke the silence and immediately started questioning the two again. \"Unlike Commander Wong, I won’t leave this alone until I find out the truth.\"","Xu Jiaqi turned to him and said, \"I have nothing more to add. Everything I told the Commander is the truth. I recruited him early on because I saw potential in him, but he chose to leave for his own reasons.\"","\"That’s difficult to believe, but given your reputation, I’ll take your word for it,\" he scoffed.","\"The question now is... where that little rat is hiding. Clearly, he never truly left the faction if his actions affected our karma. We need to find him before Heaven’s Mandate returns since they’ll definitely show up prepared next time.\"","Old Man Bi nodded and said, \"The simplest way to draw out a rat hiding in its hole is to flush it out by force. We can perform a mass recall and verify every member’s identity.\"","\"That might take a while, but it’ll definitely help us find him,\" Qiang Qing Yun said, agreeing with the plan."]},{"number":2249,"title":"Chapter 2249: Towards the Ninth Heaven!","paragraphs":["\"To make this fair, we’ll verify every single member, regardless of their status or when they joined,\" Qiang Qing Yun continued. \"After all, there’s a chance this individual is in disguise or has assumed the identity of an existing member.\"","\"Sounds good. We’ll start from those at the highest position and work our way down,\" Old Man Bi said.","\"Do I need to prove my identity?\" Xu Jiaqi suddenly asked.","\"Uh... no, I think you’re fine—\"","\"Of course, you do.\" Liu Yucang interrupted Qiang Qing Yun. \"It wouldn’t be fair to the rest of the members if we, the leaders, don’t do it first. Lead by example, right?\"","Xu Jiaqi didn’t argue with him and said, \"Then let’s do it right now. I’ll even go first.\"","\"Are you in a hurry to go somewhere?\" Liu Yucang stared at her with narrowed eyes and a provocative smile.","\"Isn’t it obvious? I need to find that Outsider to question him,\" she said.","\"Are you sure you’re not trying to hide him? Think how bad it’d look for you if you left now,\" Old Man Bi said.","\"Moreover, we’re not even prepared to begin the investigation,\" added Qiang Qing Yun.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Xu Jiaqi said, \"Very well. I will remain here until every member has been verified.\"","She walked back to her seat with her usual calmness, though the faint irritation on her face was impossible to miss.","Some time later, Old Man Bi spoke. \"Let’s begin by recalling our members. Since Lady Xu insists on going first, we’ll start with the ones recruited under her banner.\"","Every Celestial Overlord possessed a unique symbol they could pass down to their recruits. Anyone recruited by those recruits would also fall under that same banner, belonging to the Celestial Overlord who initiated the chain.","And as their leader, the Celestial Overlord could give them direct commands.","\"I’ll recall my members first, then,\" Xu Jiaqi nodded.","\"Make sure you do it right there where we can see everything,\" Liu Yucang said.","Without hesitation, Xu Jiaqi ordered all members under her banner to return to the Celestial Overlords’ headquarters.","Once such a command was issued, her subordinates were obligated to comply. Anyone who failed to return within a certain time would be flagged.","If someone was occupied and unable to return immediately, they only needed to acknowledge the order. Doing so would grant them additional time to comply.","While the members under Xu Jiaqi’s command started making their way to the headquarters, the others prepared for the verification, which required many pills and treasures.","Meanwhile, Xu Jiaqi spoke to Senior Bai using voice transmission.","\"What do you think? Could Yuan really be responsible?\"","Senior Bai sighed, \"I don’t want to believe it, but it’s very likely that he’s involved.\"","He proceeded to reveal that he’d met with Yuan right before the meeting started, as well as their conversation.","He told her about Yuan’s odd response to the news and that he’d randomly apologized afterward.","\"However, he was only at the True Immortal realm when I saw him. I cannot fathom how he managed to defeat the Second Squad of Heaven’s Mandate with his level of cultivation.\"","\"Commander Wong mentioned Void Manipulation. If Yuan had really achieved Advanced Void Understanding, then it might be possible,\" Xu Jiaqi said.","\"I know he’s good at defying logic, but there should be a limit... I also don’t understand why he’d even fight with Heaven’s Mandate,\" Senior Bai shook his head.","The others in the room were aware of Xu Jiaqi and Senior Bai speaking to each other via voice transmission, but nobody tried to stop them, allowing them to talk in private.","\"I’m sure he has a good reason.\" Despite the situation, Xu Jiaqi held faith in him. Of course, this was heavily due to Yuan being Tian Yingzhe’s reincarnation.","\"Where is Yuan right now?\" she then asked.","\"I don’t know, but he did say that he would be ascending to the Ninth Heaven soon.\"","\"I see...\"","\"What should we do about Yuan? Knowing him, he probably hid the truth so we wouldn’t be dragged into this or be directly involved, but... I don’t know what we should do now,\" Senior Bai said in a perplexed tone.","On one hand, he wanted to trust Yuan, yet on the other, the uncertainty left him unsettled. And while he didn’t feel betrayed, he was definitely disappointed.","\"I will send someone to find him,\" Xu Jiaqi said. \"I’ll decide what to do once I hear the story from his point of view.\"","\"Alright...\"","Time continued to pass, and one by one, the faction members under Xu Jiaqi’s banner gathered at the headquarters in response to her command. None of them truly understood the situation, but they were certain it was connected to their sudden loss of karma.","Once enough members had gathered, Xu Jiaqi explained the situation to them in full, leaving many of them dumbfounded.","\"I understand that this is highly irregular,\" she said, her tone calm yet firm. \"But the circumstances are unprecedented, so I ask for your understanding and cooperation.\"","Although the members were irritated by the situation, none of them blamed Xu Jiaqi. Instead, their anger was directed at Heaven’s Mandate and its brazen behavior.","\"Don’t worry, Celestial Overlord Xu! We believe in you!\"","\"How dare those bastards ask for Leader Xu’s memories?!\"","Seeing their reactions, Xu Jiaqi couldn’t help but feel a pang of guilt for lying to them, even offering a silent apology in her heart.","However, this was how much she valued and trusted Yuan, whom she firmly believed to be Tian Yingzhe’s reincarnation. Were it not for that, she would never dare to take such a risk.","Meanwhile, after meeting with Senior Bai and leaving the Myriad of Techniques, Yuan headed straight for the Stairway to Heaven, ready to begin his ascent toward the Ninth Heaven.","\"It hasn’t even been a hundred years since you began your journey in the Lower Heavens, and you’re already heading to the Ninth Heaven...\" Xiao Hua murmured as they approached the Stairway to Heaven, recalling their journey with a warm smile."]},{"number":2250,"title":"Chapter 2250: The First Trial","paragraphs":["\"When we reach the Ninth Heaven, do you think your Supreme Heaven’s Legacy will be fulfilled?\" Yuan suddenly asked.","\"The legacy doesn’t just require you to reach the Ninth Heaven. We will also need to reach a certain location, where we can get our exile curse removed. That place is likely crawling with the Celestial Emperor’s people,\" said Xiao Hua.","\"So we can only get rid of the curse ourselves, huh?\" Yuan mumbled as they arrived before the Stairway to Heaven.","Yuan had expected crowds of cultivators eager to challenge the Stairway to Heaven, yet to his surprise, the area was completely deserted. Unbeknownst to him, the Stairway could now only be attempted during designated periods, a rule that hadn’t existed in the past, leaving him entirely unaware.","This meant that nobody would be able to enter the Stairway to Heaven even if they wanted to sneak inside. However, Yuan wasn’t just anyone. As the Master of the Stairway to Heaven, he could easily enter even if the Celestial Emperor had placed restrictions on the treasure.","Without thinking too much about it, Yuan jumped straight to the top of the staircase with a single smooth movement.","\"Tian’er, open up,\" he said out loud.","The Stairway to Heaven immediately answered his will and opened its doors.","Once he stepped inside, Yuan was greeted by Tian’er.","\"Welcome back, Master. What will you be doing today?\" she asked with a respectful bow.","\"I intend on ascending to the Ninth Heaven, as well as...\" he reached into his spatial ring and retrieved the sword-shaped token, showing it to her.","Tian’er looked at the token and calmly asked, \"Do you want to access that place now or afterward?\"","\"Let’s do it afterward,\" he quickly replied.","\"I understand. Then shall I start your trial now?\"","He nodded, \"Go ahead.\"","Tian’er gave him another bow before disappearing into the void.","Soon, the darkness started to transform, and a large platform appeared beneath him.","\"When you are ready to begin, say ’I am ready’ out loud,\" Tian’er’s voice resounded.","Yuan took a deep breath and said loudly, \"I am ready.\"","In the next instant, Yuan’s vision blurred, and his scenery changed.","Meanwhile, Xiao Hua and the others watched from the spectators’ room as usual.","\"I wonder what kind of trial the Young Master will have to deal with this time. Considering that it took him a few years to complete the last one and this one being his final trial in the Stairway to Heaven, it should be quite difficult...\" Feng Yuxiang muttered out loud as she watched with anticipation.","\"What happened during the last trial?\" Lingyue asked out of curiosity, as she was asleep at that time and missed it.","\"He fought with the Great One during his last trial,\" Feng Yuxiang replied.","\"Then he’ll probably fight the Celestial Emperor for this one,\" Xiao Hua remarked.","<You have started your first trial in the Stairway to Heaven!>","Once the trial began, Yuan found himself in a vast and deserted plain, surrounded by tall grass, distant mountains, and powerful, inhuman presences.","<A formidable force had seized control of the Desolate Continent and transformed it into the Giant’s Continent! Investigate the continent’s situation!>","\"The Desolate Continent?\" Yuan mumbled after reviewing the trial details. This was the first time that he wasn’t given a clear goal.","He looked around. Sure enough, the environment looked like the Desolate Continent.","\"If I am on the Desolate Continent, then this formidable force is likely...\"","A certain individual with an overly friendly smile surfaced in Yuan’s mind.","\"Kulas...\" he mumbled this individual’s name.","After he and Ren Xia freed Kulas from the Immortal Confinement Dungeon, he vanished like a ghost, leaving no trace of his existence for over a hundred years. Then, one day, rumors surfaced from the Desolate Continent of a monstrous being with a colossal body who proclaimed himself its new ruler and slaughtered all who dared defy him.","This individual was obviously Kulas, who had returned and decided to claim the Desolate Continent for some reason.","Kulas, having pushed his Great Mammoth Body Refinement to its absolute limit, had become a near-unrivaled titan—an existence capable of slaughtering Immortals with nothing but his bare hands. His flesh alone could withstand martial techniques and even deflect sword aura, making him a being few under the heavens could hope to defeat, much less kill.","When Tian Yang learned of Kulas’ return, he didn’t rush to confront him. Instead, he chose to watch patiently from the shadows, as he was still a wanted criminal at the time, relentlessly hunted by the Immortal Clans.","In less than a year, Kulas had seized control of the entire Desolate Continent using the name Great Mammoth, as he had discarded his former name. Because of this new identity, the Immortal Clans paid no attention to him and continued to focus their efforts on hunting Tian Yang.","The only reason Tian Yang realized Kulas’ identity was because of his unique physique, which was a result of cultivating the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique.","As the years passed, Kulas continued to increase his influence in the Desolate Continent and even established his own family, which rapidly expanded into a vast and formidable power that rivaled even the Immortal Clans in terms of combat prowess.","Eventually, Kulas seized absolute control over the Desolate Continent and decreed that all outsiders not belonging to his family had one month to leave. When the deadline arrived, those who remained were mercilessly slaughtered.","From that day on, the Desolate Continent was completely sealed off from the rest of the world, and all information regarding Kulas vanished for many years. When he finally reopened its borders, the continent had transformed beyond recognition, and even its very name was changed to Giant’s Continent.","Compelled by curiosity, many ventured to the newly named Giant’s Continent. To their utter shock, its inhabitants were colossal beings who towered over buildings in an ordinary human city, instantly revealing the true reason behind the continent’s new name.","Moreover, these colossal beings did not consider themselves human; they called themselves giants, marking the birth of the Giant Race.","At first, people were either terrified or unsettled by the giants, but as time passed, they gradually adapted and grew more comfortable around them. Moreover, the Giant’s Continent proved to be a treasure trove of rare and precious resources, drawing countless cultivators and merchants to its lands.","In time, the Giant’s Continent became a popular destination for aspiring cultivators. Its lands overflowed with opportunities, and its wilderness was home to formidable magical beasts perfect for honing one’s strength.","While Yuan recalled Tian Yang’s memories, an immense surge of killing intent swept toward him, cutting his focus short.","Yuan instantly turned, raising his right arm before him. The moment he completed the motion, a massive blade came crashing down, yet he caught it with ease, leaving the ambusher stunned.","After blocking the attack, Yuan lifted his gaze toward the heavens just to meet the attacker’s eyes. The one who struck at him was a giant—both in size and cultivation—with strength at the third level of God Ascension.","\"Impossible!\" The giant exclaimed in a shocked voice after his sneak attack was halted in such a ridiculous manner by someone with a lower cultivation.","The giant quickly attempted to reclaim his saber, only for terror to seize him when it didn’t move an inch.","\"W-What the hell are you?!\" he shouted.","Instead of killing the offender, Yuan simply let go of the weapon, causing the giant to stumble backward.","\"Care to tell me why you suddenly attacked me?\" Yuan asked.","Since he knew nothing about the trial, he chose to gather information first, hence why he had spared the giant.","\"That’s none of your business!\" the giant roared.","\"Not my business?\" Yuan’s eyes narrowed, a dangerous glint flashing within them. \"You made it my business the moment you attacked me.\"","Sensing Yuan’s killing intent, the giant trembled in fear. The next moment, he lowered his head and apologized, \"I mistook you for a beast! I’m truly sorry!\"","The giant’s attitude had completely flipped.","\"What? Do you really expect me to believe that?\" Yuan frowned.","Something about the giant’s behavior felt off to him, though he couldn’t quite place why. However, one thing was for sure—that the giant was lying to him.","\"It’s true! I was hunting a beast earlier, but it escaped in this direction! You and that beast are about the same size, so I mistook you for it!\" the giant insisted. \"I promise I’ll be more careful from now on!\"","\"And as an apology, I’ll give you this, so forgive me!\" The giant handed Yuan a leather pouch.","Before Yuan could say anything, the giant continued, \"My hunting buddies are waiting for me, so I’ll take my leave now! See ya!\"","The giant immediately flew away, quickly disappearing from Yuan’s sight.","Although Yuan could’ve chased after the giant, his attention shifted to the leather pouch instead.","He opened it a moment later, revealing a pill radiating dense spiritual energy. Any ordinary cultivator would have rejoiced at the sight, certain they’d received a precious treasure. But Yuan knew better, and beneath that surging spiritual energy, he could clearly sense the presence of poison."]},{"number":2251,"title":"Chapter 2251: Colossal Mammoth City","paragraphs":["\"That giant really wanted me dead, huh? But what’s with that attitude?\" Yuan found the encounter so puzzling that he couldn’t even be angry at the fact that someone tried to take his life twice in a row.","However, when Yuan recalled what Tian Yang had experienced upon returning to the Desolate Continent after Kulas gained control, he was no longer confused.","After lingering for a few more moments, Yuan used his divine sense to survey the area around him until he found a city.","After a short while, Yuan set off toward the nearest city, the Southern Stronghold.","Along the way, he encountered several magical beasts, each ranging from the first to the third level of God Ascension. Yet their cultivation wasn’t the most intimidating part, but their sheer size.","Upon reaching the city, he wandered through its streets, checking to see what had changed compared to Tian Yang’s memories.","’It’s all giants.’ Yuan noticed very quickly that not a single human was present in the city.","He also noticed the strange gazes directed at him ever since he entered the city. Though many tried to conceal it, their killing intent was as plain as the sky. Yet, despite having such bloodlust, none of them tried to attack him like the giant he encountered before.","’If things are like this, then...’","Yuan had a good idea what the trial was about and heaved a deep sigh.","He left the city shortly after and began making his way toward the central region of the continent—toward Colossal Mammoth City, the capital of the continent.","However, halfway there, Yuan was forced to stop when his path was blocked by three giants at the first, second, and third levels of God Ascension.","Two of these giants had unfamiliar faces, but Yuan recognized one of them—the one at the third level of God Ascension.","\"You couldn’t kill me by yourself, so you brought two other people who are even weaker than you... What an odd way of thinking,\" Yuan remarked.","\"Be careful, brothers. Do not be deceived by his cultivation, as he was able to block my strike with his bare hands,\" said the giant, ignoring Yuan’s remarks.","\"So you’re done pretending you’re not trying to kill me, huh?\" Yuan said with a faint smile.","\"Let’s get him, brothers!\"","Without another word, the three giants surrounded Yuan, forming a triangle formation around him.","\"Sorry, but I’m not in the mood to play today,\" Yuan spoke in a low voice as his body suddenly surged with Eternal Essence.","\"What?!\"","While the giants were momentarily stunned by the immense pressure created from his explosive aura, Yuan used Void Manipulation to close his distance with the third-level giant.","\"You’ll go first.\"","Yuan threw a space-shattering punch straight at the giant’s face.","The giant reacted quickly, raising both hands to block, but Yuan’s fist tore through his palms and crashed into his face a heartbeat later.","The force was so overwhelming that the giant’s head burst like an overfilled balloon, his blood splattering in all directions.","\"?!?!\"","The remaining two giants widened their eyes in shock and disbelief, but Yuan didn’t give them a chance to react. He activated Void Manipulation, and in the next instant, both giants plummeted from the sky—dead before they could even move.","Without even bothering to give them another glance, Yuan continued his way toward the Colossal Mammoth City.","As Yuan continued his journey, he encountered more giants, every group larger than the last. Yet no matter their numbers, all of them were helpless before his overwhelming strength.","Eventually, Yuan arrived at Colossal Mammoth City, and unlike his last visit during the previous trial, the atmosphere was completely different—suffocating, heavy, and simmering with anger.","Yuan ignored the atmosphere and flew directly to the massive castle located on the horizon.","\"Halt!\"","Of course, it didn’t take long before someone stepped in to block his path. This time, it was a group of giants, each clad in full golden armor and wielding a massive halberd.","\"Humans are prohibited from entering this city. Leave if you don’t want any trouble,\" said the soldier in the front.","\"Prohibited? Since when?\" Yuan asked.","\"Since last year!\"","’So it’s been a year since this started...’ Yuan thought to himself.","\"Well, I’m here to see your leader, Giant Emperor Kulas.\"","\"Get lost! You’re not even worthy to utter his name, let alone meet him!\"","\"Just tell Kulas that his rival is here.\"","Instead, the soldiers raised their weapons, pointing them at him.","Yuan sighed.","Then, he took a deep breath before releasing a powerful voice that echoed through the city.","\"KULAS, IS THIS HOW YOU GREET AN OLD FRIEND?! GET YOUR ASS OUT HERE BEFORE I DRAG YOU OUT MYSELF!\"","\"T-This crazy bastard!\" The soldiers exclaimed with shocked expressions.","\"He’s going to get us killed! We must hurry and kill him before—\"","A powerful presence suddenly descended, interrupting the soldier.","Yuan raised an eyebrow at the presence. Although it was familiar, it didn’t belong to Kulas.","Soon, a figure came into view.","Yuan narrowed his eyes slightly at the approaching beautiful woman with golden hair and emerald eyes and murmured, \"Xie Mey.\"","It was Kulas’ youngest daughter.","\"Princess!\" The soldiers greeted her.","\"Please don’t worry, we’ll deal with him right—\"","\"No need,\" she interrupted. \"Let him through. He’s an acquaintance.\"","The soldiers stared at her with wide eyes, but they didn’t dare to defy her order and acknowledged it.","Once the soldiers left, Xie Mey, with a nonchalant look on her face, said to Yuan, \"Follow me.\"","\"Where’s Kulas?\" Yuan asked as he followed.","\"Father is... a bit busy right now.\"","\"Why did you come here, Senior Tian?\"","\"Am I not allowed to visit an old friend?\"","Xie Mey looked at him with a pondering gaze.","\"Did you encounter other giants on your way here?\" she then asked.","\"I have.\"","\"Did they do anything weird to you?\"","\"If by weird you mean trying to kill me, then yes, they were acting quite weird.\"","\"Sorry,\" she sighed.","\"Care to tell me what had happened to this place?\"","\"In a bit,\" she said with a slight nod."]},{"number":2252,"title":"Chapter 2252: Unknown Sickness","paragraphs":["Yuan followed Xie Mey back to the palace, but before he even stepped inside, he felt an ominous pressure hanging over the place, suffocating the air itself.","Sensing that strange pressure, Yuan silently confirmed his suspicions about the trial and mentally prepared himself.","A short while later, Xie Mey stopped before a room sealed behind a pair of grand doors.","\"Before we proceed, I must warn you about something,\" Xie Mey turned to face Yuan with a solemn look on her face.","\"The emperor, my father, he might—\"","\"Attack me?\" Yuan interrupted.","Xie Mey’s eyes widened at his words.","\"How did you...?\"","\"Let’s just say that I already have an idea about the situation.\"","Xie Mey didn’t say anything, and after a moment of silence, quietly nodded her head.","\"I’ll let you meet my father now,\" she said as she opened the massive doors.","As the doors creaked open, a lethal aura burst from the room, so dense it was visible to the naked eye, like a physical wave of killing intent. But this sensation was far more dreadful; it felt like the presence of death itself.","Xie Mey’s eyes tightened as she stared into the dark room. Yuan heard her murmur, barely louder than a mosquito, yet shaking with fear, \"It’s gotten even worse...\"","While Xie Mey’s movements were frozen with fear, Yuan strode forward without any hesitation.","\"I’ll be back.\"","\"Wait—\"","Xie Mey reached out to stop him, but Yuan didn’t stop, stepping forward and vanishing into the darkness.","Inside, he narrowed his eyes toward the far end of the shadowy corridor, where a colossal silhouette sat upon a throne the size of a mountain.","However, despite its immense size, the silhouette wasn’t robust. If anything, it looked unnervingly thin.","\"Who goes there...?\"","A coarse voice echoed through the room, sending chills down Yuan’s spine—not out of fear, but because it stirred memories he would rather have forgotten.","\"Hey, Kulas.\" Yuan calmly responded.","\"!!!\"","The massive silhouette could be seen visibly trembling upon hearing his voice.","\"You are... Tian Yang?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"S-Scram!\" Kulas suddenly roared.","\"I just got here, though?\"","\"I don’t care! Get lost!\"","\"Is this really how you treat an old friend who came to visit? I’m not leaving until I see your face.\"","\"...\"","\"Please... just leave. I don’t want you to see me in my current condition—No... I don’t want to hurt my only friend,\" Kulas responded after a brief moment of silence.","\"Hurt me?\" Yuan suddenly laughed out loud. \"Do you really think you’re even capable of that?\"","Yuan suddenly summoned some flames, lighting up the place just enough to see Kulas.","When Yuan finally saw Kulas clearly, his heart trembled, though the sight wasn’t entirely unexpected.","Kulas, once a towering figure of strength whose muscles could make any body refiner envious, was now so emaciated that his bones protruded beneath his skin. He looked no different from someone who had been starved their entire life. Hell, he looked many times worse than when he was imprisoned in the dungeon.","When Kulas first took control of the Desolate Continent and established his own family, he had been in perfect health. But sometime later, he suddenly fell ill with an unknown sickness—at least, that was what Tian Yang had believed when he’d first seen Kulas in such a condition.","This illness caused Kulas to lose his rationality at times, turning him dangerously unstable. Worse yet, it didn’t affect only him, but everyone who shared his bloodline suffered from it to some degree, spreading its influence across the entire Giant Race.","Although Kulas was not their true ancestor, the giants had inherited power from his blood, much like how cultivators absorb the blood essence of magical beasts to gain strength.","However, oddly enough, this sickness did not affect some females, primarily those with strong yin energy in their bodies, so Xie Mey wasn’t affected by it.","\"ARRRGH!\"","Kulas suddenly released a beastly roar, one that did not sound human, and his aura skyrocketed.","BOOM!","His cultivation—at the fifth level of God Ascension—surged forth like a tidal wave, and his overwhelming pressure came crashing down upon Yuan.","Suddenly, Kulas’ appearance began to change. His golden hair and emerald eyes darkened into pitch black, while his pale skin flushed a deep rosy shade, almost like an overripe tomato, skirting the edge of a demonic visage, though lacking the solid crimson hue true demons possessed.","\"Senior Tian! Please be careful! He’s going to attack!\" Xie Mey warned him from outside.","Sure enough, Kulas suddenly sprang from his throne, shooting into the air before bringing his massive arms crashing down toward Yuan.","However, Yuan didn’t even bother to dodge. Instead, he met Kulas head-on. With Eternal Essence surging through his body, he raised his hands and caught the giant’s devastating strike bare-handed.","\"You’ll need to do more than this if you want to hurt me,\" Yuan muttered softly as he overpowered Kulas, hurling him back toward his throne with overwhelming force.","\"Come. I’ll keep you entertained until you regain your sanity.\"","Yuan beckoned toward Kulas, who was drooling uncontrollably and letting out animalistic noises, as though he had devolved into a wild beast.","Kulas released a powerful roar before lunging at Yuan again.","Despite his frail appearance, Kulas was anything but weak, and every strike he unleashed sent tremors rippling through the entire city.","Yet, Yuan met all of his attacks head-on, blocking them with ease.","Kulas rampaged without rest for three straight days, but eventually his body calmed, his appearance returned to normal, and he collapsed to his knees.","\"What should I do, Tian Yang...?\" Kulas spoke in a weak voice. \"There’s this voice inside my head constantly telling me to kill. I cannot contain this madness no matter how hard I try, and it gets worse every time I lose control.\"","He lifted his head to look at Yuan with a pleading gaze, \"Please, kill me before I turn into a monster. You’re the only one I can count on.\"","Yuan didn’t respond and merely stood there in silence."]},{"number":2253,"title":"Chapter 2253: Unknown Sickness(2)","paragraphs":["\"What are you waiting for? Hurry up and kill me,\" Kulas urged when Yuan remained silent.","Yuan closed his eyes and sighed out loud, \"I wasn’t able to save you in the past because of my lack of experience, but this time, for sure...\"","\"Save me...? Can I even be saved at this point?\" Kulas gave a hollow, defeated chuckle.","In the past, Tian Yang did everything he could to find a cure for Kulas, but alas, even after traveling the entire world, he was unable to find a clue to his illness.","And while Tian Yang traveled the world, Kulas’ condition continued to deteriorate. It eventually grew so severe that he—and the entire Giant Race—abandoned their continent and embarked on a murderous rampage, slaughtering countless innocent lives.","This ignited the first great war in history before the Heavenly War of Immortals and Gods. Although its scale and destruction were nowhere near that of the Heavenly War of Immortals and Gods, and almost nobody knows of its history today, it still devastated countless lives. In the end, Tian Yang was forced to do the unthinkable—ending Kulas’ life with his own hands.","However, even after Tian Yang ended his life, Kulas’ suffering did not come to an end.","\"Get some rest, Kulas, and let me handle everything,\" Yuan said to him.","\"If you say so...\" Kulas mumbled before he closed his eyes and fell asleep where he knelt.","\"Good heavens... When were you this strong?\" Xie Mey entered the room shortly after Kulas fell asleep.","\"I’m not as strong as you think,\" Yuan said, shaking his head.","\"Well, you defeated my father, and as far as I know, he has never lost to anyone.\"","Xie Mey glanced at Kulas, then asked, \"Do you know what’s wrong with him—or with the entire Giant Race, for that matter? It all began a little over a year ago, when Father started having sudden bursts of temper. At first, we thought he was simply in a bad mood... but by the time we realized something was truly wrong, it was already too late. Medicines and treasures... nothing we tried could cure him.\"","After a brief silence, Yuan replied, \"I don’t know the full extent of what he’s afflicted with, but I do know its origin and possibly how to cure it.\"","\"Really?! That’s great news!\" Xie Mey was so overjoyed to hear this news that she started jumping up and down like an excited child.","However, Yuan shook his head and said, \"It’s going to be risky, and I’ll need some time to prepare.\"","\"Take all the time you need!\" she said. \"And is there anything I can help with?\"","\"No.\"","\"Is that so... Then when will you be ready?\"","\"Give me a week.\"","\"Okay. If there’s anything you need, let me know. I’ll be right here.\" Xie Mey said as she approached Kulas and picked him up.","\"I’ll be back after I bring him to his room.\"","She left the next moment.","When Xie Mey returned a few minutes later, she found Yuan sitting on the ground in the lotus position, his eyes closed, seemingly in a state of cultivation.","’What is that weird energy surrounding him?’ she wondered inwardly as she could somewhat sense the otherworldly aura around him.","A few days later, Yuan suddenly opened his eyes and asked, \"Do you know what an Outer God or an Eternal is?\"","\"Outer God? No, this is the first time I’ve heard of it,\" she said while shaking her head.","\"Does it have anything to do with my father’s condition?\"","Yuan nodded and elaborated, \"They’re beings that exist beyond our world—powerful existences that consider themselves the true gods of this universe. I don’t know why, but Kulas’ condition was caused by one of them.\"","\"How can you tell?\" Xie Mey asked.","\"I was told by one of these existences,\" he calmly replied.","\"What...?\" Xie Mey raised an eyebrow.","However, Yuan didn’t elaborate further.","Although Tian Yang had failed to find a cure for Kulas in time, he never stopped researching the cause even after Kulas’ death. Then, a few lifetimes later, he finally learned the truth from another Eternal.","\"This ’illness’ doesn’t target the body—it targets the soul,\" he said suddenly. \"It corrodes one’s very essence, twisting them into a mindless killer who can only think of slaughtering everything around them. It’s similar to how a cultivator might lose themselves if they fall to their heart demon. However, that’s not even the cruelest part.\"","Xie Mey swallowed nervously as she wondered what else could be worse than corrupting one’s soul.","\"Those whose souls are corrupted cannot reincarnate; they can only suffer until their very soul is destroyed. That means they won’t find rest even in death.\"","\"How cruel... why would they do something like that to my father?\" Xie Mey sighed.","\"These beings don’t normally target someone without a reason,\" Yuan said. \"In their eyes, we’re no different from ants, so they wouldn’t go out of their way to do something like this for fun. Although I’m not entirely certain, I believe Kulas may have become involved with one of them and offended it. Of course, this is just speculation, and it’s entirely possible that one of them just decided to mess with Kulas out of boredom.\"","Kulas’ situation was very similar to Xiao Cangming’s, who had once offended an Eternal and been cursed for it. However, Kulas’ case was far more severe.","Although Kulas seemed perfectly healthy before the illness took hold, the reality was that he had long been broken within. Years of ceaseless torture in the Immortal Confinement Dungeon had left deep mental scars, making him especially vulnerable to mental attacks, particularly those targeting the soul.","Yuan closed his eyes and resumed his cultivation shortly after.","After a few more days of preparation, Yuan opened his eyes again and said, \"Okay, I am ready.\"","Xie Mey nodded and led Yuan to Kulas’ bedroom. Inside, Kulas was sleeping peacefully.","\"I haven’t seen him sleep since he became sick, much less this peacefully,\" Xie Mey remarked as she gazed at his sleeping face.","She turned to Yuan and continued with a warm smile, \"This is possible only because of you, Senior Tian. Just your presence gives Father peace.\""]},{"number":2254,"title":"Chapter 2254: Curing Kulas","paragraphs":["\"I’m going to begin curing Kulas now. It might get a little dangerous, so you should leave us and wait outside,\" Yuan said to Xie Mey.","However, she frowned and said, \"No, I am going to stay here.\"","\"You don’t trust that I will cure him?\" Yuan asked with a raised eyebrow.","\"That’s not it. I just want to be here when he wakes up with a clear head,\" she replied as she slightly shook her head.","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Yuan muttered as he approached Kulas, \"Don’t blame me if anything happens.\"","\"I won’t.\"","Upon reaching the bed, which was large enough to fit tens of thousands of people with ease, Yuan sat down and pressed his hands against Kulas’ massive body.","\"I should also warn you... This process will require me to destroy his body, leaving nothing but his soul.\"","\"What?!\" Xie Mey exclaimed. \"You should’ve said that before we even entered this room!\"","\"So do you want me to stop?\" Yuan asked without even looking at her.","\"No...\" Xie Mey responded after a moment of hesitation.","\"As long as his soul is unharmed, we can just make another body for him,\" Yuan continued.","\"Creating another body...?\" Xie Mey echoed, looking utterly confused. The concept of crafting new vessels simply didn’t exist in the early years of the Primordial Era. In fact, it wasn’t known at all until much later—near the era’s end—when more cultivators reached the God Ascension realm and realized they could survive without a physical body as long as their soul was unharmed.","\"I’m starting now,\" Yuan spoke again before Xie Mey could ask him any questions, and as curious as she was, Xie Mey didn’t dare to disturb him and silently watched from afar.","A few minutes later, an otherworldly aura started surging from Yuan’s body, and the temperature in the room drastically dropped in the blink of an eye.","’W-What is this coldness?!’ Xie Mey cried inwardly as she shivered nonstop. As a giant, her body was naturally more robust and resilient than ordinary cultivators, allowing them to endure harsh climates without training.","Xie Mey, who had never experienced such cold before, trembled uncontrollably, her teeth clattering together.","<Shiva’s Eternal Frost>","Since whatever was affecting Kulas was weak to yin energy, Yuan enveloped Kulas’ body with Shiva’s Eternal Frost, the most extreme yin energy he knew. In the blink of an eye, the entire room froze over with every inch of it encased in ice.","Xie Mey enveloped herself with Celestial Qi, but it was useless against the power of an Eternal.","’Even my Celestial Qi cannot block the cold?! I’ll freeze to death at this rate!’ Xie Mey, despite her earlier words and boldness, left the room after realizing that she could not endure the cold.","Once Xie Mey left the room, Yuan’s aura abruptly surged even more, almost as if he’d purposefully held back for Xie Mey.","Now that he didn’t have to worry about her, Yuan focused entirely on curing Kulas.","Although Yuan had increased his Eternal Essence drastically after refining the essence of the void, he was still only able to maintain Shiva’s Eternal Frost for a few minutes before becoming exhausted.","Once he was exhausted, Yuan immediately started absorbing the illness that clung to Kulas’ soul, refining it into his own essence.","Time flew, and in an instant, a whole month had passed with Yuan focused solely on curing Kulas. Yet, to Yuan, who was constantly exhausting himself, the month felt like an eternity.","After a month, Yuan had managed to completely absorb whatever was affecting Kulas.","However, as a result, Kulas’ body was destroyed, leaving behind a weakened soul, just as Yuan had predicted.","Shiva’s Eternal Frost had not only weakened the sickness but also caused irreparable damage to Kulas’ body, and if Yuan hadn’t extracted Kulas’ soul, his soul would’ve likely shattered.","Yuan collapsed on the bed, his body soaked in sweat despite the freezing temperature in the room.","Although Xie Mey left the room, she never truly left and had waited outside for an entire month. When she noticed Yuan’s otherworldly aura had disappeared, she immediately opened the door.","\"Senior Tian! What happened with the treatment?!\" she cried as she entered the room.","\"Don’t worry, he’s fine. I have removed whatever was affecting him,\" he responded in a weak voice.","\"Thank you... truly...\" Xie Mey said, bawling her eyes out, but her tears froze instantly due to the cold.","Ding!","<You have cleared the first trial>","After clearing the trial, the scenery around Yuan dissolved, and he returned to the Stairway to Heaven. However, while everything from the trial should have vanished, something remained with him.","Yuan, still lying on the ground from exhaustion, stared at Kulas’ soul that was hovering above him with a calm gaze.","\"Sorry it took so long, but now, you’re free...\" Yuan muttered with a smile on his face. \"You can finally reincarnate properly.\"","Since the unknown sickness prevented Kulas’ soul from reincarnating, Tian Yang had kept Kulas’ soul with him, waiting until he found a way to cure it. Although he had discovered a method long ago, he lacked one crucial component—a yin energy strong enough to weaken the sickness so it wouldn’t destroy Kulas’ soul when trying to remove it.","Then, after many reincarnations, Yuan acquired Shiva’s Eternal Essence, the power that was needed to cure Kulas.","\"What are you waiting for?\" Yuan spoke again when Kulas’ soul remained unmoving. \"You’re no longer bound, so go reincarnate and live a new life.\"","Kulas’ soul, which had been slumbering since the Primordial Era, began to wake up, indicated by the faint aura it emitted.","Moments later, a familiar voice echoed softly, \"Tian Yang, my friend... my sworn brother...\"","\"Though it may seem as if I’ve been slumbering ever since the day you killed me and sealed my soul, I was awake and fully conscious. The journeys you took, the hardships you lived through while carrying me... I was there with you, watching over you like some sort of spiritual guardian.\"","\"Kulas...? What are you...\"","\"I don’t want to reincarnate and forget everything,\" he quickly answered. \"I want to continue going on adventures with you—not as a soul like some luggage, but by your side, just like when we journeyed through Han Zexian’s Tomb together. Moreover, I still haven’t properly thanked you for saving me.\"","Yuan’s eyes widened, but before he could respond, Kulas suddenly bellowed, his tone resolute.","\"Forge me a new body, Tian Yang!\""]},{"number":2255,"title":"Chapter 2255: The Second Trial","paragraphs":["\"You want me to forge you a new vessel...?\" Yuan stared at Kulas’ soul with wide eyes.","\"What? Don’t tell me you’re going to refuse and force me to reincarnate...\" Kulas remarked with a somewhat worried voice.","Yuan shook his head with a smile and said, \"Why would I do that? If you don’t want to reincarnate, then so be it. However, if you want me to craft you a vessel that’ll fit your taste... it might be a little difficult.\"","\"Hahaha!\" Kulas suddenly burst out laughing, \"Did you think I was asking you to forge me a giant’s body? I couldn’t care less about the size. You can forge me an ordinary body if you want.\"","\"In that case, it’s doable. However, you’ll still have to wait until I finish with the trials since I don’t have any ingredients on me at this moment.\"","\"Fine, but don’t make me wait too long, or I might accidentally reincarnate from boredom,\" said Kulas.","\"Seeing how you can already make such jokes despite everything that has happened, I think you’ll be fine,\" Yuan remarked with a smile.","Kulas fell silent for a moment before speaking again, \"Although I had my ups and downs in life, it’s nothing compared to what you have experienced. I’m merely inspired and following what you’re doing.\"","\"Is that so...\"","\"Anyway, go ahead and continue what you were doing. I may sound fine, but I am actually exhausted, so I’ll take a quick nap. Wake me up when my new vessel is ready,\" Kulas said. \"We can continue this conversation at that time.\"","\"Alright. Sleep well.\"","Kulas’ soul disappeared into the void shortly after, but he didn’t vanish. Instead, Tian’er had taken his soul and placed him somewhere safe.","Ever since Tian Qiyuan crafted the Stairway to Heaven, Kulas’ soul had resided within the treasure, arguably the safest in the Nine Heavens. After all, the Stairway to Heaven was used to traverse the Nine Heavens by its residents. It was a treasure that even the Celestial Emperor considered extremely valuable, so nobody has tried to covet or damage it.","Moreover, the Stairway to Heaven was one of Tian Qiyuan’s masterpieces, rivaling Number One Under Heaven.","After Kulas left, Yuan focused solely on recovering his energy.","Meanwhile, Feng Yuxiang and the others chatted about the situation.","\"I can’t believe that such an ancient figure is still alive,\" Feng Yuxiang remarked.","\"Giant Emperor Kulas was one of the most powerful figures of the Primordial Era, predating even the Asura Clan,\" Xiao Hua said. \"It’s no exaggeration to say he was one of the key reasons the Celestial Emperor was able to rise into existence.\"","\"Huh? What do you mean?\" Feng Yuxiang looked at her with a puzzled face.","\"The Celestial Emperor wasn’t even a concept during his time,\" she explained. \"Back then, the Nine Heavens—known as Divine Heavens were controlled by the Immortal Clans. One day, Giant Emperor Kulas waged war against the human race. He and the giant race, which was under his command, wreaked havoc across the Divine Heavens and killed countless people. The war forced the Immortal Clans and many other powerful families to come together for the first time.\"","\"However, Giant Emperor Kulas suddenly vanished into thin air one day. Without their leader, the giant race quickly crumbled, and the war ended shortly after. To this day, nobody knows what happened to Giant Emperor Kulas—well, except us.\"","\"Anyway,\" Xiao Hua continued, \"after the war, the Immortal Clans and the other families went their separate ways. But those families, having once tasted what it felt like to command the entire world, couldn’t let go of that power and began seeking ways to rule the world once more.\"","\"The Immortal Clans and many other powerful families began fighting among themselves, each seeking to rule the Divine Heavens. Although the Immortal Clans had once been the strongest, their influence had been greatly weakened by a madman who targeted them specifically, ultimately causing them to lose the war.\"","\"Of course, the Immortal Clans weren’t the only powerful families. Many hidden families stepped out from the shadows to join the war as well. After many years of conflict, one family emerged victorious and became the first Celestial Family in history.\"","\"Unfortunately, that family abused their newfound power to hell and back... and, well, you already know what happened after that, so I’ll spare you the details.\"","Feng Yuxiang listened to Xiao Hua’s history lesson with a loosened jaw.","\"I’ve never heard anything about a war between the Giant Race and humans, and I’ve read countless ancient scrolls,\" she remarked.","\"Well, it was ages ago—back when this world had only just come into existence. In those days, a few thousand years felt unimaginably long, unlike now, where cultivators can survive for tens of thousands of years with ease. I only know of this history because the Asura Clan once served the first Celestial Family. Because of that, we had access to records hidden from the rest of the world,\" Xiao Hua said with a light shrug.","Lan Yingying looked at Xiao Hua and remarked with a smile, \"To me, you’re just as ancient as the Giant Emperor.\"","Xiao Hua shook her head.","\"Although we both existed within the same era—the Primordial Era—it doesn’t feel like it. The world before the Celestial Family came into existence was vastly different.\"","Some time later, Yuan ended his cultivation and said, \"I’m ready to begin the next trial.\"","At his words, the void stirred once more.","When the shifting finally settled, Yuan found himself standing above the clouds, surrounded by an endless expanse of blue sky.","<You have started your second trial in the Stairway to Heaven!>","<A majestic palace stands before your presence...>","A colossal palace emerged on the horizon, suspended atop a platform of clouds. It exuded a boundless, divine aura, as though it were the dwelling place of a god.","When Yuan saw the familiar-looking palace before him, he sighed. Unlike the first trial, he immediately knew what he had to do in this trial.","\"That’s... the Celestial Palace!\" Xiao Hua exclaimed, her eyes widening at the sight."]},{"number":2256,"title":"Chapter 2256: Storming the Celestial Palace","paragraphs":["\"The Celestial Palace... as in the Celestial Emperor’s place?\" Lan Yingying asked.","Xiao Hua nodded. There was no mistaking it, as she’d visited that place countless times in the past.","Shortly after the Celestial Palace appeared, Yuan began making his way toward it. But barely half a minute later, he noticed several tiny black dots emerging from the palace. As they drew closer, the dots expanded into the shapes of human silhouettes, and their powerful aura became clearer.","In the blink of an eye, ten fifth-level God Ascension cultivators surrounded him, their aura surging with Celestial Qi and killing intent.","\"Evil God! How bold of you to come here by yourself! You must have finally gotten tired of living!\" One of the cultivators shouted.","\"Don’t worry, we’ll kill you soon. However, if you’re hoping it’d be a painless death, we’ll have to disappoint you.\"","\"You will pay for all of the atrocities you committed! Not only have you taken countless lives, but you also have no boundaries, killing children and the innocent without batting an eye!\"","\"We’ll definitely avenge our fallen comrades today!\"","Hearing such words made Yuan recall his final moments as Tian Xian, when he raided the Celestial Palace alone.","\"Are you done barking? If so, come at me.\" Yuan beckoned them with a nonchalant expression on his face.","\"Die! Tian Xian!\"","The ten cultivators rushed at Yuan.","Yuan didn’t utter a single word as he used Void Manipulation to not only dodge their attacks but also counterattack.","\"Ah!\"","With a single swing of his sword, Supreme Sword Aura, enhanced with Eternal Essence, erupted across the battlefield, instantly cutting down all ten of the cultivators.","The Supreme Sword Aura didn’t merely kill them... it butchered them. In the blink of an eye, their bodies were sliced thousands of times, flesh and bone shredded away until nothing remained but blood. It was as if the cultivators had exploded into a scarlet mist.","After killing the cultivators, Yuan subconsciously lifted his arm to inspect it. At that moment, he realized the trial had done more than change the scenery—it had altered his appearance to that of Tian Xian as well.","\"That appeance...\" Xiao Hua swallowed nervously after seeing Tian Xian’s appearance, her eyes flickering with deep admiration and reverence.","Feng Yuxiang and Lan Yingying couldn’t help but make strange faces when they saw Xiao Hua’s expression. It was one they had never seen on her before, and it was full of obsession.","Shortly after, more cultivators emerged from the Celestial Palace to stop Yuan.","Ten... twenty... fifty...","In the blink of an eye, the number of cultivators appearing to stop Yuan with each wave had grown into the hundreds.","\"Hahaha!\" Yuan laughed madly as he danced in and out of existence with Void Manipulation. Each time he reappeared, dozens of cultivators exploded into bloody mist, staining the sky crimson.","Thud.","Xiao Hua, watching from the spectators’ room, suddenly fell to her knees as tears streamed down her face. Yet despite her trembling shoulders, a satisfied smile bloomed on her lips.","\"I have always regretted not being able to witness this moment...\" Xiao Hua spoke in a low voice. \"If he hadn’t secretly stormed the Celestial Palace alone, I—my family would’ve surely fought alongside him. But alas, by the time we realized, everything was already over.\"","In the past, Tian Xian had secretly gone to confront the Celestial Emperor alone. Although he succeeded in defeating him, it came at the cost of his own life.","Meanwhile, Yuan continued carving his way forward, inching closer to the Celestial Palace.","Those who blocked his path ranged from armored soldiers to ordinary-looking cultivators in simple robes. Unlike the present era—where the Celestial Emperor’s fighters are almost exclusively Heaven’s Mandate—the first Celestial Emperor commanded people from all manner of backgrounds.","Eventually, after slaughtering tens of thousands of enemies, Yuan reached the Celestial Palace’s very doorstep.","Without a word, Yuan lifted his leg high and delivered a ruthless kick to the majestic doors, shattering them instantly.","\"I’m here to take your life for a second time, Celestial Emperor!\" Yuan laughed out loud as he strolled inside the Celestial Palace, where even more enemies awaited him.","\"Evil God, you won’t get to meet the Celestial Emperor, as you will be dying where you stand!\"","They immediately bombarded Yuan with powerful martial techniques that shook the entire palace.","Yuan responded to their aggression with his own, and within moments, the entire place was submerged in Supreme Sword Aura and Eternal Essence.","Minutes later, Yuan walked down the blood-soaked hallway until he reached the next area—where, once again, many people stood blocking his path.","\"S-Stop him! We mustn’t let him reach the Celestial Emperor at all costs!\"","Yuan didn’t even bat an eye as he moved forward, slaughtering everyone in the area without leaving a single soul alive.","Some time later, Yuan arrived before another majestic door. However, this one was different from the others. It was much more lavish and detailed.","As Yuan raised his leg and prepared to kick it down like he did with the others, the doors suddenly flung open by themselves.","\"Come in.\"","A calm voice echoed, beckoning Yuan.","Without hesitation, Yuan stepped through the doors and entered what appeared to be an indoor garden. His eyes narrowed at the tall figure standing among crystal flowers, back turned to him—a posture that made the figure seem unexpectedly vulnerable.","\"Just like back then, you’re tending your flowers while your subordinates are being slaughtered by me,\" Yuan said.","The Celestial Emperor replied, \"Unlike that useless bunch who can’t even stop a single intruder, these Celestial Dahlias are pleasing to the eye. Moreover, even a single petal from them can turn trash into treasure.\"","He then turned to face Yuan, his eyes calm yet carrying a faint glimmer of madness beneath the surface.","\"Tell me, Tian Xian... why reject my invitation? Had you accepted my offer, the war would have been over ages ago, and you could have enjoyed a peaceful, fulfilling life with your family until the end of time.\""]},{"number":2257,"title":"Chapter 2257: Fighting the First Celestial Emperor","paragraphs":["When Yuan heard the Celestial Emperor’s words, he fell silent for a moment before responding in a cold voice, \"I would’ve lived a fulfilling life with Xiu Mei if you didn’t assassinate them.\"","\"I did not assassinate your family. It was General Mo who stained his hands with their blood,\" the Celestial Emperor said in a calm, steady voice—one that carried the tone of someone who truly believed his own words.","\"Are you saying that General Mo assassinated my family on his own accord? That you didn’t give him the command?\" Yuan narrowed his eyes at him.","\"Does it really matter?\" the Celestial Emperor said with a slight shrug. \"It doesn’t change the fact that General Mo was the one who carried out the deed.\"","\"Hahah!\" Yuan suddenly tilted his head and burst out laughing. \"You want to know why I refused to join you? Alright, I’ll tell you.\"","He stared at the Celestial Emperor in the eyes and continued in a serious voice, \"It’s because you’re a coward.\"","\"What... did you just say?\" The Celestial Emperor frowned.","\"You’re a pathetic coward who hides behind others,\" Yuan spat with disdain. \"What did you do during the Heavenly War of Immortals and Gods besides cower in this palace like a rat? From the beginning to the very end, you never showed yourself... You never made a difference.\"","\"How dare you...\" The Celestial Emperor trembled in anger.","\"However, I don’t blame you,\" Yuan continued with a cold smile. \"After all, you were pathetically weak—far weaker than the people you sent to die for you. Even with limitless resources and countless techniques at your fingertips, you couldn’t break through to the God Ascension realm and remained bottlenecked at True Immortal.\"","\"What?!\" Xiao Hua’s eyes widened with shock at Yuan’s remarks, looking completely baffled by the revelation.","\"No way... was the first Celestial Emperor really that weak? Or is the Young Master simply taunting him?\" Feng Yuxiang questioned out loud.","Xiao Hua spoke in a dazed voice, \"Now that I think about it, we never actually witnessed the Celestial Emperor’s prowess in all the years we served him. His cultivation was always concealed, and everything we heard about his strength came from rumors... or from his own people.\"","No one had ever been bold enough to challenge the Celestial Emperor, so no one truly knew his real strength—no one except Tian Xian, who stormed the Celestial Palace after slaughtering everyone who could have protected him.","\"If the Celestial Emperor was truly that weak, then how did the Young Master die...?\" Feng Yuxiang mumbled.","\"Shut up!\" The Celestial Emperor roared after hearing Yuan’s remarks. \"So what if my cultivation is a little slow? I am still the Celestial Emperor! I stand above every being under heaven! My status and influence are the strongest!\"","\"Who are you trying to convince? Me or you?\" Yuan spoke with a mocking smile.","\"Courting death!\"","Without warning, an explosive aura erupted from the Celestial Emperor before he lunged at Yuan, his gaze burning with killing intent.","Unlike the real one, this Celestial Emperor had the cultivation of seventh-level God Ascension.","\"Hmph.\" Yuan let out a dismissive sneer before clashing with him.","With every exchange, their energies blasted out in all directions, destroying everything in sight and tearing through the Celestial Palace, reducing it to ruins within minutes.","\"You’re lasting much longer than before, but still, you’re far from being able to defeat me,\" said Yuan.","\"Shut up! You’re just an orphan raised by bandits!\"","\"You act high and mighty, but you’re no different than a dog who only knows how to bark. I’m really curious how you even managed to become the Celestial Emperor.\"","\"You don’t deserve to know anything!\" The Celestial Emperor exclaimed.","\"And you think you deserve the position of Celestial Emperor?\"","Their battle raged on for several hours, and throughout the entire clash, the two hurled mockery and insults at each other without pause.","Although the two appeared evenly matched, the truth was that Yuan hadn’t been fighting seriously at all.","\"I’m sick of seeing your face, so I’ll end it here,\" Yuan suddenly said.","\"What?\" The Celestial Emperor frowned.","Then, without warning, Yuan’s aura skyrocketed as he increased the intensity of his Eternal Essence.","\"Let’s end this like before, shall we?\"","Yuan suddenly began pummeling the Celestial Emperor with nothing but his fists. The Celestial Emperor tried desperately to retaliate, but he was utterly powerless before Yuan’s overwhelming might.","After beating the Celestial Emperor until his face was unrecognizable—swollen like a crushed blueberry—Yuan shattered his Dantian and tore his arms from his body with brutal force.","The Celestial Emperor collapsed to his knees, staring up at Yuan through the narrow slits of his swollen eyes.","\"If you think... that you’ve won... by killing me—\"","Yuan didn’t even let the Celestial Emperor finish his sentence. He seized him by the jaw, gripped his head, and tore it from his shoulders with a violent yank.","\"A puppet shouldn’t talk,\" he mumbled.","Although Yuan had defeated the Celestial Emperor, the notification confirming he had cleared the trial still didn’t appear, even after several moments had passed.","Suddenly, an unfathomable presence descended, engulfing the entire area in a suffocating pressure.","Yuan calmly turned around and lifted his head, gazing up at the sky—where a massive red eye stared down at him like a god.","\"I remember now...\" he spoke with a slight smile on his face.","\"After I stormed the Celestial Palace and dealt with the Celestial Emperor with ease, the true ruler of the Divine Heavens revealed itself to me.\"","\"Let’s see... what was your name again? Ah... Ahruk, or some dumbass name like that,\" Yuan said as he glared fearlessly up at the eye in the sky.","\"How dare a mere ant mock a God—much less destroy my property!\"","A soul-rending voice exploded within Yuan’s mind.","\"Upset that I killed your little puppet?\" Yuan raised his arm and extended his middle finger toward the eye. \"Why don’t you do something about it?\""]},{"number":2258,"title":"Chapter 2258: Evil God’s True Ending","paragraphs":["Seeing Yuan giving it the middle finger, the eye in the sky narrowed with contempt, but there was also a hint of intrigue hidden deep within. After all, this was the first time a human had ever mocked it so openly.","\"Although you’re a disrespectful little ant, I will give your boldness some credit,\" Ahruk spoke a moment later. \"I’ll give you an opportunity—the opportunity of many lifetimes. Since you killed the Celestial Emperor, I’ll give his position to you.\"","Yuan burst out laughing, \"You want me to take that bastard’s place? What’s the catch?\"","He didn’t immediately refuse, hoping to continue the conversation and recover more memories.","\"You will wield authority over the entire world, and you will gain power beyond imagination—the power of a true God. All I require of you is... to find something,\" Ahruk said.","Yuan narrowed his eyes and spoke, \"This something... is it the Absolute Power?\"","Ahruk’s eyes widened slightly, clearly surprised that a human was aware of its existence.","\"I won’t ask how you came to acquire such information, but yes, as long as you find it and offer it to me, I will make you the most powerful being in the world, even surpassing some Gods.\"","\"I see...\" Yuan mumbled as he closed his eyes.","He’d just recalled all of Tian Xian’s memories from the beginning to the very end, as well as the reason the Celestial Emperor served the Eternals.","To obtain power that transcended human limits, the first Celestial Emperor offered everything he had to the Eternals. For someone like him, the promise of unfathomable strength was simply impossible to resist.","In fact, it was likely that the Eternals had played a role in the Celestial Emperor obtaining his position in the first place. After all, it was hard to believe that someone so lacking in talent could rise to such power on his own.","As for the Eternals, since they cannot enter the Nine Heavens with their true bodies or use their powers, they are forced to rely on humans to carry out their deeds.","\"What is your answer? My patience is limited.\" Ahruk spoke again, sounding a bit irritated.","Yuan opened his eyes to look at Ahruk.","\"What if I refuse?\"","\"Then I will obliterate your soul, ensuring you will be erased from existence for eternity.\"","After taking a deep breath, Yuan spoke, \"In that case, I have made up my mind. My answer is... go fuck yourself!\"","At the end of his sentence, Yuan quickly swung his arm toward the sky, releasing an arc of Eternal Essence that shot straight at the eye.","The Eternal Essence scattered the moment it touched Ahruk’s eye, almost like throwing glass at a rock.","\"The audacity!\" Ahruk angrily roared.","\"Since you do not wish to live, I shall obliterate your soul!\"","Ahruk’s eye suddenly started glowing intensely, clearly preparing for an attack.","Yuan could tell from the sheer amount of Eternal Essence gathering that the attack would rival about 3 percent of Saaruk’s prowess.","Since he’d already survived Saaruk using 10 percent prowess, he wasn’t worried about it in the slightest and immediately prepared to confront it.","\"Perish, you insolent bug!\"","In the next moment, Ahruk unleashed a massive crimson beam of condensed Eternal Essence from its eye, shining down on Yuan like divine judgment.","Yuan made no attempt to dodge or block it. Instead, he coated his entire body in Eternal Essence, forming a sword-shaped aura that resembled the tip of a blade. When the crimson beam crashed down on him, it was split apart instantly, its power scattering outward and obliterating everything around him.","\"Is that all?\" Yuan asked afterward with an unfazed look on his face. \"You talk big, but you’re hardly any stronger than the Celestial Emperor.\"","Enraged by his remarks, bloody veins began appearing in Ahruk’s eye as he prepared to launch another attack.","This time, he unleashed a beam that was about 6 percent of Saaruk’s prowess.","Naturally, Yuan blocked the attack without any difficulty, and he continued to mock the entity.","\"No wonder the Celestial Emperor stayed weak despite your promises of unfathomable power. Did you even give him anything? I’m sure he already received your help, but given how pathetically weak you are, he was only able to reach True Immortal.\"","\"HOW DARE AN ANT LIKE YOU MOCK ME! DIE!!!\"","Suddenly, blood welled at the corner of Ahruk’s eye. A moment later, a single drop fell, but despite being only one drop, it was enormous, large enough to fill an entire lake as it plummeted toward Yuan.","Yuan didn’t dare to underestimate this drop of blood, as it contained enough Eternal Essence to rival Saaruk at 10 percent of his prowess.","Yuan unleashed as much Eternal Essence as he could muster before shooting it at the drop of blood in the sky.","When the two forces collided, they hung motionless in the sky for a brief moment—then Yuan’s Eternal Essence pierced through the blood drop, scattering it in all directions before shooting straight into Ahruk’s eye.","\"Argh!\" Ahruk screamed in pain, snapping its eye shut.","\"You will regret this! I swear I will rip your soul apart! Just you wait!\" Ahruk shouted before disappearing from the sky.","<You have cleared the second trial>","The notification finally appeared, signaling the end of the trial, and moments later, Yuan was returned to the platform within the Stairway to Heaven.","\"Haa...\" Yuan released a deep sigh as he stared at the empty void.","Although he had survived Ahruk’s attack within the trial, Tian Xian had not. In reality, Tian Xian was ultimately killed by Ahruk, mainly because he had been unable to wield Eternal Essence at the time. Fortunately, his soul was not destroyed, allowing him to reincarnate.","\"To think that was how he died in the past...\" Xiao Hua muttered in a dazed voice after witnessing everything.","\"Just how much have the Eternals influenced our world... and for how long?\" Feng Yuxiang wondered aloud.","Shortly after clearing the second trial, Yuan noticed something materializing from the void, slowly drifting toward him.","Seeing the item caused his eyebrows to rise in puzzlement."]},{"number":2259,"title":"Chapter 2259: The Third Trial","paragraphs":["As the palm-sized item reached him, Yuan caught it.","It was a golden medallion—one side engraved with a dragon, the other bearing the word ’Heaven’.","\"This is...\" Yuan’s eyes widened with surprise when he realized what he was holding.","\"T-That’s!\" Xiao Hua also expressed great shock after seeing the medallion.","\"What is that medallion?\" Feng Yuxiang asked, her face full of curiosity.","\"The Crest of Heaven!\" Xiao Hua explained, revealing its significance. \"It’s proof of the Celestial Emperor’s identity! If anyone not approved by the heavens so much as touches it, their soul will be obliterated! Basically, whoever possesses it is the Celestial Emperor!\"","Lan Yingying raised her eyebrows and remarked, \"But Yuan is holding it just fine. Does that mean he’s the Celestial Emperor now?\"","\"No.\" Xiao Hua shook her head. \"Yuan is probably fine because we’re inside the Stairway to Heaven, where that very Heaven cannot reach or influence. Things might be very different once we leave this place, though.\"","\"If it only serves to identify the Celestial Emperor, isn’t it basically a useless artifact?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","Xiao Hua’s expression turned solemn as she responded, \"It’s more than just an identifier. The Crest of Heaven... can be used to create Heavenly Laws, something only the Celestial Emperor is capable of.\"","\"What?!\" Feng Yuxiang exclaimed in shock at her words.","\"Heavenly Laws... aren’t those the rules every living being in the Nine Heavens must obey? And anyone who defies them is punished by Heavenly Judgment, right?\" Lan Yingying asked for clarification.","\"Yes, but not every Heavenly Law has the same function,\" Xiao Hua nodded. \"Let’s say the Celestial Emperor creates a Heavenly Law that prohibits everyone from eating meat. Anyone who defies this law will be punished accordingly. Then there are the ones that change nature itself, such as the one that made everyone in the lower heavens ignore the existence of ’Players’.\"","\"Can the Celestial Emperor create Heavenly Laws without restriction?\" Feng Yuxiang asked.","\"No. Even the Celestial Emperor’s authority has limits. If a Heavenly Law disrupts the world’s balance too much or goes too far against the natural order, it will be rejected. For instance, a law that forbids cultivators from refining spiritual energy wouldn’t be permitted. Another example would be a law that prohibits cultivators from killing one another.\"","\"Does that mean the Young Master can create Heavenly Laws as long as he’s within the Stairway to Heaven?\" Feng Yuxiang then inquired.","Xiao Hua shook her head.","\"The creation of Heavenly Laws can only be done at the Heavenly Jade Tablet, which is located in the Celestial Palace.\"","\"In the end, it’s still a useless piece of junk.\" Feng Yuxiang shrugged.","Meanwhile, Yuan tried to recall when or how he had obtained the Crest of Heaven. Since he died shortly after defeating the first Celestial Emperor, he never had the chance to take it from the emperor’s corpse.","\"It’s no use. I can’t remember.\" He sighed in a defeated tone as he stowed the item away.","It was likely obtained by one of his other reincarnations, but he had no way of knowing until he regained all of his memories.","Afterward, Yuan rested for a bit to recover his Soul Strength before starting the next trial.","<You have started your third trial in the Stairway to Heaven!>","The scenery changed once again, but not by much, as he was transported to the Starry Sky.","<Survive>","A single word appeared as a notification before Yuan.","The next moment, Yuan sensed multiple powerful presences appearing out of thin air, surrounding him.","Yuan calmly surveyed the figures surrounding him. Five in total—each one a towering silhouette shrouded in a black veil. Their features were hidden, but Yuan didn’t need to see their appearance to know exactly what he was facing.","\"So this is the insect who dared to defy us, huh? He’s even more insignificant than I imagined,\" one of them remarked with open disdain.","\"A mere mortal who has only recently learned to use Eternal Essence... Do you really think you have the power to defy us?\"","\"How should we destroy him? It’d be too boring to kill him normally.\"","\"Killing him would be far too lenient. We should make an example of him—for anyone who might dare defy us in the future.\"","\"I agree. Let’s cripple him and torture him until the end of time.\"","\"That’s a great idea.\"","\"Are you bastards done yapping?\" Yuan suddenly said aloud. \"Don’t be so quick to decide my fate.\"","\"...\"","The Eternals fell silent, as though in disbelief that such an audacious mortal could exist.","After a brief moment of silence, the five Eternals erupted with Eternal Essence and launched their attacks at Yuan simultaneously.","Yuan was taken aback for a split second, but the moment he sensed the strength of their Eternal Essence, he immediately counterattacked.","Even with all five of them striking together, their combined might was only comparable to Saaruk at ten percent of his power, if not slightly higher.","\"Impossible! He actually blocked our attacks!\"","The Eternals expressed shock when Yuan’s Eternal Essence perfectly canceled out theirs.","\"If this is all you’ve got, then forget crippling me—I’ll be the one crippling all of you!\" Yuan shouted as he charged at the nearest Eternal.","In response, the Eternal created a blade entirely of Eternal Essence before swinging it at Yuan.","The blade, massive enough to cleave several planets with a single motion, descended upon Yuan, who immediately activated God of War’s Astral Arts and created his own sword using Eternal Essence.","When their weapons clashed, the space around the impact point shattered, revealing a deeper, darker void beneath—one that seemed to devour the surrounding space.","However, the hole in the void quickly repaired itself.","Meanwhile, their weapons strained against each other for a few seconds, until Yuan’s strength overwhelmed it and the Eternal’s blade shattered.","Then, with another swift swing, Yuan cleaved the Eternal’s silhouette cleanly in half.","After the Eternal fell, its Eternal Essence was immediately absorbed by the remaining four, causing their strength to surge."]},{"number":2260,"title":"Chapter 2260: The Third Trial(2)","paragraphs":["Upon absorbing the fallen Eternal’s essence, the other four’s prowess strengthened drastically, even gaining slightly more than what they’d absorbed.","Although the four of them together were slightly stronger than Saaruk at 10 percent of his prowess, individually, they were still relatively weak.","\"To think a mere mortal would be able to defy us!\"","The remaining four Eternals were struck with unimaginable shock as they watched one of their own fall to Yuan. None of them had ever considered such a thing possible, so in their eyes, it was like watching a pig learning math.","\"One down, four more to go!\" Yuan laughed wildly as he immediately charged at their next Eternal.","\"You merely got lucky because he underestimated you! Don’t think it will happen again!\"","The four Eternals fought in unison, each one covering the others’ weaknesses as they pressed Yuan from all sides.","Sure enough, facing all four Eternals at once proved difficult. Yuan wasn’t being overwhelmed, nor was he struggling, but he also couldn’t instantly kill them the way he had the first. As a result, the battle dragged on.","Days turned into weeks, and after a full month of relentless clashes, Yuan finally found an opening.","Upon defeating one of the Eternals, its Eternal Essence was immediately drawn toward the remaining three. This time, however, Yuan didn’t stand by and watch. Noticing that the absorption process was taking much longer than before, he seized the moment and absorbed a portion of the essence for himself.","\"How dare a mortal covet our power!\"","The remaining three Eternals erupted in fury as they watched Yuan absorb the Eternal Essence. To them, it was like witnessing a pig feast at a banquet reserved for gods.","\"You mad? Then do something about it!\" Yuan laughed in their faces as he continued to absorb the Eternal Essence.","\"Kill him!\"","Without pausing their absorption, the Eternals attacked Yuan, desperate to disrupt him. However, just like them, Yuan was fully capable of fighting and refining at the same time.","\"How is it possible for a mortal to have such capabilities?!\"","\"He must’ve received help from another Eternal! That would explain everything!\"","\"Who! Which bastard is backing you?!\"","\"I don’t know what you’re talking about,\" Yuan calmly responded to their speculation.","\"Bullshit! There is definitely an Eternal or two helping you! Otherwise, you wouldn’t be able to use our powers!\"","\"To think an Eternal would stoop as low as helping a human! Shame on them!\"","Yuan raised his eyebrows in a puzzled manner before speaking, \"Aren’t you lot also helping the Celestial Emperor?\"","\"Hahaha! We’re not helping him! We’re using him!\"","\"The Celestial Emperor is nothing more than a slave—merely a tool for realizing our ambitions!\" the Eternal declared.","\"Although the second Celestial Emperor is still lacking, he’s much better than the first one. That ant was utterly useless. He tried to take advantage of the power we gave him to achieve his own ambitions, which led to his own death, even exposing our existence!\"","\"Hah!\" Yuan let out a mocking snort. \"Power? What power? The reason he was still weak even after receiving your so-called ’power’ is because you barely have any to give.\"","Suddenly, the void shuddered violently as the Eternals completed their absorption, their auras erupting upward like a storm unleashed.","Although Yuan had taken a portion of the Eternal Essence, the remaining Eternals grew even stronger than before. It was as if absorbing one of their own didn’t simply transfer power, but magnified it beyond its original limit.","Now, the three Eternals possessed a combined strength that surpassed Saaruk at ten percent of his power, reaching roughly fifteen percent—only five percent short of the point where Yuan had once been completely powerless.","However, Yuan’s own strength had also risen sharply after absorbing the Eternal Essence. He would likely still lose to Saaruk at twenty percent of his true power, but he would no longer be as utterly helpless as before.","\"You will die now!\"","The remaining three Eternals made their arrogant declaration as they bombarded Yuan with overwhelming Eternal Essence.","At this point, Yuan could still match their combined might, but only barely.","Because of the Eternals’ massive size, it looked as though they were clashing at close range, but in reality, they were tens of thousands of miles apart.","Their attacks were fairly simple as well. They either condensed Eternal Essence into weapons and struck with those, or they directly fired their Eternal Essence like a cultivator attacking with spiritual energy.","Their strength was so absolute that the Eternals had no need for things like martial techniques. Such methods existed only for mortals, who relied on them to overcome their own shortcomings.","Of course, some Eternals specialized in certain elements, such as Shiva. However, in truth, any Eternal could do the same if they were willing to invest the time and effort. Yet most of them consider such things pointless—mere showmanship—and instead devote themselves to strengthening their raw power.","After all, every element or power in the universe was, at its core, Eternal Essence. Fire, water, lightning, poison... even basic Qi, Immortal Qi, and Celestial Qi—all of them, when broken down to their purest form, were simply essence.","Time flowed on as Yuan clashed with the Eternals, and in the blink of an eye, three more months passed. While the Eternals’ strength remained unchanged, Yuan’s own prowess continued to rise steadily as he familiarized himself with Eternal Essence.","After all, the Eternals he was fighting were, in the end, nothing more than creations of the Stairway to Heaven.","After another two months, Yuan finally managed to defeat another Eternal.","Now, there were just two remaining, and they wasted no time absorbing what the previous Eternal left behind.","\"What’s wrong? Now that there are only two of you left, you’ve become awfully quiet.\" Yuan suddenly remarked.","\"...\"","The Eternals did not respond, but their auras continued to swell. By the time they finished absorbing the essence, each one possessed nearly ten percent of Saaruk’s prowess."]},{"number":2261,"title":"Chapter 2261: The Third Trial(3)","paragraphs":["Even though Yuan was essentially fighting the equivalent of two Saaruk at ten percent of his true power, he didn’t feel particularly pressured or overwhelmed. It was surprising, especially considering that not long ago, he had struggled just to face one.","’To think I’ve grown this much just from absorbing the Eternal Essence in this trial...’","Yuan himself was astonished by his progress. Unlike spiritual energy or his cultivation realm, gauging his growth with Eternal Essence was far more difficult; after all, the only benchmark he had to measure it against was Saaruk, who was generous enough to reveal his own prowess.","’If I have grown this much just by absorbing so little Eternal Essence, how much stronger would I get if I absorbed all of it?’","Yuan’s heart surged with excitement and anticipation. He couldn’t wait to defeat the remaining two Eternals and claim their power for himself.","He also wondered where the Eternal Essence was coming from in the first place. After all, the Stairway was essentially a spatial ring that stored treasures his previous incarnations had gathered; it didn’t possess the ability to create treasures—or essence—out of thin air.","Time flowed on as Yuan clashed with the two Eternals, the shockwaves from their exchanges rippling through the void and shattering nearby stars.","As the battle dragged on, Yuan’s mastery over Eternal Essence reached unprecedented heights, wielding it as naturally as he could wield Sword Aura.","In the beginning, he could only fire it outward without much control or use it to reinforce his body and treasures. But now, Yuan could mold Eternal Essence freely, shaping it however he pleased.","As his control over Eternal Essence deepened, its power naturally grew more intense.","Now, his attacks no longer merely canceled out the Eternals’ strikes. Instead, he was beginning to overpower them.","After another three months of relentless battle, Yuan defeated another Eternal, leaving only one remaining.","The moment the Eternal fell, Yuan and the remaining one immediately started absorbing their Eternal Essence.","\"And now, there’s only one left,\" Yuan said as he gazed at the massive silhouette in the distance.","\"Do you truly believe you have defeated us?\" the Eternal replied in a calm, almost serene voice. \"We Eternals are indestructible—unkillable. All you’ve done is delay the inevitable.\"","\"Perhaps I cannot kill you now. But eventually, I will find a way,\" said Yuan.","\"Hahaha!\" The Eternal burst out laughing. \"Good luck with that!\"","Once it finished absorbing the Eternal Essence, the remaining Eternal’s strength surpassed even Saaruk at twenty percent of his true power. Meanwhile, Yuan’s own growth left him only slightly behind.","\"This is where you perish, mortal!\" the Eternal roared, its voice shaking the void as it pressed its Eternal Essence down upon Yuan like a crushing mountain.","A vicious light flashed in Yuan’s eyes as he unleashed all of his Eternal Essence to counter the attack. Although his essence was weaker, it was still strong enough to halt the Eternal’s advance for a moment.","However, once that brief moment passed, the Eternal’s essence resumed its descent, pressing down on Yuan with enough force to threaten his very existence.","Yuan gritted his teeth and forced himself to the limit. If his Eternal Essence wasn’t strong enough, then he needed to find a way to strengthen it.","\"I know you’re not mature yet, but I need your help here!\" Yuan suddenly muttered, almost as if he was talking to himself.","Suddenly, Yuan could feel his Dantian heating up, as if it were responding to him.","<The Spirit Tree senses ???’s essence>","<The Spirit Tree trembles with excitement>","<The Spirit Tree spreads its roots throughout your body>","Yuan felt a strange sensation stir within him, spreading rapidly through every inch of his body.","<Eternal Constitution(Incomplete) activated>","In the very next moment, the Eternal’s essence pressing down on Yuan suddenly began to weaken, but it wasn’t fading into nothing, and it was flowing directly into Yuan’s body, almost as if it were being absorbed.","\"What is going on?!\" The Eternal exclaimed, puzzled, as it witnessed its essence being absorbed by Yuan at a rapid rate.","\"He’s absorbing my active essence?! That’s impossible!\"","Absorbing an Eternal’s active attack was completely different from absorbing something inactive—like Shiva’s essence or the remnant essence Saaruk had left in Xiao Cangming long ago.","Active essence was simply too volatile—too pure—for even most Eternals to take in.","Attempting to absorb it too hastily would be like trying to gather molten lava in the midst of an eruption rather than waiting for it to cool. If attempted, they would only injure themselves.","Although the vast majority of Eternals lacked such an ability, the strongest Eternals were capable of it, and this was one of the traits that set them above the rest.","And yet, Yuan absorbed active essence as naturally as he would absorb a cultivator’s strike with spiritual energy.","\"How can a mere mortal do something even I cannot?! This cannot be possible!\"","Even though its eyes were hollow—mere empty outlines in the shadowy silhouette—Yuan could still discern the fear trembling within them.","Absorbing the Eternal’s strike caused a tremendous surge of power within Yuan, but he knew it was only a temporary effect, and his actual Eternal Essence had hardly grown at all.","Seizing the moment, Yuan launched a swift counterattack. The Eternal immediately faltered, too afraid to unleash another attack, as it was fearful that Yuan would absorb it again and weaponize its own power against it.","\"Damn it! Damn it all! How am I struggling against a mere mortal?!\" the Eternal roared, its voice trembling with rage and frustration as it desperately focused on defense.","Ultimately, it took only a few days for the last Eternal to fall. Driven into desperation, it subconsciously launched another attack, but Yuan absorbed it just as easily as before, and that single mistake ended it.","<You have cleared the third trial>","The notification appeared moments later, and Yuan was brought back to the platform shortly after, where Tian’er was waiting."]},{"number":2262,"title":"Chapter 2262: Unique Trial","paragraphs":["\"Great job clearing the trials, Master.\" Tian’er congratulated him upon his return to the platform.","\"Was that the last trial?\" Yuan asked.","He was sure there would be more since it would’ve been called the ’final’ trial if it were the last one.","Tian’er shook her head and calmly responded, \"No, there is one more trial.\"","\"I figured. Then you must be here to give me my reward for clearing the previous trial.\"","However, Tian’er shook her head again and said, \"Master, I am here to warn you about the final trial.\"","\"Warn me...?\" Yuan swallowed nervously, as this had never happened before.","Tian’er continued, \"Although you haven’t cleared all of the trials, you have already received the qualifications to enter the Ninth Heaven. The next trial will be the last one, and it’ll be unlike any trial you’ve experienced before.\"","\"If I can enter the Ninth Heaven without clearing the final trial... what’s the point of the trial?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"What?\"","\"Not only is the trial unique, but it has never been challenged before, so you’ll be the first one to challenge it.\"","\"I don’t understand... why didn’t my previous incarnations challenge it?\"","\"Because the trial is time-restricted and cannot be accessed until a certain amount of time has passed. However, that restriction ended while you were still in the third trial.\"","\"In other words, it was prepared specifically for this life...\" Yuan muttered.","\"Anyway,\" Tian’er continued, \"If you wish, you may head to the Ninth Heaven right now and return to challenge the trial at a later date, but you may also choose to do the trial now.\"","\"Does it matter if I do the trial now or later? What changes?\" Yuan asked.","\"Nothing changes. The reward... the difficulty... everything will remain the same regardless of when you challenge it.\"","\"The difficulty will remain the same? Even if I were to challenge it after I become a Cultivation God?\" Yuan inquired with a puzzled face.","Tian’er quietly nodded.","\"In that case, I might as well do it now.\"","\"I understand. Here is your reward for clearing the third trial.\"","With a gentle gesture toward the void, Tian’er drew forth a radiant crystal orb. Inside it, a strange liquid churned and sparkled, its motion reminiscent of glitter drifting through oil.","Yuan knew at a glance what this item was, as it radiated with immense Eternal Essence. It was the essence of the final Eternal he defeated.","\"Since you’ve technically cleared the Stairway to Heaven, you can start the next trial whenever you want,\" Tian’er said.","Yuan nodded as he accepted the item.","\"Then I’ll start once I finish absorbing this.\"","He seated himself and wasted no time drawing the Eternal Essence out of the crystal orb.","Several days passed before he refined every last drop, and when he did, the orb crumbled into nothingness.","Yuan inspected his new prowess with a smile on his face.","\"At my current level, even Saaruk at 20 percent of his prowess would be powerless before me.\"","Some time later, Yuan spoke out loud, \"Tian’er, I should’ve asked this earlier, but how long will the final trial take? An estimate is fine.\"","\"It’s impossible to estimate,\" Tian’er’s voice resounded the next moment. \"It could take days... weeks... even years. It all depends on how you proceed with the trial. That said, time will feel and flow differently in the final trial, and it will be much faster than reality.\"","\"How much faster?\"","\"A year in the trial will only be a minute in reality.\"","\"That much?\" Yuan swallowed nervously. The implication was clear. He would likely spend many years in the final trial.","\"Whenever you are ready, Master.\"","Yuan closed his eyes and took a deep breath.","\"Let me speak with the others first.\"","\"Okay.\"","Before Yuan could even blink, he was teleported to the spectators’ room, where Xiao Hua and the others were waiting.","\"I wouldn’t be surprised if I spend a few years in this trial, so I won’t blame any of you if you wish to head to the Ninth Heaven ahead of me,\" Yuan said.","\"Why would we do that?\" Feng Yuxiang shook her head. \"We’ve spent much longer watching you do nothing—like when you spent 20 years cultivating in White Hell.\"","Yuan chuckled, \"You’re right, but I also want you to do something for me.\"","\"What do you need our help with?\" Xiao Hua asked, seemingly eager to be of help.","\"I want all of you to get stronger,\" he said.","\"Stronger...?\" Lan Yingying mumbled.","\"From this point on, everything will only become more chaotic. We’ll be facing experts who stand at the peak of the cultivation world... and beyond. That’s why I want all of you to grow strong—strong enough to protect yourselves, should there ever come a time when I can’t be there for you,\" he said gently.","\"At the moment, the two of you are far too lacking when compared to Xiao Hua,\" Yuan continued, his gaze settling on Lan Yingying and Feng Yuxiang.","\"...\"","Lan Yingying and Feng Yuxiang had no response and could only lower their heads, feeling somewhat ashamed. They already knew this truth, even without Yuan pointing it out.","\"Therefore, instead of wasting your time waiting for me, you should do something that will actually benefit you.\" Yuan continued.","\"With your talents, I’m sure you’ll be able to show significant progress by the time I finish my trial.\"","Lan Yingying and Feng Yuxiang exchanged defeated looks with each other.","\"I get it, Young Master.\" Feng Yuxiang turned to face him and sighed with a bitter smile on her face, \"Even though we’re supposed to be the new generation of Divine Supremes, we’re nothing but useless luggage at this moment.\"","\"I possess the strongest phoenix bloodline in existence, but I am still at the Immortal Realm. If I am going to be your number one servant, I will need more than just a powerful bloodline.\"","Feng Yuxiang stared at Yuan in the eyes with a resolute face and declared, \"I promise I’ll be more useful the next time you see me, Young Master!\"","Yuan shook his head and said, \"It’s not about your usefulness. I just want you to be able to protect yourself whenever you’re away from me. After all, I don’t expect you to stay by my side all the time, and I don’t want what happened with Bai Xutao to repeat itself.\""]},{"number":2263,"title":"Chapter 2263: Stairway to Heaven’s Final Trial","paragraphs":["Feng Yuxiang shuddered just from recalling her unfortunate encounter with Bai Xutao.","\"You should know that I don’t value my companions for their usefulness,\" Yuan continued. \"But if you want to keep walking this dangerous path with me—one still full of unknowns—you’ll need the strength to do so. Of course, I won’t abandon you for being too weak or having trouble catching up, but if it comes down to your safety... I will leave you behind in a secure place until everything is over.\"","\"After all, as your master, your companion, and your friend, it’s my responsibility to ensure your safety. There’s a reason I’m not traveling with Meixiu and the others right now, no matter how much I want to and how much I miss them. I can’t put their lives at risk just to satisfy my own selfish desires.\"","\"You don’t have to say any more, Yuan. We’ll do our best not to disappoint you,\" said Lan Yingying. \"Unfortunately, I don’t know where to start.\"","\"I cultivate mostly through devouring other beasts, but I have never been to the Ninth Heaven...\"","Yuan smiled and said, \"Don’t worry, I never intended to let you do this alone.\"","He turned to face Xiao Hua and said, \"Xiao Hua, I would like you to take care of Yingying just as you had taken care of me when I first came to the Nine Heavens. Since her cultivation is the weakest, I’ll feel more at ease with you by her side.\"","Xiao Hua calmly nodded, \"I’ll do my best.\"","\"What about me?\" Feng Yuxiang asked, pointing at herself. \"Honestly, I don’t mind traveling alone. I’m used to it, after all.\"","\"That may be the case, but I think it’d be better to have someone with you,\" Yuan said to her before turning to look at Yingzi.","\"What do you think, Yingzi? Can you go with her for some time? It’ll be much more entertaining than being here.\"","While Yingzi wasn’t any stronger than Feng Yuxiang, it was still better than traveling alone.","\"I don’t mind, but I won’t be able to protect her if anything she cannot handle happens,\" she calmly replied. \"If we were in the Primal Expanse, it would be a different story, but in this world, my options are limited.\"","\"I am aware, but you’re not much weaker than her.\"","Some time later, Lingyue spoke up.","\"Um... what about me, Brother Yuan?\"","\"You...\" Yuan paused for a moment before answering. \"Honestly, I’m not sure.\"","\"You’re only my servant because of Xiao Hua. I never intended to pull you into my problems. So tell me—what do you want? Whatever it is, I’ll try my best to grant it, even if you want to walk your own path.\"","Lingyue shook her head and said, \"As I already said, I won’t know what to do if I am not by your side, so I will continue to follow you. No matter where you go or how dangerous it may be, I still wish to follow you... at least until I have my own purpose.\"","Yuan silently rubbed his eyes for a brief moment before sighing, \"If that’s what you want.\"","\"It is!\" she confirmed.","Yuan nodded before continuing, \"With that being said, I am not going to treat you differently because of your circumstances. If you want to follow me, you’re also going to need sufficient strength.\"","\"I understand.\"","\"Now the question is, which group should you follow...\" Yuan pondered out loud.","\"She can follow us,\" Xiao Hua suddenly spoke out loud. \"If the dumb pigeon gets into any trouble, she won’t be able to handle more than herself, so she’ll be safer with us—with me.\"","\"What?! How dare you look down on me!\" Feng Yuxiang clenched her hands into fists and angrily stared at Xiao Hua.","Xiao Hua shrugged. \"I’m only stating the truth.\"","\"At your current level, you can handle ordinary third-level God Ascension cultivators at best—maybe fourth-level if we factor in your Supreme Seal. The Ninth Heaven is no playground. Countless powerhouses roam this realm, some even capable of matching my father. In this era, even I, a ninth-level God Ascension cultivator, cannot move freely without restraint.\"","Unable to rebuke, Feng Yuxiang could only grit her teeth in frustration.","\"Then it’s decided. Lingyue and Yingying will go with Xiao Hua, and the two of you will be together.\"","Some time later, Xiao Hua and the others prepared to leave the Stairway to Heaven.","\"I promise I’ll at least enter God Ascension by the time you finish your trial, Young Master!\" Feng Yuxiang declared with teary eyes, looking like she was about to be separated from her lover.","\"I’ll aim to reach the Immortal Realm!\" Lan Yingying spoke with determination.","\"And I’ll become a Cultivation God,\" Xiao Hua confidently declared.","Yuan responded with a smile, \"You’re making it sound like we won’t see each other for decades. It’ll only be a few years.\"","After saying their goodbyes, Xiao Hua and the others left the Stairway to Heaven and entered the Ninth Heaven.","Meanwhile, Yuan returned to the platform and prepared for the final trial.","\"I am ready to begin the final trial,\" he declared with a resolute face.","<You have begun the final trial>","In the very next moment, Yuan felt his consciousness rapidly slipping away into the void.","When he opened his eyes again, Yuan found himself in a familiar scene, and standing before him was a familiar face.","\"Tian Yang, the cultivation world isn’t all fun and games. It’s a vicious path that could easily lead to your death even when you’re not at fault, and it’s a world that we’ll be stepping into soon,\" said the young girl.","’Meng Lili...?’","Yuan immediately recognized her.","Not only did he recognize her, but he also recognized the words she’d just spoken, as it was part of Tian Yang’s memories that he’d already recovered.","’This trial must be related to Tian Yang... but...’","Yuan quickly realized that he couldn’t move his body or speak out loud, almost as if he were only a spectator, watching everything from Tian Yang’s body, just like when he first regained this piece of memory."]},{"number":2264,"title":"Chapter 2264: Stairway to Heaven’s Final Trial(2)","paragraphs":["\"If you’re afraid, then why did you agree to join the sect? You could have stayed here in the village with the others.\"","Just like Tian Yang’s memories, Yuan repeated his words to Meng Lili.","\"Although I am afraid of the cultivation world, there is something I am even more afraid of— the feeling of being powerless,\" she responded with a solemn look on her face.","Yuan watched everything unfold as usual, silently wondering when he would finally be allowed to begin the last trial.","However, he quickly realized that, unlike regaining his memories, which occurred in the blink of an eye, he was now reliving them second by second.","Every movement, every breath, every word that was uttered—Yuan felt himself living through it all, as though the past had become reality.","Time continued to pass, and the events unfolded just as they had before, from entering the Immortal Monastery to performing chores in the Bamboo Garden.","Then he began his life as an Outer Court disciple, constantly pushing himself to the limit in the hunting grounds, where he met Elder Sun.","After many years, he finally became an Inner Court disciple, and before he knew it, he was already preparing for the upcoming Core Disciple examination. To ready himself, he chose to train in the Desolate Continent, a land infamous for its brutal environment and fearsome beasts.","On his way to the Desolate Continent, he encountered a particular young lady and her family.","\"I am Inner Disciple Huang Xiao Li! It’s an honor to meet you, Senior Brother!\"","After their fateful meeting, Tian Yang and the Huang Family boarded a ship bound for the Desolate Continent.","Unfortunately, during their journey, they encountered a Flying Leviathan—an infamous, rare sea beast that had dragged countless ships to their doom and devoured innumerable lives.","Although they had managed to escape the ship with a flying treasure before the Flying Leviathan destroyed it, they were unable to escape its attention, and it quickly chased after them.","During the chase, they encountered a second sea beast, an entity of incomprehensible might, far beyond anything they understood.","While Tian Yang and Huang Xiao Li managed to escape using a life-saving treasure Tian Yang hadn’t even known he possessed at the time, the rest of the Huang Family was not so fortunate.","Unaware that her family had already perished, Huang Xiao Li traversed the Desolate Continent with Tian Yang, hoping to find them.","Tian Yang’s relationship with Huang Xiao Li deepened over the course of their journey, and the two eventually became lovers.","But their blissful days were short-lived. The Gold and Money Bandits appeared, forcing them into a desperate escape. And as if fate itself were against them, a barrier suddenly rose around the entire continent, sealing it off entirely and preventing anyone from entering or leaving.","Huang Xiao Li was killed by the bandits during the chase, and Tian Yang would have lost his life as well if not for Kulas’ intervention.","\"I’m Kulas, what about you?\"","After learning the situation from Kulas, Tian Yang agreed to enter Han Zexian’s Tomb with him.","Right before the tomb opened, Tian Yang encountered Elder Sun and learned about the life-saving treasure she had secretly given him.","However, instead of feeling grateful, Tian Yang was furious. He blamed Elder Sun for Huang Xiao Li’s death, because if he had known about the treasure beforehand, they would never have attracted the bandits’ attention, and he might have even been able to save her family.","Elder Sun was so shocked by Tian Yang’s outburst that she couldn’t even say anything before he left, ending their relationship there.","Once the tomb opened, Tian Yang and Kulas entered and undertook its trials, obtaining numerous valuable treasures and learning powerful techniques that greatly increased their strength. Their bond strengthened through it all, evolving from friendship into something akin to brotherhood, especially after they clashed with Gu Lim.","Tian Yang also met a unique woman named Ren Xia, who was Kulas’ fiancée at the time.","\"Not only are you not fearful of the Immortal Clans, but you even dare to go against them... What an interesting man...\"","However, Kulas and Ren Xia showed obvious disdain for one another, largely because their engagement had been arranged by their families, and the two didn’t like each other.","Ren Xia joined their journey briefly before going her own way, and Kulas had achieved his goal at Han Zexian’s Tomb with Tian Yang’s help, obtaining the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique.","Eventually, they discovered the location of Han Zexian’s legacy and made their way to it. However, the Immortal Clans had arrived first and already seized the entire site.","Tian Yang had no intention of getting anywhere near the place, especially since he had killed Gu Lim and was being hunted by the Gu Family.","However, Han Zexian’s legacy had other plans for him and forcefully dragged him to the entrance.","Since he was powerless against the Immortal Clans, Tian Yang had no choice but to enter the mountain that housed Han Zexian’s legacy—a place only he could access, having received the legacy’s approval.","Inside, he discovered the existence of beings far beyond their comprehension and even learned the method to communicate with one of them.","While Tian Yang spent many years secluded within the mountain, Kulas was captured by the Immortal Clans and subjected to relentless interrogation and years of torture.","When Tian Yang finally left Han Zexian’s tomb after many long years, he immediately sought out Ren Xia, hoping to learn what had become of Kulas.","That was when he discovered the truth of Kulas’ fate.","At this point, Yuan wondered if the final trial was just going to show him all of Tian Yang’s experiences.","And since he was still missing many of Tian Yang’s memories, he hoped that would be the case.","Some years later, Tian Yang and Ren Xia worked together to free Kulas from the Immortal Confinement Dungeon.","After that, Tian Yang and Ren Xia continued messing with the Immortal Clans until a particular rumor of a certain individual began to spread."]},{"number":2265,"title":"Chapter 2265: Fated to Suffer","paragraphs":["Over a hundred years had passed since Tian Yang rescued Kulas from the Immortal Confinement Dungeon.","In all that time, he hadn’t heard a single word about Kulas’s whereabouts, and devoted himself entirely to destroying the Immortal Clans.","As Ren Xia had wished, they began with the Immortal Sword Clan.","The Immortal Sword Clan had been struggling even before Ren Xia’s betrayal, leaving them already weakened. After she turned on them and ruined their plans to sell her off through a political marriage, the clan was essentially half-destroyed even without any further interference.","Although they still carried the title of an Immortal Clan in the eyes of the public, in reality, the other Immortal Clans had already severed all ties with the Immortal Sword Clan and no longer considered them one of their own.","Although Ren Xia didn’t go as far as killing her own parents or relatives, she struck directly at the Ren Family’s businesses, weakening their already fragile position to the point where they had no choice but to relinquish their status as an Immortal Clan and revert to simply being the Ren Family.","Under normal circumstances, another family would have risen to take their place, but due to the ongoing chaos, the Immortal Clans were forced to postpone the selection.","\"Now that the Ren Family is no longer an Immortal Clan, they’ll definitely be targeted by all the people they’ve offended in the past,\" Tian Yang said.","\"So what? They deserve whatever comes their way,\" Ren Xia replied, her tone casual as she gazed out the window of their hotel room.","\"What about you? Now that you’ve brought down your family and achieved your goal, what are you going to do next? Walk your own path?\"","Ren Xia shifted her gaze from the outside view to glare at Tian Yang in the face before responding, \"One goal. I have two goals in mind when I decided to follow you, and I have only achieved one of them so far.\"","\"What is your second goal, then?\" Tian Yang asked.","Ren Xia narrowed her eyes at him, silently staring at him.","A moment later, she stood up and walked over with a mischievous smile.","Tian Yang quietly observed her movements as he sat by the table.","\"Are you asking that because you genuinely don’t know, or because you’re pretending not to notice?\" she whispered while slipping onto his lap, her soft hips molding against him. One slender arm curled around his neck, guiding his face toward hers.","Tian Yang met her gaze calmly and sighed. \"How can you act like this when you just brought about your own family’s downfall?\"","\"And why are you trying to change the subject?\" Ren Xia shot back almost immediately. \"I may not look it, but my heart is anything but calm right now. In such a state, I might do something rash...\"","Ren Xia suddenly reached for his chest with her other arm.","Tian Yang shut his eyes, a quiet sigh escaping him. \"You should reconsider. Anyone who gets too close to me is fated to suffer.\"","\"That... doesn’t sound like a rejection? How surprising.\"","By this point, Tian Yang had known Ren Xia far longer than he had known Huang Xiao Li, and the two had survived multiple life-and-death ordeals together. Although he had tried his best not to develop feelings for her, such restraint was nearly impossible, especially considering Ren Xia’s overwhelming charm and his own lack of experience in such emotions.","When Tian Yang didn’t respond, Ren Xia repeated, this time in a softer voice, \"I said... it doesn’t sound like a rejection...\"","\"If you don’t give me a clear rejection, I won’t be able to help myself.\" She continued, slowly reaching into his robes and caressing his bare chest.","Tian Yang opened his eyes at this moment and stared into her eyes.","\"Don’t say I didn’t warn you later,\" he said in a clear voice.","Ren Xia froze, eyes widening in shock. She had only been teasing and never thought he’d actually accept her. But her feelings were genuine, and since he didn’t refuse her—","Without hesitation, Ren Xia closed the remaining distance between them and pressed her lips to his in a deep, passionate kiss.","After a long moment, it was only when she finally ran out of breath that Ren Xia parted their lips. Her gaze, filled with longing and desire, remained locked on him.","\"I...\" Tian Yang tried to speak but was immediately interrupted.","\"I don’t care.\" She pressed a finger against his lips. \"Even if you’ve changed your mind, it’s too late now. If you want to regret it, do it afterward.\"","Not wanting to waste another second, she rose to her feet and pulled him toward the bed, where she stripped him of his clothes, as well as her own, before savoring every inch of his body from top to bottom.","At this point, there was truly no going back.","Not even half a day after the Immortal Sword Clan had surrendered their title, Ren Xia surrendered her first time to Tian Yang, allowing his sword to penetrate deep within her body.","While the other Immortal Clans hunted them without sleep or rest, the two of them drowned themselves in each other’s embrace for days—weeks, even—ignoring the world outside.","As Tian Yang lay on the bed, his body drenched in sweat and other lingering traces of their passion, he muttered softly, \"Try not to die before I do.\"","With her head resting on his arm, Ren Xia smiled contentedly.","\"If everyone close to you suffers, then I’m probably going to die soon.\"","She brushed her cheek against him and added playfully, \"In that case, we might as well do this as often as possible, so you’ll have more memories to reminisce about when I am gone.\"","\"You truly are something else...\" Tian Yang sighed with a defeated smile.","After only a brief rest, Ren Xia wasted no time. True to her earlier words, she initiated another session, her movements full of energy and intent, almost as if it were their first time."]},{"number":2266,"title":"Chapter 2266: The Great Mammoth","paragraphs":["\"There’s a peculiar rumor going around,\" Ren Xia started a conversation as she rested beside Tian Yang on the bed.","\"Is the rumor related to the Immortal Clans?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"No, not exactly.\"","\"Then it doesn’t concern me,\" he said in a blunt, indifferent tone.","\"Are you sure you’re not interested? You might regret it.\"","Tian Yang narrowed his eyes slightly. Knowing Ren Xia’s character, she wouldn’t be so persistent in a subject if it wasn’t serious or if it was related to him.","\"If there’s something you want to tell me, just tell me. No need to beat around the bush,\" he sighed.","Ren Xia suddenly lifted herself and positioned herself on top of Tian Yang, sitting on his body. Then, with an entertained smile, she spoke, \"According to this rumor, someone claiming to be the ’Great Mammoth’ recently declared himself as the ruler of the Desolate Continent.\"","\"Great Mammoth?\" Tian Yang raised his eyebrows at this familiar name.","Ren Xia gave a calm nod and continued, \"And from what witnesses say, he’s a complete monster, standing almost four meters tall with an unprecedented physique.\"","Tian Yang shot up from the bed after hearing the details, his eyes wide with shock.","\"Oh!\" Ren Xia, who was sitting on top of him, fell backwards but gracefully caught herself.","\"Doesn’t that sound like someone we know?\" she chuckled.","\"It has to be Kulas!\" Tian Yang exclaimed.","He finally realized why the name Great Mammoth was familiar. It was the name of the technique he’d given Kulas—Great Mammoth Body Refinement!","\"What are the Immortal Clan’s reaction? Have they done anything yet?\" he then asked.","Ren Xia curled her arms around his neck, letting out a soft sigh.","\"I wish you’d show me even a little of the passion you always have for Kulas.\"","\"Are you saying that you’d rather be in Kulas’ situation rather than what you currently have right now?\"","Ren Xia fell silent for a moment before speaking again, \"I don’t think the Immortal Clan is aware of his identity.\"","She completely changed the topic. Clearly, she was satisfied with her situation after giving it some thought","\"What makes you think so?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"Well, this rumor has been floating around for two weeks already. There’s no way the Immortal Clans haven’t heard it, but they haven’t shown the slightest response. They’ve been behaving as if nothing happened.\"","\"Moreover, unless they learned about the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique from Kulas, they won’t immediately make the connections just by his size. With that said, even if they realize his identity, I doubt they’ll do anything to him now, especially how much we’ve weakened them.\"","It had been over three hundred years since the fall of the Immortal Sword Clan, and throughout that time, the two of them relentlessly chipped away at the Immortal Clans’ strength. Once untouchable, those clans were now mere shadows of their former power.","Even if they were aware of Kulas’ return, he would be at the very bottom of the priority list with Tian Yang and Ren Xia at the very top.","Naturally, Tian Yang and Ren Xia’s infamy wasn’t confined to the Immortal Clans alone. Across the whole Divine Heaven, their names resounded with fear and awe alike—Tian Yang, the Immortal Slayer, and Ren Xia, the Sword Goddess.","While their names struck fear into the hearts of many, even becoming a warning used to discipline unruly children, just as many revered them. After all, they had done the unthinkable by defying the Immortal Clans and driving them to near ruin.","Even if they were to die tomorrow at the hands of the Immortal Clans, the clans’ reputation would never recover, and the shadow of Tian Yang and Ren Xia would forever loom over them.","In fact, after so many years of failure, it wasn’t just the ordinary people—even the Immortal Clans themselves no longer believed they could defeat Tian Yang and Ren Xia.","\"I guess so...\" Tian Yang muttered with a pondering look on his face.","\"Are you going to see him?\" Ren Xia suddenly asked.","Tian Yang closed his eyes and remained silent for a moment.","\"No,\" he replied in a clear voice.","\"Really?\" Ren Xia’s eyes widened with surprise, as she had already prepared to travel to the Desolate Continent with him.","\"Why not?\" she inquired.","\"He essentially vanished the day we rescued him. Now that I know he’s alive and well, I won’t endanger him by dragging him into our mess. If I’m going to meet him again, it’ll be after we’ve completely erased the Immortal Clans from existence,\" he said, his voice filled with resolve.","If they were to meet Kulas right now, the Immortal Clan would definitely go after Kulas, too.","\"That said, I should still keep an eye on him just in case anything happens,\" he added a moment later.","\"How are you going to do that without getting close to him?\"","\"I’ll hire somebody to watch over him.\"","\"You’re acting like a stalker.\" Ren Xia chuckled.","\"If that’s how it seems, then so be it. As long as I can protect him properly this time, nothing else matters.\"","With that resolve, Tian Yang and Ren Xia intensified their assaults on the Immortal Clans, moving with a slightly greater urgency than before, as though something had spurred them forward.","Time continued to pass, and as the Immortal Clans grew weaker and lost influence, Kulas—now known as the Great Mammoth—rose in the opposite direction. He became a powerhouse and an authoritative figure within the Desolate Continent, eventually establishing himself as its undisputed ruler.","Although Tian Yang sought the downfall of the Immortal Clans, he never confronted them through outright slaughter. He wasn’t looking for massacres. If he had truly wanted to destroy them, he could have easily wiped out every member of their clans besides the Patriarchs.","Instead, he chose a different approach and targeted their businesses and allies, undermining their influence and shattering their reputation, only killing when absolutely necessary.","In this way, the Immortal Clans were forced to watch their influence and power decay year after year—slowly and painfully—much like the torture they had once inflicted on Kulas."]},{"number":2267,"title":"Chapter 2267: The Immortal Clans’ Downfall","paragraphs":["Ten years... fifty years... two hundred years...","Two hundred more years went by, and the Immortal Clans had been reduced to a state nearly unrecognizable.","They were no longer the haughty, untouchable powerhouses they had once been. Now, they were no different from ordinary families—shunned by the rest of the world, largely because people feared the consequences of siding with them. After all, Tian Yang targeted anyone who remained close to the Immortal Clans.","With their power reduced to this pitiful state, Tian Yang could eradicate them whenever he wished. Yet he chose to let them linger, allowing the remnants of the Immortal Clans to spend their final days drowning in regret for ever offending him. As for Patriarch Gu and those directly responsible for torturing Kulas, Tian Yang showed no such mercy, and he crippled every one of them, stripping away not only their cultivation but their limbs as well.","By now, Tian Yang had ascended to the Golden Immortal realm, with Ren Xia trailing just a step behind at Silver Immortal.","Though his time within Han Zexian’s tomb had greatly accelerated his cultivation, Tian Yang’s growth had slowed sharply afterward. Even after consuming countless treasures to refine his aptitude, his talent was still merely above average.","Ren Xia, on the other hand, continued to advance at a remarkable pace. Her natural talent allowed her to steadily close the gap between them.","The only reason Tian Yang even managed to reach the Golden Immortal realm was mainly due to plundering the Immortal Confinement Dungeon after learning about its vault and finding its new location, or he would still be a Silver Immortal right now.","That said, Tian Yang’s cultivation was slightly deceiving, as he also possessed numerous powerful martial techniques that gave him a massive advantage over other cultivators, allowing him to defeat most around his cultivation with ease.","\"Did you hear about the Desolate Continent? It’s no longer sealed off.\" Ren suddenly started the conversation as they sipped tea in a private room inside a high-end restaurant.","Tian Yang slowly placed down his teacup and responded, \"Of course.\"","Over the years, Kulas established his own family and empire within the Desolate Continent. Then, without warning, he sealed off the entire continent, forcing out all who were not part of the Giant Race—a race he had personally created. Those who dared to resist were killed on sight.","Because of this, Tian Yang could no longer watch over him. However, since only Kulas and his family would exist on the continent, he wasn’t too worried. That said, he was curious about the reason behind the sudden seclusion.","It had been over a hundred years since then, and just as abruptly as the Desolate Continent had been sealed, it was now being reopened to the public for reasons unknown.","\"Now that the Immortal Clans are no longer an issue, do you plan on visiting him?\" Ren Xia asked.","Tian Yang took a moment to respond.","\"I’m... not sure. It’s been almost half a millennium since we last met. I wouldn’t be surprised if he has forgotten about me.\"","\"Are you really saying that after all this time? But if you’re truly curious whether he’s forgotten you or not, go see him.\"","Tian Yang raised his teacup and sipped on it before responding, \"I guess so. It’s not like we have anything else to do at this moment.\"","Since achieving their goal of bringing down the Immortal Clans, the pair embraced a tranquil, almost retired existence together, roaming the Divine Heavens at leisure while steadily refining their cultivation in peace.","With their next journey decided, they set off for the Desolate Continent, now called the Giant’s Continent.","Although the couple could easily fly to their destination, they decided to take the ship instead, as neither of them was in a rush to see Kulas.","The journey to the Giant’s Continent stirred the bitter memories Tian Yang had long buried, from his first encounter with the Huang Family, the true beginning of his path as a cultivator, to Han Zexian’s Tomb, where he had first met Huang Xiao Li, Kulas, and Ren Xia.","Even after hundreds of years, those memories remained vivid, resurfacing as sharply as if they had happened only yesterday.","\"What are you thinking about?\" Ren Xia asked Tian Yang, who had been quietly staring out the window of their deluxe room, one of the largest and most luxurious on the ship, ever since they set sail.","\"I never told you about my first journey to the Desolate Continent... did I?\" Tian Yang muttered, his voice tinged with distant nostalgia.","\"You’ve told me many things about yourself, but you have always avoided talking about the Desolate Continent.\"","Tian Yang looked at her with a warm smile.","\"Are you willing to hear about it now?\"","She quietly nodded.","Without further ado, Tian Yang began recalling his story to Ren Xia, from his first meeting with Huang Xiao Li, his first love, to their meeting.","After listening to Tian Yang’s story, Ren Xia finally understood the depth of his hatred toward the Immortal Clans, something he had never spoken of outright.","His story not only revealed the reason behind his relentless pursuit of them, but also the exact moment Tian Yang had become the man he was today—the man she loved.","It was a tragic story, yet Ren Xia couldn’t help feeling grateful for the path it had carved. Had even a single detail of the past shifted, she might never have crossed paths with Tian Yang, condemned to remain nothing more than a tool of her family.","\"Perhaps the real reason why I refused to visit Kulas before wasn’t because I didn’t want to disturb Kulas’ peace, but because I was simply not ready to return to the Desolate Continent,\" Tian Yang sighed.","\"Well, how are you feeling now?\" Ren Xia asked.","Tian Yang looked at her with a gentle smile. \"If it weren’t for you, I wouldn’t be here right now.\"","Ren Xia’s eyes widened, delight shimmering within them.","Saying nothing, she took his hand and pulled him to the bed, where they passionately embraced until the ship arrived at its destination."]},{"number":2268,"title":"Chapter 2268: The Real Giant’s Continent","paragraphs":["\"Attention, esteemed passengers. We will be arriving at our destination, the Desolate Continent, now known as the Giant’s Continent, shortly. Please prepare to deboard!\" The captain’s voice resounded through the speakers.","’Looks like we didn’t get attacked by sea beasts this time...’ Tian Yang thought as he calmly gazed toward the horizon, where a vast stretch of land slowly came into view, growing clearer and larger with every passing moment.","Half an hour later, the captain’s voice returned.","\"We’ve arrived at our destination. Thank you all for boarding with the Purple Lion today! If you wish to return home, there will be another ship arriving in two weeks.\"","After disembarking the ship, Tian Yang and Ren Xia immediately began wandering the continent to see if anything had changed.","\"Wow, they really remodeled this entire place, didn’t they?\" Ren Xia remarked after scattering her divine sense and seeing the changes.","When they had last visited during the exploration of Han Zexian’s Tomb, the only paths on this continent were the ones carved naturally over countless years of wear.","But now, proper roads stretched before them—broad, structured, and astonishingly massive in width, almost as if they were made for large beasts rather than humans.","The cities had changed just as dramatically as the roads, completely transformed and expanded severalfold. Even the smallest buildings now stood tall and imposing, while the largest structures soared so high they seemed to pierce the clouds.","And it wasn’t only the roads and buildings that had changed. The entire continent itself had grown to an immense scale, so vast that humans wandering upon it were reduced to the size of ants in comparison.","As for the dwellers on this continent, everyone from the Giant’s Race was at least three times larger than an adult human.","Setting aside their brief encounter with Kulas in the Immortal Confinement Dungeon, this was Tian Yang and Ren Xia’s first true sighting of the Giant Race, despite the race having existed for over a century.","The giants never stepped beyond the borders of their continent, so seeing one was only possible here.","\"Just how did they grow so massive? Did Kulas teach everyone the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique?\" Ren Xia wondered out loud after seeing the giants.","Tian Yang replied, \"The Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique isn’t something anyone can learn. Even if Kulas passed the technique to everyone in the Giant’s Race, only a few of them would be able to achieve such a level of mastery, not to mention the extreme cultivation method it demanded.\"","\"Then how do you explain the Giant’s Race? Don’t tell me they’re all Kulas’ children?\"","\"We’ll find out if we ask him.\"","The two entered the nearest city to ask for directions.","\"Hey, do you know where I can meet the Great Mammoth?\" Tian Yang approached a passing giant and asked.","\"Great Mammoth? You mean His Majesty, Giant Emperor Kulas?\" The giant replied.","\"What?\" Tian Yang’s eyes widened at Kulas’ name being spoken.","Since when did Kulas stop hiding his identity?","Seeing Tian Yang’s puzzled face, the giant explained, \"Great Mammoth was the Giant Emperor’s warrior name. He now goes by his true name.\"","’Did he stop hiding because he’s aware of the Immortal Clans’ downfall?’ Ren Xia spoke to Tian Yang using voice transmission.","’Or he’s now powerful enough that the Immortal Clans no longer scare him,’ he said.","\"Anyway, why are you looking for the Giant Emperor? He’s not someone you can meet just because you want to.\" The giant suddenly asked.","\"We’re his acquaintances,\" said Tian Yang.","Although he could’ve claimed to be friends with Kulas, nobody would believe him, so he went for the most believable choice.","The giant narrowed his eyes and gave them a suspicious look.","\"What’s your name?\" he then asked.","Tian Yang didn’t hesitate to give his real name.","\"Tian Yang.\"","The giant’s eyes widened with surprise.","\"Y-You’re Tian Yang?! Really?!\" he exclaimed.","Tian Yang raised his eyebrows and asked, \"You know me?\"","\"Of course!\" he nodded. \"There is nobody among the Giant’s Race who doesn’t know your name since Giant Emperor Kulas told us to be on the lookout for you!\"","\"So he’s expecting me?\" Tian Yang muttered.","\"Sure is! The Giant Emperor said to send you his way the moment we see you.\"","The giant wasted no time pointing in a specific direction and said, \"You can find the Giant Emperor at the Colossal Mammoth City. When you meet him, please tell him that it was I, Karan, who sent you his way!\"","\"Alright...\" Tian Yang nodded, looking somewhat speechless.","\"By the way, are you Kulas’ children?\" Ren Xia suddenly asked.","\"Huh? Who are you?\"","She pointed at Tian Yang and said, \"His wife.\"","\"Ah, then you must be Ren Xia.\"","\"You also know me?\" It was Ren Xia’s turn to be surprised.","\"Yes.\" Karan nodded before continuing, \"And to answer your question, every giant is the Giant Emperor’s children in a way, since we have all received his family’s blood. However, only those who possess the Mammoth Bloodline are considered his true descendants.\"","\"So he didn’t teach you the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique?\" Ren Xia continued to ask.","\"What? There’s no way that would happen!\" Karan responded with a surprised expression. \"Only his true descendants would have such a privilege! However, we’ve all been blessed with a body refinement technique by the Giant Emperor. Why are you asking these questions?\"","\"Just curious.\"","\"Well, if you want to know more, please meet the Giant Emperor. He’s been waiting for your arrival for many years now. Now, if you’ll excuse me.\"","Karan gave them a polite bow before resuming his day.","Tian Yang and Ren Xia didn’t linger in the city and left shortly after.","\"So they never learned the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique from Kulas, but they did receive his blood. Does this mean his blood is the secret behind the Giant’s Race? This is getting more and more interesting.\" Ren Xia wondered out loud as they made their way to the Colossal Mammoth City."]},{"number":2269,"title":"Chapter 2269: Verifying His Identity","paragraphs":["As Tian Yang and Ren Xia made their way to the Colossal Mammoth City, they encountered several magical beasts that only existed within Giant’s Continent. Not only were they as massive as giants, but they also possessed overwhelming strength that far exceeded their cultivation level.","For instance, a magical beast at the first level of Divine Emperor displayed combat prowess comparable to a Divine Ancestor, which was an entire realm higher.","Moreover, magical beasts were naturally stronger than cultivators of the same realm, and when compared to humans, the gap became even more immense.","\"Good heavens, I have never seen beasts this massive before.\" Ren Xia remarked after slaying a giant bird that was nearly 300 meters long.","\"You think they also absorbed some of Kulas’ blood?\" she looked at Tian Yang and asked.","\"I cannot fathom why Kulas would feed his blood to these beasts,\" he said while shaking his head.","Ren Xia thought for a moment before speaking.","\"I’ve heard the Giant Race possesses immense strength—far beyond that of humans. Even an ordinary giant who has never trained could give a seasoned body refiner a difficult fight. Perhaps the beasts on this continent were too weak before, so Kulas strengthened them.\"","\"That’s...actually very logical.\" Tian Yang agreed with her reasoning.","\"However, can his blood even do something like this?\" he then questioned.","\"Isn’t that what the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique does? It turns him into a giant?\" Ren Xia asked.","\"No, it doesn’t automatically make them big, but it allows the person who learned it the ability to transform their size at will. I also learned the Great Mammoth Body Refinement, you know? While I am nowhere near Kulas’ level, I am able to make myself bigger if I want to.\"","\"What?! This is the first time I am hearing about this!\" Ren Xia exclaimed, her eyes shimmering with excitement.","\"If you can adjust your body size at will, does that mean you can also adjust the size of your...’that’?\" Ren Xia asked, her gaze lowering to the sword between his legs.","\"What kind of question is that?\" Tian Yang frowned, looking slightly offended.","Ren Xia chuckled, \"Ah, I’m not trying to say that I am not satisfied with your current size—if that’s what you’re worried about. I am just curious.\"","Tian Yang sighed, \"How the hell am I supposed to know? I never tried.\"","He lowered his head to look at his manhood and silently tried using the Great Mammoth Body Refinement on it.","\"Did it work?\" Ren Xia asked with a slight smile.","\"Who knows?\" Without answering her, Tian Yang continued flying to the Colossal Mammoth City.","\"Wait! You can’t leave me hanging like this!\" Ren Xia cried out loud as she chased after him.","Over the next several days, Ren Xia continued to pester Tian Yang for an answer. However, he ignored her. Eventually, they reached their destination.","\"So this is the Colossal Mammoth City. It’s even larger than I imagined, and I was being quite generous with my guesses,\" Ren Xia remarked as they hovered before the magnificent city.","Although the city was far larger and more extravagant than the others, what truly set it apart was the majestic castle dominating half its area. The structure was so immense that not even a row of a dozen towering mountains could cover its length from end to end.","\"I guess we should head straight for the castle,\" Tian Yang said.","However, right as they got close to the castle, several giants appeared before them, blocking their path.","\"Humans are not allowed beyond this point,\" said one of them.","\"My name is Tian Yang, and I am here to meet Giant Emperor Kulas.\"","\"Tian Yang? Are you sure?\"","\"Yes, I am sure.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, one of them spoke, \"Follow us.\"","Tian Yang and Ren Xia followed these giants, but they were not led into the castle. Instead, they were brought to a building outside the castle.","\"Where is this?\"","\"The interrogation room. Someone will be here shortly to verify your identity.\"","\"Is that so?\"","Tian Yang and Ren Xia sat calmly in the same chair, which was massive enough to seat several people with ease.","Some time later, a beautiful woman with golden hair and emerald eyes stepped into the building. Though her aura unmistakably belonged to a giant, her body was no larger than that of an ordinary human.","Taking a seat across from them, she asked, \"Are you the one who claims to be Tian Yang?\"","\"Indeed.\"","\"Then I’ll be asking you several questions now. If you fail even a single one, you’ll be executed for daring to trick us,\" she said.","Without giving them a chance to respond, the woman began asking her questions, \"How did you first meet the Giant Emperor?\"","Tian Yang calmly responded, \"I was on the verge of death when he showed up and saved me with some medicine.\"","The woman immediately wrote down his answer on a large piece of paper.","\"What were the treasures the Giant Emperor gave you within the Han Zexian’s Tomb?\"","Tian Yang raised an eyebrow and said, \"That happened several hundred years ago, so give me a moment to think.\"","He closed his eyes and recalled all of the treasures he’d received from Kulas, who acquired them from the trials he completed.","\"How many exchanges did the Giant Emperor have with a certain individual surnamed Gu?\"","\"The hell? How am I supposed to know that when I was busy dealing with the other guy? I doubt even Kulas himself knows the answer.\"","The woman didn’t say anything and only wrote down his answer.","\"When was the last time you met the Giant Emperor?\" she then asked.","\"At the Immortal Confinement Dungeon. I am still waiting for a thank you from him, by the way.\"","Several more questions later, the woman stood up and said, \"I am done here. I’ll return once I verify your identity.\"","Without elaborating, she left the building."]},{"number":2270,"title":"Chapter 2270: Tian Yang’s Reunion With Kulas","paragraphs":["After she left, the blonde woman entered the palace.","Some time later, she stood before a lone colossal silhouette sitting on a grand throne at the end of the room.","\"I have returned, Father.\" The woman bowed to him.","\"How did that man who claims to be Tian Yang look to you?\" The silhouette asked.","\"Well, I’ve never met him before, so I can’t really say whether he’s real or not. However, he answered the questions quite calmly,\" she said.","The silhouette extended his massive arm—thick enough to carry mountains—toward her and silently beckoned.","The woman nodded and offered the piece of paper on which she had written Tian Yang’s answers to him.","The entire room fell dead silent as the silhouette read the answers.","A moment later, the entire palace trembled as the silhouette burst out laughing.","\"F-Father?!\" The woman exclaimed, looking baffled.","\"Bring him to me!\" he spoke in a demanding and urgent voice, refusing to elaborate further.","\"Yes!\" The woman said before hastily leaving.","Meanwhile, as Tian Yang and Ren Xia waited for the woman’s return, the ground suddenly trembled beneath them, followed by the unmistakable sound of someone laughing.","\"What a powerful presence,\" Ren Xia remarked, feeling the energy that rippled through the air with that laughter.","\"It must be Kulas. I guess he’d just received my answers,\" said Tian Yang.","Minutes later, the woman returned.","\"Come with me. The Giant Emperor has summoned you,\" she said.","Tian Yang and Ren Xia followed her, while a group of giant guards trailed behind them, watching their every move to ensure they didn’t attempt anything suspicious.","They entered the palace shortly later and continued following the woman through the massive halls.","As they walked, one of the guards suddenly spoke, a hint of hesitation in his voice, \"Your highness, that voice just now... was that...\"","\"Yes, it was my father. Surprising, wasn’t it?\" she responded without stopping or looking back.","\"Yes... I have never heard His Majesty laugh in such a manner before.\"","\"Me neither.\" The woman turned to look at Tian Yang and continued, \"Whether he’s laughing because he’s angry that another imposter showed up or he’s the real deal... I guess we’ll find out soon enough.\"","Tian Yang raised an eyebrow. \"Do impostors show up often, claiming to be me? And how would they even know about my relationship with Kulas?\"","She replied, \"Plenty of humans come seeking an audience with the Giant Emperor. Sometimes, one of us accidentally mentions your name since we were all instructed to remember it, and those humans seize the chance, claiming to be you just to meet the Giant Emperor.\"","\"How did it end?\" Ren Xia asked, curiosity in her voice.","\"Not well,\" the woman replied. \"And not just for the humans who lied. The Giant Emperor was furious the first time it happened, and many suffered that day, giant or not. Since then, we’ve started requiring verification before we let anyone claiming to be Tian Yang meet the Giant Emperor.\"","Eventually, they arrived at their destination.","The woman knocked on the colossal doors and called out, \"Father, it’s me. I’ve brought them.\"","For a brief moment, everything fell silent. Then, the doors burst open with such force that a violent gust of wind surged outward, threatening to pull everyone into the room.","A voice, overbearing and regal, resounded the next moment.","\"Enter.\"","Yet, it couldn’t fully conceal the excitement simmering beneath it.","Tian Yang and Ren Xia calmly moved forward, entering the dimmed room.","But the moment the others tried to follow, the voice boomed with overwhelming force,","\"I will not allow anyone to interfere with our reunion!\"","His overbearing voice surged past Tian Yang and Ren Xia, shoving the others back. The doors slammed shut an instant later without producing the slightest noise.","Within the chamber, Tian Yang’s eyes were immediately drawn to the colossal figure seated upon a grand throne. The shadows hid his face, but the sunlight illuminated the rest of him clearly.","His body was titanic beyond reason—a fortress of muscle, with veins as wide as rivers coursing across his frame.","After a moment of stillness, Tian Yang broke the silence first.","\"It doesn’t feel like I am meeting with a friend, much less a sworn brother.\"","The colossal silhouette, which appeared as rigid and immovable as a mountain, suddenly trembled at the sound of his voice.","\"Oh my—how unbecoming of me. The excitement of seeing you again must have clouded my senses for a moment,\" the silhouette said, slowly rising from the throne.","Once he stepped off the platform and into the light, Tian Yang could finally see Kulas’ face again after hundreds of years.","Although he had grown more mature and now sported a short beard, Tian Yang still recognized Kulas instantly.","Before either of them could speak, Kulas’ massive body began to shrink, rapidly condensing until he stood at the size of an ordinary adult human.","\"I appreciate it. I don’t think my neck could handle looking up at you for too long,\" Tian Yang said with a smile.","\"How could I share words with my sworn brother while looking down on him?\" Kulas answered, his smile matching Tian Yang’s.","\"You seem to be doing well—at least much better than when I last saw you,\" said Tian Yang.","Kulas awkwardly scratched his head and said, \"Before I can even thank you for getting me out of that place, I must apologize to you for not recognizing you. I even attacked you.\"","He lowered his head and apologized in a sincere tone, \"I’m sorry for failing to recognize you.\"","Tian Yang calmly shook his head.","\"There’s really no need to apologize. I don’t even blame you. Hell, if I had been in your shoes, I would’ve likely not recognized me, either.\"","Kulas lifted his head and chuckled, \"I bet. You have no idea how many times they drugged me or used illusions, trying to extract information on you.\"","A guilty expression appeared on Tian Yang’s face as he replied, \"Honestly, I should be the one apologizing. If I had gone to save you sooner...\""]},{"number":2271,"title":"Chapter 2271: Childish Feud","paragraphs":["\"Saving me sooner, huh?\" Kulas muttered before shaking his head. \"Although it was quite painful and felt like an eternity at first, I quickly got used to it—the physical pain, that is. Due to the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique you gave me, I was not only able to grow temper by physique to an extreme level, but it stopped being painful after a couple of months.\"","\"As for the mental torture... that took far longer to overcome. It took me years to realize that all I had to do was stop believing in what I saw; once I did, it became much easier to endure. That said, I wasn’t close to many people—if any at all—so they usually used you to torment me.\"","\"If I have to be honest, I am sort of glad that it happened. After all, if not, I wouldn’t be in my current position right now. Not only have I surpassed my entire family during their peak, but I also gained a real family who wouldn’t betray me over some pressure.\"","Kulas spoke with barely a pause, hardly stopping to breathe.","\"Speaking of my family... I’ve heard what you’ve accomplished. The downfall of the Immortal Clans. You’ve finally achieved your goal. What was once mocked as foolish and impossible, you brought to reality. I wanted to help you, but doing so would have lessened your achievement, so I held back and watched from here.\"","\"Hey, I have been trying my best to keep quiet so the two of you can have a moment, but you’re acting like I am not even here. I also had a hand in the Immortal Clans’ downfall, you know?\" Ren Xia finally spoke up.","Kulas shifted his gaze to her, and the instant he did, it grew noticeably colder, faint but impossible to miss. He was clearly displeased by Ren Xia’s presence.","\"Why did you have to come here, too?\" he sighed, not even bothering to hide his displeasure.","Ren Xia narrowed her eyes at him.","\"I don’t recall doing anything to deserve that reaction—especially since we haven’t spoken since Han Zexian’s Tomb. Tell me, did you not mature even a little over all these years?\"","\"You didn’t do anything?\" Kulas sneered. \"You touched my brother with your foul hands even though I warned you not to! What are you scheming, you damn fox? Are you trying to steal his techniques? Or do you have other ulterior motives? How many men have you snared so far?\"","\"This son of a bitch... Can I beat some sense into him?\" Ren Xia asked Tian Yang as she pulled up her sleeves.","\"Oh? You want to fight? Bring it on! I have always wanted to punch that annoying face of yours at least once!\" Kulas said, raising his thick arms like a boxer.","Tian Yang pinched the bridge of his nose and sighed, \"I can’t believe the two of you are still stuck in this childish feud.\"","\"I was ready to be nice,\" Ren Xia protested, \"but he insulted my character, implying that I am a slut even though you are the only one I’ve ever been with! Dear, you can vouch for me! That during our first connection, I gushed with blood after you penetrated me with your sword!\"","Tian Yang’s jaw dropped at Ren Xia’s description.","\"I wouldn’t say it ’gushed with blood’, but it was definitely there...\" he responded in an awkward tone.","\"Wait, what the hell are you making me say?\"","\"That doesn’t prove anything!\" Kulas then said. \"There are plenty of ways to fake something like that! I bet you do that to everyone you meet!\"","\"Fuck! I’ve had it with this rude bastard! I’m going to beat him to death! Don’t try to stop me!\" Ren Xia’s aura soared the next moment.","\"Haha! Beat me to death? A mere Silver Immortal like you?! I’d love to see you try!\" Kulas also released his aura, revealing his cultivation to be at the True Immortal level.","\"Enough!\" Tian Yang suddenly roared, his voice shaking the entire room.","\"...\"","Both Ren Xia and Kulas retrieved their aura after a brief moment of stillness.","\"Kulas, you can trust her.\" Tian Yang continued as he stared Kulas in the eyes. \"She’s been by my side ever since we rescued you, and we’ve fought with our lives on the line multiple times. Hell, she even saved my butt many times. If it weren’t for her, neither of us would be where we are right now.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Kulas burst out laughing, \"I guess I went out of line with my jokes. My apologies.\"","\"Jokes? You really expect me to believe that you were just joking around?\" Ren Xia frowned.","Kulas shrugged and replied calmly, \"I’m fully aware of your relationship with Tian Yang. Every time someone mentions his name, yours follows right after. Even a blind man could see your devotion to him. I just wanted to tease you a little. Consider it repayment for all the times you annoyed me in the past. Whether you believe me or not is up to you.\"","\"Let’s leave it at that.\" Tian Yang then said.","Ren Xia didn’t say anything, quietly nodding her head.","\"Let’s continue our conversation elsewhere. Somewhere more comfortable and accommodating,\" Kulas said.","\"Alright.\"","The three of them left the room shortly after.","\"Prepare a feast, and bring our finest tea to my private dwelling,\" Kulas said to the guards waiting outside.","\"A-As your Majesty commands!\"","The guards immediately scurried away.","\"Does this mean...?\" The blonde woman muttered as she stared at Tian Yang.","\"Yes, he’s the real deal.\" Kulas nodded.","\"Let me introduce you to each other. Tian Yang, this is my youngest daughter, Xie Mey.\"","\"Xie Mey, this is my sworn brother, Tian Yang. There’s nobody I trust more than him in this world.\"","\"It’s an honor to meet you, Senior...\" Xie Mey bowed hurriedly, caught off guard by Kulas’s shocking remark.","\"I figured she was your daughter when the guards addressed her as ’Highness’, but the youngest? How many children do you have?\" Tian Yang looked at him with wide eyes.","\"You curious? Then I’ll introduce all of them to you later.\" Kulas chuckled."]},{"number":2272,"title":"Chapter 2272: Heavenly Unrestricted Longevity Pill","paragraphs":["Once they arrived at their destination, Kulas turned to look at Xie Mey and commanded her, \"I want you to gather your siblings at the throne room and wait for my return there.\"","\"All of them?\" she asked for clarification.","\"All of them.\"","\"As you wish, Father.\"","After giving them a bow, she turned around and disappeared into the halls.","Once they were seated, Kulas said, \"While we wait for the tea to arrive, why don’t we start with what you were doing inside Han Zexian’s Legacy, shall we?\"","However, Tian Yang shook his head and calmly refused, \"It’s not that I don’t want to tell you. I simply can’t. It’s for your safety.\"","\"For my safety?\" Kulas raised an eyebrow. \"I am the Giant Emperor, you know? I appreciate the concern, but I can handle anything you throw at me.\"","\"It’s useless.\" Ren Xia interjected. \"I have asked many times, but he would always refuse to tell me, saying the same thing.\"","\"What’s so dangerous about it, anyway? You’re only telling us something. How could that possibly be a problem?\" Kulas said, looking genuinely confused.","Tian Yang shook his head.","\"Unfortunately, even I don’t fully understand it. Just know this—there are still things out there far beyond our comprehension.\"","\"...\"","After a brief silence, Tian Yang continued, \"With that being said, I can tell you some things I did inside, such as what Han Zexian left behind.\"","\"Just say that from the beginning...\"","Tian Yang smiled and began telling them about the interior layout of the cavern and the priceless stash Han Zexian left behind.","\"Strange as it sounds, there was a tiny waterfall in that cavern, and the water wasn’t water at all. It was an elixir that sharpened focus to an incredible degree. With its help, my cultivation efficiency soared. That was what truly accelerated my progress.\"","\"Then there were shelves of spatial rings filled entirely with longevity pills—thousands upon thousands of them. And they were the priceless kind without a consumption limit, meaning I could take as many as I wanted and extend my lifespan endlessly.\"","Both Ren Xia and Kulas stared at him with wide eyes filled with disbelief.","\"I must interrupt you. Longevity pills without consumption limits—and in the thousands?\" Kulas said, brows furrowing with doubt. \"That borders on impossible. Such pills are exceptionally rare and priceless. How could Han Zexian have amassed such a quantity?\"","Tian Yang shrugged, \"What’s the point of lying about such things?\"","\"Did you consume all of them?\" Ren Xia asked.","\"I consumed most of them, but I kept a few of them as a memento.\" Tian Yang proceeded to retrieve two pills and placed them on the table.","\"May I?\" Kulas asked as his hands hovered over one, his eyes sparkling with curiosity.","\"Go ahead. I kept them so I could give one to you two, anyway.\"","Ren Xia and Kulas grabbed the pill and brought it close to their eyes, inspecting it with great interest.","\"Wow... this really is the Heavenly Unrestricted Longevity Pill,\" Ren Xia murmured in a daze. \"I’ve only ever seen one in my entire life, and that was back when I was still with my family, from a distance. Someone like me wasn’t even allowed to touch it.\"","\"They’re even rarer now, since they stopped appearing on the market hundreds of years ago,\" Kulas said. \"For Han Zexian to have so many... perhaps he was the creator. No one ever learned who made them in the first place.\"","Kulas shifted his gaze to Tian Yang and spoke with a stiff smile, \"And you consumed thousands of them? What were you thinking? Are you not satisfied with your already near-limitless longevity as an Immortal?\"","\"It’s related to the forbidden information,\" he shrugged.","\"Anyway, besides the pills and the waterfall, there was also a cultivation bed inside. I don’t know what it was made of, but it sped up my cultivation several-fold when I sat on it. I wish I could’ve taken it out of the cavern, but it was stuck there.\"","\"That sounds like another priceless treasure—the Heavenly Ascension Platform, to be exact,\" Ren Xia remarked. \"There are many varieties with different effects, but even the weakest ones are worth a fortune.\"","\"My family had one, but it was reserved only for the Patriarch,\" Kulas said. \"Forget about seeing it, I have never even gotten close to it.\"","\"Just who the hell is this Han Zexian, anyway?\" Ren Xia wondered out loud. \"We know pretty much nothing about him besides that he was the first one to reach the Immortal Realm. Knowing his vast fortune now, I’m not the slightest surprised.\"","\"And here is another thing Han Zexian left behind...\"","Tian Yang produced several herbs from his spatial ring—the very same ones that were growing under the waterfall. Since he wasn’t an alchemist, he wasn’t able to use them, so he simply decided to keep them.","\"Heavens!\" Ren Xia stood up in shock. \"Do you have any idea what these are?!\"","\"The ingredients to concoct the Heavenly Unrestricted Longevity Pill, right?\" he said.","\"Not just that! They’re priceless treasures used in a variety of high-end pills! They’re near extinct nowadays! But that’s not why I am surprised!\"","\"You know...\" Kulas suddenly spoke, \"Normally, you store them in containers specifically used for such treasures so they don’t lose their effects...\"","\"What?\" Tian Yang raised his eyebrows in surprise. \"I just tossed them inside my spatial ring. Are they useless now?\"","\"Of course not. It just means their effects will be weakened.\"","Kulas stood up and walked to his drawers, where he retrieved a large wooden box.","\"Here, put them in here. This will seal their aroma and keep them fresh for as long as they’re contained.\"","\"Thanks...\" Tian Yang followed his instructions.","\"But I still have no use for them now. I don’t need any more longevity pills, either. What should I do with them?\"","Kulas pondered for a moment before responding, \"I know an Alchemist. If you want, I can have him concoct a pill using those materials. It’ll greatly benefit your cultivation.\"","\"Really? That’ll be great.\" Tian Yang immediately agreed."]},{"number":2273,"title":"Chapter 2273: The Method to Becoming a Giant","paragraphs":["By the time Tian Yang finished recounting his experience inside Han Zexian’s cavern, the tea had arrived.","\"These tea leaves are exclusive to this continent—I cultivated them myself,\" Kulas said as he poured each of them a cup.","When Tian Yang took a sip, he immediately sensed a change within his body. His physique had been refined, as though he had just undergone an intense body-tempering session.","\"My body’s getting a little sore... Aren’t teas supposed to help you relax? I feel the exact opposite right now,\" Tian Yang said with a stiff smile.","Kulas burst into laughter at his remark.","\"Relax? That word doesn’t even exist in the Giant Race’s dictionary!\"","\"This isn’t going to give me a body as grotesque as yours, right...?\" Ren Xia muttered as she hurriedly set her cup down, fearing that her body might become too muscular for Tian Yang’s taste.","\"Hey, hey—who are you calling grotesque? You have no idea how much effort it took to achieve this physique!\" Kulas protested, flexing his muscles proudly.","\"This isn’t something you can get just by drinking tea, so there’s no need to worry. The tea only strengthens your foundation and repairs most of the damage in your body—even the kind of restoration pills can’t heal. The reason you’re feeling sore is because your muscles were just restored.\"","Kulas shot Ren Xia a look and sighed.","\"I don’t understand your taste. What’s so appealing about that bony physique of yours? There’s nothing to feel besides skin and bone.\"","\"I don’t expect someone built like a walking mountain to get it. Your brain is likely made entirely of muscle, too,\" Ren Xia retorted.","Kulas laughed and turned to Tian Yang.","\"Why don’t I introduce you to a few women here? Once you experience their muscles, you’ll never go back to that skeleton beside you!\"","\"You looking for a fight?!\" Ren Xia snapped. \"How dare you suggest my darling sleep with another woman right in front of me!\"","\"What’s wrong with that? It’s not uncommon for a man to have several wives, especially if they’re powerful. I have over twenty wives right now. Or do you intend on keeping him to yourself?\"","\"I know,\" Ren Xia replied, folding her arms, a hint of defensiveness in her posture. \"I’m not fond of the idea of sharing him. But if he genuinely fell in love with someone else, I’d rather accept it than let jealousy destroy what we have.\"","Tian Yang shook his head and said, \"I doubt I’ll ever love someone else, especially since I am no longer going on adventures alone, so you don’t have to worry about that.\"","\"Never say never,\" Kulas said.","\"Alright, let’s put this topic behind us. Why don’t you tell me what you’ve been doing? Especially after we rescued you from the Immortal Confinement Dungeon.\"","Kulas leaned back, closed his eyes, and crossed his arms, sinking into a wordless silence.","He broke the silence a moment later.","\"Truthfully, I barely remember anything after I was freed. My mind wasn’t stable, so I must have wandered for some time. By the time I came to my senses, I had already ended up on this continent.\"","\"Then you remember declaring yourself the ruler of this continent? Why did you do something that would only bring attention to yourself?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"I acted on instincts... probably,\" he replied.","\"Probably?\"","\"Even after I regained my senses, I wasn’t fully healed,\" Kulas said with a sigh. \"My personality was nothing like it is now, and it took hundreds of years to recover. In fact, I didn’t fully return to my original self until shortly before I reopened the continent.\"","\"Then let’s forget the reason behind your actions. How did you create the Giant’s Race? I heard from a giant that you bestowed your blood upon them. Ah, that giant was named Karan.\" Tian Yang didn’t forget his promise to give the giant’s name to Kulas.","\"That’s not entirely correct,\" Kulas said.","\"My blood is exceptionally potent, to the point where even my children have difficulty refining it, let alone ordinary people. What they carry isn’t my direct blood, but my children’s—derived from my lineage, yet far weaker in comparison. The only time I gave my blood was in the beginning, when I hadn’t fully realized the power of my bloodline.\"","\"And how does that work? Surely, they weren’t born as giants.\"","He shook his head.","\"No. Anyone not born of my direct lineage began as an ordinary human. It was only after they absorbed and refined my bloodline that they became giants.\"","\"Your bloodline... then it wasn’t a result of the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique?\"","Tian Yang muttered. \"Our understanding of bloodlines is still limited. How did you come to possess yours?\"","\"Through trial and error, I suppose. And I’d never share the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique with ordinary people. Even within my own family, I only teach them half of the full method.\"","\"Are the massive beasts your doing, as well?\" Ren Xia asked.","\"Yes. We giants possess extraordinary strength, and ordinary beasts no longer pose any threat to us, which is a problem, since we rely on them for training. So we strengthened them by giving them our blood.\"","He continued, \"Of course, training isn’t the only reason. They’re also our source of nutrients. Tiny beasts wouldn’t even fill the gaps between our teeth.\"","\"Can anybody receive your bloodline and turn into giants?\" Tian Yang then asked.","Kulas hesitated for a moment before shaking his head.","\"Of course not. Many have died attempting to become giants. But we don’t force anyone onto our path. It’s no different from the sects in the outside world—except that instead of teaching cultivation techniques, we offer the chance to undergo the transformation into a giant. Anyone who desires strength may choose it.\"","\"How would one even go about requesting such a thing? I didn’t notice any form of recruitment.\"","\"You’d be surprised by how many seek us out,\" Kulas replied with a smile. \"Most ask about our methods out of simple curiosity, but some truly wish to become giants themselves, even if it’ll bind them to this continent for the rest of their lives.\""]},{"number":2274,"title":"Chapter 2274: Giant Emperor Kulas’ Family","paragraphs":["Hearing Kulas’ words, Tian Yang finally voiced the question that had lingered in his mind ever since learning about the Giant Race.","\"I’ve wondered about this for a long time, but why don’t any of you venture beyond the continent? At first, I assumed it was simply a preference, that giants chose to remain here. But from what you’re saying... it sounds like you don’t have a choice. Is something binding your people to this land?\"","Kulas shook his head.","\"No, nothing is binding us,\" he explained. \"It’s just that the outside world isn’t ready to face our race. When we first established ourselves, a few giants did leave the continent. Every one of them faced scrutiny and harassment—constant provocation, suspicion, and hostility. Not a single one returned without injuries. That’s why we decided to remain on this continent. Those who come here are already aware of our existence, and even if they try to harass us, we’re surrounded by our fellow people.\"","\"Of course, we won’t remain secluded on this continent forever. Once our Giant’s Race is known far and wide, we’ll leave. Give it a few thousand years.\"","Even though the Giant Race had existed for hundreds of years, the Divine Heavens were so vast that most of the world remained unaware of them, particularly those living in rural regions. Not to mention, the Giant’s Continent had sealed itself off for some time.","\"With that said, we’re not in a hurry to leave this place. We’re quite satisfied with our current lives, after all,\" said Kulas.","\"Anyway, what are your plans now that you’ve defeated the Immortal Clans?\" he then asked the couple.","Tian Yang and Ren Xia exchanged glances with each other.","\"We’ve been living a quiet and peaceful life ever since then, and we don’t have any plans on changing that lifestyle anytime soon,\" Tian Yang said.","\"So you’re not particularly doing anything? In that case, what do you think about staying here with me? I’ve been looking for a new sparring partner, but it’s not easy to find a decent one since there is nobody on this continent who can even give me a challenge these days.\"","\"You want us to live in the Giant’s Continent...?\" Tian Yang muttered.","\"Of course, you can live here in the palace with me. We have plenty of spare rooms. We’ll also take care of all of your amenities.\"","\"Are you sure? I don’t want to intrude on your family...\"","\"It’s the least I can do for my sworn brother who saved my life.\"","Tian Yang looked at Ren Xia and asked, \"What do you think? Want to stay here for a little?\"","Ren Xia shrugged, \"I don’t care where we stay as long as I am with you.\"","Tian Yang smiled, \"Then it’s decided.\"","He turned to face Kulas and said, \"Please take care of us, my new sparring partner.\"","\"Hahaha! I should be saying that!\" Kulas laughed out loud.","They continued chatting for another day.","\"Alright, how about we meet the rest of my family now? They should have gathered by now,\" Kulas suddenly suggested.","\"Sounds good.\"","Tian Yang and Ren Xia followed Kulas back to the throne room where they first met.","When they arrived and entered the room, they were immediately met by over a hundred gazes.","Inside, a hundred and thirty-three giants lined up in an orderly fashion. Tian Yang’s eyes widened with surprise when he saw the scene.","\"All of them are your children?\" he asked.","\"Not all. Some of them are my wives,\" he responded with a prideful smile.","\"Looks like you’ve been doing more than just play emperor for the last few hundred years...\" Ren Xia remarked.","Rather than being offended, Kulas chuckled at her words.","He approached his family and loudly declared, \"These two will be staying with us for some time. The one to my left is my sworn brother and best friend, Tian Yang. The one to my right is his wife. Now, I want you all to introduce yourselves, starting from the oldest.\"","At his command, the man standing on the far left took a step forward and loudly introduced himself, \"I am the oldest. My name is Du Shaoweng.\"","Then, the woman standing right next to him stepped forward and spoke, \"I am his mother and the first wife, Du Xianyun.\"","One by one, his family introduced themselves without any pauses, almost as if they’d practiced for this moment.","Finally, the youngest stepped forward.","\"I am the youngest, Xie Mey. Unfortunately, my mother died right after my birth.\"","Kulas then said to Tian Yang, \"As you can probably tell from their introduction, the children take after their mother’s surname. The reason is simply that I have abandoned my surname—the same way my family abandoned me.\"","Tian Yang then stepped forward and said, \"Kulas already introduced me, but I’m Tian Yang, and I will be staying here for some time to be his sparring partner. If you have any questions or just want to talk, don’t hesitate to approach me. Let’s all get along.\"","Although no one spoke, Tian Yang could feel their intense gazes fixed on him. Some held simple curiosity, but most carried motives that were far less innocent. However, that didn’t necessarily mean their intentions were malicious.","\"Are you not going to introduce yourself, too?\" Kulas asked Ren Xia.","\"Why? You already introduced me, and I don’t really have anything else to add.\"","\"If you say so.\"","He turned to his family and said, \"You’re all dismissed.\"","They bowed immediately before leaving the room. A few of them looked as though they wanted to speak with Tian Yang, but in the end, they held their tongues and left without saying anything.","At the very end, Xie Mey stopped before Tian Yang briefly and said, \"Let’s have a chat later. I’m quite interested in the outside world.\"","\"Sure thing.\" Tian Yang nodded.","\"I’ll contact you later, then.\" Xie Mey gave a slight bow before leaving the room."]},{"number":2275,"title":"Chapter 2275: Kulas’ Personal World","paragraphs":["Once they were alone again, Kulas said, \"Your room is already being prepared as we speak, so let’s check out the training area, shall we?\"","\"Let’s.\" Tian Yang nodded.","Kulas then led them to the back of the palace, where a flower garden of massive, unknown plants was growing. As they walked through the garden path, Kulas explained, \"This is where I grow my tea leaves.\"","\"How do you grow them?\" Ren Xia asked.","Kulas showed a mysterious smile on his face, \"Are you sure you want to know?\"","Ren Xia frowned at his ominous words and quickly said, \"You’d better tell us, especially since you fed it to us.\"","Kulas let out a laugh. \"I grow them in special soil—soil that’s been infused with my blood.\"","\"Your blood, again? Do you consider it some kind of universal treasure that improves everything it touches?\"","\"If you’re worried about side effects, worry not. We’ve done extensive testing until we’re certain of their safety for consumption. Of course, this goes for the magical beasts outside, as well.\"","\"And how many people have died during those tests?\" Ren Xia asked with a quick sneer.","\"Nobody died. At worst, a few had upset stomachs for several weeks.\"","Once they left the garden, they arrived at an empty courtyard with a single guard protecting a circular platform with Array Symbols etched all over it.","\"This lowly subject greets His Majesty.\" The guard bowed the moment he saw them.","Kulas gave a slight nod of acknowledgement before speaking to Tian Yang, \"We’re almost there.\"","A moment later, they stood on the platform before being teleported to a new location.","\"Where are we?\" Tian Yang muttered as he found himself standing on a massive platform while surrounded by water.","\"We’re inside a separate dimension—one completely isolated from the outside world,\" he explained calmly.","\"What?\" Tian Yang raised his eyebrows, clearly puzzled.","At this point in history, the concept of creating one’s own world was still in its infancy, and very few people were even aware that such a feat was possible.","\"How does it work?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"It’s similar to how a spatial ring or storage pouch works. In simpler words, we’re currently inside a massive spatial ring. Not only is it much more massive, but it can also contain living beings. In here, no matter how much damage we do during our training, it won’t affect the outside world.\"","\"How does one create their own world?\" Ren Xia inquired.","\"It’s not easy or cheap. Not only does it require a tremendous amount of resources, but you will also need to maintain the world after its creation. As for how they’re created... you’ll need to ask the expert who created the world in the first place. I am only supplying the necessary spirit stones to operate it.\"","\"And how expensive is it to maintain the world?\" Ren Xia continued to ask.","\"This world is relatively small, but even a world of this size costs around a hundred million spirit stones to create and thousands of spirit stones a day to maintain it. If you train in here and damage the place, it could easily consume over a hundred thousand spirit stones for repairs.\"","\"Heavens. It is that expensive? You’re literally throwing away money at this point. Why don’t you just create a normal training ground? That will definitely be much cheaper to create and maintain—even if you destroy it and have to remake it every day.\"","\"Well, I have no other uses for spirit stones. We earn more than we ever need just from selling our materials to the merchants who visit our continent.\"","After a slight pause, he continued, \"Keep this between us, but we also have several large Spirit Veins on the continent, earning us hundreds of thousands of spirit stones a day.\"","\"Spirit Veins, huh? If word of it were to spread, there’d definitely be trouble.\" Tian Yang remarked.","Spirit Veins were the only reliable source of spirit stones and the origin of most that circulated in the world. Nearly all of them were controlled by large and powerful backgrounds, and whenever a new vein was discovered, it often sparked fierce wars as countless powers fought for ownership.","If several Spirit Veins existed on the Giant’s Continent, they would undoubtedly attract countless greedy and ambitious individuals. And while the Giant Race was exceptionally powerful—and their territory difficult to reach—that alone would not be enough to deter those kinds of people from stirring up trouble.","Given their immeasurable value, knowledge of such Spirit Veins was typically guarded from everyone, including one’s own closest allies. Yet Kulas shared it openly with Tian Yang and Ren Xia, demonstrating the extent of his trust.","\"I get that you’re rich, but it still feels a bit wasteful,\" Ren Xia said, shaking her head.","Kulas smiled. \"If we used this place only as a training ground, then yes. But it also serves as a safehouse and a vault.\"","\"A vault? I don’t see one.\" Tian Yang said as he looked around, seeing nothing but water for as far as the horizon goes.","\"A single world can have multiple layers. This world has two layers, and we’re currently in the first layer.\"","\"I see... how intriguing,\" Tian Yang murmured, the thought of forging a world of his own stirring within him.","Throughout his battles with the Immortal Clans, he had plundered their valuables whenever he could, amassing a mountain of treasures and spirit stones. But until this moment, he’d had no idea how any of it could be used.","\"Are you thinking about what I currently am?\" Ren Xia suddenly spoke to him.","\"About making our own world?\"","\"A paradise for just the two of us... It’d be very romantic,\" she chuckled.","\"We’ll have to learn the method for creating it first, though.\"","Kulas then said, \"I’ll introduce you to the expert later... if you can defeat me in a match.\"","Tian Yang looked at him with a raised eyebrow.","\"Right now?\"","\"Right now,\" Kulas confirmed."]},{"number":2276,"title":"Chapter 2276: Sparring With Kulas","paragraphs":["Kulas jumped to the center of the platform and beckoned Tian Yang, \"Don’t tell me you’re afraid of losing?\"","Tian Yang smiled at his provocation and also flew to the center of the platform.","\"Don’t cry when I beat you,\" he said.","\"Hahaha! Not only is my physique superior, but so is my cultivation!\" Kulas released his aura, and his True Immortal cultivation base surged outward like a massive tidal wave. Yet, the water around them remained still, almost as if they were simply an illusion.","\"I’d be very surprised if you could hurt me, much less defeat me!\"","\"We’ll find out soon enough.\"","The atmosphere grew heavy as both of them fell silent.","In the next instant, their figures vanished, only to collide a heartbeat later, unleashing a powerful ripple that swept across the entire world.","\"Oh? Not bad,\" remarked Kulas when Tian Yang wasn’t immediately flung away. \"Most can’t even handle this.\"","\"Well, I’m not like most,\" Tian Yang calmly responded with a smile.","\"Of course not. Would you be here if you weren’t special?\" Kulas laughed out loud as they continued to exchange blows with each other, using nothing but their physiques.","The two gradually increased their strength with each blow, and although Tian Yang managed to endure for a while, Kulas inevitably overpowered him.","\"I’m impressed—shocked, even,\" Kulas said suddenly. \"You forced me to use sixty percent of my full strength. Out of my one hundred and one children, only five can manage that. And you’re just a human with an ordinary physique.\"","\"Have you forgotten who taught you the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique? Although I am nowhere near your level, I have trained this technique quite extensively over the years since it’s the only worthy body refining technique that I know.\"","\"That makes sense. But are you sure you didn’t do it to satisfy your partner?\" Kulas chuckled.","Ren Xia’s ears twitched at Kulas’ words.","\"So you can use it to enhance that!\" she exclaimed.","Kulas looked at her with raised eyebrows.","\"What? Don’t tell me you’ve never used it on her? You have no idea what you’re missing out on.\"","Tian Yang sighed, \"Do you want to fight, or would you rather talk about nonsense? I don’t have the energy to do both.\"","\"Alright, alright.\" Kulas chuckled a little before putting on a serious face again.","\"Do you need more time to warm up?\" he then asked.","\"No, do you?\"","\"Then let’s fight seriously!\"","Their subsequent collision was no longer a contest of physique alone, and they began drawing upon their martial techniques.","Tian Yang shifted fluidly between countless styles while Kulas remained steadfast, using only his fist techniques.","Kulas hadn’t always been a fist-fighter. Once, he wielded a sword. But every technique he’d learned with it had come from the family he now despised. For that reason, he vowed never to draw a blade again.","Another reason was simple pride. He could not bring himself to rely on a weapon that was not his own flesh. Among Body Refiners, this was common; they took immense pride in their physiques and used their bodies as their primary weapons. It demonstrated both their hard work and their confidence.","As the fight dragged on, Kulas, who’d been so confident in his abilities, began to feel pressure mounting against him. The sensation baffled him. He possessed a superior physique and higher cultivation, and only minutes ago, he had overwhelmed Tian Yang with a little more than half his strength.","But now, he found himself barely keeping up with Tian Yang’s movements, as though he were getting slower.","\"What’s wrong? You’re sweating pretty heavily there.\" Tian Yang suddenly poked at him.","\"This is normal!\"","Tian Yang smiled faintly.","\"You’re incredibly strong, Kulas—no one can deny that. But you don’t know how to use that strength. At the moment, you fight like a wild beast. Your moves are simple and predictable. You depend too heavily on brute force.\"","\"Are you seriously lecturing me?!\" Kulas exclaimed, looking utterly speechless.","\"This is why we’re sparring, isn’t it?\" Tian Yang replied calmly. \"To expose each other’s flaws and improve.\"","After some time, Kulas collapsed onto the platform, a bewildered look frozen on his face.","\"I... lost?\" he murmured in a daze.","He had no serious injuries, and Tian Yang’s attacks had barely hurt him, yet somehow, he had still been defeated.","\"You lack experience, Kulas,\" Tian Yang said as he walked toward him.","\"You’ve probably defeated most—if not all—of your opponents with sheer, overwhelming strength, so you never needed to rely on proper technique. But I fought the Immortal Clans. Did you really think I defeated them through brute force alone? Not to mention that I have hundreds of years of real experience while you’re secluded in this place. When was the last time you were in a life-or-death situation?\"","\"...\"","Kulas was left speechless, partly from shock and partly because he had no rebuttal.","Despite his overwhelming strength, he undeniably lacked experience. The last time he had truly fought was during his early days, when he returned to the Desolate Continent and had to fight to prove his strength.","In recent years, he had devoted the majority of his time to governing the continent from his throne room. The rare moments he could spare for battle were limited to sparring sessions with his children or his soldiers.","In contrast to Tian Yang, who fought nearly every day at the risk of his life, the disparity between them was as great as that between heaven and earth.","After a moment of silence, Kulas suddenly burst out laughing.","\"Hahaha! You’re truly amazing, Tian Yang!\" he abruptly declared.","\"As expected of my sworn brother! I’m truly glad to have someone like you as a sparring partner starting now!\"","He sat up and continued, \"Alright, as promised, I’ll introduce the expert who created this world for me. Hell, I’ll even help you make your own.\"","\"Thanks,\" replied Tian Yang as he extended an arm to help Kulas up."]},{"number":2277,"title":"Chapter 2277: Heaven Defying Ascension Pill","paragraphs":["After their spar, Kulas brought Tian Yang and Ren Xia to their new living quarters.","\"I assumed the two of you wanted to live in the same room, so I only prepared this room. If you want separate rooms, let me know,\" said Kulas.","\"How thoughtful.\" Ren Xia remarked. \"But you’re not wrong.\"","Tian Yang walked into the room and expressed slight surprise, \"This room... is normal-sized. I thought every room in this palace was meant for giants, or did you specifically create this just for us?\"","Kulas smiled and said, \"You know, there are times when I feel like walking around in my original size, so there are rooms in here dedicated to humans. Not to mention, we receive human-sized guests all of the time.\"","\"I see...\"","\"Well, I have to return to work now. If there is anything you need, don’t hesitate to ask the servants. Of course, you can bother me whenever,\" Kulas said.","\"Thanks for everything.\"","After Kulas left, Tian Yang and Ren Xia went to familiarize themselves with their new living space. Although it existed within the palace, the room was huge, with several other connecting rooms.","\"I’m going to take a shower,\" Tian Yang said, as he was still soaked in sweat from his sparring with Kulas.","\"Sure.\"","Shortly after Tian Yang entered the bathroom, Ren Xia entered as well. Without warning, of course.","Tian Yang was resting in the bathtub when she walked in, and after quickly washing her body, she also entered the bathtub, resting her slender body on top of his.","\"How long do you think we’ll stay here?\" she asked.","\"Who knows? It’s not like we have anywhere else to be.\"","\"I guess so...\"","After several minutes of silence, Ren Xia suddenly reached for the sword pressing against her back and said, \"Once we’re done here, I want to experience what Kulas had mentioned.\"","Knowing that he can’t avoid this subject forever, Tian Yang let out a long, defeated sigh.","\"...Fine.\"","He had known this moment would come when the subject was first brought up.","Some time later, they moved into the bedroom, where Tian Yang demonstrated the capabilities of the Great Mammoth Body Refinement technique. Rather than enlarging his entire physique, however, he focused the technique on a single area.","\"Heavens...\" Ren Xia stared at his enlarged sword, her eyes wide with excitement and a hint of nervousness.","\"Will this even fit?\" she mumbled in a mosquito-like voice.","Noticing the hesitation in her gaze, Tian Yang teased, \"Don’t tell me you’re going to run away now? You’re the one who suggested this.\"","\"R-Run away? Don’t insult me,\" Ren Xia said, pushing Tian Yang down with surprising force.","She embraced him fully, accepting his enlarged sword without hesitation.","A brief wince of pain crossed her face, but it was quickly replaced by a soft gasp as discomfort quickly shifted into overwhelming warmth.","\"It feels like I am doing it for the first time again,\" she remarked with a playful smile, eyes gleaming with desire.","Thus, Tian Yang and Ren Xia began their life on the Giant’s Continent with Kulas and his family.","Several days later, Xie Mey sought out Tian Yang, eager to learn about the world beyond the continent.","He told her of his journeys through the Divine Heavens, his words flowing like stories from a book of legends, as if he were reading fairy tales to a child.","\"Thank you, Senior! I’ll visit you again later!\"","Some time later, Kulas approached Tian Yang with the expert who created his world.","\"This is Lu An, a level 6 Array Master. He’s the expert I told you about.\"","\"It’s a pleasure to meet you, Senior.\" Lu An gave a polite bow before continuing, \"The creation of a world begins with Array Symbols, so unless you are an Array Master, it’s impossible to create your own world.\"","Tian Yang nodded and said, \"I see. Although I am no expert, I have studied Array Symbol over the years. That said, I’m likely nowhere close to the level required to create my own world.\"","\"Worry not. Even if you are a complete beginner, I am here to teach you.\"","\"Really? Aren’t Array Masters typically busy? Especially one at your level?\"","Lu An smiled and said, \"Typically, yes. However, I am the Giant Emperor’s exclusive Array Master, and he instructed me to teach you, so you will be my priority until you can create your own world.\"","\"In that case, I’ll be in your care.\"","Kulas then spoke, \"By the way, remember the ingredients you showed me?\"","\"The ones I found in Han Zexian’s cavern? What about them?\"","\"Have you forgotten already? I told you that I would find an Alchemist to concoct a treasure using those ingredients. He’ll arrive in a month. If you don’t want to, let me know.\"","\"No, go ahead. It’s not like I have any other use for them.\" Tian Yang took out the sealed ingredients from his spatial ring and handed them to Kulas without hesitation.","\"Let me know when it’s done.\"","\"Sure.\"","From that day forward, Tian Yang devoted himself to learning Array Symbols under the tutelage of Lu An, a Level 6 Array Master who was considered to be at the pinnacle of his craft at that time.","Aside from studying Array Symbols, Tian Yang sparred with Kulas once a week. He also sparred with Ren Xia from time to time, but their other kind of sparring—the one that took place in the bedroom—happened nearly every day.","Several months later, Kulas gave Tian Yang the completed treasure that was created using the ingredients he found in Han Zexian’s cavern.","\"This is the Heaven Defying Ascension Pill,\" Kulas introduced the pill as if it were nothing out of the ordinary.","\"What does it do?\" Tian Yang asked.","Kulas smiled and replied, \"That’s a secret. You’ll find out once you consume it.\"","\"You’re telling me to consume a pill with unknown effects?\" Tian Yang raised his eyebrows, forgetting that was precisely what he did in Han Zexian’s cavern... several times, at that.","\"What? Do you think I’ll poison you or something?\" Kulas glared at him.","\"Of course not.\" Tian Yang accepted the pill and added, \"Thanks. I’ll take it later today.\"","At that moment, he had no idea just how precious and heaven-defying the pill truly was."]},{"number":2278,"title":"Chapter 2278: Effects of the Heaven Defying Ascension Pill","paragraphs":["\"Come see me after you consume that pill. Until then.\"","Kulas didn’t linger and immediately left.","Tian Yang returned to his room shortly after to show Ren Xia the pill.","\"Have you ever heard of the Heaven Defying Ascension Pill before?\" he asked her.","\"No, but it sounds very powerful. What kind of pill is it?\"","\"I don’t know. Kulas didn’t tell me. He said it’s a surprise.\"","Ren Xia inspected the pill for a moment before speaking, \"This pill contains ingredients other than the ones you gave him. A lot of them, actually.\"","\"I guess I’ll find out its effect soon.\"","\"Are you going to consume it now?\"","He quietly nodded.","Moments later, he tossed the pill into his mouth and closed his eyes to concentrate.","The pill dissolved almost instantly upon contact, flooding his mouth with a rich medicinal taste before flowing smoothly down his throat.","Ren Xia stood quietly at his side, her attention fixed on every subtle shift in his aura and physique.","Then, without warning, a tremendous burst of energy exploded from Tian Yang’s body. The resulting shockwave tore through the room, destroying every piece of furniture in an instant.","\"Heavens! What is this amount of energy?!\"","Before Ren Xia could even fully grasp the situation, she noticed that Tian Yang’s cultivation, which had only recently entered Golden Immortal, was soaring to the next realm.","In the span of several breaths, Tian Yang’s cultivation reached the peak of Golden Immortal, and after another moment, surged into the next realm, becoming a True Immortal.","However, it didn’t stop there, and Tian Yang’s cultivation continued to grow.","It was only when his cultivation reached the pinnacle of the True Immortal realm that his aura began to subside.","Tian Yang opened his eyes almost immediately and turned to Ren Xia with a dumbfounded expression.","Ren Xia stared back at him with the exact same look on her face.","\"How long was I cultivating just now?\" he asked in a somewhat nervous voice.","\"A minute... two minutes at most,\" she replied.","Then she asked, \"Did time feel different for you?\"","Tian Yang shook his head and explained, \"Everything happened so quickly that I was only able to watch. I didn’t even do anything after swallowing the pill.\"","\"I’ve never seen anyone’s cultivation rise that fast,\" Ren Xia murmured.","But soon, a worried look clouded her face. \"It’s incredible that your cultivation improved so quickly... but I’m afraid there might be side effects. Something this powerful can’t be without at least one or two drawbacks.\"","Tian Yang inspected his body and said, \"Besides the overflowing energy coursing through my body, I don’t feel any different.\"","He then stood up and continued, \"But I should speak with Kulas just in case.\"","Ren Xia nodded, and the two of them went to meet Kulas together.","\"You’ve returned quicker than I thought.\" Kulas smiled the moment he saw them. \"How was the pill?\"","\"It was amazing... a little too good, if I have to be honest. What did you even feed me? And do I have to worry about any drawbacks?\"","\"I told you what I gave you. The Heaven Defying Ascension Pill,\" Kulas calmly responded with a playful smile on his face. \"And you don’t need to worry about drawbacks because there are none. I also consumed one, after all.\"","Tian Yang raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Is that how you achieved True Immortal?\"","He nodded, \"Yes, and I consumed it a hundred years ago.\"","\"So, what exactly is this pill? It’s the first time I’m hearing its name,\" Ren Xia spoke up.","\"It’s a pill that will instantly improve one’s cultivation by half a realm, even if they’re an Immortal.\"","\"Wait... half a realm? Are you sure?\" Tian Yang asked in a doubtful voice. \"After all, my cultivation improved by nearly two realms.\"","\"What?\" Kulas raised his eyebrows, looking puzzled by his statement.","It was at this moment that Kulas realized Tian Yang’s cultivation had already reached True Immortal. No, it was at the peak of True Immortal!","\"What the hell?\" Kulas exclaimed as he stood up with a dumbfounded look on his face.","\"You were only at the early stages of Golden Immortal, so you couldn’t have reached True Immortal, much less the peak with the Heaven Defying Ascension Pill! I was already at the peak of Golden Immortal when I consumed the pill!\"","Tian Yang shook his head.","\"I don’t know what to tell you since it’s your pill.\"","Kulas fell silent for a long moment to ponder the possibilities.","\"Could it be due to the ingredients you gave me? They were much more potent than what I used for my own pill, after all. However, even then, it shouldn’t have increased the pill’s effect so drastically.\"","\"Now you’re making me worried...\" Tian Yang sighed.","Kulas awkwardly cleared his throat before speaking, \"Come with me. We’ll have an Alchemist take a look at your condition.\"","\"The Alchemist is still here?\"","\"Not the one who concocted the pill, but we have another Alchemist staying with us.\"","Kulas didn’t wait around and immediately led Tian Yang to said Alchemist.","\"Hello.\" A giant woman greeted them shortly after Kulas knocked on her door.","\"You are... one of Kulas’ wives?\" Tian Yang recognized this woman.","Although this is only his second time seeing her, he remembered her from the family introduction a few months ago.","\"And you are His Majesty’s sworn brother. Senior Tian Yang, correct?\" she responded with a calm smile.","\"Chao Shuying, I need you to take a thorough examination of his body immediately,\" Kulas immediately cut to the chase.","The woman named Chao Shuying transformed in the next moment, shrinking her massive form until she stood at their height.","\"What’s wrong with his body? Did he get hurt during your spar?\" she asked.","\"No, he consumed the Heaven Defying Ascension Pill, and his cultivation improved more than what should be possible. I’m worried that something might be wrong with his body,\" Kulas explained."]},{"number":2279,"title":"Chapter 2279: A Special Physique","paragraphs":["\"I see... come inside.\" Chao Shuying gestured for them to enter her room.","Once inside and seated, Chao Shuying continued, \"Now, can you elaborate on the situation for me? What was different from when you consumed it?\"","Kulas proceeded to explain the situation—how Tian Yang’s cultivation had increased by nearly two realms while his own cultivation had only improved by barely half a realm.","\"My first thought was that the ingredients used in his pill were simply of higher quality than those I had,\" he said, voicing his conclusion.","\"That is impossible,\" Chao Shuying responded immediately, her tone firm and assured.","\"I was there when the pill was concocted. In fact, I even assisted, so I’m fully aware of the potency of its ingredients. They were certainly superior, and the pill was undeniably of higher quality than yours, but not to a degree that would create such a drastic difference.\"","\"Then what do you think is going on?\" Kulas asked.","Chao Shuying turned to look at Tian Yang and replied, \"I’ll have to check his body first.\"","\"Go ahead.\" Tian Yang extended his arm toward her.","Chao Shuying immediately began examining his body with Divine Sense, then Divine Gaze.","After a long minute of silence, she released his arm and spoke in a puzzled voice, \"His body... there’s nothing wrong with it. If anything, it’s in perfect condition. As for the pill he consumed, I can still feel its energy, even though it should’ve been long gone by now.\"","\"What does that mean?\" Kulas asked.","\"In situations like these, it means he managed to absorb a higher-than-normal portion of the pill’s effects,\" she explained. \"Even if a pill is created at full efficiency, people usually absorb only ten to fifty percent of its effects while the rest are discarded. The exact amount varies greatly depending on their talent and whether they possess a unique physique.\"","\"However, Senior Tian has somehow retained the portion of the pill he wasn’t able to absorb, and it’s continuing to strengthen his body even now. As for how much he absorbed from the pill... I’d say anywhere between eighty to ninety percent...\"","\"That... sounds like a good thing?\" Ren Xia remarked.","\"That’s more than good! This is literally unprecedented! I have been an Alchemist for almost my entire life, and I have never encountered anyone who could refine more than half of a pill’s full effect!\"","\"Do you have some kind of heavenly physique?\" Kulas asked while looking at Tian Yang with a surprised face.","Tian Yang shook his head and responded confidently, \"Of course not. If I were born with such a divine physique, I wouldn’t have struggled so much in the past. Even now, my talent is only above average.\"","\"Above average? According to what criteria?\" Kulas asked. \"From my perspective, you’re already a monster. No one who is merely above average could defeat me. If that were the case, then the rest of the world would be considered below average at best.\"","\"...\"","Chao Shuying stared at Kulas in bewilderment. She had never seen him praise anyone to such a degree—not even his own children.","\"Have you ever even checked to see whether you have a unique physique?\" Ren Xia asked, cutting into the conversation.","\"I did, shortly after joining the Immortal Monastery. They examine all new disciples to ensure there’s no hidden diamond,\" he said.","\"The Immortal Monastery? Never heard of them.\" Kulas said.","\"Ah. Wait. I have,\" he quickly corrected himself. \"Weren’t they attacked by the Immortal Clans while you were still at war with each other?\"","\"Yes... They tried to draw me out by using the Immortal Monastery as bait. I nearly died on that day.\"","\"I’ve been curious about that ever since I heard what happened, but why did you take the bait?\" Kulas asked.","\"That’s...\"","A certain figure surfaced in Tian Yang’s mind.","\"I had no real attachment to that place, and I even lost a friend there. But something good did come out of it—Elder Sun.\"","\"Elder Sun...?\"","\"Do you remember the woman I shouted at outside Han Zexian’s Tomb?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"Oh, that pretty lady? Of course. I even remember her bewildered expression.\"","\"That was Elder Sun, an elder of the Immortal Monastery. Though she is not my master, she has always looked after me and saved my life several times when I trained recklessly as a disciple. If I were to describe our relationship, it would resemble that of siblings, with her as the elder sister.\"","\"I see... so you went back to save her. Well? Did you?\" Kulas asked.","Tian Yang shook his head.","\"No. She wasn’t there when I returned. Many people had died long before I showed up, and I searched through every corpse... but she wasn’t among them. After going through every corpse I could, I eventually gave up and left.\"","\"So there’s a good chance that she wasn’t at the sect at that time and is still alive,\" Kulas remarked.","\"I hope that’s really true since I still owe her an apology for that day,\" Tian Yang sighed.","After a short pause, Kulas resumed,","\"Now then, back to our main topic. Although your body was examined at the Immortal Monastery, it’s possible they failed to do so thoroughly because their equipment wasn’t sufficient. Not all sects have the proper tools, and only high-grade treasures can identify high-grade physiques, especially back then.\"","\"Considering it’s been hundreds of years since your last examination, I’d say there’s a very high chance that’s the case.\"","\"So I should evaluate my body again?\" Tian Yang asked. \"Where can I go to do that?\"","Kulas smiled and replied, \"Fortunately for you, we have just what you need already available here.\"","\"You really have everything here, don’t you?\" Tian Yang smiled.","\"Of course. This is the only way we can survive such a secluded life.\"","\"I can do the examination for you right now if you want,\" Chao Shuying said.","\"Then I’ll have to bother you a little longer.\" Tian Yang nodded."]},{"number":2280,"title":"Chapter 2280: Tian Yang’s Physique","paragraphs":["Once Tian Yang agreed to have his physique examined, Chao Shuying led him to another room, where a single large device stood alone at its center.","The device was pitch black, its surface resembling polished obsidian. Shaped like a rectangular coffin, it was covered in golden Array Symbols that shimmered softly, giving it an otherworldly beauty.","\"I was expecting something massive—something meant for giants,\" Tian Yang remarked when he saw how ordinary in size the device was.","Chao Shuying smiled. \"Do you have any idea how many materials we’d need to build one on a giant scale? Even if we had the funds, this world doesn’t have enough resources to make it.\"","\"Is that so...\"","Chao Shuying proceeded to hand him a white cloth and said, \"Remove all of your clothes and cleanse your entire body in that bathroom over there. Once you’re done, wear this and come back out.\"","Tian Yang didn’t ask any questions and simply followed her instructions.","Several minutes later, he stepped out of the bathroom wearing nothing but a white cloth wrapped around his waist.","\"You have a well-balanced physique. Are you also a body refiner?\" Chao Shuying questioned him after seeing his refined physique, neither too muscular nor too lean.","\"While I do temper my body occasionally, I wouldn’t call myself a body refiner,\" he replied.","\"Now then, all you need to do is lie inside this device and wait for me to finish. Once it begins, you’ll be submerged in liquid for a few minutes, so don’t be too surprised when it happens.\"","\"Alright.\"","Tian Yang entered the coffin-shaped device—just large enough to contain him—and watched as Chao Shuying lowered the lid, sealing him inside.","Inside, it was completely silent and utterly dark—so still that his senses began to dull within moments.","Then, without warning, he felt something warm rising around him, quickly submerging his body.","As a cultivator of the True Immortal realm, Tian Yang could hold his breath for days without difficulty. A few minutes posed no concern whatsoever.","Some time later, Tian Yang felt the liquid rapidly draining away, and moments after it disappeared, Chao Shuying opened the lid of the device.","\"It’s done,\" she said.","When Tian Yang regained his senses, he could instantly smell the strong medicinal scent on his body, presumably from the liquid.","\"What are the results?\" Kulas asked, sounding a little impatient.","\"Uhh...\" Chao Shuying looked at the device, which showed no reaction, and replied in a puzzled voice, \"He doesn’t have one...\"","\"What?\" Kulas frowned. \"How is that possible?\"","\"I don’t know, but the device isn’t reacting at all. This only happens when the individual has no physique.\"","\"So it wasn’t his physique that caused the abnormal pill absorption rate?\"","Kulas turned to look at Tian Yang and asked, \"Are you sure you don’t have a special bloodline?\"","\"I don’t know my real parents since I was abandoned before I could even crawl, but I also had my blood tested before. No results.\"","\"We can also examine your blood here if you’d like,\" Chao Shuying suddenly said. \"What do you think?\"","\"Since I am already here... might as well.\"","\"Very well.\"","Without any delay, Chao Shuying retrieved a crimson needle from her spatial ring and said, \"It won’t take more than a minute. I just need to collect a few drops of your blood.\"","Tian Yang nodded and offered his arm to her.","Chao Shuying promptly pricked his index finger with the crimson needle, drawing several drops of blood.","The blood slid down the needle’s surface and vanished, as though the needle had absorbed it.","Moments later, the needle began to tremble, and Chao Shuying felt a hot, almost searing sensation radiating from it.","\"Heavens! What kind of reaction is this?!\" Chao Shuying exclaimed, struggling to keep her grip on the needle as it grew unbearably hot.","Kulas and Ren Xia watched nervously while Tian Yang swallowed hard at the reaction from the needle.","Eventually, the needle stopped moving, and Chao Shuying released a deep sigh.","\"I’ve never seen the needle react this intensely before,\" she said as she hurriedly switched it to her other hand.","When she did, an imprint of the needle was revealed on her palm. The needle had grown so hot that it had actually branded her skin.","\"Are you okay?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"It’ll go away with a recovery pill,\" she calmly replied.","\"Anyway, judging by the needle’s reaction, you definitely possess a unique bloodline. And not just that—it’s likely a high-grade one.\"","\"High-grade bloodline? That’s impossible...\" Tian Yang muttered with a dumbfounded look on his face.","\"How high are we talking?\" Kulas questioned with a serious expression.","Chao Shuying met Kulas’s gaze and said, \"When we examined your Mammoth Bloodline, it only barely qualified as Divine-grade. But Senior Tian’s reaction was even stronger. His bloodline is definitely at least Divine-grade.\"","Kulas sucked in a cold breath at the results.","\"Do you hear that, brother? You possess a Divine-grade bloodline! Ain’t that something!\" Kulas exclaimed, turning to Tian Yang with eager anticipation.","But when he saw Tian Yang’s expression, there was no joy there, only confusion.","\"Divine-grade? There must be a mistake,\" Tian Yang quickly said, rejecting the results.","Before Kulas or Chao Shuying could respond, Ren Xia interjected, \"Wait a second—Kulas, when did you get a Divine-grade bloodline? Last I heard, you had an Imperial-grade one, same as me. We both came from the Immortal Clans, remember?\"","Kulas calmly explained, \"When I reached a certain mastery with Great Mammoth Body Refinement, it transformed my bloodline, increasing it to Divine-grade. However, my children are only between Royal-grade and Imperial-grade.\"","\"So Senior Tian... whoever your parents are, they must be from a background that surpasses even the Immortal Clans...\" Chao Shuying said.","\"Surpass the Immortal Clans? Aren’t they already the most renowned and powerful out there?\" Tian Yang asked, confusion evident.","\"Their name may be the most widely known in the Divine Heavens, but they are far from the most powerful,\" Ren Xia replied. \"Even at their height, there were at least three families they would never have dared to offend.\"","\"...\"","Tian Yang stared at her with his mouth agape, clearly in disbelief."]},{"number":2281,"title":"Chapter 2281: Three Pillars of Heaven","paragraphs":["\"Don’t look so surprised,\" Kulas chuckled at Tian Yang’s reaction. \"To ordinary people, the Immortal Clans are the pinnacle of power. Anything above that is simply beyond their understanding. However, for those of us in the Immortal Clans, we have to be aware of their existence even if we don’t want to.\"","Ren Xia then spoke, \"You know the saying ’a frog in a well’? In this case, you’re the frog, and the Immortal Clans are the sky you see above. But there’s still something beyond the sky—the Starry Sky.\"","\"Who exactly are these people?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"They are known as the Three Pillars of Heaven,\" she explained. \"They were the pioneers of cultivation. The first to discover the existence of spiritual energy and the fact that it could be absorbed through technique.\"","\"How can there be three different families, though? Did they all discover cultivation at the same time or something?\" Tian Yang inquired.","Ren Xia shook her head. \"No. They were originally a single background. But they grew so powerful that they eventually had to divide their strength into three branches.\"","Kulas continued, \"The Three Pillars of Heaven consist of the Ji Family, Tian Family, and the Sun Family.\"","\"Did you just say the Sun Family?\" Tian Yang looked at Kulas with wide eyes.","Kulas looked puzzled by Tian Yang’s reaction, but he quickly realized something.","\"Don’t tell me you think that Elder Sun of yours is related to the Sun Family? It’s a very common surname in the Divine Heavens, and there’s no way someone from the Sun Family would be working as a sect elder in a place such as the Immortal Monastery.\"","\"That’s...\" Tian Yang had no response, as Kulas had hit it right on the nail.","After a moment of silence, he sighed. \"Although she never told me her background, she would occasionally allude to coming from a prominent family. I think I even overheard her mentioning the Holy Continent in the past to another elder.\"","\"Wait. The Holy Continent? That is where the primary families of the Three Pillars of Heaven are located.\" Ren Xia said.","\"Also, if we’re talking about surnames, you have one of theirs as well—the Tian Family’s surname. What if your parents came from there?\" she continued.","Tian Yang looked at her with a bitter smile, \"It’s just a coincidence. Even though I never met my real parents, there’s no way they’d be from such a place. After all, why would they abandon me in that backwater village?\"","\"So your adoptive parents named you Tian Yang?\" Kulas suddenly asked.","\"That’s... I don’t know. However, they definitely didn’t have the same surname. In fact, they were surnamed Guan.\"","\"And you never found that weird?\"","\"I never really even thought about it.\"","Chao Shuying then spoke, \"Nobody in this world but your parents can tell you why they abandoned you, but I can tell you with certainty that you have a Divine-grade bloodline.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Ren Xia asked, \"What are you going to do now?\"","\"What even is there for me to do?\" Tian Yang shrugged. \"Even if my real parents are truly from the Three Pillars of Heaven, my connection with them was cleanly severed the moment they abandoned me.\"","\"With that being said, I still refuse to believe that my real parents are from such a place.\"","\"In that case, let’s wrap things up here,\" Chao Shuying said. \"Although you don’t have a unique physique, you possess a Divine-grade bloodline, something arguably even rarer, and that may very well be the reason behind your abnormal pill absorption rate.\"","\"Wait a moment,\" Ren Xia suddenly said. \"We’ve confirmed he has a powerful bloodline, but is there any way to identify which one? If we knew that, we could take advantage of it.\"","Chao Shuying shook her head. \"Not with the tools we currently have. This crimson needle was created only two years ago. It can measure the grade of a bloodline, but that’s all. However, if you can somehow bring me the blood of someone from the Tian Family, I can compare it with Senior Tian’s and determine if there’s a match.\"","\"Blood from the Tian Family? That’s easier said than done. At this point, I’d have better luck getting phoenix blood.\" Ren Xia sighed.","\"Then we can only make use of what little information we have—that he is capable of absorbing pill effects far more efficiently than most. Does the Tian Family have this trait within their lineage?\" Chao Shuying asked.","\"Unfortunately, even the Immortal Clans have very little information on the Three Pillars of Heaven,\" Ren Xia replied.","\"Does it even matter what bloodline I have? I already know what it’s capable of, and that’s more than enough for me.\" Tian Yang interjected.","\"Although I’m confident that it’s the work of your bloodline, we cannot be certain until we do some testing,\" Chao Shuying said.","\"More tests, huh?\"","\"It’ll be quite simple. We just need to feed you some more pills and see what happens.\"","\"Alright.\"","And so, Tian Yang began experimenting with his bloodline, taking all manner of pills—some that heightened strength, others that increased cultivation speed. Ren Xia and Kulas also took part in the tests to compare themselves with him.","Unsurprisingly, the results were exactly as expected. Every pill Tian Yang consumed produced a much stronger effect than when either of them took the same pill.","\"You should know, I was raised in a privileged environment. Envy isn’t something I’m prone to,\" Chao Shuying said. \"Yet I can’t help but be deeply envious of your talent right now.\"","\"Is it really that big of a deal?\" Tian Yang said. \"It just makes pills work better, doesn’t it? Without the money to buy them, it’s useless. No wonder I never noticed it in all these hundreds of years.\"","Chao Shuying rubbed her eyes with a weary sigh.","\"You honestly have no idea how terrifyingly powerful your bloodline is, do you? Others aside, even I would kill for such a talent.\"","Kulas laughed and said, \"You may have learned about it late, but better late than never, right? Hahaha!\""]},{"number":2282,"title":"Chapter 2282: A New Discovery","paragraphs":["\"Better late than never, huh?\" Tian Yang sighed. \"Unfortunately, there is such a thing as being too late, and I’m already at that stage.\"","\"What makes you say that?\" Kulas asked, his brows tightening.","\"Look at me,\" Tian Yang replied. \"I am already a True Immortal. At this stage, ordinary pills— even high-grade ones—are meaningless. Only something on the level of Heaven Defying Ascension Pills would benefit me to an acceptable degree. If only I had realized this talent when I was still a disciple at the Immortal Monastery...\"","\"That’s nonsense,\" Kulas said while shaking his head. \"You make it sound like True Immortal is the end of cultivation when, in reality, it’s just the beginning. There is always a higher cultivation realm, and very recently, there has been a rumor regarding the discovery of a new kind of ’spiritual energy’, surpassing even Immortal Qi.\"","\"Is that true?\" Ren Xia asked, genuinely taken aback.","Kulas shrugged. \"Why would I fabricate something like that? Though little is known right now, many believe it is the key that allows cultivators to surpass the Immortal Realm and step into an entirely different realm.\"","He turned to Tian Yang and continued, \"Therefore, you shouldn’t say something like being too late, Brother Tian. There’s still so much to be discovered in this limitless world.\"","\"I guess so.\" Tian Yang nodded, feeling much better after hearing Kulas’ words.","Once the day came to an end, Tian Yang resumed his life on the Giant’s Continent. He spent his days sparring with Kulas, studying Array Symbols under Lu An, and, of course, accompanying Ren Xia in bed. From time to time, Chao Shuying would summon him so she could further study his bloodline.","Although Tian Yang had little interest in his own bloodline, he found himself deeply intrigued by the Three Pillars of Heaven, particularly their origins, and whether Elder Sun might have come from such a background.","However, acquiring any information about the Three Pillars of Heaven was nearly impossible without traveling to the Holy Continent, which was located on the far opposite side of the world, and Tian Yang had no plans to travel so far at this moment.","In the blink of an eye, twenty years have passed since Tian Yang and Ren Xia started living with Kulas on the Giant’s Continent.","\"How is my brother’s progress with his studies on Array Symbols?\" Kulas suddenly asked Lu An one day.","Lu An gave a bittersweet smile as he replied, \"I was just about to bring that up, Your Majesty. Senior Tian... his talent for comprehension is extraordinary. He absorbs everything I teach him like a dry sponge desperate for water.\"","\"Tell me about it,\" Kulas said with an entertained smile.","\"In just twenty short years, he’d managed to catch up to me, who has studied Array Symbols for nearly my entire 700 years of life.\"","\"Are you saying that he’s already a Level 6 Array Master like you?\" Kulas asked, eyebrows raised in surprise.","Although he was already aware of Tian Yang’s terrifying comprehension talents, it was still hard to comprehend.","\"No,\" Lu An replied with a shake of his head. \"His ability to comprehend and learn is extraordinary, but that doesn’t mean he can apply it right away. Despite his terrifying comprehension, his practical experience remains quite normal.\"","\"I understand... then will you continue to instruct him?\" Kulas asked.","\"Truthfully, I have nothing more to teach him,\" Lu An replied. \"What he needs now is practice, not guidance. Of course, should he have any questions, I will gladly assist.\"","\"In that case, I shall relieve you of your duties,\" Kulas said. \"You may continue your own pursuits as you see fit. Thank you for accepting my request. I know it couldn’t have been easy for an expert such as yourself to instruct a beginner.\"","\"No, on the contrary, it was a learning experience for me as well. I’ve never seriously taught anyone before. In fact, I’m considering opening a school here on the continent so I can continue teaching others. What do you think, Your Majesty?\"","\"A school for Array Masters, huh?\" Kulas mused. \"It would advance our continent even further, and we’d have far more Array Masters in the future. Very well, I’ll allow it. No, I’ll even give you my full support.\"","\"Thank you, Giant Emperor.\"","Even after being dismissed, Lu An continued to visit Tian Yang and informed him of the situation on his next trip.","\"I understand. Thank you for all your efforts,\" Tian Yang said with a faint, bittersweet smile. \"You might be the first true master I’ve ever had.\"","\"Seriously? Didn’t you belong to a sect before?\" Lu An asked, surprised.","\"Yes, but I trained alone most of the time. And whenever I did receive guidance, it was through public lectures with hundreds of disciples all listening at once.\"","\"And unless you’re exceptionally talented or have some kind of background or reputation, the elders won’t approach you. Most disciples have to seek them out and hope to be accepted. Although I was close to an elder, I could never see her as my master, and she was more like an older sister to me.\"","\"To think you have reached your current position without a proper Master your entire life... Honestly, I’m having a hard time believing it. You always talk about lacking talent, but from where I am sitting, you’re extremely talented.\"","\"Thanks...\"","Time flowed on, seasons came and went, and in the blink of an eye, another hundred years had passed.","During this time, the Giant’s Continent continued to develop, and Kulas’ influence started to spread beyond the continent.","Ren Xia finally broke through and stepped into the Golden Immortal realm. As for Tian Yang, he remained at the True Immortal realm like Kulas. Yet the two of them could instinctively sense that they had reached a bottleneck—one that could not be surpassed through ordinary means, much like when they once stood on the verge of entering the Immortal Realm.","However, while his cultivation made little to no progress, Tian Yang had made significant progress as an Array Master and now qualified as a level 4 Array Master with his current skills."]},{"number":2283,"title":"Chapter 2283: Enlightened One","paragraphs":["\"Senior Tian, you’ve been at our place for over a hundred years at this point, but it feels like I am the only one who knows you,\" Xie Mey remarked when she visited him one day to talk about her latest training session outside the palace.","\"That’s probably because you are the only one who approaches and talks to me,\" Tian Yang said.","After a slight pause, he continued, \"Madam Chao, too, I guess.\"","\"Do you have no interest in the others? Is that why you’re not making efforts to know them?\" Xie Mey then asked.","Tian Yang shrugged and said, \"Although I see them in the halls from time to time, they have never even tried to speak with me. Hell, even their greetings are done in silence. But honestly, I don’t feel bothered by it—probably because I don’t really care.\"","\"Is that so...? Well, that works in my favor,\" Xie Mey chuckled. \"It means I get to keep you all to myself.\"","She suddenly scanned the room and then asked, \"Where’s Senior Ren? She’s usually here whenever I visit.\"","\"She recently started studying alchemy, so she spends most of her time with Madam Chao now.\"","\"So she’s finally bored with you, huh?\" Xie Mey teased.","Before he could respond, she continued, \"Say, have you ever thought about accepting another wife?\"","\"No, I can’t say that I have. Where is this coming from?\" Tian Yang looked at her with raised eyebrows.","Xie Mey let out a soft chuckle. \"Because I’ve considered becoming your partner.\"","\"Huh?\" Tian Yang blinked, startled.","\"Why are you so surprised?\" she asked, amused by his reaction. \"I’m a perfectly healthy young woman. It’s only natural for thoughts like that to cross my mind.\"","\"It isn’t the thought itself that concerns me—it’s who you’re thinking about.\" Tian Yang sighed.","\"Why me? I am your father’s sworn brother, you know?\"","\"So what? You’re not actually his brother. And you’re the only man close to me who isn’t part of my own family.\"","Not knowing how to handle her boldness, Tian Yang quickly changed the subject.","\"Have you... spoken to your father about this? If not, you really should...\"","Xie Mey smiled. \"So you’re saying that as long as he approves, you’ll accept me?\"","\"What? How did you twist my words into that?\" Tian Yang sighed.","Xie Mey chuckled, \"It sure is fun messing with you, Senior Tian. Anyway, I was just joking with you.\"","Tian Yang was speechless.","\"Now then, I’ll take my leave and continue my training. See you next time, Senior Tian.\"","Xie Mey departed shortly after.","However, instead of returning to her training as she claimed, she headed straight to Kulas, intent on discussing a certain matter.","The years drifted by, and before they realized it, another three hundred years had passed.","Two hundred years ago, news of the Immortal Monastery’s reopening reached Tian Yang through Kulas. Now, two hundred years later, they had not only fully recovered from the devastation wrought by the Immortal Clans but had even flourished, rising to become an elite sect.","A certain piece of information about a groundbreaking discovery also began spreading like wildfire, sending shockwaves throughout the cultivation world.","The rumor was said to have originated from the Holy Continent, claiming that someone had discovered an entirely new type of spiritual energy—one even stronger than Immortal Qi. It had first surfaced as nothing more than a whisper three hundred years ago, but now, it had grown into something far more substantial than a mere rumor.","\"Have you heard? They’ve named this new spiritual energy ’Celestial Qi,’ and rumors claim that cultivating it could elevate an Immortal cultivator to godhood.\"","Kulas shared the news during a private meeting with Tian Yang and Ren Xia.","\"Celestial Qi, huh?\" Tian Yang muttered with a pondering look on his face.","\"How was it even discovered in the first place?\" Ren Xia asked. \"And has this person already gone past the True Immortal realm, which is said to be the limit right now? Most importantly, can we trust this information? There have been numerous frauds throughout the years, after all.\"","\"I’m not sure how it was discovered, but the information is definitely trustworthy, as it came directly from the Three Pillars of Heaven.\"","\"The pioneers of cultivation, huh? If so, this is indeed massive,\" Tian Yang remarked.","\"Maybe for them, but I highly doubt it will benefit us anytime soon,\" Ren Xia shrugged. \"The Three Pillars of Heaven will likely keep the method to cultivate Celestial Qi to themselves until they’re far ahead of everyone else. It’s exactly what happened when they discovered Immortal Qi, too.\"","\"What? They discovered Immortal Qi as well? How...?\" Tian Yang muttered, stunned. It almost felt as though the Three Pillars of Heaven were advancing the entire cultivation world on their own.","\"They claim it came through enlightenment,\" Kulas said.","After a brief silence, he continued, \"I only learned this because I once snuck into my father’s room back when I was still in the Immortal Might Clan, but within the Three Pillars of Heaven, there is someone known as the ’Enlightened One’. This person possesses a unique talent—the ability to receive divinations directly from Heaven itself through enlightenment, and it is through these enlightenments that they learned about cultivation.\"","\"Seriously? Divination from the Heavens? That sounds like complete nonsense,\" Ren Xia scoffed, shaking her head. \"They’re clearly hiding the truth behind some fancy story.\"","Kulas shrugged. \"Honestly? As absurd as it sounds, I kind of believe it. How else would they have discovered so much?\"","\"What do you think?\" Both of them turned to Tian Yang.","\"It does sound like nonsense at first,\" he admitted. \"However, I’ve witnessed things far more unbelievable, so it doesn’t sound entirely impossible to me.\"","\"Really? Like what?\" Ren Xia asked with a weird face.","He shook his head, his tone apologetic. \"It concerns the forbidden information within Han Zexian’s tomb, so I cannot speak of it...\"","\"Oh? More unbelievable than the Enlightened One?\" Kulas replied with a smile. \"Now I’m really curious.\""]},{"number":2284,"title":"Chapter 2284: The Discovery of Celestial Qi","paragraphs":["Although the discovery of Celestial Qi had shaken the cultivation world and dominated every conversation for a time, the excitement gradually waned. People began to realize that it might still take thousands of years before anyone outside the Three Pillars of Heaven could reach whatever lay beyond the Immortal Realm.","Time marched on, and more than a thousand years had passed since the discovery of Celestial Qi was first announced. With no further developments or reports, the world gradually lost interest to the point where many had forgotten it entirely.","Moreover, there were still very few cultivators who had even stepped into the Immortal Realm at this point, so for the vast majority of cultivators, the realm beyond it was something far beyond their dreams.","As for those in the Immortal Realm, they spent most of their time attempting to sense Celestial Qi. But without even knowing what they were searching for, the effort was no different from chasing a ghost.","During these thousand years, Tian Yang and Ren Xia remained on Giant’s Continent.","Tian Yang, although still stuck in the True Immortal realm, has qualified to become a level 6 Array Master, finally reaching Lu An’s level.","Kulas continued honing his combat experience through constant sparring with Tian Yang, and once he reached a level he deemed satisfactory, he shifted his focus entirely to developing the Giant’s Continent and expanding the Giant Race’s influence beyond its borders.","After a thousand years, Kulas’ influence has surpassed even the Immortal Clans during their peak and has begun attracting the attention of other powerhouses, such as the Three Pillars of Heaven.","Meanwhile, Ren Xia caught up with their cultivation by reaching the True Immortal realm. Afterward, she took a break from alchemy to devote herself entirely to cultivation, harboring the faint hope of becoming the first to sense Celestial Qi and ascend beyond the Immortal Realm.","Of course, she knew the ambition was foolish—especially given how late she’d reached True Immortal—but she still wanted to try.","However, a few more thousand years passed with no progress related to Celestial Qi. By now, even Immortal cultivators had given up entirely, convinced that Celestial Qi had been nothing more than a hoax. And while the main cultivation world was bottlenecked, the rest of the world continued to advance swiftly, with new formations and pill recipes appearing almost every week.","\"It’s been five thousand years since the discovery of Celestial Qi, and the Three Pillars of Heaven haven’t said a single word about it since. Are we sure they’re not just playing us?\" Ren Xia asked. She had long since lost most of her hope and couldn’t help feeling skeptical.","\"I cannot imagine why they would fabricate such a lie,\" Kulas replied, still placing faith in them. \"Doing so would destroy their reputation, and their credibility would plummet to rock bottom.\"","He went on, \"Be patient. Five thousand years is insignificant to cultivators like us. Each realm takes longer to advance than the last. Frankly, it wouldn’t surprise me if no one breaks through to the next realm for another fifty thousand years, much less just five.\"","A few more years later, Tian Yang started to create his own world.","\"Before you even create your world, you must decide where you want to put it,\" Lu An said to him.","\"Where I want to put it, huh?\" Tian Yang pondered for some time but couldn’t think of anything.","\"You got any suggestions?\" He turned to ask Ren Xia.","\"Can’t we just put it somewhere around here?\" she casually replied.","However, Lu An shook his head. \"Since there’s already a personal world within the palace, it would be wiser to establish yours elsewhere. Creating two worlds in close proximity carries unnecessary risks.\"","\"Oh? What kind of danger are we talking about?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"To be frank, we aren’t certain,\" Lu An replied. \"It’s purely conjecture for now, but caution is preferable to regret, especially considering how expensive creating worlds is. Nobody wants to waste their resources, after all.\"","\"Makes sense, but what if we accidentally choose a location that’s already near another world without realizing it?\"","In response to Tian Yang’s hypothetical question, Lu An could only offer a silent shrug.","\"So, what do you intend to do? Will you leave to create your world?\" Kulas asked.","Tian Yang nodded. \"I haven’t stepped outside this continent in over five millennia. It’s about time I got some exercise. Still, I plan to return once my world is established.\"","\"Is that so...\" Kulas muttered before looking at Ren Xia. \"What about you?\"","\"Isn’t it obvious that I am going to follow him?\" she immediately replied.","\"I suppose so,\" Kulas said with a smile. \"Alright then—good luck. I’ll keep your room ready for you, even if it takes a hundred years.\"","\"A hundred years? I highly doubt it’ll take that long,\" said Tian Yang. \"That said, we might travel the world a little before returning.\"","\"Take as long as you need. There’s no need to rush.\"","A few days later, Tian Yang and Ren Xia left the Giant’s Continent for the first time in over five thousand years. Together, they wandered the Divine Heavens in search of a suitable place to create their own world.","They assumed the search wouldn’t take long, but it proved far more difficult than expected. Even after a decade, they still couldn’t find a suitable location. However, they didn’t give up. They continued wandering the world, and creating their own world gradually became a secondary priority.","Fifty years into their journey, a new rumor began to spread around the world, and it was related to Celestial Qi.","\"Did you hear? The Three Pillars of Heaven claims that someone in their family has successfully sensed Celestial Qi for the first time after its initial discovery five thousand years ago!\"","\"Does this mean we might soon learn what lies beyond the True Immortal realm?\"","\"Hard to say. A mortal may sense spiritual energy, but that doesn’t mean they can instantly draw it in and cultivate. They still require the appropriate technique. And even if the Three Pillars of Heaven already have the technique, it will still take time.\"","And just like that, Celestial Qi became a hot topic in the cultivation world again."]},{"number":2285,"title":"Chapter 2285: Sensing Celestial Qi","paragraphs":["After seventy years had passed since Tian Yang and Ren Xia left Giant’s Continent in search of a place to create their own world, they returned to the Giant’s Continent as promised.","\"Since you’re back, it must mean that you’ve created your own world.\" Kulas greeted them with a wide smile.","\"Where did you establish your world?\" he then asked.","\"Tha—\"","\"That’s a secret just for the two of us,\" Ren Xia interrupted before Tian Yang could even fully open his mouth.","Kulas shrugged lightly. \"I don’t particularly care where you choose to set up your love nest, but I must admit—I expected you to return with at least a child or two.\"","\"What?\" Ren Xia looked at him in disbelief.","\"My family has tripled in size since your initial visit,\" Kulas continued. \"And over the past seventy years, I have gained five more sons and two daughters. Meanwhile, you don’t have a single child even after five thousand years.\"","After a brief silence, Kulas asked with a solemn face, \"Ren Xia... are you infertile?\"","Ren Xia trembled with anger at his outrageous assumption and snapped, \"There is nothing wrong with me, and I am definitely not infertile! We don’t have any children because neither of us cares to have one!\"","Kulas blinked in surprise, then turned to Tian Yang. \"For real? You don’t want kids?\"","Tian Yang silently nodded with a stiff smile.","Kulas turned back to Ren Xia. \"And what about you? I find it hard to believe there are women out there who don’t want children.\"","\"What’s so great about having children, anyway?\" Ren Xia retorted. \"Not only would we have to take care of them, but I’d also have to share my dear’s love with them.\"","\"Unbelievable...\" Kulas muttered, looking utterly dumbfounded.","\"Who are you to judge us?\" Ren Xia shot back. \"If anything, we should be judging you for having so many children. Do you even remember all their names?\"","\"Of course,\" Kulas replied with a confident nod. \"Though... due to my position, I have to admit I don’t exactly have the time to get to know them.\"","\"I’m curious...\" Tian Yang suddenly said. \"What do you intend to do with so many children?\"","\"Well, someone has to inherit my throne one day—not to mention my legacy.\"","\"And you need over three hundred children for that? You could do that with just one,\" Ren Xia retorted.","\"That’s true, but I’m an Emperor. What kind of Emperor has only a single child? And besides, there’s no guarantee my first children will be qualified to inherit my legacy.\" Kulas said with a smile. \"Anyway, let’s put this topic behind us. Have you heard the Three Pillars of Heaven’s latest announcement?\"","\"By latest, you mean what they claimed twenty years ago?\" Tian Yang asked.","Kulas nodded, \"That they have managed to sense Celestial Qi.\"","\"What about it?\"","\"Truth is, I have also managed to sense Celestial Qi,\" Kulas revealed with a prideful smile.","\"What?! Is that true?!\" Ren Xia exclaimed.","Tian Yang then asked, \"When did this happen?\"","\"Only a year ago,\" he revealed.","\"Jealous? Want me to help you sense Celestial Qi?\" Kulas teased.","\"Can you really do that?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"I haven’t tried it before, so I can’t say for certain,\" Kulas admitted. \"But it should be no different from helping a new cultivator sense spiritual energy for the first time.\"","\"Then are you close to a breakthrough?\" Ren Xia asked.","Kulas laughed.","\"Of course not. Sensing Celestial Qi is one thing, but I still lack any real understanding of it. Forget cultivating it—I need to comprehend it first.\"","\"Makes sense. So... any idea how long it’ll take for you to figure it out?\"","Kulas shrugged. \"Not a clue. Honestly, I don’t even know if I can comprehend it. It’s hard to put into words, but once you sense it yourself, you’ll get what I mean.\"","\"For you to say something like that...\" Tian Yang swallowed nervously. If even someone like Kulas lacked the confidence to comprehend Celestial Qi, then what chance did he have?","\"Don’t give up before you even start,\" said Kulas after noticing his expression. \"Find me next week. I’ll help you sense Celestial Qi first.\"","\"Alright.\"","Tian Yang and Ren Xia returned to their old room shortly afterward. Just as Kulas had promised, he had kept the place spotless and free of dust for their return.","\"To think we stayed here for five thousand years without a single advancement, yet the moment we leave, so many developments occur in such a short span... Is the world trying to tell us something?\" Tian Yang wondered aloud as he reclined on the bed.","Ren Xia curled up beside him and let out a small laugh. \"In that case... should we leave for another hundred years, then?\"","\"And do what?\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Ren Xia responded, \"Dear... are you sure you don’t want any children? If you’re trying to be considerate...\"","Tian Yang replied with a slight smile, \"Are you asking me, or are you talking to yourself?\"","She sighed. \"Honestly, I’m not so sure anymore. Is it really that strange for a woman not to want children?\"","\"Then take all the time you need to think it over,\" Tian Yang said softly. \"I’m certain I don’t want any, but if you truly do, I wouldn’t mind having one with you.\"","\"If you say so...\"","A week later, Tian Yang went to find Kulas.","\"Anything I should know before we begin?\" Tian Yang asked as he sat on the ground of the throne room.","\"I don’t think so.\"","\"Then let’s begin.\"","Kulas seated himself behind Tian Yang and placed his palms on his back.","\"I will now attempt to sense Celestial Qi while sharing my senses with you. Whether you can also sense it will be entirely up to you,\" Kulas said as he closed his eyes.","\"Whenever you’re ready.\"","\"I’m ready.\" Tian Yang said.","The very next moment, Kulas took a deep breath and began sharing his senses with Tian Yang."]},{"number":2286,"title":"Chapter 2286: Sensing Celestial Qi(2)","paragraphs":["Once he confirmed that his senses were properly linked with Tian Yang’s, Kulas began attempting to sense Celestial Qi.","However, even though he had managed to sense it before, it wasn’t something he could replicate immediately. When he first successfully sensed Celestial Qi, it took him nearly ten years of straight cultivation.","Fortunately, he has gotten a lot better these days, and the last time it only took him a month.","Days passed in the blink of an eye, yet Tian Yang still couldn’t sense anything different. Kulas hadn’t sensed it either, of course, but Tian Yang didn’t know that—and speaking might disrupt their concentration. So he stayed silent.","A little over a month later, Kulas finally began to sense the Celestial Qi around them. However, he stayed silent, allowing Tian Yang the chance to perceive it on his own.","Tian Yang, not knowing when—or if—he would sense anything, maintained his focus throughout the entire month. He could tell that something had changed through Kulas’s senses, yet he still couldn’t grasp it clearly himself.","’This feels just like when I was inside Han Zexian’s cavern...’ Tian Yang thought to himself, recognizing a familiar sensation in the struggle to comprehend the unknown.","Naturally, this was nothing like attempting to comprehend the forbidden knowledge that devoured his longevity. Compared to that ordeal, his current situation was considerably more comfortable.","Minutes turned into hours, and hours into days. In the blink of an eye, another month had passed, yet Tian Yang still made no progress.","After yet another month, Kulas opened his eyes and said, \"Alright, that’s enough for me. I can only stay in this state for so long before I’m mentally exhausted.\"","Tian Yang opened his eyes as well and let out a defeated sigh. \"I wasn’t able to sense it. Or rather... I sensed something, yet couldn’t grasp it at all. Sorry for wasting your time.\"","Kulas let out a hearty laugh. \"Did you truly expect to sense Celestial Qi so quickly? I certainly didn’t think you would succeed on the first attempt. You may excel in comprehension, but Celestial Qi is something else altogether. It will be an obstacle even you will struggle with.\"","\"Also, while I may be helping you sense Celestial Qi, I am also improving my own comprehension, so it’s not like I am wasting any time.\"","\"How often will we do this?\" Tian Yang then asked.","\"If every session takes around three months, we can do it two times a year. Once a year is fine if you want to take it slower.\"","\"Let’s do it twice a year then.\"","\"Very well.\"","Although he would only attempt to sense Celestial Qi with Kulas’s assistance twice a year, Tian Yang continued to practice on his own whenever he had the time.","\"Any progress?\" Ren Xia asked Tian Yang after he returned from his tenth attempt to sense Celestial Qi.","\"Nope.\"","A hundred attempts later—","\"Any progress?\"","Tian Yang could only silently shake his head.","In the end, it took Tian Yang over one thousand attempts and 250 years to finally sense Celestial Qi, albeit only a glimpse.","\"I can sense it! I can sense Celestial Qi!\" Tian Yang exclaimed with excitement the moment he sensed it.","It had been a long time since he experienced such excitement, and it made him feel like a child again.","\"Good, now this is where the true trial begins...\" Kulas remarked with a smile.","\"Right...\" Tian Yang’s excitement quickly died down after he remembered that it would take more than just sensing Celestial Qi to reach the next cultivation realm.","\"How’s your progress?\" Tian Yang then asked.","\"As slow as a snail,\" Kulas shook his head.","While Tian Yang had at last succeeded in sensing Celestial Qi, Kulas had shown almost no improvement, and his progress was barely any different from what it had been 250 years earlier when Tian Yang first started.","\"At this rate, we probably won’t see what’s beyond the Immortal Realm for several more thousand years,\" Kulas sighed.","\"That’s a generous estimate,\" said Tian Yang. \"Not only do we need to fully comprehend it, but we also need the proper technique to cultivate it. I have a feeling that we won’t see any real progress for at least tens of thousands of years.\"","Kulas replied, \"It sucks, but what can we do about it? With that said, it’s not like it’s a race—at least not for me—so I will be taking things nice and slowly.\"","Now that he’s managed to sense Celestial Qi, Tian Yang decided to continue cultivating to make sure it wasn’t a fluke.","A year later, Tian Yang returned to Ren Xia with the results.","\"Seeing how it took you much longer to return this time, I guess you’ve finally managed to sense Celestial Qi.\" Ren Xia said, reading him like an open book.","He nodded, \"Now that I can sense Celestial Qi, I can help you sense it, too.\"","However, Ren Xia shook her head.","\"Thanks for the offer, but I want to try sensing it myself.\"","\"Why?\" Tian Yang asked, genuinely puzzled.","\"Because of my pride,\" she replied calmly.","\"I still don’t understand.\"","Ren Xia took a breath before elaborating, \"Kulas managed to sense Celestial Qi on his own. I... don’t want to lose to him, so I’m going to do it myself. Of course, I’m not belittling your achievement. This is just my own stubborn pride. Moreover, it’s not like I have anything else to do.\"","\"If that’s what you really want to do.\" Tian Yang nodded. \"If you ever change your mind, I’ll be here.\"","Ren Xia chuckled and said, \"Who knows? Maybe I will even surpass you.\"","He smiled and said, \"If you can truly comprehend Celestial Qi by yourself, then that is only a given. Hell, if it weren’t for the Heaven Defying Ascension Pill, you would’ve already surpassed me in cultivation.\"","\"Then how about a wager?\" Ren Xia suddenly said. \"Let’s bet on whether I can sense Celestial Qi within five thousand years.\"","\"What are we betting on?\"","\"If I win, you must listen to one of my demands. If I lose, I’ll listen to one of yours,\" she said.","\"That’s it?\" Tian Yang raised his eyebrows. \"If there’s something you want from me, you can just ask me, you know?\"","\"I know, but I cannot think of anything else.\"","\"I guess...\"","\"Then I’m going to start now!\"","Ren Xia wasted no time and immediately started her cultivation session.","’I should probably set a goal for myself, too.’ Tian Yang thought to himself as his gaze lingered on Ren Xia for a minute before he also started his own cultivation.","Now that he could sense Celestial Qi, Tian Yang found himself spending more and more time in cultivation. At his current cultivation level, time moved beyond recognition, especially when cultivating, and what he perceived as minutes often slipped into years without him noticing.","One thousand years... two thousand years... four thousand years passed in the blink of an eye.","Although so much time had passed, little had changed in the cultivation world. However, more and more cultivators were now reaching the True Immortal realm and had begun attempting to sense Celestial Qi.","Then, another seven hundred years passed.","\"Dear! I’ve done it!\"","Tian Yang was in the middle of cultivation when he suddenly heard Ren Xia’s excited voice coming from the room beside his.","When he opened his eyes, he could see her standing outside his open room with an exhilarated smile on her face.","\"I can sense Celestial Qi!\" she declared with a proud smile.","\"Oh? How long has it been?\" he asked.","\"Four thousand seven hundred and fifty-two years!\" she immediately answered.","\"To be honest, I was close to giving up,\" she suddenly continued. \"However, in the end, I had an enlightenment.\"","\"An enlightenment? How did it feel?\" Tian Yang asked, his interest piqued.","Ren Xia closed her eyes to recall the feeling and replied, \"It’s hard to explain... one moment I couldn’t sense anything, and the next, I could suddenly feel Celestial Qi as if it had always been there.\"","She paused for a moment before adding, \"To be honest, it feels unreal. I can sense Celestial Qi, yet it doesn’t feel like something I accomplished. It feels as though it was given to me.\"","\"What are you talking about? It’s definitely your own achievement. Or what? Are you saying that Heaven took pity on you and directly helped you? Like the Enlightened One from the Three Pillars of Heaven?\"","\"If you put it like that...\" Ren Xia muttered with a stiff smile.","\"Anyway, this means I won the bet.\"","\"Bet?\" Tian Yang wore a puzzled face.","\"Don’t tell me you forgot?\"","Tian Yang’s expression froze for a moment before he suddenly recalled the bet.","\"Ah, I remember now. Sorry, I actually forgot about it,\" he said.","\"So, what do you want me to do for you?\"","\"I’ll let you know once I think of something,\" she replied quickly.","\"You had almost five thousand years to think...\"","\"Nonsense,\" she shot back. \"I was completely focused on my goal. I didn’t have any room left to think about anything else.\"","\"If you say so.\"","\"And you? How close are you to understanding Celestial Qi?\" she then asked.","Tian Yang offered a faint, bitter smile. \"There were moments when I thought I was close. But the deeper I delve, the clearer it becomes that I’ve only touched the surface.\"","\"I see... What about Kulas?\"","\"Actually, I haven’t seen or spoken to him in a while now,\" he admitted.","\"Then let’s go see him now. I can’t wait to gloat,\" Ren Xia chuckled.","\"Alright.\" He nodded."]},{"number":2287,"title":"Chapter 2287: Mood Swings","paragraphs":["Shortly after Ren Xia emerged from her successful seclusion, she and Tian Yang went to find Kulas.","However, when they arrived at the throne room, they were met with an unfamiliar sight. The usually unobstructed entrance was now guarded by two figures standing watch outside.","\"Guards? Did something happen?\" Tian Yang wondered out loud as they approached the room.","They have been living at the palace for thousands of years at this point, but this is the first time they’ve seen guards outside the room.","When the guards noticed Tian Yang and Ren Xia, they immediately bowed and said, \"We greet Senior Tian and Senior Ren.\"","\"Hey, we’re here to speak with Kulas. He’s inside, right?\"","The guards nodded, but they continued to say, \"Yes, but we cannot let you inside without the Giant Emperor’s approval.\"","\"What kind of absurdity is this?\" Ren Xia said sharply. \"We’ve walked in and out of this place freely for thousands of years. What changed?\"","The guard offered an apologetic smile. \"I’m aware, but these are His Majesty’s orders. He expressly commanded us to prevent the two of you from entering without his consent.\"","\"He mentioned us directly...?\"","Tian Yang had a bad feeling about their situation, and he quickly said, \"Then can you let Kulas know that we’re here?\"","\"Of course.\"","One of the guards retrieved a communication jade slip and spoke into it.","Moments later, the guard returned and relayed Kulas’s response.","\"His Majesty says he’s currently occupied and will meet with you next month.\"","\"Next month?\" Tian Yang raised an eyebrow.","Though a month was nothing to cultivators at their level, it still felt strange. Kulas had never made them wait before and had always prioritized them, no matter how busy he was.","\"Alright, we’ll come back later.\"","However, Tian Yang didn’t linger and quickly left with Ren Xia.","\"Something feels off,\" he remarked as they returned to their room. \"And it’s not just the situation with Kulas. The atmosphere in this place feels different.\"","\"When was the last time you left this room?\" Ren Xia asked him.","\"About two hundred years ago, so a lot could’ve happened.\"","\"So what? Are we just going to wait?\" she then asked.","\"It’s only a month. However, I can talk to someone else.\"","\"You mean Chao Shuying?\"","\"Or Xie Mey.\"","The following day, they went to look for Chao Shuying. However, they soon learned that she was no longer staying in the palace, having moved instead to the newly established alchemy school on the Giant’s Continent.","\"I forgot they created a school for Alchemists five hundred years ago after the success of their school for Array Master,\" Tian Yang remarked.","Since these places were relatively small and operated more like ordinary schools, they were classified as such rather than as sects or other formal establishments.","These schools accepted anyone willing to learn, regardless of background. They were also free to attend, making them immensely popular, so much so that humans would travel across great distances just to study on the continent.","Over the years, the Giant’s Continent continued to expand, growing several times its original size. Not only that, its influence had already spread beyond the continent, and it was no longer an obscure power known to only a few.","In recent times, the Giant Race had begun appearing outside their continent, albeit only within nearby regions. Though they continued to draw attention and disdain, it wasn’t as intense as before.","Not wanting to disturb Chao Shuying, Tian Yang went to find Xie Mey instead.","He quickly found her at the training ground.","\"Senior Tian! It’s been a while!\" Xie Mey greeted him with a bright smile.","He nodded. \"Indeed, it has.\"","\"What brings you here?\" she asked, eyes gleaming. \"Don’t tell me you came to see me? If so, this would be the first time you’re the one seeking me out.\"","It has always been Xie Mey who approached him in the past, never the other way around.","\"Yes. I have a few questions.\"","The smile on Xie Mey’s face faded, and she asked, \"Have you spoken to my father yet?\"","Tian Yang shook his head.","\"He’s busy, so I won’t be able to see him for another month.\"","\"I see. So you’re here to ask me about my father’s situation.\"","\"Did something happen to him?\"","Xie Mey scratched her head and sighed, \"Something did happen, but it isn’t for me to tell you. If you want to know, you will have to hear it from my father.\"","\"...\"","Tian Yang fell silent for a moment before asking with a slight frown, \"Is it really that serious?\"","\"Honestly...? Not really.\"","Tian Yang was left dumbfounded. How could it not be serious when everything pointed to the opposite?","Seeing his reaction, Xie Mey shrugged.","\"You’ll know once you speak with my father.\"","Since it was only a month, Tian Yang decided to wait it out.","Time seemed to pass far more slowly than usual for him, but eventually the month came to an end, and he was finally granted an audience with Kulas.","Tian Yang and Ren Xia followed the guard, who informed them that Kulas was waiting. Upon entering the throne room, they found Kulas seated on his throne, a perplexed expression on his face.","\"What’s going on? Did something happen while we were in seclusion?\" Tian Yang went straight to the point and asked.","Kulas didn’t immediately respond.","After a long minute of silence, he eventually let out a deep sigh.","\"Honestly, I am still contemplating whether I should even tell you since it’s a little embarrassing.\"","\"Embarrassing?\" Tian Yang raised his eyebrows, looking confused.","\"Stop beating around the bush and tell us already,\" Ren Xia said, sounding annoyed.","Kulas sighed once more before nodding, a defeated look crossing his face.","\"I’ve been experiencing random mood swings that I cannot control lately—mostly anger. I thought I had completely moved past my old scars, but it seems my mental instability is slowly returning,\" he revealed."]},{"number":2288,"title":"Chapter 2288: Mood Swings(2)","paragraphs":["Kulas continued, his voice heavy. \"Because of these mood swings, my family has started avoiding me. They try to hide it, of course—but it’s obvious to me.\"","\"Wait... mood swings? That’s it?\" Ren Xia said, staring at him in disbelief. \"Are you certain this isn’t simply stress?\"","Kulas nodded and elaborated, \"The mood swings came out of nowhere and have only been growing more frequent. Not only can I no longer control them, but I’m starting to lose awareness altogether. I don’t even realize it’s happening until it’s already over. There’s no way stress would cause this.\"","Tian Yang then said, \"I agree that this doesn’t resemble stress. However, that doesn’t necessarily mean your mental instability has returned. You’ve been stable for thousands of years—why would you suddenly regress? Was there some kind of trigger?\"","Kulas pondered his question for a moment before shaking his head.","\"No, not that I can think of any.\"","\"Then there must be another explanation.\"","\"Have you seen a doctor yet?\" Ren Xia asked.","\"That was the first thing I did when it started happening. I saw several of them, too. However, they were unable to find anything wrong with me.\"","\"If I’m not ill and it isn’t stress, then there is only one explanation remaining—my mind,\" Kulas sighed. \"Despite our strong physiques and resilient mental fortitude, cultivators are not immune to mental damage. In fact, we are often more susceptible to it.\"","\"What about a heart demon?\" Tian Yang asked. \"It’s one of the most common issues cultivators face. What if a part of your mind still believes you’re trapped in the Immortal Clan’s dungeon?\"","\"I don’t possess any heart demons. I’ve already taken the Demonic Manifestation Pill, a medicine designed to forcibly expose them, and it produced no response.\"","\"Anyway, regardless of the cause, the reality remains that I’m causing trouble for my family,\" Kulas said. \"Thankfully, you haven’t seen my mood swings yet, and I intend to keep it that way.\"","\"How do you intend to do that? These mood swings are random, right? Are you only going to meet us after you’ve had one? And how bad are these mood swings?\" Tian Yang bombarded him with questions.","\"From what I’ve heard, the mood swings aren’t severe,\" Kulas explained, \"but they’re... unsightly. As for how I plan to make sure you don’t witness them—I don’t know yet. I’ll think of something. Until then, it’s best we limit our interactions.\"","Tian Yang narrowed his eyes. \"Are you saying that because you don’t want to trouble us?\"","\"Of course. What else would it be?\"","\"And yet, that’s exactly what you’re doing,\" Tian Yang replied calmly. \"Avoiding us isn’t a solution. Even if you believe it’s unbecoming, distancing yourself won’t fix anything. You’re simply running from the problem when we should be addressing it together. What do you think sworn brothers are for?\"","\"That’s...\" Kulas was left speechless by his words.","Tian Yang continued a moment later, \"If you get it, let us help you.\"","A warm smile appeared on Kulas’ face.","\"Thanks.\"","Some time later, Kulas asked.","\"By the way, why did you want to see me?\"","Ren Xia smiled and replied, \"I wanted to gloat.\"","\"About what?\"","\"That I have managed to sense Celestial Qi all by myself,\" she revealed with a prideful look on her face.","\"...\"","Kulas offered no reply, only staring at her in stunned silence, his eyes widened and his mouth slightly open.","After a moment of silence, he shifted his gaze to Tian Yang and asked, \"Is she telling the truth? You didn’t help her at all?\"","Tian Yang nodded with a smile.","\"Yes, she’s telling the truth. I offered to help her, but she refused.\"","\"And it took me less than five thousand years,\" she added. \"Now watch me enter the next realm before either of you will!\"","\"Let’s not get ahead of ourselves,\" Kulas shook his head.","They continued chatting for a little longer before Kulas brought up a new topic.","\"By the way, this may sound random, but I have been wanting to do this for a very long time.\"","After taking a deep breath, he continued, \"I am going to host a tournament on this continent.\"","\"A tournament?\" Tian Yang raised his eyebrows at this news.","Kulas confirmed with a nod.","\"The participants will only be allowed to use their physique and techniques limited to strengthening their bodies, so there will be no weapons or martial techniques allowed. I am going to call it... the Tournament of Strength!\"","\"Why are you suddenly hosting a tournament?\" Tian Yang asked, puzzled by his intentions.","\"Although anybody can participate, the giants will likely dominate it since we inherently have a superior physique. As for the purpose... I want to showcase the power of giants to the rest of the world. Oh, I also want to see if there are any excellent warriors out there for my children.\"","\"When are you going to host it?\"","\"I don’t have an exact date, but I have already begun the preparations. Maybe around fifty years from now.\"","\"I see... I’m looking forward to it.\"","\"You’re participating, right?\" Kulas suddenly asked with expectant eyes.","\"What? Me?\" Tian Yang almost couldn’t believe his ears. \"You want me to participate in a tournament? With my cultivation?\"","\"You won’t be using your cultivation, though.\"","\"It doesn’t change the fact that I’ll likely be competing with people with far less experience.\"","Kulas chuckled and said, \"You don’t have to give me an answer right now. Just think about it for now. I’ll ask you again once I have all of the details ready.\"","\"Whatever.\"","A year later, Kulas officially announced the Tournament of Strength. It instantly became a sensation across the Giant’s Continent and even drew the attention of those beyond its borders, especially after word of the tournament’s rewards spread.","The tournament was scheduled to take place in fifty years, but people were already heading to Giant’s Continent mere days after it was announced.","In the years that followed, the Giant’s Continent became more crowded with visitors than ever before, including unexpected visitors from the Holy Continent."]},{"number":2289,"title":"Chapter 2289: A Faint Presence","paragraphs":["\"Hey, brother, are you sure you don’t want to participate in the Tournament of Strength?\" Kulas asked Tian Yang as the tournament day drew closer.","\"How many times do I have to decline before you get it?\" Tian Yang sighed.","\"But don’t you want to show off your skills to the world?\"","\"Why the hell would I care about something like that? And it’s not like the world isn’t aware of me already. Have you forgotten who brought the downfall of the Immortal Clans?\"","Tian Yang’s war against the Immortal Clans had once made his name infamous across the Divine Heavens. However, with thousands of years having passed, his name—though not forgotten—was rarely mentioned anymore.","\"Also, I am technically a criminal, you know?\" Tian Yang said with a slight smile.","Kulas laughed out loud and said, \"Who’d dare hunt the man who pretty much single-handedly defeated the Immortal Clans? If anyone were to go after you, it’d be the Three Pillars of Heaven, but seeing how they’ve ignored you, you don’t have to worry about such a thing.\"","\"...\"","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang spoke, \"Now that you mentioned it... Why didn’t the Three Pillars of Heaven do anything? They basically allowed the Immortal Clans to fall.\"","If the Three Pillars of Heaven had intervened with his revenge, the Immortal Clans would’ve likely still been as powerful as before.","\"The Three Pillars of Heaven are not babysitters, nor do they have any reason to help the Immortal Clans. While they may have been on friendly terms, it’s not like they were actual friends with each other.\"","Kulas paused briefly before continuing, \"Speaking of the Three Pillars of Heaven, I received some interesting information about them yesterday. It appears that some of their people will be present at the tournament.\"","Tian Yang raised his eyebrows at this news.","\"The Three Pillars of Heaven will be participating in the tournament?\" he asked with a dumbfounded face.","\"No, they won’t be participating. They will only be spectating.\"","\"I doubt they’ll only be here to spectate.\"","Kulas nodded, \"I’m sure they have business with me, but we know too little about them to make any speculations.\"","\"Anyway, if you’re not going to participate, what are you going to do? Just spectate?\"","Tian Yang nodded.","\"What a pity. The champion of the tournament will get to fight me, too.\"","\"You make it sound like we haven’t fought each other thousands of times by now. And I’m sure you wouldn’t want to lose before so many people in public.\"","Kulas chuckled, \"Now that you’ve mentioned it, we haven’t sparred in a few hundred years, and I still haven’t beaten you yet.\"","\"If you want to fight, we can do it after the tournament.\"","\"Sounds good.\" Kulas nodded.","Tian Yang then said, \"By the way, how have you been feeling lately? I haven’t seen any mood swings since you mentioned it nearly fifty years ago.\"","\"I’m actually confused myself. I’d have mood swings several times a year, but after I spoke to you, it hasn’t happened once. If I had known it would be like this, I would’ve told you soon.\"","\"Regardless, this is a good thing.\"","\"Of course.\" Kulas agreed with a smile.","As time passed and the tournament day drew closer, more and more people flocked to the Giant’s Continent. Cultivators of great power and members of influential families alike arrived in droves, all eager to witness the prowess of the Giant Race firsthand.","Although rumors circulated that members of the Three Pillars of Heaven might appear, no one knew their identities—or if they would truly show up—leaving the crowds to speculate.","\"It’s been a while since I left the palace, so I’m going to leave for a bit.\" Tian Yang said as he approached the door.","\"Where are you going? I’ll go with you.\" Ren Xia said.","However, Tian Yang shook his head and said, \"Sorry, but I want to go alone. I have been wanting to visit this place ever since I returned to this continent, but I never found the courage to do so.\"","Ren Xia realized where Tian Yang wanted to go and calmly nodded, \"Alright. I won’t bother you then.\"","\"Thanks.\"","After leaving the palace, Tian Yang made his way to the place where he had first met Kulas... and where he had lost Huang Xiao Li.","Yet the continent had changed beyond recognition, its land expanded many times over. It took him considerable time to find the location, and when he finally stood there, it bore no resemblance to his memories. Given the thousands of years that had passed, that was only natural.","After standing motionless for many hours, Tian Yang finally reached into his pocket and retrieved a spatial ring.","\"If reincarnation is real... are you somewhere in this vast world right now, living a vastly different life? Are you living a happy life? Would I even be able to recognize you?\" he muttered.","Some time later, he put away the spatial ring and began walking a certain path.","Eventually, he reached an empty stretch of land. Once the entrance to Han Zexian’s Tomb, it was now utterly barren, with no sign that the tomb had ever existed.","According to what he’d heard from Ren Xia, the Immortal Clans had taken full control of Han Zexian’s Tomb after he entered the cavern. However, they soon realized that the trials no longer functioned, reducing the tomb to nothing more than an empty world.","After he escaped from the tomb, the Immortal Clans were forced to abandon the tomb as well because it started to collapse on itself.","’Kulas told me that he’d tried to find Han Zexian’s Tomb again but to no avail... hmm?’","Tian Yang’s thoughts were abruptly interrupted when he sensed a faint presence approaching from behind.","He turned around, and his eyes widened in shock and disbelief. It was someone he recognized.","Not only did he recognize them, but despite the thousands of years that had passed, they hadn’t changed in the slightest.","However, before Tian Yang could snap out of his daze, the individual spoke first, \"Tian Yang...?\"","\"Elder... Sun?\" he responded."]},{"number":2290,"title":"Chapter 2290: Reunion With Elder Sun","paragraphs":["The person standing before Tian Yang was none other than Elder Sun, and she looked exactly as she had the last time he saw her thousands of years ago, almost as though she hadn’t aged a single second.","Elder Sun was a beautiful young woman with short black hair that barely brushed her shoulders, clear amber-colored eyes, a slender physique, and a rather ordinary stature. She wasn’t the kind of breathtaking beauty that drew instant attention, yet there was a subtle aura about her—one that made her seem more beautiful the longer one looked.","\"Tian Yang...? Is that really you?\" Elder Sun said softly, blinking as if she couldn’t quite believe her eyes.","Unlike herself, Tian Yang had changed tremendously since the last time she’d seen him. He had grown taller, more mature, and, of course, more handsome. He was no longer the young man who had always worried her.","Yet despite his transformation, Elder Sun recognized him almost immediately.","\"Elder Sun... so you were alive.\" Tian Yang spoke with a relieved smile on his face.","\"Why would I be dead?\" she frowned slightly.","\"Didn’t you hear about what happened to the Immortal Monastery?\" Tian Yang asked quickly. \"They were dragged into my conflict with the Immortal Clans. Thousands of disciples died, and when I couldn’t find you, I assumed you were dead.\"","He paused, then asked, \"Where have you been? Why weren’t you at the sect?\"","Elder Sun sighed and replied, \"I left the sect long before that happened. As for where I went... I returned to my hometown.\"","Tian Yang narrowed his eyes slightly before asking, \"Would that happen to be... the Holy Continent?\"","Her eyes widened with surprise.","\"How did you know?\"","Her reaction confirmed Tian Yang’s suspicions. Elder Sun was undeniably from the Sun Family of the Three Pillars of Heaven.","\"I overheard you speaking with another elder. I forgot her name, but I always see the two of you together.\"","\"You mean Elder Jing?\"","Tian Yang nodded.","\"And if you’re from the Holy Continent... Do you also belong to the Sun Family, one of the Three Pillars of Heaven?\" he continued to ask.","Elder Sun didn’t immediately respond.","After a moment of silence, a slight smile tugged on her lips, and she spoke, \"To find out so much about me, even though I’ve never told you anything... You must’ve spent a lot of time investigating me. Do you have a crush on me or something?\"","\"Don’t flatter yourself, Elder Sun. I merely placed pieces of a puzzle together after learning of them by chance.\"","Elder Sun frowned, clearly displeased with his response, and said, \"You can stop calling me Elder Sun. I lost the qualifications when I left the sect.\"","\"Then what should I call you? Now that I think about it, I don’t even know your full name.\"","\"My name is... Rouxi... Sun Rouxi—but I forbid you from using my given name.\"","\"If I cannot call you Elder Sun or use your given name, what am I supposed to call you? Sister Sun? Senior Sister?\" Tian Yang said with a smile. \"Well, you were always more like an elder sister to me than anything.\"","\"An elder sister?\" she sneered. \"I thought you no longer wanted anything to do with me. Or have you forgotten about what you said to me when we last met?\"","Tian Yang’s expression stiffened when she brought up his previous outburst—that he had already severed their relationship.","\"That’s...\"","Tian Yang opened his mouth slightly, only to close it again.","After a brief silence, he lowered his body and bowed to her. \"This may sound like an excuse, but I was overwhelmed by emotion back then and wasn’t thinking clearly. I’ve regretted not being able to apologize to you ever since.\"","He paused, then said softly, \"I’m sorry. Truly.\"","\"Ahem.\" Sun Rouxi cleared her throat, covering her mouth with a fist as she tried to hide the faint smile tugging at her lips. \"Well, you were young and stupid back then, so I am willing to forgive you.\"","Tian Yang raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Speaking of age... how old are you, exactly? You haven’t changed even slightly since I last saw you, and you’re even at the True Immortal Realm now. No... You were probably already an Immortal back then and were merely suppressing your cultivation.\"","\"It’s rude to ask a woman her age,\" she said with a faint smile. \"But if you’re imagining me as some ancient monster, you’re mistaken. I’m at most a hundred years older than you. At our level, that’s hardly worth mentioning. And no—I wasn’t suppressing my cultivation back then. What you saw was my real cultivation.\"","\"So you’ve managed to reach True Immortal since then? That’s quite impressive.\"","\"Who do you think you’re talking to? If a talentless brat like you can reach True Immortal in a few thousand years, why can’t I? I am a member of the Three Pillars of Heaven, pioneers of cultivation, you know?\"","\"Honestly, besides that they discovered cultivation, I don’t know much, if anything, about the Three Pillars of Heaven. In fact, I didn’t even know about their existence until recently.\"","\"There isn’t much to know,\" she said. \"We’re no different from other families—just a bit larger and more secluded.\"","\"That... sounds like an understatement.\"","\"If you’re that curious, why don’t you come to the Holy Continent and see for yourself?\" Sun Rouxi suddenly said.","\"What?\" Tian Yang looked at her with a surprised face. \"But from what I’ve been told, the Holy Continent is a special place that most cannot enter.\"","\"That’s true, but I can give you permission.\"","\"Is it really that simple?\"","She nodded.","\"Pretty much.\"","\"I’ll think about it after the tournament ends,\" Tian Yang then said.","\"Speaking of the tournament... Are you also here to spectate the tournament?\" she asked.","\"Something like that. In fact, I have been living here for the last several thousand years.\"","\"This place? Why?\" She tilted her head slightly with a puzzled look, unable to comprehend his choice.","\"My best friend is the Giant Emperor, and I don’t have anywhere else to go,\" he said."]},{"number":2291,"title":"Chapter 2291: Sun Rouxi","paragraphs":["\"You’re friends with the Giant Emperor? Best friends, at that?\" Sun Rouxi wore a surprised look on her face after hearing this information.","Tian Yang nodded.","\"We’ve known each other long before he became the Giant Emperor, though.\"","Sun Rouxi suddenly fell silent with a pondering expression.","A moment later, she spoke, \"Since you’re his friend, do you think you can speak to him for me—the Three Pillars of Heaven? Although we came to spectate the tournament, our main purpose here is to speak with the Giant Emperor.\"","Tian Yang shook his head and said, \"That won’t be necessary. He is already expecting the Three Pillars of Heaven to contact him. But if you don’t mind me asking, what business do you have with him?\"","However, Sun Rouxi shrugged before replying, \"I don’t know. I tagged along on my own will, so I am not part of the main group.\"","\"The main group... how many from the Three Pillars of Heaven are here?\" he asked.","\"Six people, excluding me. Two from the Ji Family, two from the Sun Family, and two from the Tian Family.\"","\"I see... by the way, this may be a weird question, but what’s the Tian Family like?\"","Although he claimed that he wasn’t interested in his real background, Tian Yang couldn’t help himself.","\"The Tian Family...?\" Sun Rouxi looked at him with raised eyebrows, seemingly suspicious of his intentions.","After a moment of silence, she responded, \"You’ll need to be more specific than that. Just what do you want to know about them?\"","\"If it’s not too much to ask... What kind of unique prowess do they possess?\"","\"What?\" Sun Rouxi narrowed her eyes. \"Unique prowess... as in the power of their bloodline? Why do you want to know about something like that?\"","\"I heard a certain rumor and just wanted to confirm something.\"","\"Is that so... Unfortunately, I cannot disclose such sensitive information, even if that person is you. In fact, I’ll likely face the death sentence if I reveal such information to an outsider. If you really want to know, you’ll have to visit the Tian Family and ask them yourself.\"","Tian Yang shook his head, \"It’s nothing more than blind curiosity.\"","\"Anyway, I’ll be returning to the palace soon. Want to meet the Giant Emperor now? You can speak with him yourself.\"","Sun Rouxi then said, \"Actually, I only intended to visit this place briefly. Someone is waiting for my return, so I’ll visit the palace afterward.\"","\"Oh? Did you finally get yourself a partner after so long?\" Tian Yang remarked with a smile.","She immediately frowned.","\"What nonsense are you talking about? I came here with my friend, who you know as Elder Jing.\"","\"Hm? Elder Jing? She also left the sect?\"","\"Yes, and she has been staying at the Sun Family with me.\"","\"You’re practically sisters now.\"","\"I guess so.\"","\"Then visit the palace whenever you’re ready. I’ll see you then.\"","Tian Yang didn’t linger and left the next moment, leaving Sun Rouxi behind.","She didn’t immediately leave and stayed behind to watch his figure quickly disappear into the horizon.","\"So you had been hiding here for the last several thousand years. No wonder I couldn’t find you...\" she mumbled in a low voice.","Some time later, she also left, returning to where Elder Jing was waiting.","\"Hm? Back so soon already?\" Elder Jing remarked when Sun Rouxi returned.","\"Yes...\"","Elder Jing raised an eyebrow when she saw the look on Sun Rouxi’s face.","\"Did something happen? The last time you showed such a smile was when you learned that Disciple was alive.\"","Sun Rouxi chuckled, \"You won’t believe who I met just now.\"","\"No way...\" Elder Jing stood up with a dumbfounded look on her face. \"Don’t tell me...\"","\"Yes, I met him.\"","\"Seriously...?\"","Sun Rouxi continued, \"The reason we couldn’t track him after the Immortal Clans’ downfall was because he’d been living quietly on this continent for the past several thousand years.\"","What she didn’t mention to Tian Yang was that she had been keeping tabs on him all this time—much like how he had been watching over Kulas while he was still trying to conquer the continent. She was aware of nearly every move he’d made, right up until the moment he vanished without a trace.","\"This has to be fate or something,\" said Elder Jing. \"However, this begs the question... why have you returned so soon? It’s been thousands of years since you last spoke with each other, right? Surely, there’s plenty to talk about.\"","\"Like what?\" Sun Rouxi asked with a puzzled face.","\"Like that...?\" Elder Jing rubbed her eyes and sighed. \"Isn’t it obvious? Ask him about his affairs. Like what happened to that Sword Empress who was always by his side. About their relationship, et cetera, et cetera!\"","Sun Rouxi frowned and said, \"Did you hit your head recently? Why would I ask him about his personal affairs? It’s none of my business.\"","\"Oh, please. You don’t need to pretend when you’re with me. If you weren’t interested in him, why did you constantly watch over him for hundreds of years?\"","\"I did no such thing! You’re making it sound like I was stalking him when I only had people keep me updated on his situation from time to time so I know he’s still alive!\"","\"Yeah, yeah. Whatever you say, Lady Sun.\" Elder Jing said in a teasing tone. \"So, what are you going to do now?\"","\"I’m going to have an audience with the Giant Emperor and set up a meeting for the others,\" she said.","\"The Giant Emperor? I thought you had no intention of involving yourself with the main group.\"","\"Tian Yang is friends with the Giant Emperor. In fact, he’s staying with him.\"","Elder Jing smiled and said, \"Ah, I see. You want an excuse to continue speaking with that disciple, huh?\"","Knowing it would only be a waste of her breath, Sun Rouxi didn’t respond to her remarks and instead asked, \"I only returned to let you know. Want to come with me?\"","\"And interrupt your time with him? No thanks. I’ll just wait for you here.\"","Sun Rouxi didn’t try to convince her and left for the palace shortly after.","Some time later, Sun Rouxi arrived at the palace and said to the gate guard, \"Can you let Tian Yang know that Sun Rouxi is here to see him?\"","\"Senior Tian...?\"","The guards were surprised by her request since nobody had ever looked for him. However, since she knew Tian Yang was at the palace, it was likely because he told her, so they didn’t question her further and notified Tian Yang.","\"Senior Tian, someone named Sun Rouxi is here to see you.\"","A guard knocked on his door and announced.","\"Sun Rouxi? A woman?\" Ren Xia turned to look at him, eyebrows raised.","\"She’s Elder Sun. The sect elder I talked about before.\" Tian Yang explained. \"I met her by chance when I went out just now.\"","\"Then why is she looking for you again so soon?\"","\"She’s mostly here for Kulas. Just as we speculated, she’s from the Three Pillars of Heaven.\"","\"I see...\"","Without another word, Ren Xia stopped cultivating and followed Tian Yang to the door.","\"I have been curious about this Elder Sun ever since I heard about her. To think I’d get to finally meet her...\" Ren Xia spoke with a mysterious smile on her face.","Tian Yang didn’t think much of it and went to fetch Sun Rouxi with Ren Xia.","Once outside, Tian Yang said to her.","\"I didn’t think you’d visit so soon. If I’d known, I would’ve just waited for you.\"","\"It’s fine,\" she said.","\"So you’re Elder Sun, huh?\" Ren Xia muttered.","Sun Rouxi shifted her gaze to Ren Xia.","\"You must be Ren Xia.\"","\"Oh?\" Ren Xia wore a look of surprise after being recognized. \"Have we met before?\"","\"No, but you’re quite famous. The Immortal Slayer and the Sword Empress... even infants knew your name a few thousand years ago.\"","\"That’s an overstatement,\" said Tian Yang.","\"Anyway, I haven’t had the chance to speak with the Giant Emperor yet, so I’ll go speak with him now. You can wait in my room in the meantime.\"","\"Your room...?\" Sun Rouxi murmured with a somewhat dazed face.","\"Don’t worry, it’s my room, too.\" Ren Xia said with a smile.","\"...\"","Some time later.","\"Then I’ll be back.\"","After leaving Sun Rouxi in his room with Ren Xia, Tian Yang went to find Kulas.","\"My husband speaks quite highly of you, Elder Sun.\" Ren Xia started a conversation not even a minute after Tian Yang left.","\"Your husband...?\" Sun Rouxi’s eyebrows raised slightly at her words.","\"Honestly, we’re more like Dao Companions than husband and wife since we never tied the knot.\"","\"Is that so...\"","\"...\"","Ren Xia glared at Sun Rouxi, scrutinizing every subtle reaction she showed.","’Her reactions are weak... Not what I had anticipated at all...’ Ren Xia thought to herself.","’No... she’s just good at hiding them...’ she smiled inwardly."]},{"number":2292,"title":"Chapter 2292: Sun Rouxi(2)","paragraphs":["\"You know, I have heard a lot about you from my husband,\" Ren Xia continued.","Sun Rouxi raised an eyebrow, her eyes flickering with intrigue. \"Oh? What does he say about me?\"","\"He said you were always nagging at him.\" Ren Xia chuckled. \"That you made his life in the Immortal Monastery more difficult than it had to be.\"","Sun Rouxi shook her head with a bittersweet smile and replied, \"If I didn’t nag at him, who would? He was always getting into trouble, acting recklessly and without a care for his life.\"","\"So he was like that as a disciple, too, huh? I thought it was something he picked up after he left the sect.\" Ren Xia remarked with a surprised look on her face.","\"It was a habit of his to belittle himself, calling himself talentless and whatnot. And because of his lack of talent, he would constantly push himself to the brink of death. I have lost count of how many times I had to save him.\"","Sun Rouxi glared at Ren Xia and asked, \"What do you like about that brat, anyway? Aren’t you a young lady of the Immortal Clans?\"","Ren Xia chuckled and replied, \"It’s precisely his recklessness that I love.\"","She narrowed her eyes slightly and continued, \"And you? What was it about him that made you keep an eye on him? Disciples getting into trouble happens all the time, yet you specifically decided to pay special attention to him.\"","Sun Rouxi lifted her head to stare at the empty ceiling. After a moment of silence, she muttered, \"I wonder.\"","\"What?\" Ren Xia raised an eyebrow.","Sun Rouxi continued with a profound smile, \"If you think about it, there’s really nothing truly special about Tian Yang as a disciple. If you saw him in a crowd, he was just like any other disciple, completely ordinary. While his recklessness is on another level, he wasn’t the only disciple desperate for improvement. I see them almost daily. However, there was just something about him that I couldn’t ignore, and I am still trying to figure out the cause even to this day.\"","\"That sounds like love at first sight,\" Ren Xia chuckled.","\"What?\" Sun Rouxi looked at her with wide eyes, almost as if she couldn’t believe her ears.","She then spoke, \"I may not understand why I was attracted to him, but I can say with certainty that it wasn’t such emotions. I just got this feeling that I couldn’t leave him alone.\"","\"I was only joking.\" Ren Xia shook her head with a smile.","\"If you don’t mind me asking... Why was someone like you working as a sect elder at the Immortal Monastery? You’re a member of the Three Pillars of Heaven, right? With your qualifications, you could even ask to be its sect leader, let alone a sect elder.\"","\"Sorry, but I cannot tell you the reason. However, I can tell you that nobody at the sect was aware of my true background, as that would’ve defeated my purpose for being there in the first place.\"","’So she was in a situation where she had to keep her background hidden, huh?’ Ren Xia thought to herself.","As someone from a privileged background, she could think of several reasons why Sun Rouxi had to conceal her identity.","While Ren Xia and Sun Rouxi continued their conversation, Tian Yang spoke with Kulas.","\"So the Three Pillars of Heaven have business with me, huh? Well, I had already anticipated something like this when I heard they would show up.\"","\"Do you mind speaking with one of them right now? She’s...\" Tian Yang explained the whole situation to Kulas.","\"What? Elder Sun?\" Kulas’ eyes widened with surprise at the news. \"To think you’d meet her by chance... this is more than mere coincidence. It must be fate.\"","\"Alright, I’ll meet with her,\" he agreed.","Tian Yang returned to tell Sun Rouxi of Kulas’ approval and brought her to meet him.","Some time later...","\"It’s an honor to meet you, Giant Emperor.\" Sun Rouxi politely greeted him.","\"You can drop the formality.\" Kulas casually waved dismissively. \"You may not remember, but this is actually our second meeting.\"","\"Oh? Where and when did we last meet?\" Sun Rouxi asked.","\"Here, on this continent. Right before the opening of Han Zexian’s Tomb. Moments after you spoke with my dear friend.\"","\"Then you’re...\" Sun Rouxi immediately recalled Kulas’ words to her on that day.","Kulas silently nodded in confirmation.","\"You should’ve seen his face afterward.\" Kulas laughed out loud. \"It had nothing but guilt all over it.\"","Hearing such words, Sun Rouxi subconsciously shifted her gaze to Tian Yang, who was sighing as he rubbed his eyes.","\"Anyway, why did you want to meet with me?\"","\"The Three Pillars of Heaven has something they would like to discuss with you, and I wanted to see if we could schedule a meeting.\"","\"Schedule a meeting? You’re more reserved than I expected. I was anticipating the Three Pillars of Heaven to simply walk in here and demand an audience like they own the place.\" Kulas remarked with a smile.","\"To be honest, they’ll likely do that if you refuse.\"","Kulas then said, \"Since you’re already here, why don’t you tell me what the Three Pillars of Heaven want from me?\"","Sun Rouxi shook her head and explained, \"I may have come here with them, but I am not part of the discussion, so I don’t know what business they have with you.\"","\"Is that so? Then, do you mind me asking what sort of position you stand within the Three Pillars of Heaven?\"","\"My position, huh? I am just one of many in the main family. It’s nothing impressive.\"","\"...\"","Kulas could sense that Sun Rouxi wasn’t giving the full details, but decided to ignore it because of her relationship with Tian Yang.","\"Very well. If the Three Pillars of Heaven want to speak with me, we can do so after the Tournament of Strength. It’s not like I can turn away the most powerful family in the world, anyway.\"","\"Thank you.\"","\"Since you’re someone close to my brother, I’ll let you linger at the palace as well. Just don’t wander around alone.\"","\"I understand.\"","After her audience with Kulas, Sun Rouxi stayed a little longer to chat with Tian Yang.","\"Hey, why don’t we have a little spar?\" Sun Rouxi suddenly said.","\"Out of nowhere?\" Tian Yang looked at her with a weird expression.","\"I want to see how much you’ve grown.\"","Tian Yang smiled and said, \"Don’t complain if you lose.\"","\"Lose? To you? When have I ever lost to you? You may be a True Immortal now, but that won’t change anything.\"","\"If you say so.\"","Tian Yang brought her to the training ground inside Kulas’ world.","\"This is... a personal world?\" Sun Rouxi seemed to be surprised by its existence.","\"You look surprised. Don’t you have plenty of these at the Holy Continent?\"","\"What? Who told you that?\" Sun Rouxi looked at him with a puzzled face.","\"Nobody. It was just my own speculation.\"","\"What a wild speculation. Do you think it’s easy to create personal worlds? It requires a tremendous amount of resources and time. Even the Three Pillars of Heaven cannot make them willy-nilly. While we do have a few, they’re all used as secret vaults, not as a training ground like this...\"","\"Anyway, for this spar, I won’t use my family’s techniques to make things fair,\" she then said.","However, Tian Yang shook his head and said, \"Aren’t you underestimating me a little too much? You’re already going to lose, so why cripple yourself even more?\"","\"Looks like you’ve gotten quite arrogant since the last time I saw you,\" she said. \"How about this? If you can force me to use my family’s martial techniques, I will owe you a favor.\"","\"You know that I defeated the Immortal Clans, right?\" Tian Yang said.","\"Of course.\"","\"Yet you’re still underestimating me... You must be powerful enough to crush the Immortal Clans effortlessly, then.\"","Sun Rouxi quickly responded with a confident smile, \"If I really wanted to? I could’ve dealt with them in a few days.\"","\"Now I really cannot wait to fight you.\" Tian Yang said as he beckoned her. \"I’m ready whenever you are.\"","\"As your senior, I’ll let you make the first move,\" she said.","\"Then I won’t be humble!\" Tian Yang immediately made his move without hesitation, striking her with a lightning-quick sword technique.","In response, Sun Rouxi used a movement technique, easily avoiding his sword technique.","Tian Yang immediately followed up with another sword technique, one that Sun Rouxi was very familiar with.","\"The Immortal Monastery’s sword techniques?\"","\"There’s more where that came from!\" Tian Yang laughed as he continued using the Immortal Monastery’s martial techniques.","\"You kept training their techniques even after you left? Why?\" she eventually asked. \"I’m sure you have acquired many powerful and high-ranking techniques.\"","\"I didn’t practice them out of nostalgia or anything,\" he said with a smile. \"For some reason, using them puts me at ease, so I do so from time to time—to clear my mind or as a warm-up.\"","\"Seriously? This is the first time I’ve heard of such a thing.\"","\"What about your techniques? If they’re not from the Immortal Monastery or your family, where’d you learn such techniques?\" Tian Yang asked her.","\"There is something called the Heavenly Knowledge within the Three Pillars of Heaven. It contains countless nameless techniques created by the three families.\"","\"What? Isn’t that technically techniques from your family?\"","\"Technically, yes, but the ones I am using aren’t created by my family but the other two families, so it’s fine. Also, most of these techniques are either abandoned or unfinished, hence why they’re nameless,\" she explained."]},{"number":2293,"title":"Chapter 2293: Tournament of Strength Begins","paragraphs":["\"Heavenly Knowledge? Such a name for a place to throw away unfinished techniques. Why’d you even learn them? And are you sure it’s okay to tell me about such a place? Won’t you be punished?\" Tian Yang questioned.","Sun Rouxi shrugged, \"The Heavenly Knowledge is not a secretive place. Anyone within the Three Pillars of Heaven can access it. As for why I learned them... It’s a good way to practice.\"","\"Practice?\" Tian Yang asked, a puzzled expression on his face.","\"Trying to comprehend and complete the unfinished techniques—turning them into your own,\" she replied calmly.","Although Sun Rouxi made it sound like an ordinary thing, it was anything but. Completing another person’s unfinished technique required tremendous talent and experience, an achievement few cultivators could ever hope to accomplish.","\"There is not much to do at the Three Pillars of Heaven, so I spent most of my time cultivating and finishing techniques.\"","\"That’s how you spent the last few thousand years?\"","\"It’s a bit boring when compared to your little adventure, isn’t it? Anyway, enough chitchat. Let’s continue.\" Sun Rouxi went on the offensive this time.","Her movements were swift and graceful, like a dancer on a stage.","As their spar continued, Tian Yang noticed that he was starting to get pushed back by her.","’Even though I am not using any of my main techniques, to be pushing me back...’","Tian Yang was truly surprised that he wasn’t able to overwhelm Sun Rouxi despite his vast experience.","’Even though I should have more experience than her... how is she this powerful? This is what true talent looks like?’","He finally understood that Sun Rouxi hadn’t been looking down on him. However, that didn’t mean he would give up.","\"Hm? Looks like you’re finally starting to fight seriously,\" Sun Rouxi remarked as she noticed a shift in Tian Yang’s movements.","\"Yes, looks like I had been the one underestimating you this entire time.\" Tian Yang said. \"I’ll be fighting seriously now, so... try not to get hurt!\"","Tian Yang unleashed Limitless Sword Domain and started using other powerful martial techniques, instantly turning the tide.","\"...\"","’So this is the Immortal Slayer who caused the Immortal Clans’ downfall...’ Sun Rouxi smiled inwardly after experiencing the legend herself.","However, as much as she wanted to enjoy the moment, she knew that she could no longer take the spar lightly.","Thus, they started fighting seriously. While it wasn’t at the level where they were trying to kill each other, they were fighting with the intent of defeating the other, even if it was a little dangerous.","A few hours later.","\"You’re really something, Tian Yang. Not even the geniuses at the Three Pillars of Heaven could push me this far,\" Sun Rouxi remarked, her entire body soaked in sweat.","\"I could say the same... Not even Kulas could make me bleed this much...\" Tian Yang said, his body soaked in sweat and blood.","’I must admit...’ Sun Rouxi thought to herself. ’I won’t be able to defeat him at this rate. However, if I lose my family’s techniques... I might as well surrender.’","Meanwhile, Tian Yang pondered how he could force her to use the Sun Family’s techniques.","Then, after a few thousand more exchanges, Sun Rouxi suddenly said, \"Hah. I’m tired. I surrender.\"","\"What? Surrendering before you are forced to use your family’s technique? That’s cheating.\"","Sun Rouxi smiled and said, \"Since I admit defeat, even though I didn’t use my family’s techniques, I’ll owe you a favor.\"","\"Well, if you admit defeat...\"","Although he won, Tian Yang wasn’t happy. He knew that if Sun Rouxi started using her family’s technique, he would definitely have lost.","\"I still have a long way to go, huh?\" he muttered.","\"What?\" Sun Rouxi, who heard his mumble, uttered. \"You’re plenty strong enough already. What are you going to do with more power? Are you going to challenge the Three Pillars of Heaven next?\"","Tian Yang raised an eyebrow and replied, \"Challenge the Three Pillars of Heaven? I may be reckless, but I am not suicidal. Also, why would I challenge them in the first place? It’s not like we have any grudges.\"","\"I guess so...\"","Sun Rouxi fell silent, her gaze fixated on him.","\"If you have something you want to say, just say it.\" Tian Yang said, noticing her odd gaze.","\"Why... did you go after the Immortal Clans? Is it related to why your outburst on that day?\" she asked with some hesitancy in her voice.","This was something she had always wanted to figure out. The reason for his hatred toward the Immortal Clans, and why he’d said such things to her.","\"If you don’t want to tell me, that’s fine.\"","After a moment of silence, Tian Yang shook his head and said, \"No, you have the right to know after what happened.\"","\"It might take a while, so why don’t we do it somewhere more comfortable? I also want to wash up first.\"","\"Okay.\"","They left the training ground and returned to Tian Yang’s room.","After they both washed up, they sat down with some hot tea.","\"I will tell you everything from the start.\"","Tian Yang said, and he started telling Sun Rouxi about everything that had occurred since he left the Immortal Monastery.","From his meeting with the Huang Family to how they survived a mythical beast because of her life-saving treasure, and what happened on the Desolate Continent that led him to Han Zexian’s Tomb.","\"I see...\"","Ever since that incident, she had been trying to figure out the cause and what she had done wrong. Now, after thousands of years of doubt and confusion, Sun Rouxi finally learned the reason behind Tian Yang’s anger on that day.","\"If I were in your shoes, I would also be angry. However, I must correct you on something,\" she suddenly said.","\"What?\" Tian Yang looked at her with a puzzled face.","\"That life-saving treasure... even if you had known about it in advance, you wouldn’t have been able to save the whole family. After all, life-saving treasures are typically meant for a single person for maximum efficiency.\"","\"It was already a miracle that it managed to activate for two people. If you had tried to use it for the whole family, it would’ve likely picked its target at random, leaving behind the others or... not activate at all.\"","\"Seriously...?\" Tian Yang swallowed nervously at her words.","Sun Rouxi took out the life-saving treasure she’d retrieved from Tian Yang in the past and showed it to him.","\"If you don’t believe me, you can try it.\"","Tian Yang sighed, \"There’s no need. I believe you. It’s just that... now I feel even more guilty for trying to blame you.\"","\"No point dwelling in the past,\" she said before suddenly narrowing her eyes at him.","’But still... to think it was all because of another woman...’","Sun Rouxi felt a little annoyed for some reason.","Time continued to pass, and a few days later, the Tournament of Strength officially began.","The tournament was held on an artificial island near the Giant’s Continent. Kulas had originally planned to host it within the city, but with thousands—no, hundreds of thousands—of participants registering, he made a last-minute decision to move it elsewhere.","\"Wow, there are a lot more people here than I anticipated.\" Ren Xia remarked after seeing the crowd that had come to spectate.","\"This just shows how much influence the Giant’s Race now has,\" Kulas spoke with a satisfied smile.","He turned to look at Tian Yang and continued, \"This is your last chance to participate.\"","\"Yeah, no thanks.\"","Kulas sucked his teeth but didn’t pursue it any further.","\"Where’s Elder Sun?\" Ren Xia then asked. \"I thought she would be watching it with us.\"","\"She’s with her family,\" Tian Yang said.","\"Is that so...\"","Some time later, Kulas left his area and entered the stage.","Although he didn’t make a single sound when he appeared on the stage, the loud audience instantly halted their movements and stopped talking after sensing the immense pressure he exuded.","\"Welcome to the Giant’s Continent. I am Giant Emperor Kulas, the ruler of this land.\"","After a brief introduction, he started listing the rules. Then, without any delay, immediately started the tournament.","Given the sheer number of participants, the majority of whom were human, the tournament was bound to span days—perhaps even weeks—even if the battles continued without pause.","Once the tournament began, multiple matches unfolded simultaneously. Kulas watched from his private viewing area, with Tian Yang and Ren Xia seated beside him—a privilege not even his own children enjoyed. This arrangement drew the attention of many onlookers, especially those from powerful backgrounds.","\"Who are those two sitting beside the Giant Emperor? They look like humans. Could they be his children?\"","\"Doubtful. Look at that area below him. All of his children are there.\"","\"Look at the Giant Emperor. He’s laughing with them.\"","Unbeknownst to a few people, Tian Yang and Ren Xia were actually in disguise, so it was not surprising that nobody recognized them. However, even if they weren’t disguised, it was unlikely that anybody would recognize them. Still, they didn’t want any unnecessary attention, hence the disguise.","\"That’s Tian Yang? He looks so different from my memories.\" Elder Jing remarked after seeing Tian Yang again. \"I thought he would be more handsome.\"","Sun Rouxi smiled and said, \"He’s in a disguise.\"","\"Hm? Really? Why?\"","\"He did cause the Immortal Clans’ downfall...\"","\"If the Three Pillars of Heaven aren’t going after them, who else would?\"","\"Who knows? Better be safe than sorry.\""]},{"number":2294,"title":"Chapter 2294: After the Tournament","paragraphs":["Two weeks had passed since the Tournament of Strength began. Despite the overwhelming number of participants, it proceeded smoothly, without incident.","Although the vast majority of participants were human—and more than half were eliminated—less than one percent of those disqualified were giants.","This showcased the Giant Race’s prowess to the rest of the world, just as Kulas wanted.","\"The giant’s performance... is much better than I anticipated,\" Kulas suddenly remarked.","\"What? Aren’t they your people? How can you not know their capabilities?\" Ren Xia questioned.","\"How many giants do you think exist within the continent now?\" he replied. \"It may have been possible back when I first started this, but nowadays, it’s impossible to keep track of everyone. Hell, I am barely keeping track of my own children these days.\"","\"Sounds like it’s about time for you to stop making more, then,\" Ren Xia said.","\"Hahaha! You think I am making more children because I enjoy it? This is all to expand the Giant Race’s influence. Sooner or later, we’ll start expanding our influence outside the continent, and having more children will make that much easier.\"","Kulas spoke of things that he wouldn’t even tell his own children without any hesitation, almost as if he had no restrictions when it came to them.","Ren Xia frowned at his words and said, \"So... you’re going to use your children for your own political gain. As expected of someone from the Immortal Clans. Even if you claim to have left them behind, your nature remains the same.\"","Despite her harsh words, Kulas wasn’t offended. He knew she had always despised her family because of their arranged marriage—how they had used her for their own benefit. Of course, Ren Xia had never told him the truth. He had merely sensed that her seemingly unreasonable hostility came from somewhere, and as he grew older and more experienced, he came to understand it better.","\"Let’s not make any assumptions,\" he said. \"I am not saying that I intend to sell my children for connections. I am merely saying that without children, it won’t be possible to expand my family outside the continent.\"","\"...Sorry.\" Ren Xia offered a rare apology.","\"Oh? Look who it is.\" Kulas suddenly said, his eyes fixed on one of the platforms.","Tian Yang and Ren Xia followed his gaze to see a familiar figure. It was none other than Xie Mey.","Sure enough, Kulas’ children were also participating in the tournament. Of course, this wasn’t an order from Kulas. They simply wanted to show off their skills and hopefully make their father proud.","Xie Mey’s match ended almost in the blink of an eye. Using nothing but her innate prowess, she utterly defeated her opponent with a single punch.","Her opponent wasn’t an ordinary cultivator, either. He was clearly an experienced body refiner with his muscular physique and bulging muscles. Yet, all it took was a single punch from Xie Mey to cripple his arm.","\"Ah! I’m sorry, I didn’t know you were so fragile.\" Xie Mey apologized to the body refiner after destroying his entire arm. Though her words were sincere, they only angered the body refiner even further.","However, the body refiner calmed down after Xie Mey gave him a pill that helped him restore his arm.","\"Hahaha! That girl is always like this.\" Kulas laughed after witnessing the match.","\"I rarely see her in her giant form,\" said Tian Yang. \"Meanwhile, I’ve only ever seen your other children in their giant form.\"","\"She’s been like that for as long as I remember,\" said Kulas. \"If you want to know her reason... You should ask her later. Even I don’t know.\"","The tournament continued, and after another two weeks, the tournament reached its final stages.","Unsurprisingly, the last few participants remaining were all giants. As for Kulas’ children, they all forfeited toward the end, as they intended only to display their strength and not claim the champion.","In the end, the final victory of the Tournament of Strength was a giant by the name of Grandis.","As the victor, Grandis was granted the title of Champion and the opportunity to fight Kulas.","\"Not bad, young giant!\"","Kulas leaped from the spectator’s area to the platform.","\"As the champion, I will grant you a chance to fight me. Do you accept, warrior?\"","\"This humble warrior accepts, Your Majesty!\"","Grandis was given a pill to recover his energy before they fought.","To nobody’s surprise, the fight was one-sided, lasting barely five minutes.","After the fight—","\"It was a good fight, Warrior Grandis,\" Kulas said afterward. \"I have never accepted a disciple before, but you can be my first. What do you say?\"","\"I-It would be an honor!\" Grandis accepted without hesitation, which was a no-brainer.","Thus, Kulas acquired his first true disciple despite his thousands of years of experience.","Although the tournament ended, many visitors lingered on the continent and continued touring the area.","A week later, Sun Rouxi and the Three Pillars of Heaven arrived at the palace to fulfill their appointment.","While the six people from the Three Pillars of Heaven went to speak privately with Kulas, Sun Rouxi and Elder Jing went to meet Tian Yang and Ren Xia.","\"Do you remember me?\" Elder Jing asked Tian Yang.","Much like Sun Rouxi, she’d barely changed since the last time he saw her. Her cultivation had also reached Silver Immortal.","\"Of course, I do, Elder Jing. You were always beside Sister Sun.\"","\"Hm? Sister Sun?\" Elder Jing raised her eyebrows at the way he addressed Sun Rouxi.","\"Well, I can’t call her Elder Sun anymore, and she’s like an elder sister to me,\" he explained.","\"There’s no need to call me Elder Jing, either, as I am no longer a sect elder. Jing Ruye is my name, but you can just call me Sister Jing.\"","\"I understand, Senior Sister Jing.\"","As Tian Yang and Jing Ruye continued their conversation, reminiscing about their time in the Immortal Monastery for the next hour, the entire palace suddenly trembled, and an overwhelming pressure filled with killing intent swept through the halls, engulfing the place.","\"Wh-What’s going on?!\" Jing Ruye exclaimed as she jumped from her seat, startled by the immense killing intent.","\"This aura... it belongs to Kulas!\" Tian Yang frowned."]},{"number":2295,"title":"Chapter 2295: Kulas’ Mistake","paragraphs":["After sensing Kulas’ immense killing intent that engulfed the entire palace, Tian Yang rushed out of his room and ran toward the throne room, where Kulas was having his meeting with the Three Pillars of Heaven.","\"Hey! What’s going on?!\" Sun Rouxi asked as she and the others followed behind.","\"I would love to know, too!\" Tian Yang said.","\"Could it be one of his episodes?\" Ren Xia guessed out loud.","\"Episodes?\" Jing Ruye questioned.","\"Sorry, but it’s a little personal, so I cannot explain without Kulas’ permission,\" Tian Yang apologized.","\"Is that so...\"","They quickly arrived at the throne room, only to find that its doors were gone—not opened or shattered, but forcibly torn away. Two members of the Three Pillars of Heaven lay unconscious on the ground, their bodies strewn amid the wreckage.","Tian Yang didn’t hesitate and rushed inside. The remaining members stood before Kulas, each of them grievously injured. One, however, lay motionless on the floor, his entire head crushed beyond recognition.","\"What is the meaning of this, Giant Emperor?! Why did you suddenly attack us?!\"","\"Have you gone insane?! Not only did you attack us, but you even killed one of us! Are you trying to declare war against the Three Pillars of Heaven?!\"","The remaining members of the Three Pillars of Heaven shouted at Kulas while clutching their life-saving treasures.","However, Kulas merely stood there, as if lost in a daze.","\"Kulas!\"","Tian Yang rushed forward, positioning himself directly between Kulas and the others.","\"Kulas! What are you doing?!\"","This time, Kulas reacted. The emptiness in his gaze faded as reason swiftly returned.","\"Wh-What happened...?\" he asked in a puzzled tone.","\"That’s what we should be asking, Giant Emperor!\"","\"You suddenly attacked us while we were talking!\"","\"What!\" Kulas’ expression sank as he realized that he’d just lost his temper again.","\"How dare you act surprised like you weren’t aware?! Are you mocking us?!\"","\"Bastard, you killed one of our people unprovoked! I hope you’re prepared for the consequences!\"","\"W-Wait! I can explain!\" Kulas hastily said.","\"There’s nothing to explain!\"","\"We’ll be taking our leave now!\"","The members of the Three Pillars of Heaven were all between Bronze and Golden Immortal, so there was nothing they could do before Kulas, who was a True Immortal. Even if they wanted revenge, they would need to return to their family first.","However, just as they turned around and prepared to leave, Tian Yang stood in their way and stopped them.","\"Who the hell are you?!\"","Tian Yang then said, \"Although it won’t change what had happened, allow the Giant Emperor to explain himself first.\"","\"Are you telling us to stay here and wait for him to attack us again?! How ridiculous!\"","\"I will personally ensure that he won’t harm another hair on your bodies. I promise,\" he replied.","\"We won’t listen to the words of a nobody like you!\"","\"You can trust him,\" Sun Rouxi suddenly stepped forward and said.","\"Lady Sun...? What is your relationship with this man?\"","\"We’re acquaintances.\"","\"...\"","\"We’ll listen to your excuse, but we will leave immediately afterward.\" One of them eventually said.","Now that he had a chance to clear up the confusion, Kulas explained his condition to them. However, it didn’t lessen the victims’ anger. If anything, it only made them angrier.","\"So you decided to meet with us while knowing about your own instability?! That’s reckless and irresponsible of you, Giant Emperor!\"","\"It hadn’t happened in over fifty years, so I thought it was fine...\" Kulas sighed. \"I apologize for my mistake, and I am willing to compensate for your losses.\"","\"How dare you even speak of compensation?! You killed one of our people! There’s nothing you can do to compensate for that!\"","Kulas had no response, so he remained silent, his expression full of guilt.","Soon, Kulas’ family and guards arrived at the scene, as they also noticed the commotion.","No longer feeling safe, the members of the Three Pillars of Heaven dared not linger any longer and prepared to leave.","\"Lady Sun, we’re leaving! We must report this to the rest of the family as soon as possible!\"","Sun Rouxi wanted to stay a little longer to talk to Tian Yang more about the situation, but given the circumstances, she had no choice but to return to the Holy Continent.","Once they all left, Kulas explained the situation to his family.","\"I fucked up,\" he admitted with a heavy sigh. \"I lost my temper during our conversation, and by the time I realized, I had attacked them, even killing one of them.\"","\"This... what will happen now?\" One of his wives asked.","\"Will it lead to war?\" Another asked.","\"Given our current standing, it’s unlikely that war will break out. However, it’s not impossible,\" Kulas said after pondering for a moment.","Now that the Giant Continent had become a true powerhouse, a war with the Three Pillars of Heaven would undoubtedly affect the entire world and unleash unprecedented devastation. It was not something that could be taken lightly.","\"There’s nothing we can do but wait for their response. Until then, I am going to enter seclusion,\" Kulas suddenly declared. \"I must deal with this instability of mine once and for all, no matter what it takes.\"","\"Unless the Three Pillars of Heaven act, do not disturb me.\"","After giving instructions to his family, Kulas turned to look at Tian Yang and said, \"I’m sorry. Because of my mistake, I have offended the Three Pillars of Heaven. You should leave the Giant Continent for the time being—at least until things cool down.\"","\"Are you really going to push us away after what happened?\" Tian Yang frowned.","\"Yes, I am. Unless you know how to fix my condition, there’s nothing you can do for me. I know you’re angry and disappointed, but I would rather you feel that way for the rest of your life than endanger you.\"","\"...\"","As much as he hated to admit it, Kulas was right. There was nothing they could do, especially when they didn’t even know what was causing his mood swings."]},{"number":2296,"title":"Chapter 2296: Three Pillars of Heaven’s Demands","paragraphs":["Tian Yang sighed and said, \"Fine, I can leave the continent if you want. However, you must give me some of your blood. I’ll look for a doctor and see if we can learn more about your situation outside.\"","\"I’ll leave it to you.\"","Without the slightest hesitation, Kulas handed Tian Yang a large vial of his freshly drawn blood, stunning his own family into silence. The amount he gave was greater than all the blood he had bestowed upon them collectively.","Although Tian Yang had stayed in the palace for a long time, most of Kulas’s children had never realized how close the two truly were, for they rarely spoke to one another. Only after witnessing this did they begin to grasp the depth of their relationship.","A few of them felt the urge to voice their doubts, questioning whether Tian Yang would truly use such priceless blood to help their father—or sell it for his own gain. However, they also sensed that doing so might result in enraging their father, so they held their tongues.","After putting away Kulas’ blood, Tian Yang said to him, \"Promise me one thing. That you’ll contact me if anything happens with the Three Pillars of Heaven, or your condition gets worse.\"","\"I promise.\" Kulas nodded with a smile.","Tian Yang and Ren Xia didn’t linger at the palace and left shortly after. Rather than waiting for a ship to return home, they decided to just fly back.","\"I can’t believe that idiot actually killed someone from the Three Pillars of Heaven,\" Ren Xia sighed out loud as they traveled.","\"It’s odd. He’s been fine for fifty years, but the moment he meets with people from the Three Pillars of Heaven, his mood swings return. Is it really a coincidence?\" Tian Yang questioned out loud.","\"Are you suggesting that the Three Pillars of Heaven have something to do with his mood swings? That’s impossible, given that it has been happening to him long before they even met.\"","\"I guess... but I still cannot help but feel something off about the whole situation. Though I might just be overthinking it.\"","\"Putting that aside, what is our plan now?\" Ren Xia then asked.","\"I’m going to look for the Heavenly Doctor and see if he could figure out anything about Kulas’ condition through his blood,\" he said.","\"The Heavenly Doctor, huh? I heard he loves to wander the Divine Heavens and never stays in the same place for longer than a month. Finding him will be a pain in the ass.\"","\"Even if he moves around every day, he’s our only hope right now.\"","Thus, Tian Yang and Ren Xia started their next journey. They wandered the Divine Heaven in search of the Heavenly Doctor, who was known to be able to cure any disease.","Meanwhile, Sun Rouxi and the others returned to the Holy Continent, where they revealed the situation to the rest of the family.","Unsurprisingly, the Three Pillars of Heaven were enraged by the news, especially the Sun Family, as the only individual who died belonged to their family.","The higher-ups from the three families gathered for a meeting to discuss how they should respond to Kulas’ actions.","\"Uncontrollable mood swings? What a convenient excuse. I don’t believe it for one second,\" said one of the elders from the Ji Family.","\"I also don’t believe it,\" agreed an elder from the Tian Family.","\"So, how should we deal with this situation? Do we go to war with them?\"","\"Let’s slow down a little. I don’t think it would be wise to declare war so quickly,\" said the Patriarch of the Tian Family.","The Patriarch of the Ji Family then spoke, \"I also don’t recommend going to war with them. While their numbers are small, they make up for it with their overwhelming prowess. It wouldn’t be an exaggeration to say that in the entire Divine Heaven, they’re only below our Three Pillars of Heaven in terms of prowess.\"","\"Are you saying that we should just act like the Giant Emperor didn’t kill one of my people? The person he killed was one of our elders, no less!\" The Patriarch of the Sun Family angrily shouted, even slamming the table with a clenched fist.","\"We didn’t say that. The Giant Emperor will definitely pay for attacking us unprovoked, but we must navigate this wisely,\" said the Patriarch of the Tian Family.","\"And how the hell is sitting around a smart choice?! As you said, the Giant Race is already near our level! And it only took them a few thousand years to reach such a level! It will only be a matter of time before they catch up to us! Do you really want to wait until then to punish them?! What’s to say they won’t attack us?!\"","The Patriarch of the Tian Family let out a heavy sigh, shaking his head. \"Even if you say that, do you understand the consequences of going to war with the Giant Race? It would not only impact our families but also the entire world. If powers of our stature were to collide...\"","He paused for a second.","\"The devastation would be beyond imagining.\"","\"We just need to overwhelm them before they can do anything! Don’t tell me you’re scared of them?! We’re the Three Pillars of Heaven! The Heavens have chosen us to lead this world! How can we be scared of a few giants?!\"","Over the next several months, the Three Pillars of Heaven would argue back and forth about how they should respond to the situation.","In the end, the Three Pillars of Heaven made several demands of Kulas. If he were to fulfill these demands, they would no longer pursue the issue.","However, if he were to refuse, then the Three Pillars of Heaven had no choice but to declare war against them.","When Kulas heard their demands, he immediately erupted with rage.","\"What utter bullshit! You want me to execute ten of my own children and one of my wives because I killed one of yours?! As if I could accept these demands!\""]},{"number":2297,"title":"Chapter 2297: War With the Three Pillars of Heaven","paragraphs":["\"You sons of bitches! While I admit that I was in the wrong for killing one of your people, how could you give such outrageous demands?! Are you even human?!\" Kulas exploded with anger after receiving the Three Pillars of Heaven’s demands through one of their messengers.","The messenger continued coldly, \"You didn’t kill some insignificant nobody. You killed one of the Sun Family’s elders. We’re already being generous with our demand—because not even the lives of a hundred of your children could compensate for the loss of one of our elders.\"","Kulas trembled with anger, exuding such immense killing intent that it forced the messenger to his knees.","\"W-Was the elder not enough to satisfy you?! Are you going to kill me, too?!\" The messenger exclaimed with a terrified yet provocative expression on his face, almost as if he was daring Kulas to kill him.","\"...\"","Kulas retracted his killing intent and fell silent.","After a moment of silence, he spoke in a calm voice, \"If the Three Pillars of Heaven are so desperate for war, you need only say the word. There’s no need to make unreasonable demands or deliberately provoke me.\"","\"W-What?\" The messenger’s eyes widened in disbelief at Kulas’s words.","’He’s not actually going to go to war with the Three Pillars of Heaven over a measly few lives, right?’ he wondered inwardly.","Despite the apparent severity of the demand, the messenger truly believed it was reasonable. In his mind, Kulas would rather sacrifice a few of his own children than provoke a war with the most powerful force in the world.","In his view, defying the Three Pillars of Heaven was sheer stupidity. Were he in Kulas’s position, he would not hesitate to sacrifice his entire family to avoid offending them.","\"You heard me,\" Kulas calmly said. \"If the Three Pillars of Heaven desire war, I’ll give it to them.\"","\"W-Wait! You should reconsider this!\" the messenger shouted. \"I admit the Giant Race is formidable, but it’s incomparably weaker than the Three Pillars of Heaven! You’ll lose far more than just a few lives if this becomes a war! You have plenty of children anyway—what’s the loss of a few?!\"","\"What’s the loss of a few, you say...?\" Kulas muttered.","Then he suddenly burst into laughter. \"Hahaha! I never realized the Three Pillars of Heaven valued life so little! Did you bastards sell your souls to the devil or something?\"","In truth, the Three Pillars of Heaven were fully aware of how unreasonable their demands were. However, they deliberately made such demands to put Kulas and the Giant Race in their place.","Simply put, they sought to assert their dominance over Kulas and the growing Giant Race, hoping to keep them firmly in check even as they continued to grow stronger.","After all, the Giant Race was spreading its influence and growing powerful at a terrifying pace—so much so that even the Three Pillars of Heaven, who considered themselves unrivaled, were beginning to feel the pressure.","Kulas then spoke in a cold voice, \"I will not accept your demands. Go back and relay my message to the Three Pillars of Heaven.\"","\"You... Are you sure you want to go this route?\"","Kulas’s eyes narrowed as he snarled, \"If you don’t get the fuck out of my face this instant, I’ll have your corpse deliver my message instead!\"","\"!!!\"","The messenger didn’t dare to linger and immediately ran out of the room, tripping in the process.","After returning to the Holy Continent, the messenger relayed Kulas’s response to the Patriarchs and Elders.","\"That giant bastard was unbelievably rude and showed no respect for the name of the Three Pillars of Heaven!\"","While he conveyed Kulas’s message, the messenger did not hesitate to twist it, deliberately making it sound far worse than it truly was.","\"To dare defy us so openly... These bastards have truly grown arrogant after gaining power too quickly,\" said the Patriarch of the Sun Family. \"We must show them the consequences of their arrogance! Since they seem so eager to go to war, let’s go to war!\"","Since Kulas denied their demands, war was inevitable.","The Patriarch of the Tian Family sighed. \"You make it sound as though this would be easy. Quite frankly, they hold a significant advantage due to their location.\"","The Giant Race was largely confined to the Giant Continent—an island surrounded by a vast ocean teeming with sea beasts—granting them an immense geographic advantage. Even if war were to be declared, it would primarily be the Three Pillars of Heaven pressing for battle. As long as the Giant Race remained on the defensive, they would be forced to launch the attack themselves, placing them at a clear disadvantage.","This meant that despite being weaker than the Three Pillars of Heaven, the Giant Race would not be dominated so easily. As long as they played their cards properly, they could easily prolong the war until they were ready to fight back.","The Three Pillars of Heaven were aware of this, hence why they didn’t immediately declare war on the Giant Race.","Time passed. Although many years had gone by since Kulas rejected their demands, the Three Pillars of Heaven had yet to openly declare war. In truth, however, the war had already begun.","The Three Pillars of Heaven had quietly dispatched assassins and hired mercenaries to strike at the Giant Race, operating in ways that could not be traced back to them. As a result, aside from Kulas and the Giant Race themselves, no one else was aware that a shadow war had erupted between the two most powerful backgrounds in the world.","As a result of the war, all giants who had left the continent were recalled, and the Giant Race once again entered seclusion. However, unlike in the past, they did not seal off the continent, continuing instead to allow outsiders to enter their domain.","Meanwhile, after many years of searching, Tian Yang and Ren Xia finally found the Heavenly Doctor. Though they were unaware that war had already begun, they could sense that something had changed."]},{"number":2298,"title":"Chapter 2298: War With the Three Pillars of Heaven(2)","paragraphs":["\"I heard rumors that all the giants who were outside the Giant Continent have returned, and that none of them have left in quite some time,\" Ren Xia said to Tian Yang as they waited for the Heavenly Doctor to finish his business.","\"Maybe they’re just being cautious,\" Tian Yang replied. \"Kulas did kill someone from the Three Pillars of Heaven, after all. They might be worried about retaliation.\"","\"Even if war breaks out, they should be fine as long as they remain within their territory. The Giant’s Continent is akin to a fortress, one that is surrounded by water.\"","Some time later, the Heavenly Doctor returned.","\"I have analyzed the blood you gave me,\" he said as he returned Kulas’ leftover blood. \"I was unable to find anything out of the ordinary. He’s as healthy as one could be.\"","Tian Yang wasn’t surprised to learn that Kulas wasn’t ill, but it did nothing to explain his mood swings.","\"My friend has been experiencing intense mood swings lately,\" Tian Yang said. \"He claims they occur at random and that he doesn’t realize what’s happening until afterward. When it does happen, he gets angry and violent.\"","The Heavenly Doctor spoke, \"When it comes to this kind of instability, a few causes come to mind. I can rule out poison and illness, as I have already confirmed they are not the source. That leaves three possibilities: a curse, unresolved heart demons, or something he was born with.\"","Tian Yang said, \"Since it only started recently, it’s unlikely he was born with it. He did suffer a severe and traumatic experience long ago, one that caused him to lose his mind for a period. Still, he’s confident it isn’t a heart demon. That leaves a curse—but do curses like that really exist?\"","\"Of course. There are many powerful curses out there, and one that causes one to lose their mind is not common, but also not as rare as you might think.\"","\"How can I confirm that it’s a curse? And if it is confirmed to be one, how do I get rid of it?\"","\"There are treasures out there that can detect curses. If it is a curse, there are plenty of methods of getting rid of it. Here are a few.\"","The Heavenly Doctor wrote down the names of several treasures and pills that would help him.","\"The ones at the bottom are the most effective but also the most expensive. You might also have trouble finding them,\" he said afterward.","\"Thank you.\"","After paying the Heavenly Doctor his service fee, Tian Yang and Ren Xia left to find the treasures he had listed for them. Naturally, they didn’t even take a moment to consider the cheaper options and immediately went for the most expensive.","As Tian Yang and Ren Xia continued their journey, the Three Pillars of Heaven and the Giant Race continued their silent war in the background.","Although the Three Pillars of Heaven were the more active and aggressive side, the Giant Race did not remain passive targets. Able to shrink their bodies to human size, they infiltrated the Holy Continent and launched their own strikes against the Three Pillars of Heaven.","However, due to the immense distance between them, such attacks occurred only once every few decades. The Holy Continent lay on the opposite side of the world, and even with their vast wealth and near-limitless resources, preparing a single strike demanded tremendous time and effort.","Of course, the Giant Race faced the same issues.","Yet, it did not deter the Three Pillars of Heaven from continuing the war. After all, they had all the time and resources in the world.","Ten years... fifty years... a hundred years later.","Tian Yang and Ren Xia finally acquired the treasure needed to detect curses and cure them after a hundred years of searching.","Neither of them had anticipated that it would take this long, even though the Heavenly Doctor warned them.","After gathering the treasures, Tian Yang and Ren Xia immediately returned to the Giant’s Continent to meet with Kulas.","When they returned to the Giant’s Continent, they immediately sensed a heavy atmosphere in every city—one that had not been present before. However, most visitors seemed completely unaware of it.","While the outsiders went about their days as usual, every giant seemed to be on alert, as though they were expecting an attack at any moment.","When they arrived at the palace, they were stopped by the guards there—newly appointed guards who weren’t aware of their identity.","\"Sorry, but the Giant Emperor is not accepting any visitors at this moment.\"","Just as Tian Yang was about to introduce himself, he noticed a familiar figure approaching them from the palace.","\"Let them inside. They’re my father’s companions.\"","It was none other than Xie Mey, who had noticed their presence even before they arrived.","With Xie Mey vouching for them, the guards no longer had a reason to stop them.","Tian Yang and Ren Xia followed Xie Mey inside the palace.","\"What’s the situation like right now?\" Tian Yang asked.","\"Not good,\" Xie Mey sighed. \"You’ll understand once you see my father.\"","Xie Mey brought them directly to Kulas’ room—his private quarters rather than the throne room.","She knocked on the door and said, \"Father, Senior Tian, and Senior Ren have returned.\"","However, there was no response from Kulas.","Xie Mey turned to Tian Yang and said in a solemn tone, \"Please try not to be too surprised when you see my father’s condition.\"","After saying that, she pushed the door to Kulas’ room open.","However, even before they stepped inside, Tian Yang knew something was wrong from the ominous presence within.","With a deep frown on his face, he stepped inside the room with Ren Xia and Xie Mey.","\"What in heaven’s name...?\" Tian Yang’s eyes widened in disbelief when he saw Kulas lying on the bed, looking gravely ill.","Kulas didn’t merely look sick. He looked as though he were on his deathbed."]},{"number":2299,"title":"Chapter 2299: War With the Three Pillars of Heaven(3)","paragraphs":["\"W-What the hell is wrong with Kulas? What happened to him in the time we were gone?\" Tian Yang questioned in a dumbfounded voice as he approached the bed, a look of disbelief on his face.","They’d been gone for only a little over a hundred years, yet Kulas looked like he’d aged millions of years. Tian Yang couldn’t comprehend it.","\"It started shortly after you left,\" Xie Mey explained in a defeated voice. \"It was as sudden and random as his mood swings. At first, it started out as a cold. Then, it gradually worsened until he got a fever. Nowadays, he spends most of his time asleep, only waking up once a year for a few hours. Unfortunately, we don’t know the cause even at this very moment.\"","\"A fever? Cultivators cannot get fevers, much less a cold. And he’s no ordinary cultivator but an Immortal...\" Ren Xia remarked with a confused voice after hearing the details.","\"This is outrageous,\" Tian Yang suddenly said with clenched fists. \"How is it that every time we leave this place, something drastic happens? It’s as if the heavens are purposefully messing with me.\"","He turned to look at Xie Mey and continued, \"We spoke with the Heavenly Doctor, and he said that Kulas’ mood swings might be caused by a curse. And for the last hundred years, we have looked for treasures that could get rid of curses.\"","\"A curse, you say?\"","Tian Yang nodded and retrieved several treasures from his spatial ring. \"Although we can’t say for certain that it’s a curse, it’s the best guess we have now. I am going to examine him now.\"","Without hesitation, Tian Yang immediately used the treasures he had acquired over the past hundred years on Kulas.","As weird as it may sound, Tian Yang found himself silently hoping that Kulas was cursed. At the very least, they would then know what was wrong with him. If it wasn’t a curse, they would be back at square one.","However, even after using multiple treasures, none of them reacted, meaning they were unable to detect any curses affecting Kulas.","\"How is this possible...?\" Tian Yang muttered in a defeated voice.","\"If it isn’t poison, a curse, nor a heart demon, what could it possibly be? I doubt mental instability would put him in such a state, either.\" Ren Xia pondered out loud.","\"Uhhh... I should’ve said this sooner, but despite his appearances, my father is actually very healthy.\" Xie Mey suddenly said. \"We had many doctors look at him. And all of them said the same thing. His internal organs are healthy, and his Dantian and spiritual veins are all normal.\"","Tian Yang almost couldn’t believe his ears. How could Kulas be considered healthy while looking like a dried up corpse?","\"This situation is getting weirder by the moment,\" Ren Xia shook her head.","\"Hm?\"","Suddenly, she noticed some movements from the bed.","The next moment, a hoarse voice resounded, \"Brother... Is that you...?\"","\"Kulas?!\"","Tian Yang immediately responded.","\"What the...?\" Xie Mey mumbled with a dumbfounded look on her face.","Kulas had already woken up a week prior to their return, so she was surprised to see him wake up again in such a short time.","\"Ah... I really didn’t... want you to... see me in such a... state...\" Kulas spoke in a weak voice.","\"Rather than wasting your breath on such nonsensical words, tell me if you have any idea what happened to you,\" said Tian Yang.","Despite asking such a question, Tian Yang already knew how Kulas would respond to it.","\"I... don’t know...\" Kulas said. \"But it started... after we went to war... with the... Three Pillars of Heaven...\"","\"War with the Three Pillars of Heaven?\" Tian Yang frowned.","\"You guys are at war with them? Since when?\"","\"Shortly after you left, the Three Pillars of Heaven sent their demands to compensate for the incident. However, their demands were outrageous.\" Xie Mey spoke in her father’s stead, and she proceeded to explain the whole situation to them.","\"What a ridiculous demand.\" Ren Xia shook her head after listening to the details. \"They just want an excuse to go to war. I guess they’ve been bored out of their mind after being at the top and unmatched for too long.\"","Tian Yang remained silent for a long moment before speaking, \"What are the chances of the Three Pillars of Heaven being behind Kulas’ phenomenon?\"","\"Quite frankly, it’s not high,\" Ren Xia replied. \"However, it’s not low, either.\"","\"But how would they have done it?\" Xie Mey asked.","\"Unfortunately, there’s no way we will know unless they reveal it to us. Kulas has met with many people over the years. They could’ve pulled something at any time. This would explain why Kulas, who seemed perfectly healthy, suddenly started to have mood swings,\" said Tian Yang.","\"Perhaps they have always wanted to get rid of the Giant Race for whatever reason,\" Ren Xia shrugged. \"If the Three Pillars of Heaven are the pioneers of cultivation, then Kulas would be the creator of the Giant Race. If I had to guess, they don’t want any competition.\"","She continued, \"They have revealed themselves to be ruthless and unreasonable with their demand, after all.\"","Tian Yang clenched his teeth, anger burning within him. He could never understand why those wielding immense power so often used it to trample the weak. First the Immortal Clans, and now the Three Pillars of Heaven.","\"So, what now?\" Ren Xia asked.","\"If the Three Pillars of Heaven are truly involved, I am going to try to figure out what they did to Kulas and find a way to cure it,\" he spoke with a resolute expression.","\"How are you going to do that?\" Xie Mey asked with a puzzled face.","\"By going to the Holy Continent. I know someone from there, and she said that I could visit with her permission.\"","\"No... it’s too... dangerous...\" Kulas rejected the idea.","Tian Yang sighed, \"There’s no other way.\""]},{"number":2300,"title":"Chapter 2300: An Absurd Theory","paragraphs":["\"I know you are... doing this for me... but... it’s too dangerous.\" Kulas reiterated.","\"Dear, I have to agree with Kulas,\" Ren Xia said with a worried frown on her pretty face. \"Visiting the Holy Continent because you’re curious about them and going there to investigate them are entirely different matters. What if you’re caught? Even you won’t be able to escape them.\"","\"Then what should I do? Are you telling me to do nothing but watch my sworn brother and friend slowly die, even though there’s a chance I could prevent that?\"","Ren Xia sighed, \"I won’t stop you if you really want to go to the Holy Continent. Knowing you, you’ll go regardless of what I say, anyway. However, at least think it over some more.\"","\"Even though my father’s life is at stake, I also agree with Senior Ren. You should wait a little longer before you rush into the Holy Continent,\" Xie Mey said.","\"How long am I supposed to wait before I act? Looking at his state, he might not even have a few years.\" Tian Yang rubbed his eyes in a stressful manner.","\"You are... underestimating me... too much...\" Kulas said.","Tian Yang looked at him and responded, \"I think I am already being generous with my estimate. Look at you. You can’t even speak a full sentence without taking deep breaths.\"","\"But the doctors said that besides his appearance, everything else is healthy... Even Mother Chao said so.\" Xie Mei said. \"If it had only been one doctor who said so, I wouldn’t have believed it. However, many of them said the same thing. Moreover, my father has survived in this state for over a hundred years now.\"","\"...\"","Tian Yang fell silent, as he was unable to refute her words.","Eventually, he sighed out loud, \"Fine, I will wait a little before I head to the Holy Continent.\"","\"Thank you...\" Kulas said.","Tian Yang and the others left Kulas alone to rest shortly after.","\"I guess we’ll be staying here again for some time,\" he said to Xie Mey.","She smiled and said, \"We haven’t touched your room, and you can stay here whenever and for as long as you want.\"","Over the next several days would wander around the palace to look for any clues, hoping the Three Pillars of Heaven had left behind some evidence of foul play. Unfortunately, he found nothing.","However, a few months later, just as Tian Yang started planning his journey to the Holy Continent, something unbelievable happened.","Kulas, who had been bedridden for a hundred years, made a sudden and full recovery.","\"I don’t know what happened, but it seems I have recovered now, so you no longer have any reason to visit the Holy Continent,\" Kulas said as he stood before Tian Yang, looking as healthy as before.","\"What the...?\" Tian Yang couldn’t believe it. \"You... You aren’t pretending to have recovered just to prevent me from heading to the Holy Continent, right?\"","Kulas raised his arm into the air and swore with a serious face, \"I swear on my soul that I am not pretending.\"","\"How? This doesn’t make any sense!\"","\"This may sound crazy, but I have been feeling better ever since you returned to the palace. Not only that, but previously, I started having mood swings after you left, but the moment you returned, it stopped for fifty years.\"","Tian Yang frowned and said, \"Are you implying that I am the cure to your issues somehow?\"","\"It sounds ridiculous, I know. However, it can’t be a mere coincidence. How about this? Let’s test out my theory.\"","Tian Yang rubbed his eyes and sighed, \"So what? Are you telling me to leave the palace to see if your sickness will return?\"","Kulas nodded with a serious expression.","\"You crazy son of a bitch...\" Tian Yang was speechless.","Yet, he didn’t refuse.","After a moment of silence, he asked, \"How long do you want me to be away?\"","\"Until my condition worsens,\" Kulas quickly replied.","\"Fine. I’ll play along with your absurd theory.\"","Some time later, Tian Yang explained the situation to Ren Xia.","\"That is the most absurd thing I have ever heard!\"","To nobody’s surprise, she was shocked by it.","\"How in heaven’s name did he even come up with this?\"","Despite finding the idea dumb, Ren Xia didn’t reject the idea.","\"Let’s return to our secret home then,\" she said, as she had been wanting to return for some time now, and this was the perfect opportunity.","Before they left, Kulas handed them a treasure.","\"What’s this?\"","\"It’s a communication device. It will allow us to speak with each other even through vast distances.\"","\"Alright. Then contact me the moment you start feeling sick again.\"","\"I will.\"","Tian Yang and Ren Xia left the palace the same day.","However, not even a few days later, they were contacted by Xie Mey.","\"Please return! My father has fallen sick again!\"","\"Seriously? We aren’t even halfway to our home.\" Ren Xia complained as they turned around and started making their way back to the palace.","Upon returning to the palace, Tian Yang stayed in the palace to see if Kulas would recover again.","Sure enough, a month later, Kulas recovered from his mysterious illness.","\"???\"","Tian Yang was shocked by the results, but he still wasn’t entirely convinced.","\"Let’s do it again. This time, stay outside for at least a decade, and don’t come back even if I am sick.\" Kulas suddenly suggested.","\"Again? If this is real, you’re playing with your life.\" Tian Yang sighed.","\"What else can we do?\" He shrugged.","Thus, Tian Yang and Ren Xia left again. This time, they made it back home and stayed there for ten years before returning to the palace.","\"Father has fallen sick again,\" Xie Mey revealed to them.","\"Since when?\" Tian Yang asked.","Unlike the first time, they didn’t contact him when Kulas fell sick.","After a moment of silence, Xie Mey responded in an odd voice.","\"The day after you left...\""]}]);
